/* 段落记忆 · 词层 1：词头 → {tw:[关系词,关系类型], en, zh} */
window.APP_MERGE_NET(1,{"par":{"close":{"tw":[["closure",4],["end",2],["finish",2],["last",0],["complete",2],["draw",3],["plug",3],["open",1]],"en":"Last winter the town decided on the closure of the small library. Nobody wanted to see it close, but the money had run out. My neighbours signed a paper to ask for a new end date. After months of work we managed to complete the repairs ourselves and finish the roof before the cold came. On the last evening a reporter came to draw a picture of the empty hall. We pulled the plug of the old coffee machine and opened every window to let the dust out. It felt like an open door again.","zh":"去年冬天镇上决定关闭那间小图书馆。没有人想看着它关门，但经费已经用完了。邻居们签了一份请愿书，要求给一个新的截止日期。忙了几个月，我们自己修好了屋顶，赶在寒潮前把工程做完。最后一个晚上，一位记者来画下了空荡荡的大厅。我们拔掉了旧咖啡机的插头，把每扇窗都打开放灰尘出去。它又像一扇开着的门了。"},"climb":{"tw":[["steep",6],["raise",0],["move",2],["grow",2],["jump",3],["ride",3],["rise",2],["peak",6],["mount",0]],"en":"The path to the top is steep, and the last hour of it is a slow climb. We begin early, before the sun can raise the heat of the day. Step by step we move up and watch the farms below grow small. My brother likes to jump from rock to rock, while I prefer to ride the old cable car. Every spring more visitors rise with the first light, so we chose a quiet Tuesday instead. At the peak we mount a small flag on the stone and eat our bread in the wind.","zh":"上山顶的路很陡，最后一段更是一步一步地爬。我们很早就出发，趁太阳还没把热气升起来。一级一级往上走，看着下面的农庄变得越来越小。弟弟喜欢在石头间跳来跳去，我更愿意坐那趟旧缆车。每年春天都有更多游客跟着第一缕光上山，所以我们挑了安静的周二。到了山顶，我们在石头上竖了一面小旗，在风里啃面包。"},"shout":{"tw":[["loud",6],["call",0],["scream",3],["cry",0],["curse",3],["noise",3],["express",2],["whisper",1],["talk",2]],"en":"At the school sports day everybody shouts. My father can shout so loud that his voice carries across the whole field. He will call my name and I run faster. When our team scores, the crowd begins to scream and cry with joy. A few boys curse the referee and make a lot of noise, so a teacher tells them to express their feelings in a better way. My quiet aunt does not shout at all; she can only whisper, yet we still talk for hours. Loud or soft, her words reach me.","zh":"学校运动会那天人人都在喊。我爸喊起来响得能穿过整个操场。他一叫我的名字，我就跑得更快。我们队得分时，全场又尖叫又欢呼。有几个男孩骂裁判、闹得很吵，老师让他们换个方式表达情绪。我那位安静的姑妈从来不喊，她只能小声说话，可我们仍能聊上几个小时。无论是喊出来的还是轻声说的，她的话我都能听见。"},"hide":{"tw":[["cover",3],["change",2],["skin",0],["conceal",0],["find",6],["harbor",3],["earth",3],["reveal",6]],"en":"The little fox knows how to hide. It will cover its body with dry leaves and change the colour of its coat with the seasons. In the cold months its skin turns white, which is the best way to conceal itself on snow. We could not find it for a whole week. One morning, near the harbor, it sat on the black earth beside a boat and looked at us. It had been sleeping under that same boat the whole time. Then it moved, and the light seemed to reveal a thin line of red fur along its back.","zh":"那只小狐狸很会藏。它用干叶子盖住身子，还随季节变换毛色。天冷的那几个月，它的皮毛转成白色，这是雪地里最好的隐藏办法。整整一周我们都没找到它。有天早上，在港口附近，它坐在一条船边的黑土上看着我们。接着它一动，光似乎把背脊上一道细细的红毛露了出来。"},"pull":{"tw":[["draw",3],["push",1],["force",2],["tear",0],["move",6],["bring",3],["drive",2],["catch",3]],"en":"Our old car stopped in the mud after the rain. My brother had to pull the small trailer by hand. He used a rope to draw it forward while I pushed from behind with all my force. The work was slow and I began to tear my jacket on the door. A farmer came over to help, and together we managed to move the trailer to the road. He offered to bring his truck and used his tractor to drive both cars home. We did not want to catch a cold in the rain.","zh":"雨后我们那辆旧车陷在泥里。弟弟只好用手拖那个小挂车。他用绳子往前拉，我在后面使劲推。活儿很慢，我的外套在车门上开始撕开了。一位农夫过来帮忙，我俩一起把挂车挪到了路上。他提出开他的卡车来，最后用拖拉机把两辆车都拖回了家。我们可不想在雨里感上风寒。"},"join":{"tw":[["unite",0],["connect",2],["junction",4],["joiner",4],["fair",3],["close",3],["union",0],["meet",6]],"en":"Two villages decided to join their small schools. The teachers wanted to unite the classes and connect the old halls with a new path. At the junction of the two roads the workers built a wide gate, and a joiner made the wooden doors by hand. The two head teachers meet every Monday to plan the week. On the day of the fair, families from both sides came close to the stage and watched the children sing. The union of two schools was not easy, but now nobody can tell which child came from which side.","zh":"两个村子决定把各自的小学合并。老师们想把班级并在一起，用一条新路把两座旧校舍连起来。在两条路的交叉口，工人们修了一座宽门，一位木匠手工做了那两扇木门。两位校长每周一碰头商量这一周的安排。集市那天，两边的家庭都凑到台前看孩子们唱歌。两校合一并不容易，但现在没人分得清哪个孩子来自哪一边。"},"decide":{"tw":[["decision",4],["settle",0],["determine",2],["judge",3],["decisive",4],["rule",3],["resolve",0],["agree",6]],"en":"Our class had to decide where to spend the last school trip. The teacher said the decision must come from us. First we tried to settle the money problem, because that would determine everything else. Two students wanted the sea and three wanted the hills. We asked our teacher to judge which plan was fair. In the end his most decisive answer was simple: ask more people. When the vote was over we had to rule out the far places and resolve one last question about the bus. Everyone agreed.","zh":"我们班得决定最后一次班级旅行去哪儿。老师说这个决定必须由我们自己来做。我们先想办法解决钱的问题，因为那会决定其他一切。两个同学想去海边，三个想去山里。我们请老师来评判哪个方案更公平。最后他给出的最果断的回答很简单：多问些人。投票结束后，我们只能排除太远的地方，再解决最后一个关于大巴的疑问。所有人都同意了。"},"difference":{"tw":[["different",4],["differ",4],["differentiate",4],["conflict",0],["balance",3],["gap",3],["remainder",0],["quality",2]],"en":"The two reports about the same meeting were very different. They differ on one point only: the cost. Nobody could explain the difference, and soon it turned into a small conflict. My job was to check the balance of the two lists and find the gap between them. The remainder was small, but the quality of the work was not the same at all. In the end we had to differentiate between what we measured and what we guessed. That one difference changed the whole decision, and afterwards the two teams never worked in the same room again.","zh":"同一场会议的两份报告很不一样。它们只在一个点上不同：成本。没人能解释这个差异，很快它就变成了一场小冲突。我的工作是核对两张清单是否平衡，找出它们之间的缺口。剩余的部分很小，但工作的质量完全不同。最后我们不得不区分哪些是我们实测的、哪些是猜的。正是这一个差异改变了整个决定，此后两支队伍再也没在同一间屋里共事过。"},"judge":{"tw":[["judicial",4],["judiciary",4],["adjudicate",4],["guess",0],["decide",2],["try",0],["court",6],["jury",6],["think",2]],"en":"Nobody wanted to judge that case. The judicial system moves slowly here, and the judiciary in our town has only two small rooms. First the jury has to listen to both sides, then the judge has to decide. You cannot guess; you have to try every door and think about what is fair. To adjudicate a case like this takes weeks. Two old men sat at the back of the court all day and said nothing. When the decision finally came, the judge wrote three long pages, and everybody went home tired.","zh":"没人愿意审那个案子。这里的司法体系走得很慢，我们镇上的司法部门只有两间小屋。首先要由陪审团听双方陈述，然后由法官作出裁决。你不能靠猜，必须试遍每一条门路，想清楚什么是公平的。裁决这样一个案子要好几周。两个老人整天坐在法庭后排，一言不发。裁决终于下来时，法官写了三页长文，所有人都疲惫地回了家。"},"sense":{"tw":[["sensible",4],["sensitive",4],["sensor",4],["sensation",4],["feel",0],["smell",0],["detect",2],["understand",2],["logic",3]],"en":"There is a strange sensation in my left hand. I can feel the heat but I cannot feel the cold, and the doctor says the sensor in the skin has stopped working. It is still very sensitive to a light touch. I cannot smell the coffee any more either. The machine can detect the change, but nobody can understand it yet, and there is no logic in it. The doctors say the sense will come back slowly. A sensible person would rest at home, but I have work to do and my hands are the only tools I own.","zh":"我左手有一种奇怪的感觉。我能感觉到热，却感觉不到冷，医生说皮肤里的传感器已经不工作了。但它对轻微的触碰仍然很敏感。我也闻不到咖啡味了。仪器能检测到这个变化，却没人能解释，其中毫无逻辑可言。医生说这种感觉会慢慢恢复。明智的人会在家休息，可我还有活要干，而这双手是我唯一的工具。"},"enter":{"tw":[["entrance",4],["entry",4],["board",3],["exit",1],["record",0],["book",3],["figure",0],["leave",6]],"en":"You cannot enter the old hall through the front entrance any more. The entry in the book says the door was closed in 1974. If you want to go in, board the small bus at the gate and get off at the north exit; the guard will record your name in a thin notebook. I do not know the exact figure of visitors each year, but we never leave the place before six. The key is kept in a shop across the street, and the woman there will only give it to people she already knows.","zh":"你不能再从正门进入那座旧礼堂了。簿子上的记录说那扇门 1974 年就封了。想进去的话，在大门口坐上小巴，从北门下车，守卫会把你的名字记在一个薄本子里。我不知道每年访客的确切数字，但我们从不早于六点离开。钥匙存在街对面的一家店里，那位女士只把钥匙交给她认识的人。"},"form":{"tw":[["formation",4],["formative",4],["build",0],["class",0],["course",0],["body",2],["change",2]],"en":"The formation of a good habit takes months. My formative years were spent in a small school where the class was tiny and the course was fixed for the whole year. We had to build a routine and keep the body moving every morning before the bell. One small change in the order of things, and the whole form of the day falls apart. One winter our teacher was ill for a week, and everything we had built came apart in three days. The next year we were told to build it again, and the form we found was not quite the same.","zh":"养成一个好习惯要花几个月。我的成长岁月是在一所小学校度过的，那里班级很小，课程整年都固定不变。我们得建立起一套作息，每天早晨铃响前让身体活动起来。只要顺序上有一点小改动，一整天的形态就散了。有一年冬天老师病了一周，我们建起来的那套东西三天就垮了。第二年他们让我们重新建起来，而重新找到的那个形态已经不太一样了。"},"head":{"tw":[["heady",4],["header",4],["lead",0],["mind",0],["control",2],["chair",3],["foot",1],["chief",6]],"en":"After two cups of that strong wine I felt heady and could hardly stand. My head was hot and my mind was not clear at all. Our chief engineer took control of the meeting, and the chair of the board sat at the end of the long table and did not lead the talk at all. A small header on the first page said 'Do not open'. From head to foot I felt the same strange heat, but nobody at the table seemed to notice; they drank water and went on working.","zh":"喝了两杯那种烈酒之后我觉得头晕，几乎站不住。我的头很热，脑子一点也不清楚。我们的总工程师掌控了会议，而董事会主席坐在长桌尽头，完全没有主导讨论。第一页上有一行小标题写着「请勿打开」。从头到脚我都感到同样奇怪的热，可桌上似乎没人察觉，他们喝着水继续干活。"},"heart":{"tw":[["hearty",4],["cardiac",4],["centre",0],["middle",0],["seat",3],["pain",6],["eye",0],["brain",6]],"en":"My grandfather had a cardiac problem last year. The doctor put a small machine in the centre of his chest, right in the middle, next to the heart. He still gets a pain in the left arm sometimes, but he eats a hearty breakfast and laughs a lot. His brain and his eye are fine, he says; it is only the seat of the trouble that is old. Every afternoon he walks to the end of the street and back, and the machine in his chest keeps the time for him.","zh":"我祖父去年心脏出了毛病。医生在他胸口正中央、紧贴心脏的位置放了一个小装置。他左臂有时还会痛，但他早餐吃得很香，也常笑。他说自己的脑子和眼睛都没问题，年久失修的只是毛病所在的那一处。每天下午他都走到街尾再折回来，胸里那个装置替他计着时间。"},"heat":{"tw":[["geothermal",4],["thermal",4],["cool",1],["cold",6],["temperature",6],["fry",3],["soak",3],["passion",0]],"en":"The geothermal water under this town is very hot. In winter we use it for the thermal baths, and the temperature stays near forty degrees all year. I like to soak in it for an hour, then run outside into the cold air to cool down. My friend cooks an egg in the steam and tries to fry bread on a flat stone. He has a passion for that sort of thing, and the heat never bothers him. In summer the same pipes carry cold water to every house on the street.","zh":"这个小镇地下的地热水很烫。冬天我们用地热浴室，水温全年保持在四十度左右。我喜欢在里面泡上一个小时，再跑到外面的冷空气里降温。我朋友在蒸汽里煮鸡蛋，还试着在一块平石上煎面包。他对这类事情极有热情，再热也从不介意。到了夏天，同一批管子给街上每户人家送冷水。"},"lay":{"tw":[["layer",4],["position",0],["pose",0],["load",3],["organize",2],["bare",6],["move",2],["hand",6]],"en":"We had to lay the old floor again. First we took off the top layer and put every board in the same position on the grass. The workers organize the load into two piles, and I help to hand them the nails. Do not move the wet ones, they say, they will crack in the sun. When the floor is bare, my sister likes to pose for a photograph there. I lay my hand on the cold stone underneath and rest, because the stone is older than the house itself.","zh":"我们得把旧地板重新铺一遍。先揭掉最上面一层，把每块木板按原样摆在草地上。工人们把货分成两堆，我帮忙递钉子。他们说湿的那些别动，太阳一晒会裂。地板露出来以后，我妹妹喜欢在那儿摆姿势拍照。我把手放在底下冰冷的石头上歇一会儿，因为那石头比房子本身还老。"},"line":{"tw":[["lining",4],["liner",4],["air",0],["blood",0],["business",0],["cover",2],["fill",2],["face",3]],"en":"There is a long line at the door of the shop every morning. The lining of my coat is torn, so I wear the old wool liner under it. People in the line talk about the air, about their blood pressure, about business. When the shop opens we fill the small room and cover the counter with our bags. I never see the same face twice. By nine the bread is always gone and the line simply disappears, as if it had never been there. I stand in it anyway, every morning, because the wait is the only part of my day that belongs to me.","zh":"每天早上那家店门口都排着长队。我外套的衬里破了，所以里面套着一件旧羊毛内衬。排队的人聊空气、聊血压、聊生意。店门一开，我们就挤满那间小屋，把包堆在柜台上。我从来没见过重复的脸。到九点面包必定卖完，队伍就那样消失了，仿佛从没出现过。但我每天早上还是去排，因为等待是我一天里唯一属于我自己的那段时间。"},"picture":{"tw":[["depict",4],["pictorial",4],["photograph",0],["image",2],["illustrate",3],["figure",0],["film",0],["screen",6]],"en":"The picture on my wall is a photograph of the old harbour. It does not depict the whole town, only a small image of the boats. The book next to it is pictorial: every page has a drawing to illustrate one word. I like the figure of the boy in the corner best. In the film they showed last week, the same picture filled the whole screen for a few seconds. I bought it for almost nothing on a wet morning, and I have never wanted to sell it. It hangs a little crooked, and I have never fixed that either.","zh":"我墙上那幅画是一张旧港的照片。它没有描绘整个镇子，只有小船的一个小影像。旁边那本书是图解式的：每一页都有一幅画来解释一个词。我最喜欢角落里那个男孩的形象。在他们上周放的那部电影里，同一幅画面有几秒钟铺满了整个银幕。我是在一个雨天早晨几乎白捡来的，也从来没想卖掉它。它挂得有点歪，我也一直没去扶正。"},"sight":{"tw":[["optic",4],["visual",4],["spectacle",3],["look",2],["position",2],["deal",0],["flood",3]],"en":"The sight from the top of the hill is famous. An optic company put a telescope there, and from that position you can see a visual trick: the sun seems to rise twice. A flood of light hits the valley below, and every look through the glass costs one coin. The whole spectacle lasts two minutes. People come from the next town to see it, and they never say a word while they wait. It is still a good deal for the money. On a clear day the view reaches thirty miles, and for the rest of the week nobody talks about anything else.","zh":"山顶上的景致很有名。一家光学公司在那里放了一台望远镜，从那个位置你能看到一个视觉上的把戏：太阳像是升起了两次。一大片光倾泻到下面的山谷，每看一次收一枚硬币。整个奇观持续两分钟。人们从邻镇赶来看，等待时一句话也不说。就这个价钱来说，仍然很划算。天气晴好时视野能及三十英里，此后一整周大家都不聊别的。"},"sign":{"tw":[["signature",4],["signify",4],["mark",0],["flag",3],["write",2],["contract",0],["alarm",3],["house",0]],"en":"There was no sign on the door of the old house. The only mark I could find was a small flag on the gate and a name that somebody had been asked to write in pencil. The contract in my bag had a signature at the bottom, but I did not know what it was meant to signify. At six the alarm went off and we had to leave the room. Nobody came to explain, and the flag stayed on the gate for another twenty years. When the house was pulled down, that flag was the only thing anybody took away.","zh":"那座老房子的门上没有任何标志。我能找到的唯一记号是大门上的一面小旗，还有一个被人用铅笔写下的名字。我包里那份合同底部有个签名，但我不知道它意味着什么。六点钟警报响了，我们只好离开那个房间。没人来解释，那面小旗又在门上挂了二十年。房子拆掉时，唯一被人带走的就是那面旗。"},"stand":{"tw":[["standard",4],["stance",4],["base",0],["bear",0],["continue",2],["fight",2],["lie",1],["hold",6]],"en":"I cannot stand his stance on this question. The standard answer is to wait, but he wants to fight at once. His base is weak: he cannot bear the cost, and if he continues like this the whole plan will not hold. Everything he says seems to lie on one thin idea, and that idea is wrong. Two of his oldest friends left the room before he finished speaking. I stayed, because somebody has to tell him the truth. He will not thank me for it, but a friend who says nothing at all is not a friend.","zh":"我受不了他在这个问题上的立场。标准答案是等等看，可他想立刻开战。他的根基很弱：他承担不起这笔费用，再这样下去整个方案都撑不住。他说的每句话似乎都建立在一条单薄的想法上，而那条想法是错的。他还没说完，两个老朋友就离开了房间。我留了下来，因为总得有人告诉他真相。"},"star":{"tw":[["interstellar",4],["stellar",4],["sun",3],["ace",0],["champion",0],["idol",3],["character",2],["lead",0]],"en":"The star of our team is a quiet boy who never talks about his interstellar dreams. In the stellar light of the evening he runs faster than anyone else, and in the morning sun he trains alone before school begins. He is the ace of the school, our champion for three years, and the idol of every small child here. But his character is what I like most: he does not lead by shouting, and he never laughs at the slower boys. He left for a bigger school last year, and the sun over the field has not felt the same since.","zh":"我们队的明星是个安静的男孩，从不谈起自己星际旅行的梦想。傍晚的星光下他跑得比谁都快，清晨的太阳里他在开学前独自训练。他是学校的王牌、连续三年的冠军，也是这里每个小孩的偶像。但我最喜欢的是他的品性：他从不靠喊叫来带队，也从不嘲笑跑得慢的孩子。去年他转去了更大的学校，自那以后操场上的阳光就不一样了。"},"tell":{"tw":[["tale",4],["teller",4],["say",0],["state",0],["express",2],["answer",3],["order",0],["know",6]],"en":"Let me tell you a short tale about a bank teller. He did not say much: he would state the amount, express nothing at all, and answer only yes or no. In order to understand the man you had to know his face. People tell me he was happy in that small room behind the thick glass. He never asked about my money and he never told me his name, but for ten years we said good morning to each other every day. When the bank closed I went to say goodbye, and the glass was already gone.","zh":"让我给你讲一个关于银行出纳员的短故事。他话不多：只报出金额，不流露任何情绪，回答也无非是或否。要理解这个人，你得熟悉他的表情。人们告诉我，他在那层厚玻璃后面的小屋里其实挺快乐。他从不打听我的钱，也从不告诉我他的名字，但十年来我们每天都互道早安。银行关门那天我去道别，那层玻璃已经不在了。"},"trust":{"tw":[["trustee",4],["fiduciary",4],["believe",2],["hope",0],["credit",3],["count",3],["expect",2],["fund",6]],"en":"You cannot trust a trustee who never writes back. I still believe in him, and I hope he will return, but I do not expect it any more. The fund is small now, and the credit of the office is gone. You can count the people who still trust him on one hand; his fiduciary duty means nothing to the rest of us. His letters are still in my drawer, unopened, and I think they will stay there for a long time. The trustee was never found, and the office has since been turned into a shop.","zh":"你没法信任一个从不回信的受托人。我仍然相信他，也希望他会回来，但我已经不抱期望了。基金现在很少，那间办公室的信誉也没了。还信任他的人一只手就数得过来；他的受托责任对其余的人来说毫无意义。他的信还放在我抽屉里，没有拆开，我想它们会在那里放很久。那位受托人再没被找到，那间办公室后来改成了一家店。"},"wave":{"tw":[["waver",4],["wavy",4],["curl",0],["roll",0],["flap",3],["wake",3],["lift",3],["move",2]],"en":"A big wave hit the side of the boat. The wavy line of the water rose, curled and rolled over the deck. The sail began to flap and the wake behind us turned white. I did not move and I did not waver; the lift of the boat felt like a hand under my feet. An hour earlier the sea had been calm as a table, and by night it will be calm again. Only the rope in my hand says that any of this happened. We came in at dusk, wet through, and nobody on the shore had noticed a thing.","zh":"一个大浪打在船舷上。起伏的水线升起来，卷曲着翻过甲板。帆开始拍打，我们身后的尾迹变成了白色。我没有动，也没有动摇；船被托起来的感觉就像脚下有一只手。一小时前海面平得像桌面，到了夜里它又会平下来。只有手里这根绳子说明刚才的一切真的发生过。我们黄昏靠岸，全身湿透，而岸上的人什么也没察觉。"},"word":{"tw":[["lexical",4],["verbal",4],["phrase",0],["book",0],["news",0],["express",2],["read",6],["order",2]],"en":"One word can change a whole page. I keep a lexical notebook: every verbal form and every short phrase goes into it. When I read the news I copy the words I do not know, in order of how often they appear. A book of ten thousand words is enough to express almost everything, my teacher says, and one wrong word can cost you a friend. I have filled four notebooks since I started, and the fifth is already half full with words I use every day. In order to read them again I mark the page with a small number.","zh":"一个词就能改变整页的意思。我有一本词汇笔记本：每个动词形式和每个短语都记进去。看新闻时我把不认识的词抄下来，按出现频率排序。我老师说，一本一万词的书足以表达几乎所有东西，而一个用错的词能让你失去一个朋友。开始记以来我已经写满四个本子。为了能再读一遍，我在页边标上一个小号码。"},"death":{"tw":[["die",4],["dead",6],["mortuary",4],["end",2],["grave",3],["birth",1],["destruction",0],["demise",0]],"en":"The death of the old king changed everything. Few people died in the war itself, but the destruction of the city killed the trade. In the mortuary they counted the bodies, and the dead were carried out at dawn. The grave of his father stood next to the new one. His birth had been a feast; his demise was a silence, and the end came quietly. For a whole year afterwards the shops stayed shut and nobody sang in the streets. The grave outside the wall is small, and no name was ever cut into the stone.","zh":"老国王的死改变了一切。战争本身没死几个人，但城市的毁灭扼杀了贸易。在停尸房里他们清点遗体，死者于黎明时被抬走。他父亲的墓就在新墓旁边。他的出生曾是一场盛宴，他的离世却是一片寂静，结局来得悄无声息。此后整整一年，店铺都关着，街上再没人唱歌。墙外那座墓很小，石头上始终没有刻名字。"},"nose":{"tw":[["nosy",4],["nasal",4],["snout",3],["scent",0],["poke",0],["push",2],["throat",6],["front",2]],"en":"The dog has a cold nose and a very nasal bark. Its snout is always in the long grass, following some scent. Do not poke it and do not push it away; it will only come back. The hair on its throat is white, and the front of its face is black. My nosy neighbour says the dog knows everything that happens in this street. During the heat of the day it sleeps under the table and does not move at all. At night it pushes the gate open with its snout and walks the whole street alone.","zh":"那只狗鼻子凉凉的，叫声带着很重的鼻音。它的口鼻总埋在深草里，追着某种气味。别去戳它，也别把它推开，它只会再回来。它喉咙上的毛是白的，脸的前部是黑的。我那位爱打听的邻居说，这条街上发生的事这只狗全知道。白天最热的时候它就趴在桌子底下睡，一动也不动。到了夜里它用口鼻把大门顶开，独自把整条街走一遍。"},"office":{"tw":[["official",4],["officiate",4],["position",0],["post",0],["headquarters",3],["duty",2],["staff",2],["department",6]],"en":"The office is on the third floor of an old building. The official letter says my position starts on Monday. Our headquarters is in another city, and this post is only a small department of four people. The staff are kind. My first duty is to answer the phone; I also have to officiate at the morning meeting. The lift has not worked since March, so we all take the stairs, and the stairs are the only place where anybody speaks freely. The staff say the department will move next year, and nobody is sorry about it.","zh":"办公室在一栋旧楼的三层。公函上说我的职位周一开始。我们的总部在另一个城市，这个岗位只是一个四人的小部门。同事们都很和气。我的第一项职责是接电话，还得主持晨会。电梯从三月起就坏了，所以我们全都走楼梯，而楼梯是唯一能让人畅所欲言的地方。同事们说这个部门明年要搬走，没人为此难过。"},"please":{"tw":[["pleasant",4],["pleasure",4],["delight",0],["satisfy",2],["enchant",3],["wish",2],["displease",1],["ask",6]],"en":"It is hard to please my aunt. A pleasant word in the morning will delight her, but nothing can satisfy her for long. The garden does not enchant her any more. I only wish she would ask for what she wants; then I could please her at once. Last week I displeased her by arriving late. It is no pleasure to sit in that room with her. She says the house is too quiet, and I think that is the whole trouble. I ask her again what would please her, and she only says the name of my mother.","zh":"要让我姑妈满意很难。早上一句好听的话能让她高兴，但什么都不能让她满意太久。花园已经不再让她着迷了。我只希望她能把想要的东西说出来，那样我马上就能让她高兴。上周我迟到惹她不快。和她坐在那个房间里毫无乐趣可言。她说屋子太安静了，我想这就是全部的问题所在。我又问她什么能让她开心，她只说出了我母亲的名字。"},"water":{"tw":[["aquatic",4],["hydraulic",4],["irrigate",0],["wet",2],["dry",6],["fill",2],["sand",6]],"en":"The water in this valley comes from a spring. In summer we irrigate the fields with it, and the hydraulic pump is old but still works. The aquatic plants near the edge stay wet all year, while the sand on the far side is dry. Every evening I fill two bottles and carry them home. In winter the spring slows down and we have to walk much further for the same two bottles. My mother says the spring has never once failed us, and I hope that is still true.","zh":"这个山谷里的水来自一眼泉。夏天我们用它灌溉田地，那台水泵很旧但还能用。靠边的水生植物终年是湿的，而远处那片沙子却是干的。每天傍晚我灌满两瓶水带回家。到了冬天泉水流得慢，为同样两瓶水我们得走远得多的路。"},"admit":{"tw":[["admission",4],["accept",2],["allow",0],["permit",2],["deny",1],["acknowledge",6],["seat",3],["serve",2]],"en":"They will not admit more than fifty people. The admission desk is at the door: if they accept your ticket they allow you in, but the permit is only for one hour. They deny nothing and acknowledge every question, yet the room can serve only a few at a time. I could not find a single empty seat. Outside, a hundred people were still waiting in the rain, and nobody there looked angry. They simply waited while the rain fell on their coats and on the stone steps of the hall.","zh":"他们最多只放进五十个人。售票处在门口：如果他们收下你的票就允许你进去，但许可只限一小时。他们什么也不否认，对每个问题都有回应，可那间屋子一次只能招待几个人。我一个空座位都没找到。外面还有一百个人在雨里等着，而那边没有一个人显得生气。"},"arm":{"tw":[["armament",4],["disarm",1],["weapon",0],["sword",3],["bow",3],["instrument",2],["limb",2],["finger",6]],"en":"He hurt his left arm in the factory last month. The limb was not broken, but he cannot lift a heavy instrument any more, and his fingers are slow in the cold. In the old armament room next door they keep weapons behind glass: a bow, a sword, two long guns. The guard had to disarm a man there once, and the story is still told in the village. My brother works with one hand now and laughs about it. He says a man only needs one good arm to do the work of two.","zh":"他上个月在工厂里伤了左臂。那条胳膊没断，但他再也不能举起重工具了，天冷时手指也不灵活。隔壁那间旧军械室里，武器都用玻璃罩着：一张弓、一把剑、两杆长枪。守卫曾在那里缴过一个人的械，这事村里至今还在讲。我哥哥现在只用一只手干活，还拿这事开玩笑。他说一个人只要有一条好胳膊，就能干两条胳膊的活。"},"better":{"tw":[["bet",4],["best",0],["improve",0],["worse",1],["change",2],["build",3],["break",0],["help",3]],"en":"I made a bet with myself last spring. The best way to get better at this job, I decided, is to build one small habit and never break it. A change of hours will help; working later only makes things worse. I want to improve slowly, not quickly. My brother says I should rest more, and I am sure he is right, because he is a good worker and I am not. So far I have kept the bet for eleven weeks, and the work is easier than it was.","zh":"去年春天我和自己打了个赌。我认定，要把这活儿做得更好，最好的办法是养成一个小习惯并且不打破它。改一改作息会有帮助；干到更晚只会让情况更糟。我要慢慢提高，而不是求快。我哥哥说我该多休息，我确信他是对的，因为他是个好工人而我不是。到现在这个赌我守了十一周，活儿也比从前轻松了。"},"home":{"tw":[["homely",4],["homestead",3],["house",2],["family",0],["return",2],["away",1],["lodge",3],["rest",6],["environment",2]],"en":"My idea of home is a homely room with one window. The house is small, but the homestead behind it has been in our family for four generations. When I return from the city I sleep for twelve hours; away from it I cannot rest at all. My friends lodge in a hotel two streets from here and say the environment is the same anywhere. I tell them they are wrong, and that one room you know is worth more than a big one you do not. They return to the city on Sunday, and I stay here another week.","zh":"我心目中的家是一个带一扇窗的朴素房间。房子很小，可屋后那片宅地已属于我们家四代人了。从城里回来时我能睡上十二个小时；离开它我就完全无法休息。我的朋友们住在两条街外的一家旅馆，说环境在哪里都一样。我告诉他们他们错了，一间你熟悉的屋子比一间你不熟悉的大屋子值钱得多。他们周日回城里去，我在这儿再待一周。"},"let":{"tw":[["letter",4],["allow",3],["accept",2],["prevent",1],["rent",0],["lease",0],["admit",3],["leave",2]],"en":"They will not let us sign the lease before June. The letter says the owner will allow three people in the flat, but he will not accept a dog. Nothing can prevent him from changing his mind either, and he will not admit that the price is too high. We rent the top floor now and pay by the week. If he decides to leave the country, we will have to find another place before the summer ends. The dog sleeps under the table in the kitchen and has never once barked at anybody.","zh":"他们不允许我们在六月前签租约。信上说房东允许三个人住这套公寓，但不接受养狗。也没什么能阻止他改主意，而他也不肯承认价格太高。我们现在租顶层，按周付钱。如果他决定出国，我们就得在夏天结束前另找住处。"},"light":{"tw":[["lightly",4],["clean",0],["clear",0],["flood",3],["surface",6],["dark",1],["burn",2],["match",3],["easy",5]],"en":"The light in this room is strange. It is clean and clear in the morning, when a flood of sun hits the white surface of the wall, but by four o'clock it is almost dark. I burn one candle and read by it, or I strike a match and walk to the window. Sleep comes lightly here; the dark does not feel heavy and the light does not hurt my eyes. It is easy to work in this room, and just as easy to stop working. When the sun goes I light the lamp, and the room looks clear again.","zh":"这屋子里的光很奇怪。清晨它干净而清澈，一大片阳光打在墙的白色表面上，可到四点就几乎黑了。我点一支蜡烛就着光读书，或者划根火柴走到窗前。在这里睡觉很浅；黑暗并不沉重，光也不刺眼。在这屋里很容易干活，也同样很容易就停下不干。太阳一落我就点灯，屋子看上去又变得清晰起来。"},"mind":{"tw":[["mental",4],["head",0],["tend",3],["forget",1],["manage",2],["worry",3],["notice",2],["idea",0],["listen",0]],"en":"There is too much in my mind this week. My head is full of small numbers, and I tend to forget names. The doctor says it is not a mental problem, only tiredness. I try to manage one thing at a time. Do not worry, she says, and notice what you eat. It is a good idea, and I should listen to her, but I never do. My mother had the same mind and the same habit of not listening to anybody. This morning I put the keys in the fridge and the milk in my bag.","zh":"这星期我脑子里装的东西太多了。我满脑子都是小数字，还容易忘名字。医生说这不是精神上的问题，只是累。我试着一次只处理一件事。别担心，她说，注意你吃的东西。这是个好主意，我该听她的，可我从来不听。我母亲也有同样的脑子，也有同样的、谁的话都不听的习惯。今天早上我把钥匙放进冰箱，把牛奶塞进了包里。"},"notice":{"tw":[["notify",4],["bill",0],["knock",3],["sign",2],["ignore",1],["check",6],["card",0],["discover",0],["mention",3]],"en":"Did you notice the notice on the door? A small card says we must notify the office if we leave. Nobody told me about it; they did not even knock. There is a sign above the bell, but people ignore it every single day. I had to check the bill three times before I discovered the extra line at the bottom. When I asked about it, the man at the desk did not mention it once. He only looked at his hands. The next day a card was on the door again, with the same three lines on it.","zh":"你注意到门上那张告示了吗？一张小卡片说我们离开时必须通知办公室。没人跟我说过这件事，他们连门都没敲。铃上方有个标牌，可人们每天都视而不见。我把账单核对了三遍，才发现底部多出的那一行。我去问时，柜台后面那个人一次也没提。他只是看着自己的手。第二天门上又出现了一张卡片，还是那三行字。"},"pass":{"tw":[["passage",4],["clear",3],["break",3],["change",2],["fail",1],["carry",3],["leave",2],["draw",0]],"en":"You cannot pass this road in winter. The passage over the hill is clear for only three months, and one bad storm can break it completely. If the weather does not change, we will fail to reach the village at all. Two men carry the mail on foot and leave before dawn. I draw a map every year and it is never the same twice. Still, the post always gets through in the end, and that is the only thing that matters up here. One year the passage was clear in February, and everybody talked about it until June.","zh":"冬天你没法通过这条路。翻过山口那条通道只有三个月是通的，一场坏风暴就能把它彻底毁掉。如果天气不变，我们根本到不了那个村子。两个人徒步送信，天不亮就出发。我每年画一张地图，从来没重过样。可邮件最后总能送到，而在这山里那是唯一要紧的事。有一年二月山口就通了，大家一直议论到六月。"},"present":{"tw":[["presence",4],["face",0],["date",3],["inform",2],["past",1],["stage",0],["state",2],["deliver",0]],"en":"At present there is no water in the tank. The presence of two engineers did not help; they only informed us of the date of the repair and left. On the stage above the door someone has written the state of the pump every day for ten years. In the past we never had to check it. The man who comes to deliver the parts knows the problem by heart, but he did not show his face for three days. Until then we carry water from the well in the yard, which is what everyone did in the past.","zh":"目前水箱里没有水。两位工程师在场也没用；他们只是通知了我们维修的日期就走了。门上方那块平台上，有人十年来每天都记下水泵的状态。从前我们根本不用检查。来送零件的那个人对这个问题了如指掌，可他整整三天没露面。在那之前，我们从院子里的井里打水，过去大家也都是这么做的。"},"sound":{"tw":[["soundly",4],["voice",0],["acoustic",6],["noise",3],["silence",1],["heavy",0],["blow",3],["announce",2],["good",5]],"en":"The sound in the old hall is beautiful. A single voice fills it, and the acoustic roof holds every note. There is no noise from the street, only a heavy silence between the songs. When the singer stops you can hear the wind blow across the roof. The man at the door will announce the next piece in a low voice. At night the whole building sleeps soundly. It is a good place to sit and think, and nobody asks you to leave. The heavy door closes behind you, and the noise of the town is simply gone.","zh":"那座旧厅里的声音很美。一个人的嗓音就能填满它，声学屋顶留住了每一个音。街上没有噪音，歌声之间只有沉沉的寂静。歌手停下时，你能听见风掠过屋顶。门口那个人会用低沉的嗓音报出下一曲。夜里整栋楼睡得很沉。那是个适合坐着想事的好地方，也没人赶你走。沉重的门在身后关上，镇上的噪音就那样消失了。"},"base":{"tw":[["basal",4],["bag",0],["bed",3],["bottom",2],["floor",0],["build",3],["control",2],["foot",0]],"en":"The base of the old tower is wider than the top. At the bottom there is a thick basal layer of stone, and below that only sand. We had to build a floor of wood over it so that nobody would fall through. Every bag of tools sits in the corner. From the control room you can see the whole valley, and it is a long way down to the foot of the hill. A bed of dry grass used to cover the stone, but the rain took it years ago.","zh":"那座古塔的基部比顶部宽。底部有一层很厚的基底石，再往下就只有沙子了。我们不得不在上面铺一层木地板，免得有人掉下去。每袋工具都堆在角落里。从控制室能看到整个山谷，往下到山脚还有很长一段路。从前有一层干草铺在石头上，但多年前就被雨水冲走了。"},"bet":{"tw":[["count",0],["pot",3],["trust",2],["raise",3],["gamble",2],["cash",6],["play",3],["better",4]],"en":"Do not bet on that horse. I do not trust the man who owns it, and I can count the times he has actually paid on one hand. The pot is small tonight, but he will raise it as soon as you sit down. My cousin likes to gamble and always plays with cash. You will feel better if you keep your money in your pocket. I learned that lesson in a single evening, and it was not a cheap one to learn. I still go to the track, but I only watch the horses and count my own money.","zh":"别赌那匹马。我不信任它的主人，他真正付过钱的次数我一只手就数得过来。今晚的赌池很小，可你一坐下他就会加注。我表弟喜欢赌，而且总是用现金玩。把钱留在口袋里你会好受些。我是在一个晚上学会这个教训的，而那学费并不便宜。我还会去马场，但只看马，只数自己的钱。"},"board":{"tw":[["boarder",4],["card",0],["catch",3],["enter",2],["commission",6],["room",0],["deal",3],["table",2]],"en":"The board meets at eight. Each member puts a card on the table, and the chairman reads out the name of every boarder in the house. We deal with one question at a time, and only one. A small commission was set up last year to check the accounts, and nobody has entered that room since March. I try to catch the chairman before the meeting, but he is never alone. Last week they sat for four hours and decided nothing at all. The card with my name is still on the table, and the room is still locked.","zh":"董事会八点开会。每位成员把一张卡片放在桌上，主席逐一念出屋里每位寄宿者的名字。我们一次只处理一个问题，而且只处理一个。去年成立了一个小委员会来查账，可自三月起没人进过那个房间。我想在会前逮住主席，可他从没落单过。上周他们坐了四个小时，什么也没定下来。桌上那张写着我名字的卡片还在，那个房间还锁着。"},"carry":{"tw":[["carriage",4],["bear",2],["deal",3],["act",2],["express",0],["fly",3],["bring",2],["hold",0]],"en":"I have to carry these boxes to the station. The carriage of the train leaves in an hour, and the porter will not bear more than two at a time. We deal with the heaviest first and then act quickly. If we are late they will not hold the train, and my sister will have to bring the rest tomorrow. The express never stops here. Nothing flies out of this town, so everything goes by rail. The porter says the same thing every winter, and every winter he turns out to be right.","zh":"我得把这些箱子搬到车站去。那趟火车的车厢一小时后开，搬运工一次不肯扛超过两箱。我们先处理最重的，然后动作要快。要是迟了他们不会等车，剩下的就得让我妹妹明天带来。快车从不停这里。这个镇上什么也飞不出去，所以一切都走铁路。"},"catch":{"tw":[["catchment",4],["see",0],["bag",3],["board",2],["stop",0],["fish",3],["throw",6],["view",0]],"en":"We could not catch a single fish all morning. The catchment above the dam is full of rain water and the fish are deep. I stood on the board and could not see a thing; my bag was still empty at noon. Then one careless throw of a stone by a boy on the far bank moved the whole shoal at once. From where I stood the view was lovely, but that does not stop me from wanting one fish. Next week I will try the other side, where the water is slower.","zh":"整个上午我们一条鱼也没抓到。水坝上游的集水区灌满了雨水，鱼都沉在深处。我站在木板上什么也看不见；到了中午我的袋子还是空的。后来一个男孩扔了块石头，整群鱼一下子全动了。从我站的地方看出去景色很美，可这并不能阻止我想要一条鱼。下周我要去另一边试试，那边水流更缓。"},"count":{"tw":[["counter",4],["bet",0],["total",3],["depend",0],["poll",3],["trust",2],["result",6],["look",0]],"en":"We count the votes twice. The counter at the front of the room is an old wooden table, and the total is written on the wall in chalk. You cannot depend on one count, and you cannot trust the first result either. At the last poll two hundred people came, and the look on his face said everything. I would bet the second count is the true one. Nobody argues after the second count; they simply pick up their coats and go home. The total goes on the wall in chalk, and the rain washes it off by morning.","zh":"我们把票点两遍。屋子前面那张计数器是一张旧木桌，总数用粉笔写在墙上。你不能只靠一次计数，也不能相信第一次的结果。上一次投票来了两百人，而他脸上的表情说明了一切。我敢打赌第二次计数才是真的。第二次计数之后没人再争，他们只是拿起外套回家。总数用粉笔写在墙上，到早上被雨冲掉。"},"die":{"tw":[["death",4],["break",0],["fall",3],["change",2],["pass",0],["crash",3],["feel",2],["fail",0]],"en":"Old engines do not die all at once. First a small part breaks, then the pressure falls, and the change is very slow. You can feel it in the steering wheel months before the end. If the pump fails, the car will crash into the wall at the next bend. The death of an engine is a long story, and most of it happens quietly. Mine passed away on a Tuesday, in front of my own house, with the key still in the door. I still feel for the brake when I hear that particular sound.","zh":"老发动机不会一下子死掉。先是某个小零件坏掉，接着压力下降，变化非常慢。在结局到来前几个月，你就能在方向盘上感觉到。如果水泵失灵，车会在下一个弯道撞上墙。一台发动机的死亡是个漫长的故事，而且大部分是悄无声息地发生的。我那台是在一个星期二咽气的，就在我自己家门口，钥匙还插在门上。每当听到那种特别的声音，我还是会去踩刹车。"},"doctor":{"tw":[["doctoral",4],["fix",0],["fill",3],["better",2],["nurse",6],["repair",0],["piece",3],["restore",0]],"en":"The doctor came at seven. He fixed my arm, filled a small cup with something bitter, and said I would feel better in a week. A nurse held the lamp; she said the same doctor had repaired her father's leg and restored it to full use. He showed me one small piece of bone in the palm of his hand. He is writing a doctoral paper about exactly this sort of injury. He told me I was lucky, and I did not argue with him. The nurse filled in the form, and he signed the bottom of the page.","zh":"医生七点来的。他给我接好了胳膊，倒了一小杯很苦的东西，说我一周后就会好些。一位护士举着灯；她说同一位医生修好过她父亲的腿，并让它完全恢复了功能。他摊开手掌给我看一小块骨头。他正在写一篇关于这类损伤的博士论文。他说我很幸运，我没有跟他争。护士填好表格，他在纸的下方签了名。"},"draw":{"tw":[["drawer",4],["force",0],["arrange",2],["match",6],["line",0],["catch",3],["win",6],["lot",0]],"en":"Let us draw for the first turn. In the drawer of the little table there are four cards; arrange them face down and each of us takes one. Catch your card before it falls on the floor. The match is won by the highest line, so look at it carefully. I never win anything by luck, and a lot of people at this table say the same. You can force the card if you want, but then there is no point in playing at all. I drew the lowest line, as usual, and the drawer was closed again.","zh":"咱们抽签决定先手吧。小桌的抽屉里有四张牌；把它们正面朝下摆好，每人拿一张。牌掉到地上之前接住它。比赛由点数最大的那一行获胜，所以要看仔细。我从来没靠运气赢过什么，这张桌上很多人也这么说。你想的话可以硬来，但那样玩起来就没意思了。我照例抽到了最小的一行，抽屉又合上了。"},"drive":{"tw":[["drift",4],["cause",0],["lift",3],["fight",2],["force",0],["pull",3],["hit",2],["push",0]],"en":"It is a long drive to the coast. The road begins to drift west after the bridge, and the wind can cause the car to lift on the open bends. My father would push the speed up and then pull it back again; he never liked to fight the wheel. One year a stone hit the glass and we ran the last ten miles with no window at all. I drive slowly now, and the force of the wind still surprises me every time. My son does not like the coast road, and I do not push him to drive it.","zh":"开车到海边要走很久。过了桥这条路就开始向西偏，在开阔的弯道上风能把车掀起来。我父亲会把速度推上去再收回来；他从不喜欢跟方向盘较劲。有一年一块石头打在玻璃上，我们最后十英里是没窗跑完的。我现在开得慢，而每次那股风力还是让我吃惊。我儿子不喜欢那条海边公路，我也不催他去开。"},"earth":{"tw":[["terrestrial",4],["ground",2],["floor",3],["concern",2],["space",6],["land",0],["forest",3],["hide",2],["world",0]],"en":"The earth here is red and thin. On the ground under the trees there is a soft floor of leaves, and the forest hides more than it shows. Scientists come to study the terrestrial plants; others look up at the space above the trees and forget the land under their feet. Their only concern is the rain, and the rain comes when it wants to. For me this small piece of earth is the whole world, and I do not want to leave it. The ground is soft in May and hard in August, and I know every metre of it.","zh":"这里的土又红又薄。树下的地面上铺着一层松软的落叶，森林藏起来的比露出来的多。科学家来研究陆生植物；另一些人抬头看树顶以上的太空，却忘了脚下的土地。他们唯一关心的是雨，而雨想来就来。对我来说这一小块土地就是整个世界，我不想离开它。五月的土地松软，八月就硬了，每一米我都熟。"},"edge":{"tw":[["edgy",4],["inch",0],["shoulder",3],["line",2],["march",0],["margin",3],["side",2],["border",3],["corner",6]],"en":"We walked along the edge of the field for an hour. The border with the next farm is only a line of small stones, and the margin of the wood lies on the far side. At the corner an old man was marching up and down with his shoulder against the wind. I moved an inch at a time, because the drop below was long. My friend felt edgy and would not look down once the whole way. We sat down at last, well back from the edge, and ate the bread we had brought.","zh":"我们沿着田边走了一个小时。与隔壁农场的分界只是一排小石头，树林的边缘在更远的一侧。拐角处有个老人顶着风来回踱步，肩膀迎着风口。我一次只挪一寸，因为下面的落差很大。我朋友一路上都很紧张，一次也没敢往下看。"},"face":{"tw":[["facial",4],["front",2],["bottom",3],["cover",2],["look",0],["top",3],["lie",2],["present",0]],"en":"I did not want to face him again. His face was in the front room, at the top of the stairs, and the look on it had not changed at all. He would not lie down and sat in the chair by the window all night. The bottom of the door was covered with old letters that nobody had opened. His facial expression was calm, too calm. At present I still do not know what I said to him that evening. The front door was open, and his coat was on the top step where he left it.","zh":"我不想再面对他。他的脸在前面那间屋里、楼梯顶端，脸上的表情一点没变。他不肯躺下，整夜坐在窗边那把椅子上。门的下半部堆满了没人拆过的旧信。他的面部表情很平静，平静得过分。直到现在我也不知道那天晚上我对他说了什么。前门开着，他的外套还留在他放的那个最高一级台阶上。"},"fire":{"tw":[["fiery",4],["burn",0],["bake",2],["hire",1],["raise",0],["excite",3],["explosion",6],["attack",2]],"en":"The fire started in the bakery at two. The old oven was still burning when we came, and the smell of baked bread was everywhere in the street. Someone raised the alarm, and the explosion of the gas bottle woke the whole neighbourhood. It was a fiery hour, and the thought of it still excites me. Nobody knows what could attack the wiring like that. They will not hire a new baker until the roof is fixed. The cat was found two streets away the next morning, asleep under a car.","zh":"火灾是两点在面包房起的。我们赶到时那个旧烤炉还在烧，街上到处是烤面包的味道。有人拉响了警报，煤气瓶的爆炸惊醒了整个街区。那是火光冲天的一小时，现在想起来还让我激动。没人知道是什么能那样侵蚀线路。屋顶修好之前他们不会雇新面包师。"},"fix":{"tw":[["fixture",4],["cook",0],["care",3],["better",2],["plug",6],["doctor",0],["dress",3],["hole",0]],"en":"Can you fix this lamp? The fixture is loose and the plug is broken. My brother cooked dinner while I worked, and my sister dressed the children and put them to bed. There is a hole in the wall behind the lamp that I cannot fill. The doctor who lived here before us took better care of this house than we ever did. I will fix it properly on Sunday. Until then we will sit in the dark and talk, which is not such a bad thing. The children do not mind the dark at all, and my brother cooks better by candlelight.","zh":"你能修一下这盏灯吗？灯具松了，插头也坏了。我干活时我哥哥做了晚饭，我姐姐给孩子们穿好衣服哄他们上床。灯后面墙上有个洞，我填不上。住在我们之前的那位医生对这房子比我们上心得多。我周日会好好修它。在那之前我们就摸黑坐着说话，这也算不上什么坏事。孩子们一点也不介意黑，我哥哥在烛光下做得反而更好。"},"green":{"tw":[["greenery",4],["park",0],["sprout",3],["site",2],["ripe",1],["emerald",3],["vegetable",2]],"en":"The green field behind the house turns yellow in July. The greenery along the river is thick, and in spring every small sprout comes up between the stones. We chose the site for the new park because it stays green all year. The emerald water below the bridge is cold, and the vegetable garden next to it is not ripe yet. My mother says green is the only colour she can trust. She has planted the same three rows for forty years. In winter the field is grey, but the sprout in the window stays green all year.","zh":"屋后那片绿色的田到七月就变黄了。河边的草木很茂密，春天每一个小芽都从石缝里钻出来。我们把新公园选在这里，是因为它整年都是绿的。桥下那水呈翡翠色，很凉；旁边的菜园还没熟。我母亲说绿色是她唯一能信任的颜色。同一片三行地她种了四十年。冬天田野是灰的，可窗台上那株小苗整年都是绿的。"},"hand":{"tw":[["manual",4],["deal",3],["pass",0],["reach",0],["left",3],["right",3],["side",2],["hard",6]],"en":"Take my hand and do not let go. The manual says you must deal with the switch with your left hand only, and pass nothing to the other side of the machine. If you can reach the lever, pull it once and pull it hard. On the right there is a small wheel, and on the back a box of tools. My grandfather worked with either hand and never read a manual in his life. He says the hand knows more than the head, and for this job he is right.","zh":"抓住我的手，别松开。手册上说，操作这个开关只能用左手，而且不能把任何东西递到机器的另一侧。如果你够得到那根杠杆，就拉一次，用力拉。右边有个小轮子，后面有个工具箱。我祖父两只手都能干活，一辈子没读过手册。他说手比脑子懂得多，干这活儿他说得对。"},"lock":{"tw":[["locker",4],["curl",0],["engage",0],["hold",2],["hook",6],["mesh",0],["hair",2],["prop",6]],"en":"The lock on the old locker is broken. Inside there is a rope, a metal hook and a piece of mesh that used to hold the window shut. You have to engage the small lever first, then turn the key twice, and only then will the prop stay in place. My sister's hair was caught in it once, in a single curl, and she has never touched the door since. I keep a spare key in my pocket for the days when it refuses to open. The locker is empty now, and the hook still holds the mesh in place.","zh":"那个旧储物柜的锁坏了。里面有一根绳子、一个金属钩子，还有一块以前用来顶住窗户的铁丝网。你得先把小杠杆卡上，然后把钥匙转两圈，这样撑杆才待得住。我姐姐的头发曾被卷进去过一缕，从那以后她再没碰过那扇门。我在口袋里放了一把备用钥匙，专对付它打不开的日子。柜子现在是空的，钩子还挂着那块铁丝网。"},"mouth":{"tw":[["oral",4],["lip",0],["shout",3],["tongue",6],["speak",0],["sing",3],["communicate",2],["talk",0]],"en":"Keep your mouth closed when you chew. The oral exam next week will test how you open a speech, and my teacher wants us to speak slowly. When you shout, the tongue moves differently than when you sing. She says a mouth can talk all day and communicate nothing at all. Her lower lip is dry and her voice is thin now. Do not touch the microphone with your lips. My mother puts a finger to her lips whenever I open mine at the table. She never learned to sing, she says, because nobody in the house ever listened.","zh":"嚼东西的时候把嘴闭上。下周的口试要考你怎么开头演讲，老师要我们说慢一点。喊的时候，舌头的动作和唱歌时不一样。她说一张嘴能说一整天却什么也没表达。她的下唇很干，嗓音如今也细弱了。别用嘴唇碰麦克风。她说她从没学会唱歌，因为家里从来没人听。"},"move":{"tw":[["motion",4],["act",2],["beat",3],["cause",2],["continue",6],["run",0],["begin",3],["change",2]],"en":"We have to move the piano before Friday. The motion of the truck on these roads will damage it, so we wrap every leg in cloth. I cannot act alone; two people have to lift at the same time, to the same beat. Nothing will cause more trouble than the stairs. If it starts to rain we will begin again in the morning. Water can change the shape of wood in one night, so we cannot stay outside. The whole move should take two hours if nobody runs. We will continue with the small boxes indoors.","zh":"我们得在周五前把钢琴搬走。卡车在这些路上的颠簸会把它弄坏，所以我们把每条腿都裹上布。我一个人做不了；两个人得同时抬，按同一个节拍。没有比那几级楼梯更麻烦的了。要是下起雨来，我们就第二天早上重来。水一夜之间就能改变木头的形状，所以不能放在外面。只要没人乱跑，整个搬运两小时就能完。"},"name":{"tw":[["nominal",4],["call",0],["refer",6],["discover",0],["raise",3],["appoint",2],["family",2],["figure",0]],"en":"Nobody knows the real name of the old man at the gate. People call him 'the captain', but that is only a nominal title; nobody has been able to discover where it came from. His family name is carved above the door, and I have to refer to it every morning when I raise the flag. The committee will appoint a new watchman in June. The figure of a woman on the gate carries the same name. Even the map of the town carries the same name in its corner. It has been there since 1893, and nobody has ever tried to change it.","zh":"没人知道大门口那位老人的真名。大家叫他「船长」，可那只是个名义上的称呼；没人能查清它的来历。他的姓氏刻在门楣上，我每天早上升旗时都得提到它。委员会六月要任命一名新看守。大门上那个女人的雕像也带着同一个名字。"},"need":{"tw":[["needy",4],["ask",0],["want",0],["demand",0],["cost",3],["condition",2],["poverty",2],["cry",3]],"en":"Tell me what you need. Do not ask twice and do not demand; just say it once. The cost of the repairs is small, but the condition of the roof is not, and sooner or later we will have to deal with it. There are two needy families in this street, and one of them lives in real poverty. I heard a child cry last night, in the house at the corner. I am sure they want nothing more than a warm room. The cost of coal has gone up again, and the condition of those houses is a demand nobody will answer.","zh":"告诉我你需要什么。别问两遍，也别强求，说一次就够了。修理的花费不大，可屋顶的状况不好，迟早得处理。这条街上有两户穷苦人家，其中一户真的是一贫如洗。昨晚我听见一个孩子在哭，就在拐角那栋房子里。我敢肯定，他们想要的不过是一间暖和的屋子。煤价又涨了，而那些房子的状况是没人愿意回应的一项诉求。"},"note":{"tw":[["annotate",4],["bill",0],["quote",6],["line",0],["mark",0],["read",6],["state",2],["excuse",3]],"en":"I left a note on the table. It says the bill has been paid and the spare key is under the pot. I had to annotate the last page, because the small line at the bottom is easy to miss. Do not quote me on any of this, and do not read the note to the king; he will only look for an excuse. The state of the accounts is written in the same note, and I put a mark next to every name. If you read it again in the morning, do not quote the last line to anybody.","zh":"我在桌上留了张字条。上面写着账单已经付了，备用钥匙在花盆底下。最后一页我不得不加注，因为底下那一小行很容易看漏。这些话别引我的话，也别把字条念给国王听，他只会找个借口。账目状况也写在同一张字条上，我在每个名字旁都做了记号。如果你早上再读一遍，别把最后一行引给任何人听。"},"nurse":{"tw":[["nursery",4],["hold",0],["midwife",3],["care",2],["entertain",0],["matron",3],["feed",2],["nanny",0]],"en":"The nurse comes at six and the matron at eight. In the nursery next door there are twelve small beds, and a nanny feeds the smallest ones by hand. The midwife who delivered my brother still works here; she says care is the only medicine that never runs out. I hold the lamp for her while she works. She will entertain the children for an hour and then send them all to bed. In the winter she stays until midnight, and nobody asks her to. The children call her by her first name, which the matron does not like at all.","zh":"护士六点来，护士长八点来。隔壁的育婴室里摆着十二张小床，一位保姆用手一口口喂最小的那几个。当年接生我弟弟的助产士如今还在这儿干；她说照护是唯一永远不会用完的药。她干活时我替她举着灯。她会陪孩子们玩一个小时，然后把他们全都打发上床。"},"position":{"tw":[["posit",4],["lay",0],["dress",3],["move",2],["office",0],["face",3],["state",2],["post",0]],"en":"My position in the office is a small one. I lay out the letters in the morning and move the files from one post to another. The face of the building is being repaired, so we dress the windows with paper. I would posit that nobody here knows what the final state of the plan will be. However, we will keep working. The sign on the door still carries the old name. Every day I do the same three things, and every day they take the same time. My desk is by the window, and I can see the river from it.","zh":"我在办公室里的职位很小。早上我把信件摊开，把文件从一个岗位挪到另一个岗位。大楼的正面正在维修，所以我们用纸把窗户糊起来。我敢假定这里没人知道这个计划最终的状态是什么。不管怎样，我们还会继续干。门上的牌子还挂着旧名字。"},"post":{"tw":[["poster",4],["carry",0],["express",3],["call",2],["press",6],["office",0],["locate",3],["list",2],["position",0]],"en":"Every post brings two letters and a newspaper. The office cannot locate the missing parcel, and nobody can tell me which list it is on. I put a poster on the wall: 'Do not post cash'. We carry the bags to the express box before nine, and the press calls us every afternoon, sometimes twice. My position here is simple: I sort the mail and I keep quiet. At Christmas the bags are so heavy that two of us have to carry them. Nobody writes letters any more, they say, but the bags are never lighter.","zh":"每一班邮件送来两封信和一份报纸。办公室查不到那个丢失的包裹，也没人告诉我它在哪张清单上。我在墙上贴了张海报：「勿寄现金」。九点前我们把邮袋送到快递箱，报社每天下午都打电话来，有时打两次。我在这里的岗位很简单：分拣邮件，闭嘴干活。"},"race":{"tw":[["run",0],["heat",3],["act",2],["contest",6],["wash",0],["tear",3],["move",2],["rush",0]],"en":"The race begins at noon. Nobody can act as if it is only a game: the heat of the day will decide half of it. We watch from the bank, where the water can wash the mud off our shoes. A hundred people run, and the crowd cannot move at all when the rush starts at the first corner. This contest is older than the town. One year the wind was strong enough to tear every flag off the poles. Another year the river rose and the whole contest was moved to the road above the town.","zh":"比赛中午开始。谁也不能装作这只是一场游戏：当天的暑气会决定一半的胜负。我们在河岸上看，那里的水能洗掉鞋上的泥。一百个人在跑，第一个弯道拥挤开始时，人群根本动不了。这项比赛比镇子还老。有一年风大得把所有旗子都从杆子上扯了下来。又有一年河水涨了，整场比赛挪到了镇子上面那条路上。"},"sing":{"tw":[["song",4],["talk",2],["chant",3],["sound",2],["tune",6],["whistle",0],["hum",3],["listen",6],["interpret",2]],"en":"Please sing that song again. My grandmother could talk about music for hours; she said every tune has a sound of its own. In the old church they chant without a book, and the children hum along. When I was small I could only whistle, never sing. I listen to the same three songs every winter, and each time I interpret the words a little differently. The last line is always the same, and that is why I remember it. If you want, we can sing it together on Sunday evening.","zh":"请把那首歌再唱一遍。我祖母谈起音乐能说上几个小时；她说每支曲子都有自己独特的声音。在那座旧教堂里，人们不看谱子吟唱，孩子们跟着哼。我小时候只会吹口哨，从不会唱。每年冬天我都听同样的三首歌，而每一次我对歌词的理解都略有不同。"},"skin":{"tw":[["skinny",4],["bark",0],["scalp",3],["hide",0],["jacket",3],["bag",2],["breast",6],["struggle",0],["climb",2]],"en":"The skin on his hands is hard and dark. He is skinny now, and his jacket hangs loose on him. A leather bag, made from the hide of an old cow, sits on the floor next to his boots. The bark of the tree outside is rough, like his scalp. He has a mark on his breast, near the throat, from a struggle twenty years ago. Every winter he has to climb the same hill twice a day. He says the cold has taken the feeling out of it, and he does not miss it.","zh":"他手上的皮肤又硬又黑。他如今很瘦，夹克挂在身上空荡荡的。一个用老牛皮做的皮包放在地上，挨着他的靴子。外面那棵树的树皮很粗糙，就像他的头皮。他胸口靠近喉咙处有一道疤，是二十年前一场扭打留下的。每年冬天他都得每天爬两次那座山。"},"speak":{"tw":[["speech",4],["address",0],["sound",2],["listen",6],["mouth",0],["shout",3],["communicate",2],["continue",3]],"en":"I cannot speak in front of a crowd. My speech was ready, but when I stood up my mouth went dry and the sound of the room was louder than my voice. People began to shout from the back. I tried to continue and then to address one man only. It is easier to listen than to speak, and much easier to keep quiet. Next time I will try to communicate something shorter. My hands shake when the room is quiet, and they shake even more when it is not.","zh":"我无法在人前讲话。讲稿早就写好了，可我一站起来嘴就发干，屋里的声音比我的嗓音还大。后面的人开始喊。我试着继续说下去，接着只对着一个人讲。听比说容易，闭嘴不说更容易。下次我要试着讲短一点。"},"state":{"tw":[["civil",4],["country",0],["propose",2],["express",2],["answer",3],["attribute",2],["law",6],["land",0],["add",3]],"en":"The state of the roads is the main question here. Our country has a new law about land, and the administration wants to add three more. I cannot propose anything better: no state can express what the farmers feel when the water comes. You can attribute the damage to the rain, but that is not the answer. The civil servants came, wrote one page and left. Every spring we wait for them to come back. The old man who keeps the records says the state of things was worse in his father's day.","zh":"道路的状况是这里的主要问题。我们国家有了一项关于土地的新法律，行政部门还想再加上三条。我提不出更好的办法：没有什么状态能表达农民在水来时的感受。你可以把损失归因于雨水，可那不是答案。公务员来了，写了一页纸就走了。每年春天我们都等着他们再回来。"},"study":{"tw":[["student",4],["consider",0],["check",3],["research",6],["field",0],["major",3],["think",2],["learn",2]],"en":"I study in the room above the shop. There is one small window and a table full of books. My sister is a student of science; she comes here to research the plants in the field behind the house. We check each other's work every evening. I think this is the only way to learn: consider one thing at a time and then leave it alone. Her major is much harder than mine. My father studied in the same room and never got further than the second book. He says a good table is worth more than a good teacher.","zh":"我在店铺楼上那间屋里学习。屋里只有一扇小窗和一张堆满书的桌子。我妹妹是学理科的学生；她到这里来研究屋后地里的植物。每天晚上我们互相检查作业。我想这是唯一的学习方法：一次只琢磨一件事，然后就放手。她的专业比我的难得多。"},"tie":{"tw":[["draw",0],["ground",3],["finish",2],["marry",0],["join",3],["relate",2],["round",6],["attach",3],["straight",6]],"en":"He wore a black tie to the wedding. The two families will join their names, and after the ceremony they will marry in the old church, on the ground floor of which his mother was born. I had to finish the flowers before nine and attach a card to each one. It is hard to relate one thing to another here. We sat round the table and nobody could draw a straight line. The knot took me ten minutes, and in the photograph it is still crooked. My mother laughed at me and tied it again in one movement.","zh":"他打了条黑领带去参加婚礼。两家人要合成一个姓，仪式之后他们将在那座老教堂里成婚——他母亲就出生在那教堂的底层。我得在九点前把花弄完，并在每一束上别一张卡片。在这里很难把一件事和另一件事联系起来。我们围着桌子坐着，没人能画出一条直线。"},"time":{"tw":[["clock",0],["dead",3],["experience",2],["clip",0],["hour",3],["term",2],["next",6],["sentence",0]],"en":"We have no time, and the clock on the wall is dead. It stopped at five past four one afternoon in June, and nobody has touched it since. Experience tells me the next hour will decide everything. The term ends on Friday, and my last sentence has to be in by then. I will clip the papers together and hand them over at the door. It is the same every year. I have written the date on every page so that I will know the time of it later. Someday someone will read these pages and count the days between them.","zh":"我们没有时间，而墙上的钟是停的。它在六月的一个下午四点零五分停了，此后没人碰过它。经验告诉我，接下来的一个小时会决定一切。学期周五结束，到那时我最后一句必须交上去。我会把纸夹在一起，在门口交出去。每年都是这样。"},"touch":{"tw":[["tactile",4],["concern",0],["catch",3],["act",2],["easy",6],["meet",0],["cover",3],["change",2],["reach",0]],"en":"Do not touch the glass. The tactile map behind it is for blind visitors, and every finger leaves a mark. I have one small concern: the cover of the case is loose. It is easy to change the paper, but you must act before the glue dries. We will meet on Thursday and catch up on the rest. The hand of the woman in the picture is reaching for the same door. The guard watches everybody's hands, and nobody has ever touched the glass twice. He stands there all day and says nothing at all.","zh":"别碰玻璃。后面那张触摸地图是给盲人访客用的，每根手指都会留下印子。我有一个小顾虑：盒子的盖子松了。换纸很容易，但必须在胶干之前动手。我们周四见面，把剩下的部分跟上。画里那个女人的手也正伸向同一扇门。"},"try":{"tw":[["trial",4],["hear",0],["best",3],["act",2],["bring",6],["judge",0],["control",3],["taste",0]],"en":"I will try once more, and then I will stop. The trial next week is about a small house near the river, and the judge has asked me to bring the old papers. We will hear the first witness on Monday. Nothing here is under my control; the best I can do is act quickly and taste the food before I serve it. There is a pain in my back that will not go away. My sister says I should give up, and I tell her that trying is all I have.","zh":"我再试一次，然后就停下。下周的庭审涉及河边一栋小房子，法官要我把旧文件带过去。周一会听第一位证人陈述。这里没有一件事在我掌控之中；我能做的最好的事就是动作快一点，上菜前先尝一口。我背上有一处疼痛怎么也不消。"},"type":{"tw":[["typify",4],["character",0],["breed",3],["write",2],["example",6],["eccentric",0],["shift",3],["adult",2]],"en":"What type of dog is that? The breed is old and rather eccentric: it will typify the whole group in every show. Its character is calm, and the adult dogs sleep all day. I have to write four pages about this type of animal, with an example of each. The night shift begins at ten, and the same man has worked it for years. He says he knows every type by its bark alone. There are forty types in the book, and I have to describe every one of them.","zh":"那是什么品种的狗？这品种很老，也相当古怪：每到比赛它都能代表整组狗的特点。它的性情温和，成年的狗整天睡觉。我得写四页讲这类动物，每一类都要举一个例子。夜班十点开始，同一个人已经干了好几年。他说只听叫声就能认出每一种。"},"use":{"tw":[["usage",4],["employ",0],["apply",0],["drink",3],["demand",2],["require",6],["exercise",0],["board",3],["act",2]],"en":"The use of this room is written on the board. You may employ the machine for two hours a day, but you have to apply in writing first. The usage is strict: no drink near the desk. Older people require a chair and will demand one. We exercise every morning before the doors open, and the act of standing up is the hardest part. Nobody has ever asked me what the machines are for. The man who wrote the rules retired in 1990 and has not been back since. Everyone here knows the rules, and nobody has ever read them.","zh":"这间屋子的用途写在牌子上。你每天可以用这台机器两小时，但得先书面申请。规矩很严：桌边不许喝饮料。年纪大的人需要椅子，而且会开口要。每天早上开门前我们做操，而站起来这个动作是最难的一环。从没有人问过我这些机器是干什么用的。"},"wait":{"tw":[["waiter",4],["expect",3],["extension",3],["act",2],["stay",6],["hold",0],["ambush",3],["look",0]],"en":"We had to wait two hours for a table. The waiter told us to expect another twenty minutes, and then another. My sister could not stay; she had work to do. I left my name at the extension desk and sat in the corner, where I could look at the door. The ambush in the book I was reading lasted three pages. I had to hold the book with both hands, it was so cold. When the table was ready at last, my sister had already gone home. The waiter said the delay was nobody's fault, but every act of service in that place takes an hour.","zh":"我们等位子等了两个小时。服务员说再等二十分钟，然后又二十分钟。我妹妹待不住，她还有活要干。我把名字留在分机台，坐到角落里，从那儿能看见门口。我读的那本书里，一次伏击写了三页。我不得不用两只手抱着书，实在太冷了。"},"wall":{"tw":[["mural",4],["fence",2],["gable",3],["surround",0],["parapet",3],["layer",2],["floor",6],["object",2],["street",6]],"en":"There is a wall around the old garden. On the inside, the mural above the door shows the whole history of the street. The parapet is broken in two places, and a wooden fence covers the gap. Every layer of paint on the wall belongs to a different year. The gable of the house next door leans over it, and on the floor near the gate somebody has left a heavy object. The wall will surround this garden long after we are gone. I sit on the floor by the fence and count the layers of paint with my finger.","zh":"老花园四周有一道墙。墙内侧、门上方那幅壁画讲着这条街的整部历史。墙头有两处塌了，用一道木栅栏挡着缺口。墙上每一层漆都属于不同年份。隔壁房子的山墙朝它倾斜过来，大门附近的地上有人撂下了一个很重的东西。等我们都不在了，这道墙还会围着这座花园。我坐在栅栏边的地上，用手指一层层数那些漆。"},"weight":{"tw":[["weighty",4],["burden",0],["load",3],["charge",2],["maximum",6],["bias",2],["excess",6],["angle",0]],"en":"The weight of the box was more than I expected. It is a weighty thing, and the burden of carrying it up the stairs fell on my brother. The maximum load for the old lift is eighty kilos, so we had to go on foot. He put it on the table at an angle and said the charge would be extra. There is a bias in the way we measure these things: two men always say a box is lighter than one man does. The excess goes back to the yard, where the same two men will argue about the angle of the ramp.","zh":"那个箱子比我想的重。它很沉，搬上楼的担子就落在我哥哥身上。这部旧电梯的最大载重是八十公斤，所以我们只好走楼梯。他把箱子斜着放在桌上，说搬运要另收费。我们衡量这些东西时是有偏见的：两个人总说箱子比一个人说的要轻。"},"book":{"tw":[["booking",4],["hold",0],["card",3],["register",2],["novel",6],["record",2],["ticket",3],["essay",6]],"en":"I read one book about the sea every winter. It is not a novel; it is the record of a man who worked on a boat for thirty years. He could not hold a pen at first, so his wife wrote the booking of every trip in a register and kept a ticket from each town they came to. The card inside the cover is my grandfather's, and the essay at the back was written by a schoolboy. Every page is thin and dry, and the words on them have lasted much longer than the boat did.","zh":"每年冬天我都读一本关于海的书。那不是小说，而是一个在船上干了三十年的人的记录。他起初握不住笔，所以他妻子把每次出航的登记都写进一本登记簿，还留下他们到过的每个城镇的船票。封面里那张卡片是我祖父的，后面那篇文章是一个小学生写的。"},"case":{"tw":[["casing",4],["cause",0],["box",3],["problem",2],["trial",6],["slip",0],["face",0],["pack",3]],"en":"In this case there is no easy answer. The problem is not the box; it is the casing inside it, which is thin. Nobody can find the cause. At the trial the judge asked for a slip of paper with the numbers on it, and my face gave me away. I had to pack the whole thing again and take it home on the bus. The next case on the list was even worse. Two weeks later a man came to the door with the same box and asked me the same question again.","zh":"这个案子里没有简单的答案。问题不在箱子，而在里面那层很薄的壳体。没人找得出原因。开审时法官要一张写有数字的纸条，而我的脸色把我出卖了。我只好把东西重新打包，坐公交带回家。清单上的下一个案子更糟。"},"class":{"tw":[["classify",4],["course",0],["count",3],["league",2],["standard",6],["family",0],["rank",6],["form",0]],"en":"Our class has twenty-two children in it. The teacher has to classify them by age and by reading level, and the standard of the older ones is not much higher. We play in a small league on Saturdays, and my rank in the group is fourth. The course lasts one year. The form of the test has changed twice since I came. In my family nobody finished school, so I count myself lucky to be here at all. The teacher says a good class is not a list of names but a habit of working that lasts for years.","zh":"我们班有二十二个孩子。老师得按年龄和阅读水平给他们分类，而大孩子的水平并不高多少。我们周六参加一个小联赛，我在组里的名次是第四。课程为期一年。我入学以来考试的形式已经改过两次。我们家没人读完过中学，所以我觉得自己能在这儿已经很幸运了。"},"country":{"tw":[["rural",4],["land",0],["open",3],["region",2],["nation",0],["state",0],["far",6],["space",3]],"en":"I grew up in the country, in a rural region where the land is cheap and the roads are empty. Our nation has eight such regions, and the state pays for the schools in all of them. The open field behind our house is the only space the children have. The nearest town is far; my aunt says it takes an hour if the wind is against you. In summer the whole country smells of cut grass. The government sends one bus a week, and the driver knows every family in the valley by name.","zh":"我在乡下长大，那是个土地便宜、道路空旷的农业地区。我们国家有八个这样的地区，所有地区的学校都由政府出资。屋后那片开阔的田是孩子们仅有的空间。最近的镇子很远；我姑妈说，要是逆风得走一个小时。夏天整个乡下都是青草被割过的味道。"},"father":{"tw":[["paternal",4],["mother",1],["patriarch",3],["head",2],["grandfather",6],["generate",0],["parent",2],["engender",0]],"en":"My father was born in a house that no longer exists. His paternal grandfather, an old patriarch, was the head of a family of eleven. My mother says the two of them could generate an argument out of nothing, and that noise would engender more noise. Every parent in that street knew everybody else's business. My father never spoke of it, and I only learned the whole story from my aunt. My mother kept a photograph of the old house in a drawer for forty years, and then it was lost.","zh":"我父亲出生在一栋如今已不存在的房子里。他父系那边的祖父，一位老家长，是十一个人大家庭的户主。我母亲说那两个人能凭空吵出一场争论，而那吵闹又会生出更多吵闹。那条街上每对父母都知道别人家的私事。我父亲从不提这些，整个故事我还是从我姑妈那儿听来的。"},"flower":{"tw":[["floral",4],["bloom",0],["bud",3],["develop",2],["tree",6],["prime",0],["daisy",3],["garden",6]],"en":"The flower show opens on the first Saturday of June. Every garden in the village brings something: one rose, one daisy, one strange plant in a pot. The floral tent is the biggest in the county. My aunt watches her buds for weeks; a flower that is not yet in bloom cannot win, and one past its prime cannot either. The tree by the gate develops its leaves late and loses them early. The judge looks at the colour first and the shape last, and he never hurries. The show closes at six and the tent is taken down the same evening.","zh":"花展六月的第一个周六开幕。村里每座园子都拿出点什么：一支玫瑰、一朵雏菊、一盆奇怪的植物。那座花卉帐篷是全县最大的。我姑妈守着花苞看了好几周；还没开的花赢不了，过了盛期的也赢不了。大门边那棵树发芽晚，落叶却早。"},"number":{"tw":[["numeric",4],["square",3],["company",2],["total",3],["count",0],["several",6],["least",6],["bit",0]],"en":"Write your number at the top of the page. The system is numeric: no letters, no dashes. Our company counts every call, and the total last month was a little over nine hundred. Several of them were wrong. A square of paper with the same number is pinned to the board. I am tired, and it takes the least bit of noise to make me lose the count. The office has a number for everything: the door, the phone, the pile of paper on the shelf. I write mine on the back of my hand so that I will not forget it.","zh":"把号码写在页面顶端。格式是纯数字：不要字母，不要短横。我们公司统计每一通电话，上个月的总数略超九百。其中有几通是错的。一张写着同样号码的方纸钉在告示板上。我累了，一点点响声就能让我数乱。"},"school":{"tw":[["scholastic",4],["educate",2],["conservatory",3],["college",6],["train",0],["swim",2],["graduate",6],["civilise",0]],"en":"The school stands at the end of the street. Its scholastic record is not famous, but it has educated half the village. There is a conservatory behind it where the children train in music, and a small pool where they swim in summer. My sister went on to college and will graduate in July. Nobody here speaks of civilising anybody; they only want the children to be able to read. The building is old, and the roof was repaired with money the parents collected themselves. Every year the oldest children repaint the front wall before the summer.","zh":"学校坐落在街的尽头。它的学业成绩并不出名，却教出了半个村子的人。后面有个玻璃琴房，孩子们在那里练音乐；还有个小水池，夏天他们在里面游泳。我妹妹后来上了大学，七月就要毕业。这里没人说什么开化谁，他们只想让孩子能读书。"},"simple":{"tw":[["simplicity",4],["bare",0],["square",3],["complex",1],["perfect",6],["mere",0],["fool",3],["straightforward",6]],"en":"The answer is simple. The plan has a kind of simplicity that fools people: a bare room, one square table, one chair. Any honest worker would call it straightforward. The truth is that it is not complex, and it is not perfect either. It is elementary, and only a fool would try to improve it. My father built the whole thing in a single week, and it still stands. For a mere fifty pounds we could make it better, but nobody wants to spend the money. So we leave it as it is, and it works.","zh":"答案很简单。这个方案有一种会骗人的简洁：一间空屋、一张方桌、一把椅子。任何老实的工人都会说这很直白。事实是它不复杂，也不完美。它很基础，只有傻子才会想去改进它。我父亲用一周就把它全做出来了，而它至今还立在那儿。"},"space":{"tw":[["spatial",4],["blank",0],["hole",3],["distance",0],["infinite",0],["shuttle",6],["key",3],["earth",6]],"en":"There is no space left in the cupboard. A hole in the wall behind it gives us a little more, and the distance from there to the window is about a metre. In the city the shuttle bus comes every ten minutes. My teacher says space is infinite and the earth is not, and then he draws a blank on the board. The key to the whole problem is spatial: it is about where things are, not what they are. The hole is blank and the distance looks the same from every angle in the room.","zh":"柜子里没地方了。它后面墙上的一个洞给了我们一点余地，从那儿到窗户的距离大约一米。在城里，穿梭巴士每十分钟一班。我老师说空间是无限的，而地球不是，然后他在黑板上画了个空白。整个问题的关键在于空间：它关乎东西在哪里，而不是它们是什么。那个洞是空的，从屋里每个角度看距离都一样。"},"suppose":{"tw":[["supposition",4],["guess",0],["suspect",3],["assume",2],["premise",3],["presume",6],["imagine",0],["say",0]],"en":"I suppose you have heard the story. It is a supposition, nothing more; nobody can say where it began. I suspect the first man only wanted to make us guess. Do not assume that the premise is true, and do not presume that I know either. Imagine a village where nobody had ever left, and you will understand why the story grew. That is the whole of it. I have told it to my children exactly as it was told to me, without adding anything. They will tell it to theirs, and the supposition will be the same.","zh":"我猜这个故事你听过。它只是一个推测，仅此而已；没人说得出它从哪儿开始。我怀疑最初那个人只是想让我们猜。别认定那个前提是真的，也别以为我就知道。想一想一个从没有人离开过的村子，你就会明白这故事为什么会越传越大。事情就是这样。"},"term":{"tw":[["terminal",4],["condition",0],["subject",3],["word",2],["current",6],["terminus",0],["predicate",3],["quantity",2]],"en":"The term ends in three weeks. In this subject the predicate carries most of the meaning, and one wrong word can change the whole sentence. The quantity of reading is small; the interest is not. I stand at the bus terminal every morning and watch the current of people go past. The line stops at a terminus two streets from my house, and the condition of the road there is terrible. My father uses the same word for the season, the school and the length of a loan. He says a word is only a tool, and a tool should be used more than once.","zh":"学期还有三周就结束了。在这门学科里，谓语承载了大部分意思，一个用错的词就能改变整句。阅读量不大，趣味性却不少。每天早上我站在公交总站看人流经过。这条线路的终点站离我家两条街，而那里路况糟透了。"},"wild":{"tw":[["wilderness",4],["crazy",0],["barren",3],["tame",1],["fish",6],["waste",0],["bird",6],["furious",0]],"en":"The garden has gone wild again. Beyond the fence there is a piece of wilderness where no bird has nested for years and the ground is barren. My neighbour is furious about the waste of good land, and he says only a crazy man would leave it like that. His own cat is tame and fat. I go there to fish in the small stream and to be alone for an hour. In spring the stream is full of small fish and the birds come back to the fence. Nobody in the village has walked to the far end of it for years.","zh":"园子又野了。栅栏那边有一片荒地，多年没有鸟在这里筑巢，土地贫瘠。我邻居对这么好的一块地被浪费感到愤怒，他说只有疯子才会让它这样。他自己那只猫又温顺又肥。我去那里的小溪里钓鱼，独自待上一个小时。"},"act":{"tw":[["begin",3],["serve",2],["refrain",1],["move",0],["deal",3],["event",2],["order",6],["play",0]],"en":"The act begins at seven. First they serve the soup, then the play starts, and nobody may move from their seat. I have to deal with the last table and give the order to the kitchen before the second act. Please refrain from talking during the music. The whole event lasts two hours, and by the end my feet are dead. The same thing happens every Friday, and I still enjoy it. The young woman who plays the mother has never acted before, and she is very good. After the last curtain we wash the glasses and count the money.","zh":"这幕戏七点开始。先上汤，然后戏才开演，谁都不许离开座位。我得收拾最后一张桌子，并在第二幕之前把点单送进厨房。音乐响起时请勿交谈。整个活动持续两小时，结束时我的脚都站麻了。每周五都是这样，而我依然挺喜欢。"},"add":{"tw":[["bring",0],["subtract",1],["combine",6],["total",0],["include",3],["count",2],["extra",6],["contribute",0]],"en":"Please add these two figures and bring me the total. You may not subtract anything, and you must include the extra charge for delivery. If you combine the two lists, the count will be wrong by one. Everyone in the office had to contribute a little. I checked it twice before I took it in, and the answer looked simple to everybody. The figures come from two different books, and each one has its own way of counting. If the total is not the same in both, we start again from the beginning.","zh":"请把这两个数字加起来，把总数拿来给我。不许减掉任何一项，还必须把额外的运费算进去。如果把两张清单合并，计数就会差一个。办公室里每个人都得出一点力。我交上去之前核了两遍，而在所有人看来答案都显而易见。"},"agree":{"tw":[["check",0],["accept",2],["disagree",1],["consider",6],["fit",0],["meet",3],["suit",2],["negotiate",6]],"en":"I agree with you about the price, but I cannot accept the date. We can meet on Thursday and negotiate the rest. Let me check the small room first; if the table does not fit, the whole plan is no good. Consider the other offer before you decide. My brother disagrees with me and says the later date would suit him much better. He wants the later date because his son will be home from the army by then. That is a good reason, and I have no good reason of my own.","zh":"价钱上我同意你，但日期我不能接受。我们周四见面，其余的事再谈。先让我看看那间小屋；桌子放不下的话，整个计划就不行。做决定前你也考虑一下另一个报价。我哥哥不同意我，他说晚一点那个日期对他合适得多。"},"allow":{"tw":[["admit",3],["accept",2],["deny",1],["require",6],["trust",3],["assign",2],["enable",6],["grant",0]],"en":"They do not allow dogs in the shop. The sign says they cannot admit animals, and they deny that it has anything to do with the owner. Anyone who wants to bring one must accept the rule. The job will require an hour of training, and the manager will assign somebody to help you. This small key will enable you to open the back door. I trust they will grant us one more week. The shop next door allows them, and half the street goes there instead. The owner says he will not change his mind, and I believe him.","zh":"他们不许带狗进店。牌子上说不能接纳动物，他们否认这与主人有关。想带狗来的人必须接受这条规矩。这份活需要一小时培训，经理会指派一个人帮你。这把小钥匙能让你打开后门。我相信他们会再宽限我们一周。"},"answer":{"tw":[["reply",2],["field",3],["meet",2],["question",1],["serve",3],["counter",3],["state",2],["result",0]],"en":"I wrote my answer and put it on the counter. There was no reply for a week, and then a short letter came. The state of the field is the real question here: nobody can meet in a wet meadow, and the result would be a mess. I asked again at the second window, and the woman there could not serve me either. So I went home and waited for the third letter. In the third week I met the owner himself at the door of the office. He answered every question except the one I had actually asked.","zh":"我把答案写好放在柜台上。一周都没有回音，然后来了一封短信。这里的真正问题是场地状况：没人能在湿草地里集会，结果只会一团糟。我又到第二个窗口去问，那里的女士也帮不了我。于是我回家等第三封信。"},"bottom":{"tw":[["bed",0],["base",3],["hit",2],["side",2],["spot",6],["behind",0],["foot",3],["land",2],["plate",6]],"en":"At the bottom of the garden there is a bed of stones. The base of the old wall is under it, and on the far side you can see a plate of iron fixed into the ground. We used to hit it with a stick when we were children. The spot behind the tree is where my dog liked to sleep. From there you can put your foot on the land beyond the fence. In summer the whole garden smells of wet stone, and the bed under the wall is the coolest place in it.","zh":"园子最底下有一片石头地。那堵旧墙的基座就在下面，靠外的一侧能看到一块嵌进地里的铁板。我们小时候常拿棍子敲它。树后那一处是我家狗爱睡的地方。从那儿你可以把脚伸到栅栏外的土地上去。"},"break":{"tw":[["blow",3],["change",2],["repair",1],["check",0],["chip",3],["dance",2],["die",0],["back",6]],"en":"Take a break at four; you look tired. A single blow from that hammer can chip the stone, and the break in the wall will only get worse. Nobody can repair it in one day, and a small change here will not help. Check the back of the house first, where the wind comes in. The old tree will die this year. Come and dance with me instead; the wall has waited thirty years. The crack runs from the window down to the floor, and in winter it lets the cold air in.","zh":"四点歇一下吧，你看上去累了。那把锤子敲一下就能把石头崩出缺口，而墙上的裂口只会越来越大。一天之内谁也修不好，在这里做点小改动也没用。先去查看房子背面，风是从那儿灌进来的。那棵老树今年会死。不如过来跟我跳舞吧，那堵墙等了三十年了。"},"change":{"tw":[["alter",0],["break",3],["dress",2],["stay",1],["exchange",0],["cut",3],["travel",2],["reason",6],["shift",0]],"en":"You cannot change this without asking. Nothing can alter the size of the door, and if you cut the frame you will break the glass. There is a good reason for the rule: the shift of the wind in winter is strong enough to travel through any small gap. I had to dress in two coats and stay inside. In the future we will exchange the old panes for new ones. Anything you alter in this room has to be written in the book by the door. The book has been there for a hundred years and the handwriting is very small.","zh":"不打招呼你不能改动这里。门的尺寸无法更改，要是削了框子就会打碎玻璃。这条规定有它的道理：冬天风向一变，风大得能从任何小缝里钻进来。我不得不穿上两件外套待在屋里。以后我们会把旧玻璃换成新的。"},"clean":{"tw":[["clear",0],["wash",3],["change",2],["dirty",1],["enough",6],["fair",5],["brush",3],["remove",2],["water",6],["fresh",0]],"en":"Keep the room clean: wash the floor, brush the table and remove every plate before you leave. The water in the bucket must be clear, not fresh, and the cloth has to be clean enough to use twice. If the sheets are dirty, change them. It is not fair to leave that work to the next person. I have done it for eleven years, and the room has never once been dirty on my shift. When the shift ends I put the brushes back in the cupboard and lock it. The next person will find everything exactly where it belongs.","zh":"把屋子保持干净：走之前擦地、刷桌、把所有盘子收走。桶里的水要清，不必是新打的；抹布得干净到还能再用一次。床单脏了就换。把活儿留给下一个人是不公平的。我干了十一年，我班上这屋子从没脏过。"},"comfort":{"tw":[["ease",0],["calm",3],["aid",2],["discomfort",1],["sense",6],["console",0],["relief",3],["condition",2]],"en":"The old chair gives me more comfort than the new one. It has a calm shape and a soft cushion, and when my back is bad it is a real aid. The discomfort in my knees goes away within a minute of sitting down. My only sense of relief in the evening comes from that chair. My sister tries to console me by saying it is an ordinary chair, but she does not have to sit in it all day. For ease of mind I have written its condition on a card and hung the card on the back of the chair.","zh":"那把旧椅子比新的更让我舒服。它形制沉静、坐垫柔软，我背痛的时候它真帮得上忙。一坐下不到一分钟，膝盖的不适就消失了。晚上我唯一的放松感就来自那把椅子。我妹妹想安慰我，说那只是把普通的椅子，可她不用整天坐在上面。"},"continue":{"tw":[["cover",0],["carry",3],["act",2],["discontinue",1],["bring",6],["stay",0],["cross",3],["talk",2],["extend",0],["move",6]],"en":"We will continue the work tomorrow. Nobody can carry on like this: two of the men have gone home and the rain shows no sign of stopping. Every act of repair here begins in the rain. If they discontinue the service, we will have to cover the roof ourselves and stay until it is done. I cannot talk about it any longer. Let us cross the yard, move the boxes inside, and then we will extend the plan by a week. Somebody has to bring the tarpaulin before the night shift starts.","zh":"明天我们继续干。没人能这样撑下去：两个人已经回家了，雨也没有要停的样子。这里每一次修理都是在雨里开的头。要是他们停掉这项服务，我们就得自己盖屋顶，一直干完为止。我不能再聊这个了。我们穿过院子，把箱子搬进屋，然后把这个计划延长一周。"},"air":{"tw":[["aerial",4],["line",0],["breath",3],["dry",2],["light",6],["aerate",4],["send",0],["note",3],["gas",2],["jet",6],["atmosphere",0]],"en":"The small radio station sits on a hill where the air is dry and clear. Every morning the engineer opens the windows to aerate the room before the first show. She sends the signal along one line to a tall aerial on the roof, and from there it travels by jet to towns far away. The music she plays has a simple air, a tune you can hum note by note. The light from her desk lamp is the only other thing in the room. She takes a deep breath, waits for the gas heater to warm the air, and thinks about the wide atmosphere outside.","zh":"那座小电台坐落在山丘上，那儿的空气又干又清。每天早上，工程师都要打开窗户，让直播间的空气流通一下，然后才开始第一档节目。她把信号顺着一条线路送到屋顶那根高高的天线上，再从那里传往很远的小镇。她放的音乐调子很简单，是可以一个音符一个音符哼出来的。书桌台灯的光是屋里唯一另外的亮处。她深吸一口气，等着煤气取暖器把空气烘暖，心里想着外面那一片广阔的天地。"},"live":{"tw":[["liver",4],["experience",2],["board",3],["dead",1],["except",6],["hot",0],["camp",3],["alone",6],["last",0]],"en":"My uncle has lived in a camp near the river for ten years, mostly alone. He is not dead, though some of the men he worked with are. He says the only thing that makes a long stay bearable is experience: you learn which food is safe and which water is hot enough to drink. Except for the winter, he is out on the board path every morning. Doctors once told him his liver was weak, so he eats little meat and walks a lot. He wants to live in a real house last of all, but not yet.","zh":"我叔叔在河边的一个营地里住了十年，大多时候是一个人。他没死，虽然跟他一起干过活的人里有些已经不在了。他说，能让这种长住熬得下去的只有经验：你得知道哪些东西能吃，哪里的水烧热了才能喝。除了冬天，他每天早上都出门，走那条木板路。医生曾说他肝不好，所以他少吃肉、多走路。他说到最后还是想住进一间真正的房子，但不是现在。"},"sky":{"tw":[["celestial",4],["flip",0],["lag",3],["horizon",6],["fling",2],["pitch",0],["submarine",3],["bright",6],["toss",0]],"en":"On the last night of the trip we lay on the deck and watched the sky. It was bright, with no cloud at all, and a few celestial bodies moved slowly above the horizon. My brother began to toss a coin and flip it, trying to catch it in the dark. Each pitch of the boat made him lag behind the beat of the waves, and once the coin went over the side. A submarine lamp far off threw a pale line on the water. He gave a little fling of his arm and laughed. We stayed out until the sky turned grey.","zh":"旅途的最后一晚，我们躺在甲上看天。天很亮，一丝云也没有，几颗星星慢慢地移过地平线。我弟弟开始抛硬币、翻着玩，想在黑里接住它。船每颠一下，他就比浪的节拍慢半拍，有一次硬币掉进了海里。远处一盏潜水艇的灯在水面上投下一道淡淡的白线。他手臂一甩，笑了。我们在外面待到天色发灰。"},"cry":{"tw":[["call",0],["noise",3],["change",2],["laugh",1],["remember",6],["shout",0],["tear",3],["express",2],["wonder",6],["scream",3]],"en":"When the baby began to cry, my sister did not shout or scream. She picked him up and made a low sound, a kind of call that he seemed to remember from another night. The noise in the flat was terrible, so she took him to the window for a change of air. He would laugh, then cry again, and a single tear ran down his cheek. I wonder how a small child can express so much with one sound. She said that all mothers learn it, and that she would remember it for the rest of her life.","zh":"孩子一哭，我姐姐既没有喊也没有尖叫。她把他抱起来，发出一个很低的声音，像是某种呼唤，他好像记得这是从别的夜里听过的。屋里的噪声糟透了，她抱他到窗边换换空气。他笑一下，又哭起来，一滴眼泪顺着脸颊往下流。我奇怪一个这么小的孩子怎么能用一声哭表达这么多。她说当妈的都会这一手，她一辈子都会记得。"},"empty":{"tw":[["abandon",0],["clear",3],["change",2],["fill",1],["inside",6],["discharge",0],["bleed",3],["leave",2],["room",6],["hollow",0]],"en":"The old factory was empty when we got there. Someone had left the gate open, and a clear wind blew through a broken window. We had come to change the locks and fill the holes in the floor. Inside, a great hollow tank stood against the wall where the water used to be stored. They had to discharge the last of it through a pipe, and a thin stream continued to bleed onto the concrete for an hour. I could not abandon the place; it was the room where my father worked. We would leave it standing, at least for one more year.","zh":"我们到的时候，那家老厂是空的。有人把大门敞着，一股清亮的风从破窗里穿过去。我们来是为了换锁，再把地板上的洞补上。屋里靠墙立着一个巨大的空罐子，从前就是在那儿储水的。剩下的水得从一根管子里排出去，细细的一股流在水泥地上淌了一个小时。我没法把这儿丢下不要；这是我父亲当年干活的车间。我们决定先让它立着，至少再留一年。"},"express":{"tw":[["carry",0],["drop",3],["mail",2],["local",1],["message",6],["state",0],["raise",3],["communicate",2],["service",6],["convey",2]],"en":"The local post office will not carry a parcel that is too heavy, so I had to express it instead. The clerk asked me to state the value and then to raise the box onto the scale. She said the mail service would get the message to my brother by Friday. I tried to convey how urgent it was, and she promised to drop it in the first van out. The old way of sending letters could not communicate such speed. I paid, took the receipt, and left feeling that the whole thing had gone well.","zh":"本地的邮局不收太重的包裹，所以我只好走快递。柜台的人让我报一下价值，再把箱子抬到秤上。她说邮件服务周五之前能把消息送到我哥哥手上。我想让她明白这事有多急，她答应把这箱子塞进第一班发走的车里。从前寄信的老法子根本传达不了这么快的速度。我付了钱，拿了收据，走的时候觉得整件事办得挺顺。"},"fall":{"tw":[["autumn",0],["break",3],["change",2],["rise",1],["end",6],["drop",3],["rain",3],["die",2],["since",6],["hang",0]],"en":"Since the end of summer, the leaves have begun to fall. Each autumn I watch them drop from the tall trees behind the house, and they hang in the wet air before they reach the ground. The change comes quickly here: one week it is warm, the next the rain will not stop. Prices rise, the shops break their old rules and close early, and a few small birds die in the cold. My mother says this is the finest time of year, when the garden falls quiet. It is only October, and already the wood box by the door is full.","zh":"入夏以来，叶子就开始落了。每年秋天我都看着它们从屋后那些大树上掉下来，落地之前先悬在潮湿的空气里。这里变天变得快：这一周还暖着，下一周雨就下个不停。物价往上涨，店家打破了老规矩提前关门，几只小鸟冻死了。我妈说这是一年里最好的时节，园子静下来的时候。才十月，门边那只木箱子已经装满了。"},"feed":{"tw":[["course",0],["waste",3],["move",2],["starve",1],["consume",6],["eat",0],["dine",3],["provide",2],["grow",6],["run",0]],"en":"My aunt runs a small farm and has to feed forty animals before she can feed herself. Of course the cost has gone up, and she refuses to waste a single sack of grain. Each morning she will move the sheep to a new field, then provide water for the cows and let the young ones run about. In winter there is little to eat, and the weakest may starve if the hay does not last. At night she will dine alone in the kitchen, proud that the whole place can grow and consume and still pay for itself.","zh":"我姑姑经营一个小农场，得先把四十头牲口喂饱，才轮到自己吃饭。成本当然涨了，她一袋粮食都不肯糟蹋。每天早上她把羊赶到新的一片地里，然后给牛添水，让小牛四处跑。冬天没什么可吃的，草料要是撑不到开春，最弱的那几头就可能饿死。晚上她一个人在厨房吃饭，很得意这块地方能种能养、还能自己养自己。"},"fill":{"tw":[["meet",0],["answer",3],["change",2],["empty",1],["extra",6],["satisfy",0],["close",3],["enough",2],["room",6],["fulfil",0]],"en":"We had to fill the hall before eight o'clock, but the room was still half empty when the band began. An extra row of chairs helped, and by the time the door had to close there was enough space for everyone. The manager said we could not satisfy a crowd like that with a small show, so he had to change the programme and answer a few angry phone calls. In the end we did meet the promise and fulfil the plan. I sat at the back and watched the seats fill one by one.","zh":"我们得在八点前把礼堂填满，可乐队开场时屋子还空着一半。加了一排椅子才管用，等到不得不关门的时候，位子已经够所有人坐了。经理说这种规模的观众，小节目是满足不了的，于是他改了节目单，还接了几个气冲冲的电话。最后我们总算兑现了承诺，把计划做成了。我坐在最后一排，看着座位一个个被填满。"},"find":{"tw":[["chance",0],["catch",3],["act",2],["lose",1],["how",6],["discover",0],["count",3],["change",2],["sure",6],["feel",3]],"en":"I had to find the key before my father came home, and I was not sure how to do it. There was a chance he had left it in the car, so I went out to look. I had to act quickly, count the minutes while I searched, and feel along every shelf. I did not want to lose my nerve or let the light change before I was finished. Then I began to discover small things: a torn ticket, a note, and at last the key itself. I managed to catch the door just as he turned into the road.","zh":"我必须在爸爸回家之前找到钥匙，可我不确定该怎么办。有可能他把它落在车里了，于是我就出去找。我得赶紧动手，一边找一边数着分钟，把每个架子都摸一遍。我不想在这期间慌了神，也不想等天光变了还没找完。后来我开始发现一些小东西：一张撕破的票、一张纸条，最后就是钥匙本身。他拐进这条路的时候，我刚好把门接住。"},"finish":{"tw":[["close",3],["break",3],["act",2],["start",1],["straight",6],["complete",0],["draw",3],["coat",2],["round",6],["end",3]],"en":"The painter said he would finish the room in three days, but the start was slow. He had to draw the shape of each window first, then work in a straight line down the wall. We would break for tea at eleven and close the door so the dust did not reach the hall. The first coat took a whole day; the second was quicker. At the end of the round he asked me to act as judge and look for any thin patch. It was complete by Friday, and the whole job turned out better than I had hoped.","zh":"油漆工说三天就能把这间屋子刷完，可开头很慢。他得先把每扇窗的形状描出来，再顺着墙面一笔直着往下刷。十一点我们会停下来喝茶，把门关上，免得灰飘到走廊里。第一遍漆刷了一整天，第二遍就快多了。这一轮收尾的时候，他让我当裁判，去找有没有刷薄的地方。到周五就全完工了，整件活儿比我想的还好。"},"follow":{"tw":[["watch",0],["carry",3],["act",2],["precede",1],["change",6],["observe",0],["chase",3],["check",2],["see",6],["trace",0]],"en":"A good guide will follow the old path and never act on guesswork. He will watch the sky, observe where the birds go, and check the marks on the trees. The men who precede him leave signs, and he can trace every one of them. If the wind should change, he must carry on without complaint and chase the last of the light. I have seen him do it a hundred times. You follow because you trust him, not because you can see the way yourself. The rest of us simply walk behind and try not to lose him.","zh":"好向导会跟着那条老路走，绝不凭猜行事。他会看天，观察鸟往哪儿飞，检查树上的记号。走在他前面的人留下标记，他能把每一个都追踪出来。风要是变了向，他也得一声不吭地往前走，追着最后一点天光。我见他这么干过一百回。你跟着他，是因为信得过他，不是因为你自个儿看得清路。我们这些剩下的人只管在后面走，尽量别跟丢。"},"foot":{"tw":[["base",0],["bed",3],["add",2],["head",1],["hole",6],["pick",0],["paw",3],["bottom",2],["inside",6],["infantry",0]],"en":"There was a hole in my boot, and by the end of the walk my foot was wet. The base of the hill is soft, so each step sank a little, and I had to pick my way between the stones. My dog ran ahead on a heavy paw, then stopped and put his head down at the bottom of a wall. Inside the old shed we found a bed of dry grass and a line of marks that looked like an army. My father said the infantry had camped there long ago, before the road was built. He added that his own feet still hurt from that winter.","zh":"我靴子上有个洞，走到最后脚全湿了。山脚下土很松，每一步都往下陷一点，我只得在石头之间挑着路走。我的狗用一只厚爪子跑在前面，忽然停下来，把头低在一堵墙脚下。在那间旧棚子里，我们找到一片干草铺的窝，还有一排看着像脚印的痕迹。我爸说很久以前、路还没修的时候，步兵在这儿扎过营。他又说他的脚到现在还记得那个冬天。"},"free":{"tw":[["rid",0],["clear",5],["issue",2],["confine",1],["without",6],["innocent",0],["cut",3],["pass",2],["allow",6],["loose",5]],"en":"The court set him free after nine months. He had been confined to a small cell without a window, and no one would allow him to see the papers in his own case. The judge said he was innocent, that the police had no right to cut him off from his family, and that the whole issue was a mistake. He walked out, let his shoulders go loose, and took a clear breath of morning air. He wanted only to be rid of the past and to pass through the gate like any other man.","zh":"九个月后，法庭把他放了。他先前被关在一间没有窗的小牢房里，谁也不让他看自己案子的卷宗。法官说他是无罪的，警方没有权利把他和家人隔开，说整件事就是个错误。他走出来，把肩膀松开，清清爽爽地吸了一口早晨的空气。他只想把过去甩掉，像个普通人一样从大门走出去。"},"freeze":{"tw":[["block",0],["ice",3],["act",2],["boil",1],["resume",6],["frost",3],["fixate",3],["change",2],["unless",6],["halt",0]],"en":"Unless the pipes are wrapped, the water in them will freeze on the first cold night. Last year the ice blocked the whole line and the heating had to halt for two days. My neighbour began to fixate on the weather report, watching for frost and for any change in the wind. We agreed to act together: he would boil water for the old man next door while I went to get salt. In the morning the thaw came, and the traffic could resume along the main road. For a week nothing moved, and we counted the days by the marks on the kitchen wall.","zh":"管子要是不包上，里头的水在第一个寒夜就会冻住。去年冰把整条管线堵死了，暖气不得不停了整整两天。我邻居开始盯着天气预报不放，一心等霜冻、等风向有什么变化。我们说好一起动手：他去给隔壁老人烧水，我去弄盐。早上化冻了，大路上的车又能走了。那一个星期什么也动不了，我们就在厨房墙上划道子数日子。"},"front":{"tw":[["face",3],["nose",3],["lie",2],["back",1],["inside",6],["look",0],["bow",3],["line",2],["behind",6],["breast",0]],"en":"The old house stands at the front of a narrow street, with a small garden behind it. Its face is grey, and the paint on the nose of each window has worn away. Inside, a long line of photographs hangs on the wall, and the ones at the back are almost white. My grandmother would look at them and bow her head a little. She said the house must not lie empty, that a family should live at its breast, close to the road, where everyone can see who comes and goes.","zh":"那栋老房子立在一条窄街的最前头，后面有个小园子。它的门面是灰的，每扇窗子凸出来的那块漆都磨掉了。屋里墙上挂着一长排照片，靠里的那些几乎白得看不清了。我奶奶会看着它们，微微低下头。她说这房子不能空着躺在那儿，一家人该住在它的胸口上，紧挨着大路，好让谁都看得见谁进谁出。"},"good":{"tw":[["dear",0],["basic",3],["advantage",2],["bad",1],["sure",6],["full",0],["better",3],["quality",2],["think",6],["near",0]],"en":"My grandfather always said that a good name is worth more than money. He kept the shop near the bridge for forty years and never once sold anything of poor quality. Of course it was hard to make a living, but he thought the basic advantage of the work was simple: people trusted him, and trust is a dear thing. When trade turned bad he did not complain. He was sure that if he stayed full of patience things would get better, and in the end they did. That, he said, was the whole of the matter.","zh":"我爷爷总说，好名声比钱值钱。他在桥边开那家铺子开了四十年，一回也没卖过差东西。谋生当然不容易，但他觉得这活儿最基本的好处很简单：人家信得过他，而信得过是很金贵的东西。生意变差的时候他也不抱怨。他认定只要耐着性子熬着，日子总会好起来，后来果然就好了。他说，事情的全部就是这个。"},"ground":{"tw":[["base",0],["build",3],["hit",2],["figure",1],["fire",6],["earth",3],["floor",3],["paint",2],["inside",6],["land",2]],"en":"The workers had to clear the ground before they could build anything. They hit a thick layer of clay at the base of the slope, and the figure on their plan had to be changed. Inside the fence the floor of the old shed was still there, with a door of green paint and the marks of an old fire on the wall. The land belonged to a family who had farmed it for a hundred years. Now a line of lorries carries away the earth and nothing will grow on that ground for a long time.","zh":"工人们得先把地清出来才能动工盖东西。他们在坡底下一头撞上厚厚一层黏土，图纸上的数字只得改了。围墙里面，那间旧棚子的地面还在，还有一扇刷绿漆的门和墙上的一个壁炉。这块地属于一家人，他们种了一百年。现在一队卡车把土一车车运走，那片地上很久都不会再长出什么来了。"},"hit":{"tw":[["reach",0],["bottom",3],["move",2],["miss",1],["run",6],["shoot",0],["cut",3],["touch",2],["double",6],["strike",0]],"en":"The batsman waited, watched the ball, and then hit it hard. The crowd rose as it began to reach the far side of the field, and the men on the boundary had to run. He did not miss once that afternoon, and twice he made the ball touch the top of the wall for a double. When the light began to go, the captain told him to cut the risk and stop trying to shoot at everything. He moved down the pitch slowly, took one last strike, and the ball rolled to the bottom of the bank.","zh":"击球手等着，盯着球，然后狠狠一击。球开始飞向场地那头，看台上的人都站起来了，边界上的几个球员只得跑起来。那天下午他一次也没落空，还有两回让球碰到墙顶，跑成两分。天光渐暗时，队长叫他别再冒风险，不要见什么都打。他慢慢地走下球道，最后一击，球滚到了坡底。"},"issue":{"tw":[["cut",0],["change",3],["store",2],["recall",1],["question",6],["matter",0],["check",3],["write",2],["whether",6],["return",0]],"en":"The manager had to recall a whole line of tins and issue a notice to every store in the district. The question was whether the fault came from the factory or from the long journey in the heat. He asked me to check the records and write a short report on the matter. There had been a change in the way the lids were cut, and nobody could say when it started. We had to return three hundred boxes to the plant. It was a small issue, but it cost us a month.","zh":"经理不得不召回一整批罐头，并向区里每家商店发一份通知。问题在于毛病出在工厂，还是出在炎热天气里那趟长途运输。他让我去核一下记录，就这件事写一份简短的报告。罐盖的裁切方式有过一次改动，谁也说不清是从什么时候开始的。我们得把三百箱货退回厂里。事情本身不大，却耗了我们一个月。"},"last":{"tw":[["close",0],["run",3],["measure",2],["first",1],["ago",6],["end",2],["wear",3],["rank",2],["since",6],["final",0]],"en":"My last summer at the school began long ago in the first week of June and ended in the middle of August. I had to run a mile every morning, and the coach would measure the time and write it on the board. Since the oldest boys always took the top rank, I never came close to them. By the final week my shoes had begun to wear through at the toe. On the last day the whole class stood in a line at the end of the field, and the headmaster said a few words that I have carried with me for a long time.","zh":"我在学校过的最后一个夏天，是从六月的第一周开始，到八月中结束的。每天早上我都得跑一英里，教练会量时间，再写在校牌上。因为最高名次总被年纪最大的那几个占着，我从来没能靠近他们。到了最后一周，我的鞋脚尖已经开始磨穿了。最后一天，全班在场地尽头站成一排，校长讲了几句话，那些话我一直记到今天。"},"law":{"tw":[["lawyer",4],["police",0],["force",2],["justice",6],["legal",4],["philosophy",2],["statute",6]],"en":"My cousin trained as a lawyer and now works for a small firm that takes cases the police will not touch. He says the law is not the same thing as justice, and that any statute can be read in two ways. The force of an old rule may last for a century after the reason for it is gone. At night he reads a little philosophy, because the questions he meets in court are older than any legal book. He tells me that most of what people call justice is really just care taken with details.","zh":"我表哥学的是法律，现在在一家小事务所做事，接的都是警方不愿沾的案子。他说法律和公正不是一回事，任何一条成文法都能有两种读法。一条旧规矩的效力，可能在它的道理早就没了之后还要撑上一百年。夜里他会读一点哲学，因为他在法庭上遇到的那些问题，比任何法学书都古老。他跟我说，人们嘴里的公正，多半不过是对细节的一点点用心。"},"leave":{"tw":[["allow",0],["pass",3],["change",2],["arrive",1],["stay",6],["forget",0],["remember",3],["lose",2],["return",6],["lead",3]],"en":"We had to leave the hotel before six, and the manager would not allow us to stay a minute longer. The train was due to arrive at half past, so we had to pass through the empty streets with our bags. My mother kept checking that she was not forgetting anything, and then, of course, she would remember something else. I was afraid we should lose the connection at the next station. But the change was easy, and by noon we had returned to the town that had led us out thirty years before.","zh":"我们六点前就得离开旅馆，经理一分钟都不肯让我们多留。火车半点到，所以我们只好拎着箱子穿过空荡荡的街道。我妈一遍遍检查自己有没有忘东西，然后当然又想起来了别的。我担心我们在下一站会误了换乘。可换车很顺利，中午的时候，我们已经回到了三十年前带我们离开的那座小镇。"},"level":{"tw":[["charge",0],["high",3],["state",2],["raise",1],["current",6],["flat",0],["low",3],["talk",2],["below",6],["floor",3]],"en":"The engineer stood on the floor of the hall and checked the level of the water in the tank. It was still low, only a metre below the mark, so he had to raise the pipe and let the current run for an hour. He did not want to charge the whole system again, because the pressure was already high. His talk with the manager had been short and flat: either the state of the pumps improved, or the building would have to close for a week. In the end he found a simple answer and wrote it down on the wall.","zh":"工程师站在大厅的地面上，查看水箱里的水位。水还很低，离刻线只差一米，所以他得把管子抬高，让水流上一个小时。他不想再给整个系统充一次压，因为压力本来就高。他跟经理那番谈话又短又平淡：要么水泵的状况好转，要么这栋楼就得关一个星期。最后他想出个简单的办法，把它写在了墙上。"},"lie":{"tw":[["rest",0],["back",3],["position",2],["sit",1],["hide",6],["consist",0],["charge",3],["exist",2],["else",6],["dwell",0]],"en":"The old dog likes to lie in the same place every evening, at the back of the kitchen where nobody else goes. His position never changes; he will rest there for hours and only sit up when he hears a car. I asked the vet whether any trouble might hide behind such quiet habits, and she said that a dog's health can consist of very little: food, warmth, and a good place to sleep. She told me not to charge him with anything more, and to let him dwell in his own corner as long as he exists.","zh":"那条老狗每天傍晚都要躺在一个固定的地方，就是厨房里头谁也去不到的角落。它的位置从不改变；它能在那里歇上好几个钟头，只有听见车声才坐起来。我问兽医，这么安静的习性背后会不会藏着什么毛病。她说狗的健康其实可以由很少的东西组成：吃食、暖和，再加一个睡觉的好地方。她叫我别再给它加什么负担，让它就在自己的角落里待着，活一天算一天。"},"like":{"tw":[["care",0],["love",3],["see",2],["dislike",1],["look",6],["same",5],["please",3],["desire",2],["well",6],["wish",0]],"en":"My sister and I look exactly the same, and we like the same things. But she does not care for cold mornings, and I dislike them even more. As you wish, she said one day, but I should love a walk by the river. I could see she was not well, so I did not please her. Her one desire was a hot drink and a long rest. I looked at her face and thought how much alike we were, and how little it mattered. We were like two cups thrown by the same hand, and neither of us could be happy alone.","zh":"我和姐姐长得一模一样，喜欢的东西也一样。可她受不了冷天早晨，我比她更讨厌。有一天她说：随你吧，不过我倒是很想沿河走一走。我看得出她身子不舒服，就没顺着她。她唯一的念头是一杯热饮和好好歇一会儿。我看着她那张脸，心想我们俩多像啊，而这又多么不重要。我们像同一双手捏出来的两只杯子，谁单独一个都不会快活。"},"love":{"tw":[["bed",0],["romance",3],["like",2],["hate",1],["dream",6],["dear",0],["worship",3],["object",2],["mind",6],["bang",0]],"en":"My grandmother says she did not fall in love with my grandfather at first sight; she simply liked him and went on liking him. There was no romance in the little flat where they began, only one bed and a window over the yard. I hate to say it, she told me, but after fifty years the dear old man is still the first object in my mind. She keeps his picture by her bed and worships the ground he walks on. She has a dream that they will meet again. Then she banged the kettle down and laughed at herself.","zh":"我奶奶说，她对我爷爷不是一见钟情；她只是一开始喜欢他，然后就一直喜欢下去。他们起头的那间小公寓里没什么浪漫，只有一张床和一扇朝院子的窗。她跟我说：我不愿意这么说，可过了五十年，这个老头子还是我心里头头一件放着的事。她把他照片摆在床边，把他走过的地都当圣地。她还做着再见到他的梦。说完她把水壶往下一磕，自己笑了。"},"man":{"tw":[["human",0],["black",3],["island",2],["woman",1],["boy",6],["piece",0],["white",3],["work",2],["old",6],["world",3]],"en":"The old man lived alone on the island for eleven years after his wife died. He was the only human being there, and for a long time he did not see a woman or a boy. His house was one long piece of white stone above the black rocks, and he kept it in good work by mending the roof every spring. When people asked how he could bear it, he said the world was large enough for one man if he watched it closely. Now he is gone, and only the garden shows where he lived.","zh":"妻子去世后，那个老人在岛上独自住了十一年。整座岛上只有他一个人，很长一段时间里，他见不到一个女人，也见不到一个男孩。他的房子是黑礁石上头一块长长的白石头，每年春天他修一次屋顶，把它收拾得挺像样。有人问他怎么熬得住，他说，一个人只要看得够仔细，这世界对他就够大了。现在他不在了，只有那片园子还显示他曾经住过。"},"manage":{"tw":[["care",0],["build",3],["act",2],["fail",1],["help",6],["deal",0],["meet",3],["control",2],["need",6],["handle",0]],"en":"She has to manage a small shop and a family at the same time, and she does it well. She will build the week's plan on Sunday, deal with the suppliers on Monday, and meet her customers every day. If she should fail at anything, she does not need anyone to tell her. She can handle a difficult customer better than most people I know, and she is never rude. The one thing she cannot control is her own tiredness. I act as if I were fine, she says, and then I take care of myself on Sunday. Her sister comes in to help on Saturdays.","zh":"她既要管一家小店，又要管家，两头都顾得很好。她星期天把一周的打算排出来，星期一跟供货的人打交道，每天还要见客人。要是哪件事没办成，她不用别人说。难缠的客人，她应付得比我认识的多数人都好，而且从不失礼。唯一她管不住的就是自己的累。她说：我就装作没事，然后星期天再照顾自己。星期六她妹妹会过来搭把手。"},"miss":{"tw":[["drop",0],["cut",3],["woman",2],["hit",1],["play",6],["lose",0],["forget",3],["avoid",2],["title",6],["escape",0]],"en":"The woman in the next seat told me not to miss the first ten minutes of the play. She had a title in her hand and kept checking it. If you drop in late, she said, you lose the whole point. I did not want to hit anyone with my bag, so I cut along the wall and sat down quickly. I tried to avoid the man with the loud voice, but I could not forget how close I had come to being late. That day I learned to leave the house early and never miss a train again. There is no escape from that lesson once it is learned.","zh":"邻座那位女士叫我千万别错过这出戏开头那十分钟。她手里捏着节目单，一遍遍看。她说：你要是迟到了再进去，整出戏的意思就丢了。我不想用包撞到人，就贴着墙边挤过去，赶紧坐下。我想躲开那个嗓门大的男人，可忘不掉自己差一点就迟到。那天我算是学乖了：出门要早，再也不能误车。这教训一旦学到手，就再也躲不开了。"},"open":{"tw":[["clear",0],["establish",3],["move",2],["close",1],["next",6],["subject",0],["gap",3],["start",2],["round",6],["loose",0]],"en":"The committee met in an open room on the second floor, with a clear view of the yard. Before the start of business they had to establish who would speak first, then move the tables into a loose round so everyone could see the others. There was a gap at the door, which they left open for air. Half the subject that day was the next budget, but by six o'clock they had still not voted to close the meeting. In the end they agreed to carry the matter over to the following week, and the room emptied in a minute.","zh":"委员会在二楼一间敞亮的屋子里开会，从那儿能把院子看得清清楚楚。开会之前，他们得先定下谁第一个发言，然后把桌子摆成一个松松的圈，好让每个人都看得见别人。门那儿有条缝，他们就让它敞着透气。那天的议题有一半是下一年的预算，可到六点他们还没表决要不要散会。最后他们说好把这事推到下个星期，屋子里一分钟就走空了。"},"question":{"tw":[["doubt",0],["problem",3],["ask",2],["answer",1],["whether",6],["head",0],["pump",3],["subject",2],["reason",6],["wonder",3]],"en":"The teacher would ask one question and then wait, with her head a little to one side. There was no doubt in her mind that a good problem is worth more than a quick answer. I wonder, she would say, whether any of you can tell me the reason for this. Then she would pump the water out of an old pipe to show us what she meant. The subject of the lesson was pressure, but what she really taught us was to sit with a question instead of reaching for the first thing that came.","zh":"老师会先提一个问题，然后等着，头微微偏到一边。她心里从不怀疑：一个好问题比一个快答案值钱。她会说：我倒想知道，你们谁说得清这里头的道理。接着她会用一根旧管子把水抽出来，让我们看看她是什么意思。那节课的主题是压力，可她真正教我们的是：守着一个问题待着，别急着去抓头一个冒出来的东西。"},"quiet":{"tw":[["calm",5],["compose",3],["comfort",2],["active",1],["little",6],["silence",0],["lull",3],["order",2],["usual",6],["smooth",0]],"en":"After the storm the sea went quiet, and a smooth calm spread over the water. My father, who is not usually a still man, sat on the wall and said nothing. It is a lull, he told me, not a silence. The little harbour was in good order again, and the boats lay at rest in it. He is active all day and does not know how to compose himself, but on that evening he found comfort in just sitting. I did not disturb him; I only watched the light move.","zh":"暴风雨过后，海静了下来，一片平顺的安宁铺在水面上。我爸平时不是个能静住的人，那天却坐在墙上什么也不说。他告诉我：这只是暂时的平息，不是真正的寂静。小港湾又整整齐齐了，船都安安静静停在里头。他一天到晚闲不住，不知道该怎么让自己沉下来，可那天晚上，光是坐着就让他觉得宽慰。我没去打扰他，只是看着光线一点点移动。"},"raise":{"tw":[["climb",0],["carry",3],["bet",2],["lower",1],["pay",6],["farm",0],["draw",3],["better",2],["benefit",6],["fire",0]],"en":"The men on the farm had to raise the new barn before the winter. They would climb the frame with a rope, carry each beam up by hand, and draw it into place. One of them made a bet that he could lift the heaviest piece alone, and lost. The owner agreed to pay them better for the extra days, because the benefit to the whole village was clear. In the evening they lit a fire by the road and talked about the year to come. Nobody mentioned the lower price of grain.","zh":"农场上的那些人得赶在入冬前把新谷仓立起来。他们拿绳子爬上架子，把每根梁用手抬上去，再拉到位。有一个人打赌说他一个人能抬起最重的那根，结果输了。东家答应对多加的这几天给更好的工钱，因为这对整个村子都有好处，谁都看得见。傍晚他们在路边生了一堆火，聊起明年。没人提粮价走低的事。"},"record":{"tw":[["book",3],["card",3],["list",2],["erase",1],["consecutive",6],["enter",0],["cut",3],["save",2],["straight",6],["read",0]],"en":"The clerk kept a record of every visitor in a thick book by the door. She would enter the name, read the card, and then write a straight list of the hours each one stayed. No two entries were consecutive; the numbers jumped about all day. If she made a mistake she would erase it with a small knife and cut the page away. I save these, she said, because one day someone will want to know who came and went. She has kept the same record for thirty years.","zh":"门房在门边一本厚本子里记下每个来访的人。她会写下名字，看一眼证件，然后把每人待了几个钟头一行行直着列出来。没有两条是挨着的，一整天数字都在乱跳。要是写错了，她就用小刀刮掉，把那一块裁下来。她说：这些我都留着，总有一天有人想知道谁来过、谁走了。同一本记录她记了三十年。"},"remember":{"tw":[["think",0],["mind",3],["mention",2],["forget",1],["maybe",6],["recall",0],["qualify",3],["associate",2],["imagine",6],["retrieve",0]],"en":"I cannot always remember names, but I can recall a face for years. My mother would mention someone at dinner and I would think, without being able to qualify it, that I had met them before. Maybe that is why I associate certain rooms with certain people. I try to imagine what my grandfather looked like, and I can still retrieve the sound of his voice. What I forget is small: the day, the street, the colour of the door. He said once that the mind keeps what matters and lets the rest go.","zh":"我不总能记住名字，但一张脸我能记好些年。饭桌上我妈提到某人，我心里就会觉得以前见过，可说不清是怎么个见过法。也许正因如此，我总把某些屋子和某些人连在一块儿。我试着去想我爷爷长什么样，还能把他说话的声调捞回来。我忘掉的都是些小事：哪一天、哪条街、门是什么颜色。他生前说过，脑子留下来的都是要紧的，其余的全放走了。"},"ride":{"tw":[["drive",0],["boat",3],["climb",2],["walk",1],["bike",6],["sit",0],["bus",3],["continue",2],["track",6],["mount",0]],"en":"We used to ride the old bus up the valley every summer. My father would drive to the station, leave the car, and climb aboard with two bags. On the boat we would sit at the back and watch the track of white water behind us. Sometimes he would let me mount his bike and walk it along the road beside him. When the light began to go he would say we should continue a little further, and we always did. I have never found a journey I liked better.","zh":"每年夏天我们都坐那趟老旧的公共汽车上山谷去。我爸先开车到车站，把汽车留下，再拎着两个包爬上车。在船上我们就坐在船尾，看身后那道白色的水痕。有时候他让我骑上他的自行车，他在旁边推着走。天光开始暗下来时，他总说再往前一点吧，而我们每回都真的往前了。我后来再没遇到过比那更让我喜欢的旅程。"},"right":{"tw":[["good",0],["floor",3],["change",2],["left",1],["without",6],["proper",5],["access",3],["hand",2],["back",6],["correct",0]],"en":"The right to walk on that ground belonged to the village, but nobody had the proper papers. A man came from the city and put a fence across the path, so we had to go round by the left side of the hill. My grandfather said it was not good, and that without access to the water the farms would change hands within a year. He wrote to the council and got the correct answer at last: the fence came down. He kept the letter in his hand all the way home, and on the back he wrote the date. Then he laid it on the floor of the hall and read it to us twice.","zh":"在那片地上行走的权利本来是村里的，可谁手里都没有正式的文件。城里来了个人，在路当中拉起一道栅栏，我们只好绕到山左边走。我爷爷说这样不行，要是取不到水，这些农地一年之内就得易主。他给镇公所写了信，最后得了个正确的答复：栅栏拆了。他一路把那封信捏在手里回家，还在背面写下了日期。"},"rise":{"tw":[["climb",3],["head",3],["change",2],["fall",1],["decline",6],["grow",2],["wave",3],["look",2],["surge",6],["jump",3]],"en":"We climbed to the head of the valley to watch the sun rise. The price of grain had begun to decline that spring, and the farmers said the change would not last. They would look at the sky and guess, and when the wind came the wheat would wave like water. In a dry year the crop can grow quickly and then fall in a single night. My uncle said the worst thing was the surge of hope in June. Then he jumped the wall and went in for breakfast.","zh":"我们爬到山谷顶上去看日出。那年春天粮价开始往下走，种地的人说这变化长不了。他们会抬头看天、凭经验猜，风一来，麦子就像水一样起伏。碰上旱年，庄稼能长得飞快，然后一夜之间全倒。我叔说最难受的是六月里那阵子希望往上涌的时候。说完他跳过墙，进屋吃早饭去了。"},"round":{"tw":[["around",0],["bottom",3],["call",2],["square",1],["final",6],["beat",0],["rubbish",3],["change",2],["match",6],["attack",0]],"en":"The final round of the match was played in front of a small crowd. There is a square of grass at the bottom of our street, and the players had to walk around a rubbish bin to reach it. The drummer would beat his drum and call out the score after every point. Our side came under attack early, and the coach had to change the plan twice. It was a hard game, and by the end the whole team was too tired to speak. They lost, but the crowd stood up for them all the same.","zh":"比赛的最后一轮是在一小群观众面前踢的。我们这条街尽头有块方方的草地，球员得绕过一只垃圾桶才能走到场上。鼓手每得一分就敲鼓、报比分。我们这边一开场就被压着打，教练不得不两次改打法。那是场硬仗，到终场时整队人都累得说不出话。他们输了，可观众还是都站起来为他们鼓掌。"},"run":{"tw":[["carry",0],["cut",3],["break",2],["idle",1],["start",6],["course",0],["double",3],["change",2],["home",6],["draw",3]],"en":"My brother used to run the two miles home from school every day. He would cut across the field, break through the hedge, and arrive at the door with his shirt out. He never sat idle; if the weather was bad he would run the course indoors, up and down the stairs. He would draw a mark on the door frame after every run, and twice he ran a double distance on purpose, just to see what his body would do. Our mother would carry a glass of water out to him, and he would drink it standing up. That was the start of a habit that has never changed.","zh":"我哥哥从前每天从学校跑两英里回家。他抄过那片田，钻过树篱，到门口时衬衫都跑出来了。他从不闲坐着；天气不好就在屋里跑那条路线，楼上楼下地跑。每跑完一趟他就在门框上画一道记，还有两回他故意跑双倍的路，就想看看自己身体能扛成什么样。我妈会端杯水出去给他，他就站着喝。这个习惯从那时候起就没变过。"},"second":{"tw":[["back",0],["climax",3],["position",2],["first",1],["final",6],["bit",0],["pinpoint",3],["support",2],["straight",6],["minute",0]],"en":"She finished a very close second in the final race of the season. For a bit she stood at the back of the field and could not look at anyone. The climax had come in the first hundred metres, when she was still in a good position; after that the winner moved away and she could not pinpoint where she had lost the time. One minute, her coach said, and you would have had it. He asked her to hold her back straight and to support her weight on the other foot. She simply nodded.","zh":"赛季最后一场比赛，她以极小的差距拿了第二。有一小会儿，她站在场地最后头，谁也不敢看。最要紧的那一刻出现在头一百米，那时候她的位置还很好；之后领先的人跑远了，而她说不出自己是在哪儿丢掉了时间。她教练说：就差一分钟，你就拿下了。他让她把背挺直，把重心换到另一只脚上撑住。她只是点了点头。"},"sell":{"tw":[["deal",3],["clear",3],["exchange",2],["buy",1],["purchase",6],["trade",0],["market",3],["sale",2],["cash",6],["betray",0]],"en":"My father used to sell vegetables at the market on Saturday mornings. He would make one deal with the man on his left and a better one with the woman on his right, and by nine the best of the boxes were gone. He took cash and would not exchange a purchase without a receipt. Once you sell, he said, you must not betray the buyer by sending him a poor crate. He was in the trade for thirty years and never made a sale he could not stand behind. I remember him clearing the stall in the rain.","zh":"我爸从前星期六早上在集市上卖菜。他会跟左边那人讲一笔，再跟右边的女人讲一笔更好的，到九点最好的几箱就都出手了。他只收现钱，没有收据就不肯换货。他说：东西一旦卖出去，你就不能给买家发一箱烂的，那叫背叛人。他在这行做了三十年，没有一笔买卖是他不肯担的。我记得他在雨里收摊的样子。"},"set":{"tw":[["arrange",2],["bed",3],["change",2],["rise",1],["next",6],["dress",0],["charge",3],["choose",2],["break",6],["fit",0]],"en":"Every evening my grandmother would set the table before the sun began to rise. She would arrange the plates in a row, choose the bread, and then dress the salad with oil. When the heat came on she had to charge the old cooker and wait for it to fit the temperature she wanted. The next thing was the bed, which she made with a stiff cover. Nothing would make her change the order: set the table first, break the bread last. It was the same in every house she ever lived in.","zh":"每天傍晚，太阳还没下去，我奶奶就把桌子摆好了。她把盘子排成一行，挑好面包，再给沙拉浇上油。暖气一上来，她就得给那台老灶添料，等着它到她要的温度。接下来是床，她用的是硬挺的床罩。什么也改不了她那套顺序：先摆桌，最后才掰面包。她住过的每一间屋子都是这样。"},"show":{"tw":[["express",0],["finger",3],["appear",2],["hide",1],["watch",6],["picture",0],["fly",3],["inform",2],["film",6],["present",0]],"en":"The teacher wanted to show us how a moth hides from a bird. She would hold up a picture, then point one finger at the shape on the wall. Watch closely, she said, and you will see it appear and then vanish. She had a short film on an old machine, and she used it to express the same idea in another way. Her aim was to inform, not to amuse us. At the end she asked each of us to present one thing we had learned, and then let a moth fly out of the window.","zh":"老师想让我们看看飞蛾是怎么躲开鸟的。她会举起一张图，再用一根手指点着墙上那个形状。她说：看仔细了，你会看见它先出现，然后又不见。她还有一部旧机器放的短片，就用它把同一个意思换个法子讲了一遍。她的目的是让我们知道些什么，不是逗我们乐。最后她让我们每人讲一件学到的事，然后把一只蛾子从窗口放了出去。"},"side":{"tw":[["face",0],["edge",3],["cut",2],["bottom",3],["rest",6],["position",0],["front",3],["line",2],["back",6],["slope",0]],"en":"Our house stands on the side of a hill, with a steep slope at the front. If you look at its face from the road, you see a line of small windows and a door at the bottom of three steps. On the back side there is a bench where my father likes to rest. He will cut the grass along the edge of the path and then sit down with his back to the wall. From that position he can watch everyone who comes up the road. It is the best seat in the village, he says.","zh":"我们家在山坡上，前面是一道陡坡。你要是从路上看它的门脸，会看到一排小窗，还有三级台阶底下的一扇门。背面有条长凳，我爸喜欢在那儿歇着。他会沿着路边把草剪齐，然后背靠着墙坐下。从那个位置，他看得见每个上坡来的人。他说，这是全村最好的位子。"},"sit":{"tw":[["ride",0],["lounge",3],["serve",2],["lie",1],["wait",6],["seat",0],["perch",3],["travel",2],["stay",6],["model",0]],"en":"On long journeys my aunt would rather sit than lie down. She says that in a lounge car you can watch the country travel past, and that a comfortable seat is worth any amount of money. She used to ride the night train to the coast and perch on a small stool by the window for hours. A waiter would come to serve coffee, and she would stay there until dawn. She has never learned to rest in a bed on a train. I am not a model of good sense, she says, but I do not miss much.","zh":"长途旅行的时候，我姑姑宁可坐着也不肯躺下。她说在休息车厢里能看着乡野往后走，一个舒服的座位值多少钱都行。她从前常坐夜车去海边，一连几个钟头就栖在窗边一张小凳上。服务员会过来送咖啡，她就在那儿一直待到天亮。她始终学不会在火车卧铺上歇着。她说：我不是什么明白人的榜样，但我没漏掉多少东西。"},"slow":{"tw":[["behind",0],["delay",3],["decrease",2],["fast",1],["pace",6],["easy",0],["clog",3],["decelerate",2],["steady",6],["dim",0]],"en":"The traffic was slow all the way out of the city. A single broken lorry had begun to clog the road, and the pace of every car behind it fell to a walk. My father kept a steady voice, but he would not drive fast in the dim light. There is no need to delay anyone, he said, and no harm in being a little behind. When the road opened his worry decreased slowly, and then the speed picked up again. He told me that an easy journey is one where you never have to decelerate suddenly.","zh":"出城的路上一直堵得很慢。一辆坏了的货车把路堵住了，跟在它后面每辆车的速度都降到步行的样子。我爸声音很稳，但天色昏暗他不肯开快。他说：没必要耽误别人，落在后面一点也没什么坏处。路一通，他的担心慢慢消下来，车速也就重新提起来了。他还告诉我，一趟舒服的行程，就是你从来不用猛地减速。"},"start":{"tw":[["begin",2],["birth",3],["act",2],["finish",1],["next",6],["first",0],["fall",3],["leave",2],["break",6],["jump",0]],"en":"The race would start at the first light, and by then the whole village was awake. My cousin had trained all year for it, and he meant to finish in the top ten. At the next bend the road begins to fall away, so the runners have to take it easy or they break their step. I watched him leave the gate and jump the low wall at the corner. It was the birth of something new in him, I think. He said afterwards that the act of starting is the only part that ever frightened him.","zh":"比赛天一亮就开始，到那时候全村人都醒了。我表哥为这场赛跑练了一整年，一心想跑进前十。下一个转弯处路面开始往下斜，所以跑的人得悠着点，不然步子就乱了。我看着他从大门出去，跳过拐角那道矮墙。我觉得，那是他心里有什么新东西生出来了。后来他说，真正让他害怕的只有起跑那一下。"},"stop":{"tw":[["bar",0],["call",3],["act",2],["start",1],["move",6],["break",3],["close",3],["stay",2],["prevent",6],["catch",2]],"en":"The bus makes one stop at the end of our road, and if you do not catch it there you must walk. The driver will call out the name of the place and then close the doors. There is a metal bar across the front window, and a small sign that says you must not stay on after the last stop of the day. In winter the ice can prevent the bus from moving at all, and then my mother has to act quickly and find another way to get to work. The rain began to break just as we started out.","zh":"公共汽车在我们这条路尽头有一站，要是在那儿没赶上，就只能走路了。司机报出地名，然后关门。前窗上横着一根金属杆，还有块小牌子写着：到当天最后一站后不得继续留在车上。冬天结冰能让车根本动不了，那时候我妈就得赶紧想办法，另外找路去上班。我们刚出发，雨就开始小下来了。"},"tail":{"tw":[["behind",0],["tree",3],["cut",2],["head",1],["nose",6],["bottom",0],["brush",3],["end",2],["snout",6],["dog",0]],"en":"My dog will run in circles and chase his own tail until he falls over. He is a small thing with a black nose and a wet snout, and he keeps his head down when he is working. At the bottom of the garden there is an old tree, and he likes to sit behind it. I have to brush him every week and cut the hair that grows long at the end of his back. He watches me with his tail still, waiting for the brush to come near him again.","zh":"我的狗会绕着圈跑，追自己的尾巴，一直追到摔倒。它个头小，黑鼻子，鼻头总是湿的，干活的时候脑袋低着。园子尽头有一棵老树，它喜欢坐在树后面。我每个星期都得给它刷毛，把脊背末端长出来的毛剪掉。它尾巴一动不动地盯着我，等刷子再靠近它。"},"top":{"tw":[["clear",0],["head",3],["complete",2],["bottom",1],["key",6],["cover",0],["tail",3],["degree",2],["hold",6],["lead",0]],"en":"We climbed to the top of the hill on a clear morning. My brother held the key to the gate in his hand and would not let go of it. At the bottom of the slope a road led away to the next town, and above our heads the cover of cloud began to lift. A dog ran past us with its tail up, and we watched it go. He wanted to complete the walk before noon, so we had to hold a good speed. It was, to a high degree, the best morning of that whole year.","zh":"一个晴朗的早晨，我们爬到了山顶。我弟弟手里攥着大门的钥匙，怎么都不肯放。坡底下有条路通向邻镇，我们头顶上的云层开始散开。一条狗翘着尾巴从我们身边跑过，我们看着它跑远。他想在中午前走完这趟，所以我们得保持一个不错的速度。那真是那一年里最好的一个早晨，好得没法说。"},"wake":{"tw":[["heat",0],["call",3],["change",2],["sleep",1],["fall",6],["awake",0],["ferment",3],["island",2],["fear",6],["arouse",0]],"en":"The heat would wake me before six every morning that summer, and I would lie still and try to sleep again. My father would call from the yard, then fall quiet, waiting for me to come down. On the island there was nothing to fear and nothing to hurry for. The change came slowly: by August I was awake at five without any noise at all, and I began to ferment ideas about what I would do when we went home. He could arouse me with a single word. Years later I still wake at that hour, and the old house comes back to me in the dark.","zh":"那年夏天，每天早上六点不到，热气就把我叫醒了，我就躺着不动，想再睡一会儿。我爸会在院子里喊我，然后安静下来，等我下楼。在岛上没什么可怕的，也没什么要赶的。变化是慢慢来的：到了八月，我五点就醒，一点动静都不用，脑子里开始发酵起回家以后要干什么的念头。他一个字就能把我叫起来。很多年以后我还是那个点醒，那栋老房子就在黑里回到我眼前。"},"waste":{"tw":[["blow",0],["burn",3],["act",2],["conserve",1],["water",6],["wild",0],["rubbish",3],["kill",2],["garbage",6],["rot",0]],"en":"It is a waste to burn good wood in an open fire, and my father would not act so foolishly. He told us to conserve what we had and never to let food rot in the box. The wild part of the garden was full of rubbish and old garbage, and he made us clear it every spring. If a storm should blow down a tree, we had to cut it up that week or the water would get in and kill the wood. He said a house that lets things go is a house that is already lost.","zh":"在明火上烧好木头是浪费，我爸不会干这种蠢事。他叫我们省着用手里有的，别让吃食在箱子里烂掉。园子荒着的那半边净是垃圾和烂七八糟的旧东西，他每年春天都逼我们去清一遍。要是风把树刮倒了，我们得在那个星期里把它锯开，不然水汽钻进去，木头就废了。他说，一栋什么都撒手不管的房子，其实早就没了。"},"wind":{"tw":[["lead",0],["ball",3],["move",2],["unwind",1],["rain",6],["lift",0],["clue",3],["raise",2],["water",6],["nose",0]],"en":"The wind came up the valley just before the rain started. My uncle had to lead the boat round, and my job was to raise the sail and keep the nose of it into the weather. There was no clue where the storm would move next. A ball of grey cloud sat on the hills and would not lift. When it was over I would unwind the wet rope and hang it on the fence. Over the water afterwards there was a fine line of foam as far as I could see.","zh":"雨还没下，风就先顺着山谷上来了。我叔得把船领回去，我的活儿是把帆升起来，让船头迎着风。谁也说不准风暴接下来往哪儿挪。山上蹲着一团灰云，怎么也不肯散。事后我把湿绳子解开绕松，挂在栅栏上。那之后水面上拉着一条细白的泡沫，一眼望不到头。"},"cat":{"tw":[["feline",4],["guy",0],["man",2],["dog",6],["sick",0],["woman",2],["rabbit",6],["cast",0]],"en":"The woman next door keeps a cat that has never once been friendly to me. She says it is a feline thing, and that a dog would be easier, but she is fond of it. There is a man down the road who swears he saw it cast a shadow on the wall like a person. Once, when the animal was sick, she would not leave the house for a week. My brother, who is a quiet guy, says the rabbit in our garden is the reason it comes over our fence so often.","zh":"隔壁那位女士养了一只猫，那猫从来没对我友好过。她说这是猫的天性，还说养条狗会省事些，可她就是喜欢它。路那头有个男人一口咬定，说他见过这猫在墙上投下一个像人一样的影子。有一回这猫病了，她整整一个星期没出门。我弟弟是个安静的人，他说我们园子里那只兔子，就是它总翻过篱笆过来的原因。"},"cause":{"tw":[["causal",4],["drive",0],["bring",3],["origin",2],["risk",6],["engine",3],["venture",2],["result",6]],"en":"Nobody could say what the cause of the fire had been. The engine of the old car was cold, and there was no sign of anyone in the yard. My father said the most likely origin was a wire under the floor, though he admitted that was only a guess. He would not risk another night in the house, so he asked me to drive to my aunt's. She asked him to bring the papers with him, and he did not venture an opinion again until the morning. The result of the inquiry was the same: no clear reason. He said a causal chain like that is easy to see afterwards and impossible to see at the time.","zh":"没人说得清那场火是因何而起的。旧车的发动机是凉的，院子里也没有人来过的痕迹。我爸说最可能起头的地方是地板下的一根电线，不过他也承认这只是猜的。他不肯再在这屋里冒险住一晚，于是我们开车去了姑姑家。她叫他把文件带上，他一晚上没再开口说什么，直到第二天早上。查问的结果还是一样：没有明确的原因。他说，这样的因果链，事后看得清，当时看不见。"},"dress":{"tw":[["dresser",4],["clip",0],["change",3],["cook",2],["wear",6],["coat",3],["finish",2],["attire",6]],"en":"My mother would dress for dinner even when there was nobody to see her. She would change out of her working clothes, clip her hair back, and put on a dark coat. She would wear the same one for twenty years. Her attire never changed with fashion. Then she would cook, and the finish of the meal always mattered more to her than the dress itself. The dresser in her room still holds the same things: a comb, a pin, and a photograph of her mother in a dress of pale blue.","zh":"哪怕没人看，我妈吃晚饭也要换身体面的衣服。她脱下干活的衣裳，把头发别上去，再穿上一件深色外套。同一件她一穿就是二十年。她的穿戴从不跟着时兴走。然后她去做饭，而对她来说，一顿饭最后收得好不好，比身上这条裙子要紧得多。她房里的梳妆台里还是那几样东西：一把梳子、一根别针，还有一张她母亲穿浅蓝裙子的照片。"},"mother":{"tw":[["maternal",4],["father",1],["care",2],["daughter",6],["generate",0],["parent",2],["husband",6],["fuss",0]],"en":"My mother was the quiet one in our house; my father made all the noise. She had a maternal way with every child on the street, and she would care for them as if they were her own. When my sister had a daughter of her own, my mother went to stay for a month and would not let anyone else take over. She and my father had been husband and wife for forty years, and she still made a fuss over his birthday. She used to say that a parent is not a person who generates rules but one who keeps them company.","zh":"在我们家，我妈是安静的那个，闹出动静的全是我爸。她对街上每个孩子都有股母性，会像对自己孩子一样照顾他们。我姐姐生下自己的女儿以后，我妈过去住了一个月，不让别人插手。她和我爸做了四十年夫妻，她还照样为他的生日忙前忙后。她生前常说，当父母不是定规矩的人，而是陪着他们的人。"},"person":{"tw":[["personify",4],["individual",0],["creature",3],["man",6],["soul",0],["tyrant",3],["woman",6],["mortal",0]],"en":"He was the kind of person who remembers your name after one meeting. My grandfather used to personify patience for me: he would let a man talk for an hour and never once look at the clock. He said that no individual is only one thing, and that the worst creature in the village had a soul as well. He had lived under a tyrant in his youth, and it had taught him to be gentle with every woman and man he met. He was, for all his faults, the most mortal and the most decent of us.","zh":"他见过一面就能记住你的名字，就是这种人。在我眼里，我爷爷简直就是耐心的化身：他能让人讲上一个钟头，一眼都不看钟。他说，没有哪一个人只是一样东西，村里最坏的家伙也有一颗心。他年轻时在暴君底下活过，这让他对遇见的每个女人男人都和和气气。他毛病不少，可他是我们当中最像个凡人、也最厚道的一个。"},"song":{"tw":[["sing",4],["strain",0],["carol",3],["sound",2],["pop",6],["vocal",0],["anthem",3],["tune",6]],"en":"My aunt could sing anything, from a carol at Christmas to a pop song on the radio. She had a strong vocal line and could hold a tune for a whole verse without effort. When the old anthem was played at the village meeting, she stood up and the sound of her voice filled the hall. She said she had learned it all by ear, and that a strain of music heard once was enough for her. She never sang for money. At the end of the evening the whole room would ask her for one more, and she always gave it.","zh":"我姑姑什么都能唱，从圣诞的颂歌到收音机里流行的曲子。她嗓子很稳，一整段调子不用费劲就能托住。村里聚会上放那首老颂歌的时候，她站起来，她的声音把整个礼堂都填满了。她说她全是听会的，一段曲子只要听过一遍就够她用了。她从不为钱唱。晚上快结束时，满屋的人都会再要一首，她从来没推过。"},"tend":{"tw":[["tender",4],["run",0],["garden",3],["attend",2],["alike",6],["lean",0],["suffer",3],["incline",0]],"en":"My grandmother used to tend the garden in the mornings, before anyone else was up. She would lean on her stick to reach the far bed, and she had a tender way with young plants that I have never been able to copy. She had to attend to the roses first, then run a hose along the wall. She said that all living things are alike in this: they suffer when they are forgotten. I incline to think she was right. In July the garden gave back more than she could eat, and she would leave boxes of it at the gate.","zh":"我奶奶从前每天早上都照料园子，比别人起得都早。她会撑着棍子去够最远那畦，对嫩苗那份轻柔劲儿，我怎么学也学不来。她得先照看玫瑰，再顺墙拉一条水管浇水。她说所有活物在这一点上都一样：没人管，就受苦。我也倾向认为她是对的。到了七月，园子里长出来的东西她根本吃不完，就把一箱箱菜放在大门口。"},"will":{"tw":[["willing",4],["leave",0],["remember",3],["decide",2],["testament",0],["devise",3],["purpose",2],["bequeath",0]],"en":"My great-uncle was a man of strong will and few words. He was willing to help anyone, but he would not be told what to do. When he could no longer leave the house, he decided to write his testament himself, and he would remember every cousin by name. He devised a simple plan: the land to his son, the tools to the man who had worked for him longest. He said his purpose was only to avoid a quarrel after he was gone. He would bequeath nothing that could be argued over.","zh":"我叔公是个意志很硬、话很少的人。他愿意帮任何人的忙，但谁也别想指挥他。到出不了门的时候，他决定自己写遗嘱，还把每个表亲的名字都记得清清楚楚。他定了个简单的方案：地给儿子，工具给跟他干得最久的那个伙计。他说他的用意只是免得自己走以后有人吵架。凡是可能被人争的东西，他一件都不留。"},"address":{"tw":[["call",0],["ask",3],["use",2],["message",6],["cover",0],["approach",3],["access",2],["public",6],["deal",0]],"en":"The chairman had to address a room of two hundred people, and he was not used to it. He would call a name, ask a question, and then wait too long for an answer. His message was simple, but he had to cover a great deal of ground before he came to it. He had no access to the figures, so he had to approach the problem from the side. It was a public meeting, and by the end even the people at the back had understood what he wanted.","zh":"主席得对着一屋子两百号人讲话，他不习惯这个。他会点一个名字，问一个问题，然后等答案等得太久。他要说的其实很简单，可走到正题之前得铺陈好大一片。他手头没有数据，只好从侧面去谈这个问题。那是一场公开的会，到散场时，连最后一排的人也知道他要的是什么了。"},"ask":{"tw":[["need",0],["call",3],["address",2],["tell",6],["demand",2],["cost",3],["communicate",2],["want",6],["require",0]],"en":"If you need to ask a favour of my father, you should call him in the evening and tell him plainly what you want. He does not like a long speech. He will demand to know the cost before he agrees to anything, and he will require you to say when you need it. He is not easy to address on the phone, because he does not like to communicate in that way. But once he has said yes, he will not go back on it. That, to him, is what an honest answer means.","zh":"你要是有事求我爸，就在晚上给他打电话，直截了当跟他说你要什么。他不爱听长篇大论。答应任何事之前，他都要先问清代价，还得让你说准什么时候要。在电话里跟他说话不容易，因为他不喜欢用这种方式交流。可一旦他点头，就不会反悔。在他看来，说一句实在话就是这个意思。"},"ball":{"tw":[["egg",0],["football",3],["dance",2],["kick",6],["lump",0],["bowl",3],["wind",2],["catch",6],["formal",0]],"en":"My cousin played football every Saturday and could catch almost anything with one hand. Before a game he would eat two eggs and a bowl of rice, and then kick a ball against the wall for an hour. After the game there was a dance at the club, and he had to wear something formal for it, which he hated. He was never good at that side of things. In a hard wind he would stand with his hands in his pockets and roll a small lump of bread between his fingers.","zh":"我表哥每个星期六都踢球，几乎什么东西单手都能接住。比赛前他会吃两个鸡蛋、一碗米饭，然后对着墙踢一个小时球。比赛结束后俱乐部有舞会，他得穿点正式的衣裳，他讨厌这个。这方面他从来不行。刮大风的时候，他就把手插在兜里站着，指头间搓着一小块面包。"},"bar":{"tw":[["cake",0],["close",3],["room",2],["shop",6],["stop",0],["save",3],["support",2],["block",2]],"en":"There is a small bar at the corner of our street, and the man who keeps it knows everyone. He will close the shop at eleven, wipe the bar, and put a cake under a glass cover for the morning. People come in to stop for a while and talk about the weather in the back room. He has one rule: if you cannot support yourself on the stool, you have had enough. In winter the snow can block the door, and he will not let anyone save him the trouble of clearing it himself.","zh":"我们街角有个小酒吧，看店的那个人认识所有人。他十一点打烊，把吧台擦干净，再把一块蛋糕搁在玻璃罩下留着早上。人们进来歇一会儿，在里屋聊聊天气。他有一条规矩：你要是坐都坐不稳，那就是喝够了。冬天下雪能把门堵住，他不让别人替他省这份力气，自己扫。"},"bear":{"tw":[["accept",3],["deal",3],["act",2],["bull",1],["little",6],["birth",0],["drop",3],["big",6],["carry",3]],"en":"There was a bear in the woods above the village that summer, a big one with a little cub. The farmers would not accept it; they said it would deal with the sheep the way a bull deals with a fence. My father had to act fast, so he and two others went up with a lamp and a gun. They did not shoot. They watched the mother carry her cub across the stream and drop into the dark on the far side. He said afterwards that he had seen a birth and a death in the same minute, and that he would not go up there again.","zh":"那年夏天，村子上头的林子里来了一只熊，个头很大，带着一只小崽。种地的人不肯认这事，说它对付羊就像公牛对付栅栏一样。我爸得赶紧行动，于是他和另外两个人提着灯、带着枪上了山。他们没有开枪。他们看着母熊把小崽叼过溪水，落到对岸的黑地里去。事后他说，他在同一分钟里看见了生和死，以后再也不上去了。"},"beat":{"tw":[["dead",0],["full",3],["move",2],["upset",6],["pound",0],["kill",3],["play",2],["win",6],["round",0]],"en":"You could hear the beat of the drum from the far end of the field. It was a full band, and the players had to move with the music or lose the round. My brother was upset before the match; he said his legs felt dead and heavy. He began to pound the ball against the wall to warm up, and after ten minutes he could play again. In the last minute they managed to win, and the crowd made a noise like a heart beating. It was the sort of afternoon that could kill a man's nerve, and he came through it.","zh":"从场地那头就能听见鼓点。那是个满编的乐队，球员得跟着音乐动，不然这一轮就丢了。比赛前我弟弟心里发慌，他说两条腿又沉又死。他开始对着墙猛砸球热身，十分钟以后又能踢了。最后一分钟他们赢了，看台上的声浪像心跳一样。那种下午最能毁掉一个人的胆气，而他从里面走了出来。"},"bed":{"tw":[["bottom",0],["course",3],["plant",2],["room",6],["love",0],["lift",3],["supply",2],["bare",6],["bang",0]],"en":"The bed in my room stood under the window, and in summer I could see the bottom of the garden from it. Of course it was too small for me by the time I was fifteen, and my feet hung over the end. On the far side there was a bare wall where my mother had tried to plant a rose that never grew. She would lift the mattress every spring to air it, and she kept a small supply of clean sheets in a box underneath. In winter the wind would bang the shutter against the frame all night, and I would love it.","zh":"我屋里的床摆在窗下，夏天我能从床上看见园子的尽头。当然，到我十五岁它就太小了，脚都搭在床沿外。对面是一堵光墙，我妈曾在那儿试着种一棵玫瑰，没活。每年春天她都会把床垫抬起来晾一晾，床底下的箱子里存着一小摞干净床单。冬天风整夜把窗板拍在框上，我倒很喜欢。"},"bill":{"tw":[["card",0],["check",3],["advertise",2],["repeal",6],["charge",0],["menu",3],["list",2],["tax",6],["note",0]],"en":"The bill came to more than we had expected, and my father asked to see the menu again. He would check every item on the list, note the charge for the bread, and then take out his card. The owner had begun to advertise a new tax on the board outside, and my father said a good council would repeal it within the year. He paid without another word and left the note on the table. On the way home he told me that a bill is a promise written down, and that it should be read twice.","zh":"账单比我们预想的高，我爸要求再看一遍菜单。他把单子上的每一顶都核了一遍，记下面包收的那笔钱，然后掏出卡。店主已经在外面板子上开始宣传一项新税，我爸说，一个像样的议会一年之内就会把它废掉。他一句话没说就付了钱，纸条留在桌上。回家路上他跟我说，账单就是写下来的承诺，得读两遍。"},"blow":{"tw":[["snow",0],["box",3],["lay",2],["attempt",6],["waste",0],["burn",3],["move",2],["pull",6],["bump",0]],"en":"The wind began to blow hard in the night and the snow came with it. In the morning the whole lane was under a white cover, and my father had to pull on his boots and move the car out of the way. There was a bump in the road that nobody could see, and it took him three attempts to get past it. He would burn the old boxes in the yard rather than waste them, and then lay a plank over the gap so the milkman could get through.","zh":"夜里起大风，雪跟着来了。早上整条小路都盖在白色底下一层，我爸只好蹬上靴子把车挪开。路上有个谁都看不见的坎，他试了三回才过去。他宁可把旧木箱在院子里烧掉，也不肯白白扔了，然后铺一块板子盖住坑，好让送牛奶的能过。"},"bother":{"tw":[["pain",0],["harass",3],["affect",2],["guess",6],["trouble",0],["plague",3],["confuse",2],["hurry",6],["devil",0]],"en":"It did not bother my grandmother that the tap dripped all night; she said a small trouble was better than a silent house. The pain in her knee would affect her in the mornings, and she would have to hurry less than she wanted to. I guess she was lonely, though she would never say so. The neighbours began to harass her about the garden, and one of them, a real devil of a man, would plague her every week. It only seemed to confuse her that anyone should mind so much.","zh":"水龙头整夜滴水，我奶奶一点不烦；她说有点小麻烦总比静得没声的屋子好。早上膝盖的疼会影响她，她想赶也赶不起来。我猜她是孤单的，虽然她从不这么说。邻居开始为园子的事来烦她，其中有个真像恶鬼一样的男人，每个星期都来缠她。别人这么在意，反倒让她摸不着头脑。"},"bring":{"tw":[["add",0],["return",3],["change",2],["help",6],["land",3],["fetch",3],["attract",2],["need",6],["play",0]],"en":"Every Sunday my uncle would bring the boat back to the harbour and bring the nets with him. He would return the key to the office, add a line to the list on the wall, and then fetch his bicycle. The land around the harbour had begun to change, and the new houses would attract people who had no need of a boat at all. He said he would help anyone who asked, but he would not play along with the council. In the end he sold up and moved inland.","zh":"每个星期天，我叔都把船带回港里，顺便把网也带回来。他把钥匙还给办公室，在墙上那张单子上添一行，然后去取自行车。港口周围的地开始变了，新盖的房子会招来那些根本用不着船的人。他说谁开口求他他都帮，但他不陪着镇公所作戏。最后他把东西都卖了，搬到了内地。"},"build":{"tw":[["figure",0],["lock",3],["better",2],["construct",6],["form",0],["raise",3],["body",2],["develop",6],["shape",0]],"en":"They had to build the new shed before the winter, and there was little time. The figure on the plan was simple, but nobody could agree on the form it should take. They would raise the walls first, then lock the two halves together with a long bar. My father said they would have to develop the design as they went, and change its shape twice before it was right. In the end the body of the shed was stronger than the old house, and better built, too. He had watched men construct barns all his life, and he knew that a good frame is never hurried.","zh":"他们得在入冬前把新棚子盖起来，时间不多。图上的尺寸很简单，可谁也说不准该做成什么形状。他们先把墙立起来，再用一根长杆把两半锁在一起。我爸说设计得边干边改，形状换了两回才对。最后棚子的主体比那栋老房子还结实，活儿也干得更好。他这辈子看着人盖谷仓，知道好架子从来不是赶出来的。"},"burn":{"tw":[["cut",0],["flame",3],["feel",2],["smoke",6],["fire",0],["blaze",3],["pain",2],["tear",6],["bite",0]],"en":"The fire in the field began to burn along the dry grass and the smoke could be seen from the road. My uncle had to cut a strip of ground to stop it, and by the time he had finished he could feel the heat through his boots. A single flame had started the whole blaze. He had a bad burn on one hand, and the pain kept him awake. It made his eyes tear. He said it was nothing, but he could not hold a cup without biting his lip.","zh":"地里的火顺着干草烧起来，从路上就能看见烟。我叔得先割出一条空地把它拦住，等他割完，隔着靴子都能感觉到烫。整场大火是从一簇火苗起的。他一只手烧伤了，疼得整夜睡不着，眼睛都给熏出泪来。他说没事，可是端起杯子就忍不住咬嘴唇。"},"call":{"tw":[["address",2],["bet",3],["ask",2],["answer",6],["cry",0],["double",3],["guess",2],["talk",6],["promise",0]],"en":"My father had to make one call and then he would leave the office. He asked for the number, gave his address, and waited for an answer. Then he had a long talk with a man he had worked with for years, and they made a bet about which of them would retire first. He could not guess his own luck well enough to double the stake. As he put the phone down he heard a cry from the street. He had promised to be home by six, and it was already past six.","zh":"我爸打完一个电话就要下班了。他问了号码，报了自己的地址，等着对方接。接着他跟一个共事多年的男人聊了很久，两人还打赌看谁先退休。他摸不准自己的运气，不敢把赌注翻倍。放下电话时，他听见街上一声喊叫。他早就答应六点前到家，可已经过六点了。"},"can":{"tw":[["behind",0],["head",3],["room",2],["able",6],["bottom",0],["retire",3],["remove",2],["need",6],["fire",0]],"en":"The can of paint stood at the bottom of the shelf behind the door, and nobody in the room seemed able to reach it. My grandfather would need a ladder, or he would have to remove the boxes in front. He would not retire until he had done the job himself, and he was not going to ask anyone. He put his head round the corner, took a long breath, and lifted the can down. There is no need for a fire, he said. It is only paint. Then he carried it out to the yard.","zh":"那罐油漆放在门后架子的最下层，屋里好像谁也没本事够到它。我爷爷要么得找把梯子，要么得把前面的箱子挪开。活儿没自己干完他是不肯收手的，也不打算开口求人。他把头探过拐角，长吸一口气，把那罐子端了下来。他说：用不着生火，就是油漆而已。然后他把它拎到院子里去了。"},"care":{"tw":[["charge",0],["mother",3],["control",2],["benefit",6],["concern",0],["nurse",3],["help",2],["medical",6],["deal",0]],"en":"My mother gave up her job to take care of my grandmother, and she did it for six years. She would deal with the nurse every morning, and she knew more about the medical side of it than any of the doctors. She had to control her own worry, because my grandmother could read a face at once. Her only concern was that the old woman should not feel a burden. She said there was no charge for what she did, and no benefit she wanted out of it. I never heard her ask anyone for help.","zh":"我妈辞了工作去照顾我奶奶，一照顾就是六年。每天早上她跟护士打交道，对这病医药方面的事，比哪个大夫都清楚。她还得管住自己的担心，因为我奶奶一眼就能看出人脸上的心思。她唯一在意的是别让老太太觉得自己是个累赘。她说她做的事不要钱，也不图什么好处。我从没听她开口求过谁帮忙。"},"chance":{"tw":[["find",0],["room",3],["try",2],["opportunity",6],["happen",0],["say",3],["measure",2],["hope",6],["luck",0]],"en":"There was a chance that the shop would close, and I wanted to find out before it happened. I went in and asked, and the woman said she would try to keep it open for another year. The room at the back was full of old stock, and the opportunity to sell it was small. You have to measure your hope, she said, and then take the luck that comes. I did not know what to say. I bought a book and left, and I still go back when I can.","zh":"这家店有可能要关，我想在它关掉之前弄清楚。我进去问了，那位女士说她会尽量再撑一年。里屋堆满了旧货，能卖出去的机会不大。她说：希望得掂量着来，然后来了运气就接住。我不知道该说什么。我买了一本书就走了，到现在有机会还回去看看。"},"charge":{"tw":[["bill",0],["bother",3],["change",2],["discharge",1],["criminal",6],["care",0],["check",3],["cost",2],["excite",0]],"en":"The charge against the man was serious, and nobody in the village wanted to talk about it. He was said to have set fire to a shop over a bill he could not pay, though the whole cost was small. The police had to discharge the case for lack of proof, and the criminal court never saw it. The change in the town afterwards was strange: people who had not bothered to speak to him before began to care what happened. I was excited and ashamed at the same time. My father told me to check my own books first.","zh":"对那个人的指控不轻，村里谁都不愿提这事。据说他为一笔付不起的账放火烧了一家店，其实总共也没多少钱。因为证据不足，警方只好撤了案，刑事法庭根本没审。之后镇上的变化很怪：先前连话都懒得跟他说的人，忽然开始关心起他的下场。我既兴奋又羞愧。我爸叫我先把自己那本账查清楚。"},"check":{"tw":[["agree",0],["card",3],["bill",2],["notice",6],["break",0],["catch",3],["change",2],["collect",6],["chip",0]],"en":"Before we paid, my mother would check the bill twice and then check it again. She would agree to nothing until she had seen the card in the window with the prices on it. There was a small notice by the door, and she read it while I waited. If the figures did not change, she would collect her bag and walk out without a word. My brother said she had a chip of ice where other people keep their patience. I took it as a break from the heat, and I did not catch her eye.","zh":"付钱之前，我妈要把账单核对两遍，然后再核一遍。没看见窗户上那张写着价钱的牌子，她什么都不会答应。门边有一张小告示，我等着的时候她把它读完了。数目要是不改，她就收拾起包，一声不响走出去。我弟说她身上那块地方别人都长着耐心，她长的是一块冰。我只当这是热天里歇口气，没敢跟她对上眼。"},"chip":{"tw":[["bit",0],["scale",3],["cut",2],["computer",6],["check",0],["splinter",3],["shape",2],["micro",6],["crisp",0]],"en":"There was a chip in the glass, a small bit of it missing at the edge, and it had a strange shape. I had to check it against the scale on the wall before I could say how deep the cut went. My father said the whole thing would break if we left it, so he took a splinter of wood and worked at it. He had a computer in the back room, and he used it to look up the price. A micro part of the surface was all that mattered. He said a crisp new one would cost too much.","zh":"玻璃上崩了一块，边上缺了小小一角，形状还挺怪。我得对着墙上的标尺量一下，才说得清那道口子有多深。我爸说这么放着整块都会裂，于是他拿了一根木片慢慢修。里屋有台电脑，他用它查了价钱。要紧的就是表面上极小的那一块。他说换一块又新又脆的要花太多钱。"},"clear":{"tw":[["clean",0],["approve",3],["change",2],["bounce",1],["without",6],["light",0],["commission",3],["empty",2],["open",0]],"en":"The water in the tank was clear again, and you could see the bottom of it in the light from the door. The man from the water commission came to approve the change we had made, and he said the whole job was clean work. He had to bounce a stone off the wall to test how hard it was. The room was empty except for a chair. We cannot go on without a proper cover, he said. Leave the lid open when you are finished. I wrote it down and he signed the paper.","zh":"水箱里的水又清了，顺着门口透进来的光能看见箱底。自来水委员会的那个人来查看我们做的改动，说这活儿干得干净。他用一块石头在墙上弹了一下，试试墙有多硬。屋里除了一把椅子什么都没有。他说：没有个像样的盖子，这么下去不行。收工的时候把盖子敞着。我记了下来，他在纸上签了字。"},"colour":{"tw":[["distort",0],["blue",3],["change",2],["palette",6],["gloss",0],["green",3],["interest",2],["bright",6],["tinge",0]],"en":"The colour of the sea changes ten times in a day, and no painter can hold it. My aunt would put a blue and a green on her palette and then add a tinge of grey, and by the afternoon the whole canvas had gone wrong. A photograph can distort what you saw, she said, and a gloss will hide the rest. Her real interest was in the light, not in the paint. The bright hours on the water were the ones she wanted. I watched her work for a whole summer and still cannot say how she did it.","zh":"海的颜色一天能变十回，哪个画画的都抓不住。我姑姑会在调色板上挤一坨蓝、一坨绿，再添一丝灰，到下午整幅画就全不对了。她说：照片会把你看见的东西扭歪，再上一层亮油就把剩下的都盖住了。她真正上心的是光，不是颜料。水面上那几段亮堂堂的时辰才是她想要的。我看她画了一整个夏天，到现在也说不出她是怎么画的。"},"company":{"tw":[["party",0],["chorus",3],["unit",2],["firm",6],["society",0],["cohort",3],["complement",2],["subsidiary",6],["accompany",0]],"en":"My father worked for a small firm for most of his life, and he was happy there. The company had one unit in the north and a subsidiary in another town, and he would have to accompany the manager on the long drive between them. At the office party each winter the whole cohort would stand up and sing in a chorus, badly. He said there was no better society than people who work well together. When a new man joined, my father told him he was a useful complement to the team, and meant it.","zh":"我爸大半辈子在一家小事务所做事，在那儿过得挺开心。这家公司北边有一个部门，另一个镇上还有家子公司，他得陪着经理在两头之间开长途。每年冬天公司聚会上，他们那一拨人都会站起来合唱，唱得很难听。他说再没有比一起把活干好的人更好的群体了。来了新人的时候，我爸会跟他说他是队里缺的那一块，而且是真心这么说的。"},"complete":{"tw":[["finish",0],["close",3],["end",2],["full",6],["over",0],["top",3],["fill",2],["entire",6],["perfect",0]],"en":"The work on the house was complete by the middle of June, and the whole family came to see it. We had to finish the top floor last, and it took a week to fill the gaps and close every door properly. The entire roof was new, and over the gate my father had put a small stone with the date on it. He said the house was not perfect, but it was full of light and it was ours. At the end of the day we sat in the yard and watched the sun go down.","zh":"房子到六月中就完工了，全家人都来看。顶楼是最后收的尾，光补缝、把每扇门关严实就用了一个星期。整个屋顶都是新的，大门上方我爸嵌了块小石头，上面刻着日期。他说这房子算不上十全十美，可是光线足，而且是咱们自己的。那天傍晚我们坐在院子里看太阳落下去。"},"concern":{"tw":[["care",0],["involve",3],["anxiety",2],["impact",6],["fear",0],["matter",3],["enterprise",2],["strong",6],["interest",2]],"en":"My uncle's only concern was that the enterprise should outlive him. He had built it from nothing, and he would involve himself in every small matter, from the price of wood to the colour of the sign. His anxiety before each winter was strong, and I came to share his fear of a bad season. He used to say that the impact of one bad year can undo ten good ones. He did not care much for money, but he cared a great deal about the interest of the people who worked for him.","zh":"我叔唯一放心不下的是这份事业得比他活得久。他是从一无所有把它做起来的，事无大小都要自己插手，从木料的价钱到招牌的颜色。每年入冬前他都格外焦虑，我也跟着他一起怕遇上坏年景。他生前常说，一个坏年头的折腾能把十个好年头搭进去。他对钱不怎么在意，可对跟着他干活那些人的利害，他上心得很。"},"control":{"tw":[["check",0],["card",3],["power",2],["system",6],["hold",0],["catch",3],["test",2],["force",6],["insure",0]],"en":"The control room was small and hot, and there was a card on the wall with the names of everyone who had ever worked there. You had to check the board every hour, and if a light went red you had to catch it at once. The whole system depended on one man keeping his hold on himself. The power came from two old wheels in the river below. A sudden force of water could test the best of them. They would insure the building against fire, but nothing could insure a man against his own temper. My father learned that in his first year and never forgot it.","zh":"控制室又小又热，墙上钉着一张卡片，写着所有在这儿干过活的人的名字。你得每小时查一次仪表盘，哪个灯变红了就得马上发现。整套系统全靠一个人把自己稳住。电从下面河里的两只旧水轮来。水势猛地一冲，最能干的人也经不住考。他们会给这楼保火险，可谁也没法给一个人的脾气保险。我爸头一年就懂了这一点，一辈子没忘。"},"cook":{"tw":[["fix",0],["brown",3],["change",2],["curry",6],["prepare",0],["dress",3],["cheat",2],["lamb",6],["ready",0]],"en":"My mother could cook anything, even a curry that my father said was the best he had ever eaten. She would prepare the lamb the night before, dress it with salt and herbs, and let it stand. In the morning she would brown it in a heavy pan and then change the heat. I used to fix the table while she worked, and I was never ready when she called. She said a cook who cheats with the timing will always be caught by the taste. Once a week she would let me stir the pot and tell me what to look for.","zh":"我妈什么都会做，有一道咖喱我爸说他一辈子没吃过更好的。她会头天晚上就把羊肉备好，撒上盐和香料，放着入味。第二天早上用厚锅把肉煎上色，再调火。她做饭的时候我就摆桌子，可每次她喊我，我都还没弄完。她说做菜的人在火候上偷懒，味道一定会把他揪出来。每个星期她会让我搅一次锅，告诉我该看什么。"},"course":{"tw":[["class",0],["round",3],["hunt",2],["long",6],["feed",0],["waste",3],["move",2],["beyond",6],["form",0]],"en":"I took a long course in woodwork one winter, and it was the best thing I ever did. There were twelve of us in the class, and the teacher would move from bench to bench and feed us advice in small amounts. In the first round he had us form a simple joint, and half of us made a waste of good timber. Beyond the window there was a field where he liked to hunt for old wood after a storm. It was the only course I ever finished. I still have the box I made in it, and the lid does not fit.","zh":"有一年冬天我上了一门很长的木工课，那是我做过最值的一件事。班上有十二个人，老师一个工作台一个工作台地走，一点一点给我们喂经验。头一轮他让我们做一个简单的榫接，我们一半人把好木料糟蹋了。窗外有块地，他一刮完风就爱去那儿捡旧木头。这是我唯一读完的一门课。我做的那只盒子还在，盖子合不上。"},"court":{"tw":[["romance",0],["chase",3],["act",2],["judge",6],["tribunal",0],["display",3],["room",2],["supreme",6],["courtyard",0]],"en":"The court sat in a small room at the back of the building, with a courtyard where the cars were parked. The judge came in, and everyone had to stand. It was not a supreme tribunal; it was a local matter about a fence. The two families had been in a long romance with the law, and each of them would display every paper they had ever signed. The younger son would chase the older one round the yard before the hearing began. It was hard to believe that any of it was meant to act as justice.","zh":"法庭设在楼后一间小屋里，外头是个停车的院子。法官进来，所有人都得站起来。这不是什么最高法院，只是为一堵篱笆闹的本地小事。这两家人跟法律纠缠了好些年，各自都愿意把签过的每一张纸摊出来。正式开庭前，小儿子还绕着院子追大儿子。很难相信这中间有哪一样是为了主持公道。"},"cover":{"tw":[["address",0],["coat",3],["dress",2],["short",6],["back",0],["course",3],["fire",2],["full",6],["continue",0]],"en":"The cover of the old book had come away at the back, and the address of a bookshop was written inside it in pencil. My mother would dress the torn corner with a piece of cloth, and then put a coat of thin glue along the spine. It took a short time to do, but it had to be done again every year. Of course she could not continue like that for ever. One winter evening, when the fire was full and the house was warm, she read the whole book aloud to me instead.","zh":"那本旧书的封面在书脊那边脱开了，里面用铅笔写着一家书店的地址。我妈会用一块布把撕破的角贴好，再沿着书脊抹一层薄胶。这花不了多少工夫，可每年都得再来一遍。她当然不能一直这样下去。有一个冬天的晚上，炉火正旺、屋里正暖，她索性把整本书念给我听了。"},"cross":{"tw":[["cover",2],["course",3],["meet",2],["along",6],["mark",0],["drive",3],["pass",2],["through",6],["track",0]],"en":"There is a stone cross at the place where two tracks meet, and you have to drive past it to reach the farm. We would walk along the field edge and then cross the stream at the old course. My father would mark the spot with a stick so we could find it again in the dark. As we came through the gate the rain began, and he put a cover over his head. It was a long pass of bad weather, and we were glad to see the light of the house.","zh":"两条小路交汇的地方立着一座石十字，开车去农场得从它旁边过。我们会沿着田边走过去，再从老河道那儿蹚过溪。我爸用一根树枝在那儿做个记号，好让我们黑天也能再找到。我们穿进大门的时候下起了雨，他把一块布顶在头上。这一阵坏天气拖得很久，远远看见屋里的灯，我们都松了口气。"},"cut":{"tw":[["burn",0],["check",3],["change",2],["drop",6],["issue",0],["kill",3],["free",2],["over",6],["track",0]],"en":"The cut on my hand was small but deep, and it would not stop bleeding. My mother had to check it twice, then change the cloth and hold it down hard. She said the cold could kill the feeling in my fingers, so she kept the fire going all night and would not let it burn out. In the morning the doctor had to cut the thread and set me free. No sport for a week, he said, and dropped the needle in the tray. I went back to the track the next day anyway, over the field behind the house. The issue never came up again.","zh":"我手上那道口子不大，可很深，血止不住。我妈核了两遍，换过布，又使劲按住。她说受凉会让手指头没了知觉，所以整夜守着炉子，不让火灭下去。早上去拆线，医生把线剪开，我就自由了。他说：一个星期不许运动，顺手把针丢进盘子里。第二天我照旧上了那条跑道，从屋后的田里绕过去。这事后来再没人提起。"},"deal":{"tw":[["address",0],["market",3],["act",2],["bid",6],["care",0],["meet",3],["board",2],["plan",6],["cover",0]],"en":"The deal was made in the market on a Saturday, with no paper and no witness. My father would meet the man at the board by the gate, shake hands, and then act as if nothing had happened. He had to bid low at first, because he did not care to look eager. His plan was always the same: wait until the other man was tired, then cover the last offer and walk away. I once asked him for the address of the buyer, and he said he had never needed one.","zh":"这桩买卖是星期六在集市上谈成的，没有纸，也没有证人。我爸会在门边那块木板旁跟人碰头，握个手，然后装作什么都没发生。开头他得压低价，因为他不乐意显出着急的样子。他那套打算从来不变：等对方累了，再把最后那个价码补上，然后走人。有一回我问他买主的地址，他说他从来用不着。"},"dig":{"tw":[["labour",0],["drive",3],["touch",2],["hole",6],["grasp",0],["figure",3],["understand",2],["mud",6],["excavate",0]],"en":"We had to dig a hole for the new tree, and the ground was hard as stone. My grandfather did the labour himself, though he could hardly grasp the handle by the end. He would drive the spade down with his foot, touch the mud at the bottom to see how wet it was, and then go on. He said I should figure out where the roots would go before I started. It took me years to understand what he meant. When they came to excavate the old bed years later, the tree was still standing.","zh":"我们得给新树挖个坑，那土硬得像石头。活是我爷爷自己干的，到后来他几乎握不住锹把。他用脚把铲子蹬下去，摸摸坑底的泥看湿不湿，然后接着挖。他说动手之前我该先琢磨清楚根会往哪儿伸。等我明白他的意思，已经过去好几年了。多年后有人来挖那口旧花坛时，那棵树还站着。"},"dirty":{"tw":[["soil",0],["pollute",3],["change",2],["clean",1],["stuff",6],["foul",3],["splash",3],["trash",6],["grime",0]],"en":"The dog came in dirty from the yard, and there was grime on every step he crossed. He had rolled in something foul and then splashed through the puddle by the gate. My father had to change the cloth on the floor and take the whole thing out to the trash. He said the soil near the road had been polluted for years, and that nothing but weeds would grow there. Do not let him bring that stuff inside, my mother said. I had to give him a bath before he could come in. He was a different animal once he was clean, and he knew it.","zh":"狗从院子里进来，脏得不行，它踏过的每一级台阶上都留下污印。它先在一摊臭东西上滚过，又从门边的水坑里扑腾过来。我爸只好换掉地上的布，把脏东西全都扔到垃圾堆去。他说路边那块土被污染好些年了，除了野草什么都长不出来。我妈说：别让它把那些玩意儿带进屋。我只好先给它洗个澡才让它进来。干净以后它就成了另一只狗，它自己也知道。"},"discover":{"tw":[["break",0],["blow",3],["tell",2],["how",6],["find",2],["see",3],["spy",2],["locate",6],["hear",0]],"en":"I had to discover where the noise was coming from, and I did not know how to start. I could hear it in every room but could not locate it. Then the wind gave a great blow and the door began to break loose in its frame. I went out to see what it was, and I had to tell my mother at once. There was a small pipe under the step, and when I put my hand on it I could find the leak. My neighbour had once worked as a spy, and he said he would have taken half an hour to do the same.","zh":"我得弄清楚这声音是从哪儿来的，可我不知道该从哪儿下手。每个屋里都听得见，就是找不着它在哪。后来一阵大风刮过，那扇门在框子里松开了。我出去看是怎么回事，得马上告诉我妈。台阶底下有根细管子，我手一放上去就摸到了漏的地方。我邻居从前干过谍报，他说同样的事他得花半小时。"},"dog":{"tw":[["tail",0],["tree",3],["catch",2],["cat",6],["track",0],["quest",3],["support",2],["horse",6],["chase",0]],"en":"The old dog could not chase anything now, but he still liked to follow a track along the field. He would put his nose down at the tree by the gate and go on for an hour. Once he caught a cat in the yard and never heard the end of it. He had been a support to my father in the years when there was little else. My grandfather kept a horse in those days, and the two animals were a strange pair, with the dog wagging his tail at the stable door. His last quest was for a bone he had buried himself.","zh":"那条老狗现在什么也追不上了，可它还是喜欢顺着田边跟一条踪迹走。它会在大门旁那棵树底下把鼻子贴到地上，一跟就是一个钟头。有一回它在院子里逮住了一只猫，从此这事被念叨个没完。在那些什么都没有的年头，它是我爸的一个依靠。我爷爷那时候养着一匹马，这两只牲口是奇怪的一对儿，狗总在棚门口摇着尾巴。它最后一次找东西，是找自己埋起来的一根骨头。"},"drink":{"tw":[["swallow",0],["carry",3],["use",2],["beer",6],["toast",0],["milk",3],["consume",2],["juice",6],["pledge",0]],"en":"After the long walk the old man stopped at the well and had a drink of cold water. He would not swallow it fast, though the day was hot and his shirt was wet. He had carried a small tin cup for years, and he used it now, the way his father had. On the table by the door stood a bottle of beer, a glass of milk and some juice for the children, because young bodies consume more than his does. At dinner his son raised a toast to him and said a few quiet words. Then they all made a pledge to walk that road again next spring.","zh":"走了大半天的路，老人在井边停下，喝了一大口凉水。天热，衬衫都湿透了，可他喝得并不急。那只小铁杯他带了很多年，这回还是用它，跟他父亲当年一样。门边的桌上摆着一瓶啤酒、一杯牛奶，还有给孩子们准备的果汁，年轻人的身子总比他耗得多。晚饭时儿子向他举杯，说了几句轻的话。然后一家人立了个约：明年春天再走那条路。"},"drop":{"tw":[["fall",0],["blow",3],["change",2],["rise",6],["miss",0],["forget",3],["drug",2],["price",6],["spend",0]],"en":"When the price of the drug dropped at the chemist on the corner, the whole street felt the change. The old woman did not want to miss it. She had to spend most of her money on it every month, and she could not forget the winter when the cost began to rise. A cold wind began to blow along the pavement, and a leaf started to fall past the window. She watched one single drop of rain slide down the glass and stop. In her hand the small box was light, almost nothing. She put it in her bag and walked home slowly.","zh":"街角药铺里那种药一降价，整条街都感觉到了变化。老太太不想错过。她每个月都得把大部分钱花在这上面，也忘不了药价开始往上涨的那个冬天。冷风沿着人行道吹，一片黄叶开始从窗前落下。她看着一滴雨顺着玻璃往下滑，停住了。手里那只小盒子轻得几乎没分量。她把它放进包里，慢慢走回家。"},"end":{"tw":[["close",3],["break",3],["change",2],["begin",1],["next",6],["death",3],["complete",3],["start",6],["finish",0]],"en":"On his last day at the mill my father stayed until the end of the night shift. There was no break, and no one asked for one. He had begun there at eighteen and finished at sixty-two, and in all those years the only real change was the new machines. At close of day the manager shook his hand. Then, at the start of the next week, he found that work was not everything. The death of a friend that autumn had taught him that. Something was complete, and another thing was just beginning. He walked home slowly in the dark, past the empty yard and the locked gate.","zh":"父亲在厂里的最后一天，一直干到夜班结束。中间没歇，也没人提。他十八岁进厂，六十二岁收工，这么多年里唯一真正变了的就是那些新机器。收工时经理跟他握了手。到了下一个星期开头，他才发现干活并不是一切。那年秋天一个朋友的去世让他明白了这个道理。一件事算完了，另一件事才刚刚开始。他摸着黑慢慢走回家，路过空荡荡的院子和锁着的大门。"},"excuse":{"tw":[["pardon",0],["plead",3],["note",2],["mistake",6],["apology",0],["alibi",3],["forgive",2],["wrong",6],["justify",0]],"en":"The boy stood at the door with a note in his hand and asked the teacher to pardon him for being late. It was a mistake, he said, and he began to plead his case. His excuse was that the bus had broken down. He even had an alibi: two friends who had waited with him. She read the note twice and put it down. There was no apology for the noise he had made the day before. She said she would forgive him this time, but that he could not justify the same thing twice. Nothing was wrong with the story, only with him.","zh":"男孩站在门口，手里捏着一张条子，请老师原谅他迟到。他说是自己的错，接着就开始辩。他找的理由是公交车坏在了半路。他甚至还有人为他作证：两个跟他一起等的同学。老师把条子读了两遍，放在桌上。他对自己前一天闹出的那阵动静，一句道歉也没有。她说这回可以原谅他，但同样的事没有第二遍的道理。故事本身没毛病，毛病在他身上。"},"experience":{"tw":[["feel",3],["burn",3],["change",2],["physical",6],["live",0],["die",3],["content",2],["good",6],["see",0]],"en":"My grandmother used to say that a long life is only a long experience. She had lived through a war, lost a brother, and seen a whole street fall down and change. In her last years the work in the garden was too physical for her, but she would not stop. She liked to feel the sun on her back. She had one burn on her arm from a hot pan, and she showed it to me as if it were a medal. She was content with small things. A year later she died, and I still think of her. She was good at that, at being happy.","zh":"奶奶常说，活得久不过就是一段长的经历。她经过一场战争，失去过一个兄弟，也亲眼见过整条街塌掉、变了样。最后那几年，园子里的活对她身子来说太重了，可她不肯停。她喜欢太阳晒在背上的感觉。她胳膊上有一块被热锅烫的伤，拿给我看的时候像在展示一枚奖章。小事就能让她满足。一年后她走了，我到现在还常想起她。她这个人，很会高兴。"},"family":{"tw":[["class",0],["couple",3],["unit",2],["father",6],["home",0],["sex",3],["relative",2],["mother",6],["house",3]],"en":"Ours was a family of six in a house too small for a class of that size. My father worked nights, my mother kept the accounts, and a couple of relatives lived with us for two winters. When the school sent a form home, it asked for the name, the age and the sex of each child, and my mother filled it in without a word. She said a family is not a unit of the state; it is only people who stay. I did not understand her then. Now that both of them are gone, I do. She wrote our surname slowly, in her careful hand.","zh":"我们家六口人，挤在一栋小得装不下这样一个班的房子里。父亲上夜班，母亲管账，有两三个亲戚跟我们一起住过两个冬天。学校把表格发到家里，上面要填每个孩子的姓名、年龄和性别，母亲一句话没说就填了。她说家不是国家的一个单位，只是几个肯留下来的人。那时我不懂她这话。如今他们两个都不在了，我懂了。她一笔一笔慢慢写下我们的姓，字写得很仔细。"},"farm":{"tw":[["grow",0],["carry",3],["collect",2],["mill",6],["raise",0],["ranch",3],["work",2],["plant",6],["produce",0]],"en":"My uncle runs a small farm near the old mill. In spring he has to plant and to grow enough food for the winter, and in autumn he will collect what the fields produce. He raises a few cows and, on the other side of the road, his brother has a ranch where they raise horses. Every morning he must carry water out to the animals before the work begins. He says a farm is not land. It is a habit. He has never wanted anything else, and he has never once been away from it. The house smells of wood smoke and old bread all year.","zh":"我叔在老磨坊旁边经营一小块农场。春天他得下种，种出够一冬吃的粮食；秋天他要收地里长出来的东西。他养了几头奶牛，路另一头他兄弟有个牧场，养马。每天早上开工之前，他得先把水挑出去喂牲口。他说农场不是一块地，是一种习惯。他从没想过要别的，也从没离开过这里一天。那屋子一年到头都是柴火和旧面包的味道。"},"fear":{"tw":[["care",0],["scare",3],["worry",2],["anger",6],["concern",0],["alarm",3],["respect",2],["blame",6],["awe",0]],"en":"Nobody in the village felt fear of the old shepherd, only a kind of awe. He carried a stick and a dog, and he did not care what people said about him. When a dog began to scare the sheep, he would stand still, and the animal would stop. His only concern was the weather. He used to say that worry is a tax you pay before the bill comes. Once I saw anger in his face, when a boy threw a stone. He did not blame the child. He just raised his arm, and there was alarm in every eye on the road. But no one ever lost respect for him.","zh":"村里没人怕那个老牧羊人，只有一种敬畏。他拿着一根棍子，带着一条狗，别人怎么说他都不在乎。有条狗开始吓羊的时候，他就站住不动，那畜生也就停下了。他唯一在意的是天气。他常说，担心是在账还没来之前就先交的税。有一次我看见他脸上有了怒气，是有个孩子扔石头。他没有怪那孩子，只是抬了抬胳膊，路上每一双眼睛里都是惊慌。可是谁也没有失掉对他的敬重。"},"fellow":{"tw":[["associate",2],["date",3],["friend",2],["young",6],["familiar",0],["dog",3],["man",2],["veteran",6],["mate",0]],"en":"The fellow who kept the shop was an old veteran with a bad leg. He was familiar with every man on the street and every dog in it. A young friend of mine used to sit at his counter for hours. They were mates, in a way, though one was eighty and the other sixteen. His only associate in business was a cousin who came on the same date each month to bring the money. I never heard him call anyone by a title. He called them all by name, and that was enough. He died the winter after I left, and the shop closed with him.","zh":"开那家小店的伙计是个腿有旧伤的退伍老兵。街上每个人、每条狗他都认得。我有个年轻朋友，常在他柜台边一坐几个钟头。他们算是哥们儿，尽管一个八十，一个十六。他生意上唯一的合伙人是位表亲，每月同一天来送钱。我从没听他用头衔叫过谁，都是直呼其名，这就够了。我走后的那个冬天他走了，小店也跟着关了。"},"field":{"tw":[["study",0],["court",3],["answer",2],["team",6],["subject",0],["flat",3],["choose",2],["run",6],["discipline",0]],"en":"The field where we played was flat and bare, with a court drawn on the ground in white chalk. Our team had to choose a captain before the match, and nobody could answer at first. The study of the game was my uncle's whole subject; he had a discipline about it that we never had. He would run up and down the side with us until it was dark. I remember the field more clearly than the games. I can still see the grass, the lines, and the long shadow of the goal. It is a car park for the new office now.","zh":"我们踢球的那块场地又平又空，地上用白粉画出一个球场。比赛前我们队得选一个队长，起初谁也说不出话来。对这门球艺的研究是我叔的全部功课，他在这上头有种我们从来没有的严格。他会跟我们一起沿着边线跑上跑下，跑到天黑。那块场地我记得比比赛还清楚。我到现在还能看见那片草、那些线，还有球门拉出的长影子。如今那儿是新办公楼的一个停车场。"},"fight":{"tw":[["press",0],["box",3],["advertise",2],["bring",6],["push",0],["settle",3],["try",2],["face",6],["battle",0]],"en":"There was a fight behind the pub on Saturday night, and it took two men to settle it. One of them boxed badly; he kept his face open and took a blow on the nose. The other would only push, never strike. The owner of the shop next door came out to bring them apart. He did not advertise it, but he had been a soldier, and he had seen a real battle once. He did not press charges. He just told them to try again in the morning, when they were sober, and they did. Nobody was hurt enough to call a doctor.","zh":"星期六晚上酒馆后面有人打架，两个人才能拉开。其中一个拳法很糟，脸敞着，鼻子上挨了一下。另一个只是推，从不出拳。隔壁铺子的老板出来把他们分开。这事他不张扬，可他当过兵，真见过一回战场。他没有去告谁。他只叫他们等早上酒醒了再试一次，他们真就照办了。谁也没伤到要请大夫。"},"film":{"tw":[["movie",0],["roll",3],["record",2],["documentary",6],["picture",0],["object",2],["feature",3],["comic",6],["shoot",0]],"en":"My father had one roll of film from the year I was born, and he would shoot a picture of the same street every spring. He kept every object in the house in its place, and every record on the shelf in order. He loved a good movie, but he never liked a comic one. There was a short documentary about the old market that used his film, and it was the only feature my mother ever watched twice. He said a photograph is not a memory. It is only proof that you were there. I have the camera still, and no film for it.","zh":"父亲有从我出生那年留下的一卷胶卷，每年春天他都去拍一张同一条街。屋里每样东西他都摆在自己该在的位置，架子上的每张唱片也按次序放好。他喜欢好电影，可从来不爱看滑稽的。有一部讲老市场的短片用了他的胶片，那是母亲唯一看过两遍的片子。他说，照片不是记忆，它只证明你当时在那儿。那台相机我还留着，只是没胶卷了。"},"first":{"tw":[["low",0],["former",3],["position",2],["last",1],["early",6],["start",0],["threshold",3],["gear",2],["offset",0]],"en":"At the start of the race my brother was in the first position, and he held it for the whole first lap. Then his gear slipped and he dropped to the low side of the pack. The former winner, who had started early, was behind him now. He crossed the threshold of the last corner and did not look back. That small offset in the time was enough. He came in second, and he was happier than he had been the year he won. He had trained on that hill all winter, alone, before anyone else was up. After the race he sat on the kerb and drank water slowly.","zh":"比赛一开始，我哥就排在第一位，第一圈一直守着。后来变速器一打滑，他掉到了队伍靠后的位置。那个早出发的前冠军这会儿在他后头。他冲过最后一个弯角前的界线，没有回头。时间上那一点小小的偏差就够了。他跑了个第二，比当年拿第一那年还高兴。整个冬天他一个人在那道坡上练，天没亮就起来。赛后他坐在路沿上，慢慢喝水。"},"fit":{"tw":[["agree",0],["hang",3],["shape",2],["better",6],["check",0],["look",3],["adapt",2],["sure",6],["meet",2]],"en":"The coat did not fit my sister, though she liked its shape and cut. In the shop she had to check it three times before she would agree. The woman there kept a mirror hanging behind the door, and my sister would look at herself and then look again. She was not sure about the length. In the end, she asked them to adapt it a little, a better plan than sending it back. She had to meet the tailor the next week. She said a thing can be made right, and that was why she never returned anything. The tailor only laughed at that.","zh":"那件外套我姐穿着不合身，尽管她喜欢那版型和剪裁。在店里她得来回看三遍才肯点头。那女的在门后挂了面镜子，我姐照了又照。她拿不准长短。最后她请他们改一改——这比退回去强。她得下星期去见裁缝。她说，东西是可以改好的，就为这个她从来不退货。裁缝听了只是笑。"},"floor":{"tw":[["base",0],["startle",3],["beat",2],["room",6],["deck",0],["loft",3],["control",2],["window",6],["dump",0]],"en":"The floor of the old room was bare wood, and the base of every wall was dark with age. A loud knock at the window startled me, and my heart began to beat fast. Up in the loft above, my brother was moving boxes, and his boots shook the deck of boards over my head. He had no control over his temper in those days. He would dump everything on the floor and leave it there. I stood at the door and said nothing. Twenty years later I bought that house, and I put in a new floor. It is a plain floor, and I like it.","zh":"那间老屋的地板是没上漆的木头，每面墙的墙根都黑得发旧。窗户上一声重响把我吓了一跳，心开始猛跳。楼上阁楼里，我哥在搬箱子，靴子踩得头顶那层板子直响。那些年他管不住自己的脾气，什么都往地上一扔就不管了。我站在门口一句话没说。二十年后我把那栋房子买了下来，换了新地板。地板很素净，我喜欢。"},"fly":{"tw":[["wing",0],["break",3],["change",2],["sail",6],["flee",0],["escape",3],["hit",2],["cruise",6],["pilot",0]],"en":"The fly came in through the open window and could not find its way out again. It would hit the glass and then change direction, and its wing made a small dry sound. My father, who had been a pilot, watched it for a while from his chair. He said that a bird can sail on the wind, and a man can cruise over a whole country, but a small thing like this can only flee or break. Then he opened the door wide and let it escape. He never killed anything in the house, not even a fly. That was one of the last things he taught me.","zh":"那只苍蝇从开着的窗户飞进来，怎么也找不着出去的路。它撞一下玻璃，换个方向再撞，翅膀发出很轻的干响。当过飞行员的父亲在椅子上看了一会儿。他说，鸟能借风滑行，人能驾机飞过一整个国家，可这么小的东西只能逃，或者撞断。然后他把门大敞开，放它出去了。屋里他从没弄死过什么，连一只苍蝇也没有。那是他教我的最后几件事之一。"},"force":{"tw":[["draw",0],["moment",3],["act",2],["military",6],["drive",3],["nose",3],["cause",2],["command",6],["power",0]],"en":"The force of the wind that night was enough to move a truck. It began to draw the door open, and for a moment nobody could close it. My neighbour, an old military man, took command at once. He told us to act and not to talk, and we pushed back with all our power. The wind had the drive of a train and hit the house nose first, like something alive. It was the cause of the flood two days later. I have never since felt so small in front of weather. The roof came off in one piece.","zh":"那一夜风的力道足以推动一辆卡车。它开始把门往外抽，有一阵子谁也关不上。我邻居是个老兵，他立刻接了手。他叫我们动手别说话，我们使出全副气力往回顶。那风像火车一样有劲，正对着房子撞上来，像是活的。两天后那场洪水就是它引起的。从那以后，我在天气面前再没觉得自己这么小过。屋顶整块被掀了下来。"},"game":{"tw":[["back",0],["catch",3],["bet",2],["season",6],["halt",0],["rabbit",3],["play",2],["match",6],["plot",0]],"en":"Every season the men in the village play the same game in the back room of the pub. One of them will bet on the first card and then lose it. My uncle had a plot of land behind his house where he once kept a rabbit hut. When the game came to a halt at midnight, they would stop the match and walk out slowly. Somebody would always catch the last bus. I used to sit under the table as a boy and watch their faces. In winter the room was cold and the window ran with water.","zh":"每年这个季节，村里的男人都在酒馆后屋玩同一种牌。总有人第一张牌就下注，然后输掉。我叔家后面有一小块地，以前搭过一个养兔子的棚。半夜牌局一停，他们就收了这一场，慢慢往外走。总有人赶得上末班车。小时候我常坐在桌子底下，看他们脸上的神情。冬天那屋子冷，玻璃上全是水。"},"get":{"tw":[["arrive",0],["break",3],["change",2],["sure",6],["beat",0],["buy",3],["experience",2],["want",6],["begin",0]],"en":"You could not get a seat on the early bus unless you arrived before seven. That was the first thing I learned, before I had any experience of the city at all. I had to buy a monthly ticket and be sure to keep it dry. On the day the engine began to break down, the driver would beat the panel with his hand, and nothing would change. I did not want to be late, so I walked. I got there in fifty minutes. After that I never took the bus again. The walk was long, and I liked it.","zh":"早班车你要是七点前不到，就抢不上座。这是我头一条学会的事，那时我对这座城市还毫无经验。我得买月票，还得保证别把它弄湿。发动机开始出毛病的那天，司机会用手砸仪表板，什么也不会变。我不想迟到，就走路。五十分钟到。从那以后我再没坐过那趟车。路很长，我却喜欢。"},"give":{"tw":[["afford",0],["allow",3],["accept",2],["need",6],["break",3],["deal",3],["change",2],["want",6],["feed",0]],"en":"My mother would give away anything she could not afford to keep. She would never allow a thing to sit unused in the house. If a neighbour needed a coat, she would accept nothing for it. Then, at the end of the deal, she would want to feed them before they left. She had a break in her voice when she spoke about the war, and a change would come over her face. There was nothing I could give her back. That is the part I still cannot manage. She died in March, in a small room full of white flowers.","zh":"我妈手里留不住东西，凡是养不起的，她都送人。她从不让一样东西在屋里搁着不用。邻居要是缺件外套，她什么也不收。事情办到最后，她还想留人家吃顿饭再走。提起那场战争，她声音里会有一下停顿，脸上也会起变化。我没什么能还给她。这一点我到现在也做不好。她三月里走的，在一间摆满白花的小屋里。"},"go":{"tw":[["break",3],["blow",3],["act",2],["want",6],["die",0],["check",3],["change",2],["sure",6],["fit",0]],"en":"The old pump had to go on working through the summer, or the whole garden would die. My father would check it every evening and be sure the belt was tight. He did not want to act too soon or too late, and he would not change a part that still fit. Then one night the handle began to break, and with a single blow the thing stopped. Water went everywhere. He stood there in the wet grass and laughed, which was not like him at all. A new pump came a week later. I remember the sound it made when it stopped.","zh":"那台老水泵得整个夏天一直转，不然满园子的东西都得死。父亲每天傍晚都去查看，确认皮带是紧的。他不肯动得太早或太晚，也不肯换掉还合用的零件。后来有天夜里，把手开始裂，就那么一下，机器停了。水淌了一地。他站在湿草里笑了，那一点也不像他。一星期后新泵来了。它停住时那声响我还记得。"},"grow":{"tw":[["farm",0],["carry",3],["change",2],["mature",6],["raise",0],["cut",3],["increase",2],["shrink",6],["rise",0]],"en":"On the farm my grandfather would grow the same three crops for fifty years, and he did not change them once. He had to carry the water himself until the pipes came. He would raise the young plants in boxes and cut the old trees back each spring. When the price of grain began to rise, his small plot seemed to increase in value, though his own share did not. He watched the fruit mature and then watched it shrink in the dry weeks. Carry, he said, and wait. That is what it is. I did not understand him then. I do now.","zh":"在农场，我爷爷五十年就种那三样庄稼，一次也没换过。水管接来之前，他得自己挑水。每年春天他把幼苗养在箱子里，把老树剪一剪。粮价开始往上涨的时候，他那一小块地看着是值钱了，可分到他手里的那份没变。他眼看着果子熟起来，又眼看着它们在干燥的几周里缩下去。他说：就挑着，等着，事情就是这样。那时我不懂他。现在我懂了。"},"handle":{"tw":[["address",0],["field",3],["control",2],["need",6],["care",0],["nurse",3],["touch",2],["without",6],["cover",0]],"en":"The handle of the ward door was worn smooth by years of hands. A nurse came out and asked for the address of the family, and I gave the one in the field beyond the river. My mother needed care at night, and someone had to touch her hand now and then so she would not feel alone. She could not control her own voice any more. There was a cover over the window, and without it the room was too bright. I stood there and did not know where to put myself. The handle was the last thing I touched.","zh":"病房门上的把手被无数只手磨得发亮。一位护士出来问家属的地址，我报的是河那边地里的那一处。母亲夜里需要人照料，得有人时不时碰一下她的手，让她不觉得孤单。她已经控制不住自己的声音了。窗户上有块遮布，没有它屋里太亮。我站在那儿，不知道把手往哪儿放。我最后碰到的是那个把手。"},"hang":{"tw":[["fall",0],["suspend",3],["drop",2],["shed",6],["dangle",3],["fit",2],["composite",6],["flow",0],["attend",0]],"en":"A lamp used to hang from the beam in my father's shed, and it would dangle a little whenever the wind came through. In autumn the leaves would fall, and one long thread of spider silk would suspend a single drop of rain above the door. He had a composite picture on the wall there, made of a hundred small photographs, and it did not fit the room at all. I had to attend to it when the glass broke. Water would flow down the inside of the wall after rain. He never fixed any of it. The shed came down with the house.","zh":"父亲棚子里从前梁上挂着一盏灯，风一吹进来它就轻轻晃。秋天叶子会落，一根长长的蛛丝会把一滴雨悬在门上头。那面墙上有一张拼起来的画，是一百张小照片拼的，跟那间屋子一点也不配。玻璃碎了的时候，得我去照应。下雨后水会顺着墙里侧往下流。这些他一样也没修过。棚子后来跟着那房子一起拆了。"},"hear":{"tw":[["discover",3],["catch",3],["concentrate",2],["tell",6],["listen",0],["incline",3],["probe",2],["answer",6],["see",0]],"en":"From my room I could hear the river, and if I held still I could catch the sound of a boat far off. I had to concentrate to tell one from the other. In the mornings I would listen for my father's step on the stairs, and I would incline my head towards the door. He never liked to be asked a direct question; he would probe the matter from the side and then not answer at all. I did not discover until much later that he had been ill that whole winter. Now I see the house in my sleep, and I still hear things in it.","zh":"从我屋里能听见那条河，要是屏住不动，还能听出远处一条船的声音。得集中注意力才分得清哪个是哪个。早上我会听着父亲的脚步声上楼，把头往门那边偏一偏。他不喜欢被直接问，总是从侧面探一探，然后干脆不回答。很久以后我才发现，那一整个冬天他都在生病。如今我在梦里还能看见那栋房子，还能听见里面的动静。"},"help":{"tw":[["serve",2],["care",3],["better",2],["bring",6],["service",0],["comfort",3],["support",2],["need",6],["aid",0]],"en":"When my aunt could no longer care for herself, the family had to choose between a private nurse and the public service. The clinic would serve her at home, and a young woman came twice a day to help. She would bring hot food and, better than that, she brought comfort. My aunt needed very little in the way of aid, only someone to support her arm on the stairs. I used to sit with her and read, and she would say that help is not a favour. It is a habit you learn. She died at home, in her own bed.","zh":"等我姑妈自己照顾不了自己的时候，家里得在私人雇的护士和公家的服务之间做选择。诊所可以上门，一个年轻女人一天来两趟帮忙。她带来热饭，比这更好的是带来了安慰。姑妈要的帮衬很少，只是上下楼时有人扶一把胳膊。我常坐在她那儿读书给她听，她总说：帮忙不是人情，是学会的一种习惯。她是在家里、在自己床上走的。"},"hold":{"tw":[["admit",3],["arrange",3],["continue",2],["meet",6],["agree",0],["call",3],["control",2],["bring",6],["bear",3]],"en":"The manager had to hold the meeting in the small office at the back. She would admit no one before nine, and she could not bear to be late herself. She had arranged the chairs in a circle so everyone could see the others. We had to agree on the price before we could continue. Then she had to call the supplier and bring the matter up again. I watched her hold her temper for an hour without a break. Later she told me that control is not a gift. It is a decision you make every morning. I still hear her voice when I have to wait.","zh":"经理只能在后头那间小办公室里开会。九点之前她谁也不放进去，自己也受不了迟到。她把椅子摆成一圈，好让每个人都看得见别人。价钱谈定之前，我们没法往下走。接着她得给供货商打电话，把这事重新提一遍。我看着她一个小时都没发火。后来她跟我说，克制不是天赋，是每天早上都要做的一个决定。要等的时候，我还能听见她的声音。"},"hole":{"tw":[["fix",0],["cup",3],["hit",2],["putt",6],["mess",0],["eye",3],["mouth",2],["bunker",6],["jam",0]],"en":"The hole on the fourth green was the worst on the course, and it took me three putts to get the ball near the cup. My first hit went straight into a bunker. My friend did not say a word; he just kept his eye on the ball and closed his mouth. The whole thing was a mess, and I had no idea how to fix it. A jam of players waited behind us. I picked up the ball with the club and laughed. It was the last time I ever tried to play this game. My friend never asked me again.","zh":"第四洞那个洞是全场最糟的，我推了三杆才把球推近洞口。第一杆直接打进了沙坑。朋友一句话没说，只是眼睛盯着球，闭着嘴。整件事一团糟，我根本不知道怎么补救。后面还堵着一堆打球的人。我用杆把球捡起来，笑了。那是我最后一次试着打这玩意儿。朋友后来再没叫过我。"},"honour":{"tw":[["observe",0],["letter",3],["accept",2],["occasion",6],["respect",0],["glory",3],["recognize",2],["medal",6],["award",0]],"en":"The medal came by post, in a plain envelope with a short letter inside. It was, he said, the only honour he had ever wanted, and he would not accept any praise for it. On such an occasion my father would say only that the award belonged to the men who were not there. We all had to observe his silence and say nothing. Later, at the small dinner, the old men stood up to recognize him, and there was a good deal of glory in the room that night. I have kept the medal. Respect, he said, is not something you can carry home.","zh":"奖章是邮寄来的，一只素净的信封里夹着一封短信。他说，这是他一辈子唯一想要的荣誉，他不肯为它接受任何称赞。遇上这种场合，父亲只会说，这奖该属于那些不在场的人。我们都得安静着，什么也不说。后来在那顿小饭局上，几个老人站起来认他，那晚上的屋里很有些光彩。奖章我留着。他说，敬重这东西，你带不回家。"},"hope":{"tw":[["promise",0],["rainbow",3],["plan",2],["despair",1],["bring",6],["trust",0],["wish",2],["chance",6],["desire",2]],"en":"After the flood our only hope was the small plan my uncle had written on the back of an envelope. He had made a promise to the village that he would not leave, and he kept it. There was a rainbow over the water on the third morning, and he said that was a good sign, though none of us had any trust in signs. I began to wish I had his calm. The chance of a good harvest that year was small, and there were days of real despair. But his desire to stay never moved. He would bring us bread from the next town.","zh":"洪水过后，我们唯一的指望就是叔叔写在信封背面的那份小计划。他跟村里许过诺，说他不会走，他做到了。第三天早上水面上有道彩虹，他说这是好兆头，可我们谁也不信兆头。我开始盼着自己能有他那样的镇定。那年收成好的机会很小，也有过真正绝望的日子。但他要留下的心从没动过。他会从邻镇给我们带面包回来。"},"hunt":{"tw":[["run",0],["drive",3],["club",2],["kill",6],["search",2],["rabbit",3],["chase",2],["wolf",6],["trace",0]],"en":"The hunt began at dawn, when the men would drive the rabbits out of the long grass towards the line. My grandfather never used a club. He would run with the dogs and then stand still and search the ground for a trace. A wolf had been seen near the wood that year, and it had taken two lambs. He said he would not kill anything he did not need. The chase was the part he loved, not the end of it. I followed him once, and I was too slow. He just laughed and told me to stay home.","zh":"天一亮就开始打猎，男人们把兔子从长草里往这一线赶。爷爷从不用棍子。他跟着狗跑，然后站住，在地上找痕迹。那年树林边出现过一条狼，叼走了两只羊羔。他说用不着的东西他不杀。他要的是追赶本身，不是结局。有一回我跟着他，太慢了。他只是笑笑，叫我待在家里。"},"hurry":{"tw":[["rush",0],["run",3],["act",2],["bother",6],["speed",2],["dash",3],["travel",2],["wait",6],["haste",0]],"en":"There is no need to hurry, my mother would say, whenever we were late. She would never rush, and she would not let us run in the street. In her view, haste was the reason most things went wrong: you act too fast and then you have to wait twice as long. She did not bother about the clock at all. She would travel with a small bag, and at the station she would walk at her own speed. Once I saw her dash for a train. She made it, and she did not even breathe hard. That is the only time I remember.","zh":"我们快迟到的时候，我妈总说：用不着赶。她从不慌，也不让我们在街上跑。在她看来，事情办砸多半是因为急：动手太快，后来就得等两倍的时间。她根本不在乎钟点。出门她只带一个小包，在车站按自己的速度走。有一回我看见她冲着一趟火车跑过去。她赶上了，气都没喘。我就记得那么一次。"},"insure":{"tw":[["check",0],["card",3],["protect",2],["incentive",6],["control",3],["doom",3],["guarantee",2],["ensure",6],["cover",3]],"en":"The man who came to insure the shop had to check every room and fill in a card for each one. He said the cover would protect us against fire and flood, though it could guarantee nothing about the street itself. His only incentive, he said, was the small sum he earned on each contract. There was no way to control the wind that came off the hill. My father signed anyway, and in a strange way it took the doom out of the winter. To ensure one more year, he said, is worth the money. The shop is still there.","zh":"来给铺子上保险的那个人把每间屋都查了一遍，一间填一张卡。他说这份保障能保我们不怕火灾和洪水，但街上本身的事它保证不了。他说自己唯一的动力就是每份合同上赚的那点小钱。从山上刮下来的风是管不住的。我父亲还是签了，奇怪的是，这一下把那个冬天的晦气拿掉了不少。他说，能再保一年，这钱就值。铺子现在还在。"},"interest":{"tw":[["concern",3],["right",3],["power",2],["credit",6],["worry",0],["absorb",3],["share",2],["term",6],["occupy",0]],"en":"The small shop occupied the corner of our street for forty years. When the owner died, the question of interest on the credit he had given came up at once, and nobody wanted to talk about it. My mother had a share of the place, on paper at least, and her only concern was that the right people should not lose money. The bank had the power to change the terms, and the worry of it absorbed her whole summer. She read every letter twice. I never once saw her cry. She was that kind of woman, and I am not.","zh":"那家小店在街角开了四十年。店主去世后，他生前赊出去那笔钱该算多少利息，这问题马上摆了上来，可谁都不愿意提。那地方我母亲是有一份的，至少在纸面上有，她唯一在意的是别让该得的人吃亏。银行有权改条件，这桩心事占了她整个夏天。每封信她都读两遍。我一次也没见她哭过。她就是那样的人，我不是。"},"job":{"tw":[["business",0],["game",3],["book",2],["better",6],["line",0],["position",3],["work",2],["good",6],["problem",0]],"en":"My first job was in a small business that sold school books. The manager gave me one line to look after and told me to keep the shelf in good order. It was not a game, she said, though the rules were much the same. My position there was the lowest in the building, and the work was dull. But it was better than waiting at home, and I learned how to deal with a problem without making it worse. I stayed for three years. When I left, she gave me a book. I still have it, and I still cannot read it.","zh":"我的头一份工作是在一家卖教科书的小公司。经理交给我一条货架，叫我保持整齐。她说这不是玩游戏，可规矩差不多。我在那儿的位置是整栋楼里最低的，活儿也闷。可总比在家等着强，我也学会了怎么处理麻烦而不把它弄得更糟。我在那儿待了三年。走的时候她送了我一本书。那本书我还留着，也还是读不下去。"},"jump":{"tw":[["rise",0],["shy",3],["change",2],["drop",6],["spring",0],["bounce",3],["enter",2],["climb",6],["start",0]],"en":"The rabbit would jump the low wall in one movement and drop into the field on the other side. My sister, who was shy, would start every time she saw it. In spring they came into the garden and would bounce around the young plants. I used to climb the wall and watch them until the light began to change. The number of them seemed to rise each year and then fall again. I never dared to enter that field. I was not a brave child. I would sit on the warm stones and count them out loud, one by one.","zh":"那只兔子一下就能跳过矮墙，落到另一边的地里。我妹妹胆子小，每回看见都要一惊。春天它们进园子，在新苗周围蹦来蹦去。我常爬上墙头看它们，一直看到天色变了。它们的数目一年年像是多起来，后来又少下去。我从没敢进那块地。我不是个胆大的孩子。我会坐在晒热的石头上，一个一个数出声来。"},"keep":{"tw":[["continue",3],["carry",3],["act",2],["break",1],["sure",6],["hold",3],["control",3],["cook",2],["save",0]],"en":"My grandmother had to keep the household going for thirty years, through the war and after it. She would cook three meals a day and carry the water from the well before sunrise. She had to hold her tongue when her husband acted badly, and she had to control her face in front of the children. She would save every scrap of paper. There was a break in her life that she never spoke about. She was sure of very few things, she said, but she was sure of the house. So she continued. The house is mine now, and it is still standing.","zh":"我奶奶得把这个家撑三十年，从战时一直到战后。她一天做三顿饭，天不亮就去井边挑水。丈夫做事不像样的时候，她得管住嘴；在孩子面前，她得管住自己的脸色。每一片纸她都留着。她这辈子有过一道坎，她从没提过。她说她能确定的事很少，但这座房子她是确定的。于是她就这么撑下来了。房子现在归我了，还立在那儿。"},"kick":{"tw":[["charge",0],["report",3],["blow",2],["minute",6],["bang",0],["protest",3],["dance",2],["ball",6],["beef",0]],"en":"A boy gave the gate a hard kick, and the bang brought the whole street to the window. He wanted to protest about something, but he could not say what. Then he took a ball and began to kick it against the wall, once a minute. A man came out and asked him to stop, and the boy answered him with a blow to the air. Later the shop reported the damage and did not charge us for it. At the village dance that night he was the first on the floor. He had eaten nothing but beef and bread.","zh":"一个男孩朝大门狠狠踢了一脚，那声巨响把整条街的人都叫到了窗前。他想抗议点什么，可自己也说不清。然后他拿了个球，一分钟往墙上踢一下。有人出来叫他停手，他朝空中挥了一下拳头算是回答。后来铺子报了损失，也没让我们赔。那天晚上村里的舞会上，头一个下场的就是他。他一整天只吃了牛肉和面包。"},"kid":{"tw":[["fry",0],["orphan",3],["tease",2],["boy",6],["minor",0],["peanut",3],["leather",2],["dude",6],["jolly",0]],"en":"The kid next door was an orphan, and he lived with an aunt who fried peanuts and sold them in paper bags. A bigger boy used to tease him about his leather shoes, which were too large and had belonged to someone else. He was a minor, so nobody could do much about it. But he was a jolly child, and he never once told on them. The young dude on the corner would buy a bag every day and say nothing. That small kindness was the whole of his luck. He is a tall man now, with a shop of his own.","zh":"隔壁那个小孩是个孤儿，跟一个姨妈过，姨妈炸花生米，用纸袋装着卖。有个大点的男孩总拿他那双皮鞋取笑他，那鞋太大，是别人穿过的。他还是未成年人，谁也不好插手。可他是个快活的孩子，一次也没告过状。街角那个年轻小子每天来买一袋，什么也不说。这点好意就是他的全部运气。现在他是个高个子了，自己开了家铺子。"},"kill":{"tw":[["pop",0],["shoot",3],["drink",2],["destroy",6],["defeat",0],["stone",3],["end",2],["escape",6],["obliterate",0]],"en":"The frost that year killed almost everything in the garden, and it was the end of my mother's roses. My father used to shoot the birds that came for the seed, though he never meant to kill them; he aimed above their heads. Then one dry summer a fire came up the hill and seemed to destroy the whole wood. We could hear a sharp pop from the trees. It was the only time I saw him drink in the daytime. He said the weather could defeat any man, and that a single stone of hail could obliterate a year of work. My mother escaped it all by sleeping.","zh":"那年的霜几乎把园子里的一切都冻死了，我母亲的玫瑰也就此完了。父亲以前会打那些来吃种子的鸟，不过他并不想打死它们，总是往头顶上打。后来有个干旱的夏天，火从山坡上烧上来，好像要把整片林子都毁了。我们能听见树里噼啪的响声。那是我唯一一次看见他白天喝酒。他说天能打垮任何人，一颗冰雹就能把一年的活计抹掉。我母亲一直睡着，什么也没赶上。"},"knock":{"tw":[["bang",0],["attack",3],["blow",2],["grab",6],["bump",0],["blame",3],["hit",2],["pull",6],["pink",0]],"en":"Someone gave a knock at the door at three in the morning, and then a second bang that woke the dog. My father pulled the bolt and opened it a little. A young woman stood there with a pink scarf over her head; her hand was bleeding and she could not say where the blow had come from. He did not blame her for anything. He told her to sit, then he grabbed a cloth and told me to bump the kettle onto the stove. Nobody had attacked anyone, as it turned out. She had simply hit the kerb with her bicycle.","zh":"凌晨三点有人敲门，接着又是一声重响，把狗都吵醒了。父亲拉开插销，把门开了一条缝。门外站着个年轻女人，头上搭着条粉色的围巾；她的手在流血，自己也说不清那一击是从哪儿来的。他一句也没有怪她，只叫她坐下，然后抓了块布，让我把水壶磕到炉子上去。后来才知道，谁也没袭击谁。她只是自行车撞到了路沿。"},"land":{"tw":[["bring",2],["floor",3],["arrive",2],["property",6],["country",0],["forest",3],["change",2],["territory",6],["earth",0]],"en":"The land my family bought was poor, a thin strip between the forest and the road. My father used to say that in this country a man who owns property owns trouble. He would bring back stones from the field and use them to build up the floor of the barn. When we arrived there in the spring, the whole place seemed about to change. Beyond the fence the territory belonged to somebody else, and we never crossed it. He turned the earth with his own hands for eleven years. The barn is a ruin now, and the forest has taken the rest.","zh":"我家买下的那块地很贫，是林子和大路之间窄窄一条。父亲常说，在这个国家，有地的人就有麻烦。他会从地里把石头捡回来，用来垫高谷仓的地面。我们春天到那儿的时候，整个地方都像是要变样了。篱笆那一边的地界是别人的，我们从没越过去。他用自己的手翻了十一年的土。谷仓现在塌了，剩下的地方被林子占了。"},"lead":{"tw":[["chair",3],["hand",3],["position",2],["deficit",1],["second",6],["head",0],["captain",3],["round",6],["leave",2]],"en":"The chair of the committee asked the captain to lead the discussion, and she took her position at the head of the table. There was a deficit in the accounts, and every round of talks ended in the same place. A man in the second row raised his hand and asked to speak. Nobody would second him, so he sat down again. The chair had to leave early for another meeting. Afterwards I asked her whether she would take the post again next year. She said she would, and that surprised me. She had been doing it for nine years by then.","zh":"委员会的主席请船长来主持这场讨论，她在长桌的主位坐了下来。账上有个缺口，每一轮谈来谈去都停在同一个地方。第二排一个人举手要求发言。没人附议他，他又坐下了。主席得先走，去赶另一个会。会后我问她，明年这个位子她还接不接。她说接，这让我有点意外。那时候她已经做了九年了。"},"leg":{"tw":[["stage",0],["pin",3],["cut",2],["thigh",6],["branch",0],["fork",3],["support",2],["knee",6],["peg",0]],"en":"His left leg had been bad since the accident, and the knee would not bend. He had to support himself on a stick cut from a branch at the fork of the old tree. There was a peg by the door where he hooked it at night. The wound on his thigh had healed but he still kept a pin in his coat. We walked the road in stages, and at each stage he would sit and rest. Nobody ever heard him complain. He used to say a leg is only a leg. He died at seventy, on a Sunday.","zh":"他的左腿从那次事故以后就一直不行，膝盖弯不下去。他得靠一根棍子撑着，那棍子是从老树分叉处砍下来的一根枝子。门边有个木钉，晚上他把棍子挂在那儿。大腿上的伤好了，可他外套口袋里还是揣着根别针。我们走那段路是分段的，每走一段他就坐下歇歇。从没听人听他抱怨过。他常说，一条腿就是一条腿。他七十岁那年走了，是个星期天。"},"lift":{"tw":[["raise",0],["climb",3],["better",2],["pull",6],["rise",3],["shoulder",3],["call",2],["push",6],["wind",0]],"en":"My father would lift the bag onto his shoulder without a word, then climb the stairs to the third floor. He had to pull himself up by the rail when the wind was strong at the door. There was no lift in that building, so every delivery was a slow rise from the street. He said the work made him better and not worse. Once he had to call a doctor for another man whose back had gone. We pushed the cart together after that. I was ten, and I could not raise the bag at all. He never asked me to try again.","zh":"父亲一句话不说就把麻袋扛上肩，然后爬上三楼。门口风大的时候，他得拽着栏杆把自己往上拉。那栋楼里没有电梯，所以每送一趟货都是从街上一层层慢慢上。他说这活儿让他身子变好了，不是变坏。有一次他还得替另一个背伤了的男人叫了大夫。从那以后我们一起推车。那年我十岁，那麻袋我根本举不动。他再没叫我试过。"},"list":{"tw":[["lean",2],["post",3],["move",2],["represent",6],["heel",0],["schedule",3],["position",2],["exception",6],["tilt",0]],"en":"The ship began to list to one side before we had left the harbour. The cargo had moved in the night, and the whole deck started to tilt. The mate would lean over the rail and shout the position of every post along the shore. Our schedule had to change, and for once nobody made an exception. My heel hurt for a week from standing so long. The captain sent a man to represent us at the port office. He said a list of that kind is not a small thing in open water. We reached the next port two days late.","zh":"船还没出港就开始往一侧倾。夜里的货挪了位，整层甲板都歪了起来。大副会趴在栏杆上喊出沿岸每一个标桩的位置。我们的日程只好改，这一回谁也没破例。我站得太久，脚后跟疼了一个星期。船长派了一个人去港务处代表我们。他说在大海上，这种倾斜可不是小事。我们晚了两天才到下一个港口。"},"listen":{"tw":[["hear",0],["attend",3],["concentrate",2],["tell",6],["mind",0],["incline",3],["obey",2],["speak",6],["heed",0]],"en":"My mother would listen at the door before she came into a room. She could hear what was not said, and she would not tell us what she thought. She had a mind of her own, and she did not always obey my father. In the evening she would incline her head towards the radio and concentrate on the news. We learned to speak quietly in that house. If you did not heed her one warning, you got no second one. She would not attend any meeting where people simply shouted. I have never met anyone who listened the way she did.","zh":"我母亲进任何一间屋之前，总先在门口听一听。她听得出没说出口的话，却从不把她的想法告诉我们。她有自己的主意，也不是什么都听我父亲的。傍晚她会把头偏向收音机，专心听新闻。在那栋房子里，我们都学会了低声说话。她的一句提醒你要是没听进去，就没有第二句。凡是只靠嚷嚷的会，她都不去。我从没见过谁像她那样听人说话。"},"load":{"tw":[["charge",0],["pack",3],["concern",2],["extra",6],["stretch",0],["pill",3],["fill",2],["handle",6],["burden",0]],"en":"The load on the cart was heavier than it looked, and the man had to pack it twice before it would hold. He would charge a small sum for the extra weight. His only concern was the horse, which had to stretch its neck to pull at all. He would fill a bag with food and take a pill for his back before they set out. The handle of the cart was smooth and dark. He said a burden shared is half a burden. Then he took the whole weight himself. I have never forgotten that cold morning, or the sound of the wheels.","zh":"车上的货比看上去重，那人装了两回才装住。多出来的分量他会收一点钱。他唯一惦记的是那匹马，它得伸长脖子才拉得动。出发前他会装一袋吃的，再吃一片治背的药。车把被磨得又滑又黑。他说，担子分着挑就轻一半。可最后整副重量还是他自己扛的。那个冷清的早晨，还有车轮的响声，我一直没忘。"},"look":{"tw":[["appear",0],["cut",3],["care",2],["how",6],["bet",0],["eye",3],["lie",2],["little",6],["count",0]],"en":"Take a good look at that photograph and tell me how many people you can count. My aunt had a look of her own, and she did not care what the neighbours thought of it. She would appear at the gate with her hair cut short and her eye on the weather. I would bet she never told a lie in her life. There was very little money in that house, and that was the one thing she minded. She said a face is only a face, and it does not decide anything. I still have her photograph on the wall.","zh":"好好看看那张照片，告诉我你能数出几个人。我姑妈有她自己的那副神情，邻居怎么看，她不在乎。她会站在大门口，头发剪得短短的，眼睛盯着天色。我敢打赌她一辈子没说过一句谎话。那家里没什么钱，这是她唯一放在心上的一件事。她说，脸就是一张脸，它决定不了什么。她的照片我还挂在墙上。"},"lord":{"tw":[["master",0],["count",3],["god",2],["lady",1],["sir",6],["divine",0],["peer",3],["king",6],["noble",0]],"en":"The old lord of that valley was a hard master, and nobody in the village would say so to his face. He was the count of three small towns, and he liked to be called sir. His lady came from a noble house and never once spoke to a servant. People said the king himself had given him the land as a reward. He would talk of divine right as if it were a fact. A peer from the next valley came once a year to hunt with him. They called each other friend. They did not mean it. At the harvest he thanked God and then raised the rent.","zh":"那一带的老爷是个厉害的主人，村里没人敢当着他的面这么说。他是三个小镇的伯爵，喜欢别人称他阁下。他的夫人出身贵族，从没跟下人说过一句话。人们说，这片地是国王亲自赏给他的。他谈起神授之权来，像是在说一件事实。邻谷的一位贵族每年过来一次，跟他一起打猎。他们互称朋友，可并不是。收庄稼的时候他谢过上帝，然后就把租子涨了。"},"lot":{"tw":[["deal",3],["party",3],["condition",2],["maybe",6],["draw",0],["flood",3],["divide",2],["good",6],["luck",0]],"en":"A lot of the fields by the river were under water that spring, and the flood took the lower road as well. The condition of the soil after it went down was not good. We had to divide what was left of the seed between three families by drawing straws, and our party drew the shortest one. Maybe that was the last piece of bad luck that year. My father made a deal with the mill and got us through. He said a man should not complain about the draw he is given. He put the seed in the ground and never spoke of it again.","zh":"那年春天河边很多地都泡在水里，洪水连下面那条路也冲了。水退之后土的情况不太好。剩下的种子要在三户人家之间分，我们用抽签的办法，我家抽到最短的一根。也许那就是那一年最后一件倒霉事。父亲跟磨坊谈成了一笔交易，把我们撑了过去。他说，抽到什么签，不该抱怨。他把种子埋进地里，这事以后再没提过。"},"make":{"tw":[["build",0],["add",3],["act",2],["break",1],["need",6],["cause",0],["bring",3],["enough",6],["clear",0]],"en":"The old man had to make a new gate for the yard, and he would not let anyone help. He had to build it from boards he had kept for years, and add a bar across the top. It was clear from the start that he had no need of advice. He would act slowly, measure twice, and never break a piece. He said a bad joint is the cause of half the trouble in this world. He had enough wood in the end, and he did not have to bring anything from the shop. It took him nine days. The gate is still there.","zh":"老人得给院子做一扇新门，他不让别人搭手。他得用存了多年的木板来做，再在上面加一道横杠。从一开始就看得出，他不需要谁出主意。他动手很慢，量两遍，从不弄断一块料。他说这世上有一半的麻烦，都是一个接得不好的榫头造成的。最后木料够了，他也不用去铺子里拿什么。这只门他做了九天。门现在还在。"},"master":{"tw":[["control",2],["command",3],["beat",2],["tutor",6],["lord",0],["subjugate",3],["key",2],["bachelor",6],["main",0]],"en":"The old master of the little college had a bachelor's degree from a school nobody had heard of, and he never let anyone forget it. He could not control his temper when a tutor asked a question he thought foolish, and he would command silence with one hand. In his own room he was a lord. He would beat every student at chess and then explain, for an hour, why. The main reason people stayed was his library; the key to it hung at his belt. He never managed to subjugate anyone who laughed. I think that was his only weakness.","zh":"那所小学堂的老先生有个谁也没听说过的学校的学士学位，他从不让人忘记这件事。辅导老师问了个他觉得蠢的问题，他就管不住脾气，一抬手就能叫全场安静。在他自己那间屋里，他就是个老爷。下棋他谁都能赢，赢完还要讲上一个钟头为什么。人们留下来的主要原因是他的藏书室，钥匙就挂在他腰上。谁要是一笑，他就降不住谁了。我想这是他唯一的软处。"},"matter":{"tw":[["count",0],["least",3],["concern",2],["question",6],["issue",0],["solid",3],["trouble",2],["how",6],["subject",0]],"en":"What matters most in a small town is not how much you own but whether you can be counted on. That was my father's one subject, and he raised it at every table. The question of the new road came up again that autumn, and it was the least of anyone's concern at first. Then the issue of the solid ground under it turned out to be serious. There was real trouble at the meeting. My father said the matter was simple: either you build it well or you do not build it. For once, nobody in the room argued with him.","zh":"在一个小镇上，最要紧的不是你有多少产业，而是别人能不能指望你。这是我父亲唯独爱讲的题目，每回饭桌上都要提。那年秋天新修那条路的问题又摆上来了，起初谁也没把它当回事。后来路基下面土质是否结实这一条，成了大问题。会上真吵了起来。父亲说，这事很简单：要么好好修，要么别修。这一回，屋里没人跟他争。"},"meet":{"tw":[["fill",0],["answer",3],["experience",2],["hold",6],["fit",0],["club",3],["cope",2],["next",6],["play",0]],"en":"The school held a swimming meet in the last week of term, and everyone in the club had to fill in a form and answer two questions about their health. My sister, who had little experience of racing, was not sure she would fit in. She had to cope with a bad start and a lane that was too narrow, and the hall was loud. She came fourth, not last. The next morning she told me she would do it again. She did not play any other sport that year. I think that was the first time I saw her really want something.","zh":"学期最后一周，学校办了一场游泳比赛，俱乐部里每个人都得填一张表，回答两个关于健康的问题。我妹妹比赛的经验很少，不确定自己能不能跟得上。出发没起好，泳道又窄，她都得扛下来，馆里还吵。她拿了第四，不是最后。第二天早上她跟我说她还要再来一次。那年她再没玩别的项目。我想那是我头一回看见她真想要一样东西。"},"mention":{"tw":[["note",2],["raise",3],["notice",2],["question",6],["credit",0],["remember",3],["state",2],["answer",6],["observe",0]],"en":"At the meeting nobody wanted to mention the money. I had made a note of it in my book, and I raised the question just before we closed. The chairman did not answer at first. He looked at the window, as if he had noticed something in the street. Then he said, in a flat voice, that the state of the accounts was not what we had been told. He gave credit to the woman who had kept the books, and he asked us to remember her name. I observed that one man at the end of the table said nothing at all.","zh":"会上谁都不愿提到钱的事。我在本子上记了一笔，快散会的时候把这个问题提了出来。主席起初没有答话。他看着窗户，像是街上有什么引起了他的注意。然后他平平地说，账目的状况跟我们听到的不一样。他把这份功劳记在那个管账的女人名下，叫我们记住她的名字。我注意到，桌子那头有一个人一句话也没说。"},"mistake":{"tw":[["slip",3],["stumble",3],["identify",2],["wrong",6],["fault",0],["blot",3],["misconception",2],["excuse",6],["error",0]],"en":"The clerk made one small mistake in the ledger, a blot of ink on the wrong line, and it cost the office a week. He had meant to write a name and wrote another one instead. It was not his fault; the two names were almost the same, and anyone could stumble over them. The manager let him explain, because she did not want him to look for an excuse. He did not slip again that year. He said later that a misconception is harder to fix than an error, because nobody can identify it. I have thought about that ever since.","zh":"那个职员在账本上出了个小错，一滴墨落在了不该落的那一行，办公室为此搭进去一个星期。他本来要写一个名字，写成了另一个。这不能全怪他：两个名字几乎一样，谁都会绊一下。经理让他自己说明，因为不想让他去找借口。那一年他再没出过这种岔子。后来他说，错的理解比错本身更难改，因为谁也指不出来它在哪儿。这话我到现在还在想。"},"noise":{"tw":[["racket",0],["background",3],["cry",2],["loud",6],["resound",0],["boom",3],["sound",2],["alarm",6],["dissonance",0]],"en":"The noise in the street that afternoon was a great racket, and above the background of the traffic came a cry from near the bridge. Then a boom, and the whole window shook. The sound of it resounded off the buildings on both sides. We ran out, but nothing was there except a lorry with a broken drum. Somebody had set off the alarm in the shop next door by mistake. It was so loud that my ears rang for an hour. My father said that what we had heard was not music but dissonance, and that he preferred it to silence.","zh":"那天下午街上的响动是一片大嘈杂，车流的背景声之上，桥那头传来一声喊叫。接着一声闷响，整扇窗子都晃了。那声音在两边的楼之间回荡。我们跑出去，什么也没有，只有一辆鼓破了的卡车。隔壁铺子里的警报被人误碰响了。响得我耳朵嗡了一个钟头。父亲说，我们听见的不是音乐，是刺耳的不谐，他还说他宁愿这样，也不要安静。"},"offer":{"tw":[["pass",0],["special",3],["act",2],["purchase",6],["crack",0],["hook",3],["market",2],["deal",6],["propose",0]],"en":"In the market a woman offered me a special price on a piece of cloth. I passed her stall twice before I made the purchase, because I could not see a crack in the offer. There was a hook near the door with a coat on it, and she kept her money in a bag under that coat. She proposed a deal that sounded generous until I did the sum. I did not act at once. She laughed and said I was the first customer that week who had counted. Then she took a little off the price, and I bought it.","zh":"市场里有个女人向我报了一块布的特别价钱。我从她摊前走了两趟才买下来——我看不出这报价里有什么破绽。门边有个挂钩，上面挂着件外套，她的钱就放在那外套下面的袋子里。她提的那个交易听着挺大方，直到我心算了一下。我没有马上答应。她笑了，说我是那一周头一个会算账的客人。然后她让了一点价，我买下了。"},"order":{"tw":[["arrange",2],["call",3],["act",2],["disorder",1],["allow",6],["club",0],["hunt",3],["rule",2],["rate",0]],"en":"The club had one rule about the order of things, and it was written on the wall in the hall. No one was allowed to call out a number before the chairman had arranged the list. The rate of the fee went up that year, and there was some disorder at the meeting about it. The old men would hunt through the papers for the same page again and again. I was told to act as secretary and keep the record. Nobody ever thanked me. It was, I think, the most useful year of my life. I learned more from those papers than from any book.","zh":"俱乐部对于次序只有一条规矩，写在走廊的墙上。主席把名单排好之前，谁也不许报号。那一年的会费涨了，会上因此有点乱。那几个老人一遍遍地翻那些纸，找同一页。他们让我当秘书，负责记录。从来没人谢过我。我觉得，那是我这辈子最有用的一个年头。我从那些纸上学到的，比从任何一本书上都多。"},"pack":{"tw":[["camp",0],["bag",3],["arrange",2],["pick",6],["carry",0],["nest",3],["fill",2],["grab",6],["ring",0]],"en":"We had to pack for camp in one afternoon, and my mother would not let me carry the bag until it was properly arranged. I had to pick what I needed, fill the bottom with the heavy things, and grab a coat at the last minute. There was a bird's nest in the roof of the shed, and a ring of eggs lay in it, cold and blue. My father put a ring through the handle of my bag so I would not lose it. He said the first rule of the road is to travel light. I did not. My bag weighed more than I did.","zh":"我们得用一个下午收拾去露营的东西，母亲不肯让我拎包，非要我先理整齐。我得挑出要用的，把重的塞在底下，最后一刻再抓一件外套。棚子顶上有只鸟窝，里面一圈蛋，又冷又青。父亲在我包的提手上套了个环，免得我丢了。他说出门第一条规矩是轻装。我没做到。我的包比我还沉。"},"pain":{"tw":[["bother",0],["try",3],["upset",2],["pleasure",1],["stress",6],["hurt",0],["distress",3],["stomach",6],["trouble",0]],"en":"The pain in her stomach came back every evening, and it did not bother her as much as it bothered us. She would try to eat a little and then put the plate aside. It upset my father more than he would say, and the stress of those months showed in his face. She said the trouble was not the pain but the waiting. There was real distress in her voice on the bad nights. But she would still take some pleasure from a warm room and a quiet hour, and that was what hurt me most. I have never been able to forget it.","zh":"她胃里的疼每天晚上都回来，这疼烦我们比烦她自己还多。她会试着吃一点，然后把盘子推到一边。父亲心里比嘴上难受得多，那几个月压出来的痕迹都写在他脸上。她说，难受的不是疼，是等。夜里厉害的时候，她声音里真有痛苦。可她还能从一间暖屋子、一个安静的小时里得到一点慰藉——正是这一点最让我难受。这事我一直忘不掉。"},"paint":{"tw":[["key",0],["charge",3],["coat",2],["brush",6],["pigment",0],["prime",3],["cover",2],["plastic",6],["rouge",0]],"en":"The painter came with a key to the back door and a brush in each hand. He had to prime the wall first, then put on one coat of paint and let it dry. He said the pigment in the cheap kind goes grey within a year. He would not charge us for the plastic sheet he used to cover the floor. My aunt wanted a small tin of rouge for her face and he brought it with the paint. He worked slowly, whistling. When he had gone, the room looked as if it had been given a new set of walls.","zh":"油漆匠来了，手里拿的是后门的钥匙和两把刷子。他得先把墙打底，再刷一道漆，等它干。他说便宜的那种漆，颜料一年就发灰。他给我们盖地板用的那块塑料布不收钱。我姑妈想要一小盒擦脸的胭脂，他连漆一起带来了。他干得慢，还吹口哨。他走了以后，那间屋子像是换了一套新墙。"},"pick":{"tw":[["choice",0],["decision",3],["choose",2],["spot",6],["clean",0],["pleasure",3],["knock",2],["chance",6],["foot",0]],"en":"At the market I had to pick a place to stand, and the choice was harder than the decision to come at all. I could choose between the clean spot near the door, where the light was good, and the shade at the foot of the wall. It was a pleasure to be out so early. A man came and gave a light knock on the table, and I moved my basket. I had one chance at a good morning, and I took it. I sold nearly everything by noon. I have never had a better day at that stall.","zh":"到了市场上，我得挑个地方站，这个选择比决定来不来还难。我可以挑门边那块干净的地方，那儿光线好；也可以挑墙根下的阴凉。这么早出来是件快活事。有个男的过来，在桌上轻轻敲了两下，我把篮子挪开了。好早上就这一回机会，我抓住了。到中午差不多都卖光了。那个摊子，我再没有过更好的一天。"},"piece":{"tw":[["bit",0],["base",3],["eat",2],["simple",6],["man",0],["black",3],["join",2],["pick",0]],"en":"An old man sat on the base of the stone wall with a piece of bread in his hand, eating it slowly. He wore a black coat, and there was a bit of thread hanging from one sleeve. He would pick the crumbs off his knees and eat those too. It was a simple meal, and he was in no hurry. When he had finished, he joined his hands behind his head and looked at the sky. I wanted to ask him something. I did not know what. He looked as if he had all the time there was in the world.","zh":"一个老人坐在石墙的墙基上，手里拿着一块面包，慢慢地吃。他穿件黑外套，一只袖子上挂着一根线头。他会把膝盖上的碎屑捡起来吃掉。一顿很简单的饭，他一点也不急。吃完以后，他把两只手交叉垫在脑后，望着天。我想问他点什么，可又不知道该问什么。他那样子，像是世上的时间全归他。"},"plan":{"tw":[["programme",0],["hope",3],["idea",2],["propose",6],["design",0],["engineer",3],["think",2],["deal",6],["project",0]],"en":"The engineer came to the site with a plan he had drawn himself, and he hoped nobody would ask him where the idea came from. It was part of a larger project, a government programme for the valley. He had to design a small bridge, and he proposed to build it in one summer. I asked him to think about the winter water. We made a deal on the price and shook hands. He said no design survives the first flood, and then he laughed. He was right. The bridge is still standing, twelve years on, and it has never moved.","zh":"工程师带着他自己画的一份方案到了工地，他盼着没人问他这主意是从哪儿来的。这是一个更大工程的一部分，一项针对这条河谷的政府计划。他得设计一座小桥，他提出用一个夏天建成。我请他把冬天水大的情况想一想。我们谈定了价钱，握了手。他说，没有哪个设计能扛过第一场洪水，然后他笑了。他说得对。十二年过去，桥还立在那儿，一动没动。"},"plant":{"tw":[["establish",0],["bed",3],["stock",2],["factory",6],["institute",0],["fix",3],["communicate",2],["facility",6],["embed",0]],"en":"The plant on the edge of town was the largest factory of its kind in the region, and the institute in the next street had helped to establish it forty years before. My father worked the night shift at that facility, and he would fix the same machine every week. He kept a small bed of flowers outside the gate, and he would communicate with them, he said, more easily than with the men inside. There was a stock of old parts in the yard, going to rust. Someone had embedded a coin in the concrete step, and nobody knew why. He showed it to me once.","zh":"镇子边上的那家厂是这一带同类工厂里最大的，隔一条街的研究所四十年前帮着把它办了起来。父亲在那座厂里上夜班，每星期都要修同一台机器。他在大门外养了一小畦花，他说跟花说话比跟里面的人说话容易。院子里堆着一堆旧零件，正在生锈。有人在水泥台阶里嵌了一枚硬币，谁也不知道为什么。他带我看过一次。"},"pot":{"tw":[["deal",0],["flood",3],["stake",2],["bread",6],["kettle",3],["lot",0],["belly",2],["cake",6],["mess",0]],"en":"There was a pot of soup on the stove and a kettle beside it, and the whole kitchen smelled of bread and cake. My grandmother had a lot of rules about the order of cooking. She would deal with the flood of relatives at Christmas by cooking for two days. The stake in the garden, which held up the washing line, was the only thing she would not let anyone move. She had a great belly and a laugh to match it. When she died the kitchen was left in a mess, and none of us could find anything. I still have her pot.","zh":"炉子上有一锅汤，旁边一把水壶，整间厨房都是面包和蛋糕的味道。我奶奶对做菜的次序有很多规矩。圣诞节一大家子人涌来，她就连做两天饭来应付。园子里那根撑着晾衣绳的木桩，是唯一不许人动的东西。她肚子大，笑声也大。她走以后，厨房乱成一团，我们谁想找什么都找不着。她那只锅我还留着。"},"pound":{"tw":[["beat",0],["flap",3],["blow",2],["ounce",6],["hammer",0],["thrash",3],["hit",2],["barrel",6],["poke",0]],"en":"In the yard behind the garage a man was trying to pound out a dent in an old wing with a hammer. Every blow made the metal flap and ring. He would hit it, stop, look, and hit it again. A barrel of oil stood beside him, and he knew the weight of it to the ounce. He did not thrash about like a young man; he worked with small, exact strokes. Once he gave the panel a light poke with his finger and shook his head. I asked him if it could be saved. He said cars can always be beaten back into shape, if you have the time.","zh":"修车铺后面的院子里，一个人正拿锤子想把旧挡板上的一块凹痕敲平。每一下都让铁皮颤着响。他敲一下，停住，看看，再敲。旁边立着一桶油，那分量他不用称也知道到几盎司。他不像年轻人那样乱砸，下手又小又准。有一回他用手指轻轻戳了戳那块板，摇了摇头。我问他还能不能救。他说，只要有工夫，车总能敲回原来的形状。"},"power":{"tw":[["force",0],["control",3],["state",2],["system",6],["king",0],["degree",3],["provide",2],["pressure",6],["index",0]],"en":"The power station on the hill used to provide light for four villages. The system was old, and to a large degree it depended on one man who could control the whole thing from a small room. In winter the load was heavy, and the pressure in the pipes would rise until the needles went off the index. He would open a valve by main force and stand there, counting. The state never sent anybody to look at it. He used to say he was the king of that hill. When he retired, the lights went out twice in the first month.","zh":"山上那座电站过去给四个村子供电。这套系统老了，很大程度上全靠一个人——他在一间小屋里就能控住整台机器。冬天负载重，管子里的压力会一直往上涨，直到指针跑出表盘。他会使出大劲扳开一个阀门，然后站在那儿数数。上面从来没派人来看过。他常说自己是那座山上的国王。他退休以后，头一个月就停了两次电。"},"press":{"tw":[["fight",0],["newspaper",3],["advertise",2],["news",6],["push",0],["rush",3],["count",2],["interview",6],["contract",0]],"en":"The press office was one room above a newspaper shop, and on a busy night the whole floor would shake. There was always a fight over the last telephone. A young man would push through the crowd with a sheet of paper and shout the count for the front page. They had to advertise twice a week, or the paper lost money, and the news went to the printer in a rush at midnight. I once sat in on an interview with the owner and he said a contract was only paper. I still read that paper every morning. It closed in the end, like most things.","zh":"报社编辑部是报纸铺子楼上的一个房间，忙的晚上整层楼都在抖。总有人为最后一台电话吵起来。一个年轻人会举着一张纸挤过人群，大声报出上首页的条数。他们一周得登两次广告，不然报纸就赔钱，夜里新闻赶着送印刷厂。有一回我旁听老板接受采访，他说合同不过就是纸。直到现在我每天早上还看那份报。后来它还是关了，像大多数东西一样。"},"programme":{"tw":[["plan",0],["bill",3],["system",2],["launch",6],["broadcast",0],["patch",3],["schedule",2],["aim",6],["syllabus",0]],"en":"The college had a programme for older students, and my mother signed up for it in her fifties. The syllabus ran to forty pages, and the schedule gave her two evenings a week. Her aim was simple: she wanted to read the news without help. The system was not kind to people who worked all day, and a few of them left in the first month. There was a plan to launch a second course the next year, and they would broadcast it on the local radio. The bill for the books was small. She finished the course, and she patched up her old dictionary with tape.","zh":"学院有个面向年纪大的学生的课程，我母亲五十多岁报了名。教学大纲印了四十页，课程表给她排了一周两个晚上。她的目的很简单：她想不用人帮忙就能读报。这套办法对整天上班的人并不友好，头一个月就走了几个。第二年打算再开一门课，还要在当地电台播出。买书的账单不多。她把课上完了，还用了胶带把她那本旧词典补了补。"},"push":{"tw":[["advertise",2],["bill",3],["deal",2],["pull",1],["step",6],["drive",0],["nose",3],["move",6],["fight",2]],"en":"My father had to push the cart up the hill every morning, and he would never let anyone pull it for him. Step by step, with his nose almost touching the handle, he would move it two hundred metres to the market. The deal he had with the shop next door was that he took their boxes as well. He did not advertise; people simply knew. He would fight the wind and the wet road without a word. At the end of the month he would pay every bill on the same day. He said a man who drives himself does not need anyone to drive him.","zh":"每天早上父亲都得把车推上坡，他从不让别人替他拉。一步一步，鼻子几乎贴到车把上，他把车挪两百米推到市场。他跟隔壁铺子说好的事是：再帮他们捎上箱子。他不做广告，人们自己知道。风、湿滑的路，他一句话不说地对着干。到了月底，他同一天把每笔账都结清。他说，自己开车的人，用不着别人来开。"},"rate":{"tw":[["order",0],["beat",3],["charge",2],["increase",6],["grade",0],["seed",3],["measure",2],["rise",6],["range",0]],"en":"The rate they paid for the seed began to rise that spring, and it threw the whole order of the work out. My father had to measure every sack twice and then increase his price by a small amount. He would beat the old grade of wheat into the ground and try a new one. The range of what he could grow on that soil was narrow. Some years he made nothing at all, and the charge for the mill came out of his own pocket. He never missed a payment. He said a rate is not a promise, it is only weather written down.","zh":"那年春天种子的价钱涨了，把整个活计的次序都打乱了。父亲得把每袋量两遍，再把他的卖价往上提一点。他会把旧等级的小麦砸进地里，试一种新的。那块土上能种什么，范围很窄。有的年份他什么也没挣着，磨坊的钱还得从自己兜里出。他从没欠过一次账。他说，价钱不是承诺，只是把天气写下来而已。"},"reach":{"tw":[["hand",0],["deal",3],["arrive",2],["rest",6],["hit",0],["find",3],["move",2],["chance",6],["pass",0]],"en":"We had to reach the village before dark, and my father would not rest on the way. He would find the path by hand when it grew too black to see. The wind began to hit us from the left, and every chance of a shortcut was gone. He did not move quickly; he was past sixty, and he had made a quiet deal with the road. We passed two empty farms and a broken bridge. When we arrived, the inn was shut. He sat on the step and said that a man can get anywhere, if he does not mind being tired.","zh":"我们得在天黑前赶到那个村子，父亲一路上不肯歇。黑得看不清路的时候，他用手摸着找道。风开始从左边打过来，走近路的指望全没了。他走得不快，六十多了，跟这条路之间有一种不说出口的默契。我们经过两座空农舍和一座断桥。到的时候，客栈已经关了。他坐在台阶上说，一个人哪儿都到得了，只要不怕累。"},"read":{"tw":[["record",0],["call",3],["talk",2],["write",6],["say",3],["strike",3],["understand",2],["copy",6],["study",0]],"en":"My grandfather could not read until he was fourteen, and he never let anyone forget it. He would study a page for an hour and then say only that he did not understand it. In the evenings he would ask my mother to read the record of the farm aloud, and he would copy the figures into his own book. A word would strike him and he would stop everything. When the school called about me, he went himself and had a long talk with the head. He could not write his name, but he could tell a good teacher from a bad one.","zh":"我爷爷十四岁才会读书，这事他从不让人忘掉。一页纸他能看上整整一个钟头，然后只说一句他看不懂。傍晚他让我母亲把农场的账念出来，他把那些数字抄进自己的本子里。碰到一个让他心里一动的词，他会把手里的事全停下。学校为我打电话来的时候，他自己跑了一趟，跟校长谈了很久。他连自己的名字都写不了，可他能分得出好老师和坏老师。"},"red":{"tw":[["loss",0],["squeeze",3],["radical",2],["yellow",6],["scarlet",3],["cardinal",3],["sum",2],["blue",6],["crimson",3]],"en":"The fabric shop had one wall of red cloth, and the woman there could tell scarlet from crimson without looking twice. She said the yellow and the blue on the next shelf had been there a year, but the red moved. A radical change in fashion had come that spring, and nobody could explain the sum of it. Her loss that winter had been heavy, and she had to squeeze every coin. A cardinal once came into the shop, in his dark coat, and bought a metre of the plainest stuff. She told the story for years. Red was the only colour she trusted.","zh":"那家布店里有一面墙全是红布，店里的女人一眼就能分出猩红和深红。她说旁边架子上的黄的和蓝的搁了一年了，红的一直在动。那年春天风气变了个大的，谁也说不清加起来是怎么回事。她那年冬天亏得厉害，一个铜板都得抠着花。有一次一位红衣主教穿着深色外套进店，买了两尺最素的料子。这故事她讲了好多年。红色是她唯一信得过的颜色。"},"relate":{"tw":[["concern",0],["involve",3],["tell",2],["understand",6],["touch",0],["remember",3],["think",2],["describe",6],["associate",0]],"en":"My aunt would never tell a story straight. She would describe a room, a smell, the way a hand touched a shoulder, and only then come to what the thing was about. As a child I could not understand why she took so long. Now I think it was her way of saying that everything is related to everything else. She had a concern for small facts, and she would remember a date from forty years back. Anything that did not involve her she still talked about as if it did. I associate her voice with that kitchen. It smelled of apples and wet stone.","zh":"我姑妈从来不会直着讲故事。她先说一间屋子、一种气味、一只手搭上肩膀的样子，然后才说到事情本身。小时候我不明白她为什么要绕这么久。现在我想，她是在说，什么跟什么都是连着的。她对小事很在意，四十年前的一个日子她都记得。凡是跟她没干系的事，她讲起来也像跟自己有关。我一想起她的声音，就想到那间厨房。里面是苹果和湿石头的味道。"},"report":{"tw":[["cover",0],["exclusive",3],["inform",2],["according",6],["paper",0],["gossip",3],["news",2],["press",6],["story",0]],"en":"According to the report in the local paper, the fire had started in a shed. The press sent one man to cover it, and he got an exclusive from a neighbour who had seen everything. The story was full of gossip about the family, and half of it was not true. He had to inform the office by telephone from the pub, because there was no other line. My father read the paper twice that night and said nothing. Then he folded it and put it under the coal bucket. He did not like the news to be wrong. He said a wrong line is worse than no line.","zh":"照当地报纸那篇报道说的，火是从一个棚子里烧起来的。报馆派了一个人去采访，他从一个什么都看见了的邻居那儿拿到独家。那篇故事里全是这家人家的闲话，一半都不真。他得从酒馆打电话回报社，因为再没有别的线路。父亲那天晚上把报纸读了两遍，一句话没说。然后他把它折起来，塞到煤桶底下。他不喜欢新闻里出错。他说，一行错字比没有这行还糟。"},"return":{"tw":[["fall",3],["drive",3],["answer",2],["leave",6],["issue",0],["home",3],["bring",2],["end",6],["pass",0]],"en":"My uncle had to leave home at nineteen and did not return for eleven years. He would drive a lorry for a company that never answered his letters. The issue was money, and he did not like to talk about it. When he came back, the whole village had begun to fall apart, and the mill had closed. He had to pass the old house twice before he could bring himself to go in. At the end of that week he told my mother he would stay. He did not say for how long. It turned out to be the rest of his life.","zh":"我叔十九岁就得离家，一走十一年没回来。他给一家公司开卡车，那家公司从不回他的信。症结是钱，他不愿意谈。等他回来时，整个村子已经开始散了，磨坊也关了。他在老屋前来回走了两趟，才狠下心进去。那个星期末他跟我母亲说他要留下来，没说留多久。后来才知道，是留了一辈子。"},"ring":{"tw":[["call",0],["tire",3],["sound",2],["triangle",6],["pack",0],["nest",3],["touch",2],["gate",6],["telephone",0]],"en":"The ring of the telephone would sound three times before anyone in the house moved. My mother kept it on the shelf by the gate, next to an old tire that my father used as a flower bed. When the call came, she would touch the receiver and wait, as if she were listening for something behind the voice. A pack of dogs would start up in the yard. There was a small triangle hanging in the nest of the old tree, and the wind made it ring all night. That was the only sound she really liked. I have never heard anything like it since.","zh":"电话铃要响三下，屋里才有人动。母亲把它放在大门边的架子上，旁边是父亲当花坛用的一个旧轮胎。电话一来，她会摸摸话筒等着，像是在听声音背后的什么。院里一群狗会跟着叫起来。老树的洞里挂着一个小三角铁，风一吹整夜都响。那是她唯一真正喜欢的声音。这样的声音，我以后再没听过。"},"rock":{"tw":[["shake",0],["roll",3],["move",2],["band",6],["stone",0],["crystal",3],["material",2],["pop",6],["tilt",0]],"en":"My brother's band practised in the old stone barn at the end of the lane. The rock they played was loud enough to shake the roof, and the whole floor would move under us. They had a crystal glass on a shelf for luck, and it would tilt and roll whenever the drums started. The material on the walls was too thin for that kind of noise, but nobody minded. People from the village came and stood outside. Some of them hated pop and said so. I sat on a stone by the door and listened to all of it. That summer I learned every song.","zh":"我哥的乐队在巷子尽头的老石头谷仓里排练。他们弹的那种摇滚响得能把房顶震松，整个地面都在我们脚底下动。架上有一只水晶杯，当吉祥物用的，鼓一响它就歪过来滚过去。墙上的料子太薄，挡不住这种动静，可没人在乎。村里的人跑来站在外面听。有人讨厌流行歌，还亲口说了。我坐在门口的一块石头上，从头听到尾。那个夏天我把每首歌都听熟了。"},"roll":{"tw":[["wave",0],["ball",3],["bread",2],["hot",6],["wheel",0],["clue",3],["change",2],["cover",6],["wind",0]],"en":"Every morning the baker would roll out the dough and cut it into shapes, and the smell of hot bread would cover the whole street. He had lost a wheel on his cart the year before and never found the clue as to where it went. In summer the wind came off the water in long waves, and he would roll the cover of the stall down and wait. A boy would kick a ball against the shutters until he was sent away. Nothing about the shop changed for thirty years. Then one morning it did, and the street was quieter.","zh":"每天早上面包师都要把面团擀开，切成各种形状，热面包的香味会罩住整条街。他前一年丢了推车上的一只轮子，一直没弄清它到底去了哪儿。夏天风从水面上成排地吹过来，他就把摊子的遮布放下来等着。有个男孩总往卷帘门上踢球，直到被赶走。这家铺子三十年没什么变化。后来有一天早上变了，街上也静了些。"},"rule":{"tw":[["find",0],["order",3],["control",2],["regime",6],["govern",0],["dictate",3],["decide",2],["under",6],["normal",0]],"en":"The rule in our house was that nobody dictated anything at the table. My father had grown up under a regime of silence and had decided that his own children would not. He could not control much else in his life, so he governed that one hour. He would find a way to make everyone talk, even about nothing. It was not the normal way for a man of his time. He said that order in a family is not the same as peace. When he died we kept the rule for a year, and then we lost it. I still hear his voice at my own table.","zh":"我们家的规矩是：饭桌上谁都不许发号施令。父亲从小在一种沉默的管教下长大，他打定主意不让自己的孩子也这样。他一辈子别的事都管不了，就管这一个钟头。他总能想出办法让每个人都开口，哪怕是说些没用的。在他那个年代的男人里，这不是常态。他说，家里的次序跟安宁不是一回事。他走后这条规矩我们还守了一年，然后就丢了。如今在我自己的饭桌上，我还能听见他的声音。"},"sail":{"tw":[["sheet",0],["boat",2],["ship",6],["sweep",0],["run",3],["move",2],["fly",6],["cruise",3],["beat",3]],"en":"The sail of the small boat had been cut from a sheet that had once covered a bed, and it would beat against the mast in the wind. My father could not afford a ship, so he sailed that thing along the coast for years. He would run with the wind until the whole shore would sweep past us, and we would not move a muscle. On clear days we could watch the gulls fly out and a white cruise boat far off. He used to say that a man needs very little: water under him, air above him, and time. I have never owned a boat since.","zh":"小船的帆是用一条旧床单裁的，风里总是啪啪地拍着桅杆。父亲买不起大船，就驾着这个玩意儿沿着海岸跑了好些年。他顺着风跑，岸边一路掠过去，我们一动不动。天晴的时候能看见海鸥飞出去，远处还有一条白色的游轮。他常说，人要的东西很少：身下有水，头上有天，还有点工夫。那以后我再没拥有过一条船。"},"scare":{"tw":[["fright",0],["terrify",3],["fear",2],["mad",6],["panic",0],["awe",3],["stimulate",2],["blow",6],["dash",0]],"en":"A blow on the door in the middle of the night gave us all a fright. My mother would not show fear in front of us, but she went mad with worry, and I could see it. The whole village was in a panic for two days. It turned out to be a boy who had been paid to dash through the lanes and terrify the older people. My father did not shout at him. He said a scare of that kind can stimulate a whole town into something worse. Standing in front of the crowd, he had a strange kind of awe about him. Then everyone went home.","zh":"半夜门上挨了一下，把我们全吓了一跳。母亲在我们面前不肯露出害怕，可她心里急得快疯了，我看得出来。整整两天全村都慌了。后来才知道，是个男孩，有人给他钱，让他在巷子里乱窜吓唬老人。父亲没有冲他吼。他说，这样一场惊吓能把一个镇子激到更糟的地方去。他站在人群前面的时候，身上有一种说不出的威严。然后大家都回家了。"},"seat":{"tw":[["behind",0],["box",3],["space",2],["front",6],["bottom",0],["chair",3],["support",2],["rear",6],["sit",0]],"en":"I had a seat at the front, in a box near the window, and behind me sat an old woman who never stopped talking. There was no space between the chairs, and her knees were against my back. She had to support herself on the rear of the one in front to stand up. At the bottom of the hall a man was selling programmes. I did not sit down again after the break. I stood at the side and watched the crowd instead. It was easier than telling her to be quiet. I never went back to that hall.","zh":"我的座位在前排靠窗的一个包厢里，我后面坐着个老太太，一直说个不停。椅子之间没有空隙，她的膝盖顶着我的背。她起身得扶着前排椅子的后靠。大厅最下面有人在卖节目单。中场休息之后我没再坐回去，站在旁边看人群。这比叫她安静容易。那间大厅我再没去过。"},"secure":{"tw":[["fix",0],["hang",3],["close",2],["ensure",6],["good",0],["tie",3],["attach",2],["maintain",6],["insure",0]],"en":"We had to secure the boat before the weather turned. My father would tie the rope twice, attach it to the post, and then hang the oars up under the roof. He had to fix the loose board on the shed door as well. To ensure that nothing moved, he would pull on the rope with his whole weight and wait. He said it is not enough to close a door; you have to maintain the habit of checking it. The man who came to insure the boat once a year always said the same thing: a good knot is cheaper than a new one.","zh":"天要变之前，我们得把船系牢。父亲会把绳子打两遍结，拴到桩子上，再把桨挂到棚顶下面。棚门上一块松了的板他也得钉好。为了确保什么都不动，他会用全身的重量去拽绳子，然后等一等。他说，光把门关上说不够，得养成检查的习惯。每年来看船保险的那个人总说同一句话：一个好结比一条新船便宜。"},"send":{"tw":[["air",0],["blow",3],["move",2],["deliver",6],["charge",0],["express",3],["transfer",2],["help",6],["post",0]],"en":"My grandmother would send a parcel every month, and the post in that town was slow. She had to pay a charge for the express service once, and it arrived five days late anyway. She would move the box to the counter herself and wait while the clerk wrote out the form. She liked to deliver her things by hand when she could. In winter the air off the river had a hard blow in it, and she would stand outside with the box against her coat. She never asked anyone for help. You could transfer her to another town and she would find the counter.","zh":"我奶奶每个月都要寄一个包裹，那镇上的邮局慢得很。有一次她付了快递的加急费，结果还是晚了五天才到。她会自己把箱子挪到柜台前，等着职员填单子。能亲手送的时候，她喜欢自己送去。冬天河上来的空气里带着一股硬风，她就抱着箱子贴在外套上站在外头。她从没开口求过谁帮忙。把她换到另一个镇子，她也能找到那个柜台。"},"serve":{"tw":[["answer",0],["act",3],["move",2],["hold",6],["help",3],["admit",3],["spend",2],["rest",6],["service",0]],"en":"My father served in that shop for thirty-one years, and he would not admit that he had ever wanted another life. He had to hold two jobs in the first years and would spend his rest day behind the counter. He could act as cook, driver, or watchman, whichever was needed. When a customer asked something he could not answer, he would move to the back room and look it up. He did not serve people for the money; he said it was a service you did for the street. Nobody ever helped him close up. I did not understand that until I had a shop of my own.","zh":"父亲在那家铺子里干了三十一年，他从不承认自己想过换一种活法。头几年他得兼两份工，休息日也在柜台后面过。他什么都能顶上：厨子、司机、看夜的。有客人问到他答不上来的事，他就走到后屋去查。他服务人不是为了钱，他说这是给这条街做的一件事。从来没人帮他收过摊。这话我到自己开了铺子才懂。"},"service":{"tw":[["help",0],["none",3],["care",2],["private",6],["serve",0],["stand",3],["company",2],["travel",6],["overhaul",0]],"en":"The bus service in that valley had none of the comforts of a city line. The company ran three old buses, and they would serve the villages twice a day if the road was clear. A private car was a luxury nobody had. When the rain came there was no help at the stop, but my mother would stand there for an hour in it and still say a good word for the driver. The care they took with the old machines was real. Every autumn the company would overhaul each one, and then the winter travel was safe. She never once complained. The buses stopped running in the end.","zh":"那条谷里的公交服务，跟城里的线路一点没法比。公司只有三辆旧车，路通的时候一天往村里跑两趟。私家车是谁也买不起的奢侈品。下起雨来，站台上也没人帮她，可母亲还是会在雨里站上一个钟头，上车后还要替司机说句好话。他们对那些老机器是真上心。每年秋天公司会把每辆车大修一遍，这样冬天的出行才安全。她一次也没抱怨过。后来那几趟车还是停了。"},"settle":{"tw":[["decide",0],["clear",3],["accept",2],["aside",6],["fall",0],["judge",3],["agree",2],["dispute",6],["determine",0]],"en":"The dispute over the two fields had gone on since before I was born, and nobody could decide who was right. My father would set the whole thing aside each winter and say it would settle itself. Then the old judge came out of retirement and agreed to hear it. He spent a day walking the ground until the line between the fields was clear. He determined that the hedge had moved, not the stone. Both families had to accept it. The matter fell quiet after that, and the two of them spoke again. I think they were both relieved.","zh":"那两块地的事，从我没出生就争起，谁对谁错没人说得清。父亲每年冬天都把这事搁到一边，说它自己会了结。后来那位老法官退了休又出来，答应听这件事。他用了一天在地里走，直到两家的界线弄清楚了。他判定是篱笆动了，不是那块石头。两家都得认。这以后事情就沉了下去，两个人也重新说话了。我想他们都松了口气。"},"shake":{"tw":[["excite",0],["roll",3],["change",2],["pull",6],["rock",0],["fan",3],["drink",2],["hard",6],["shiver",0]],"en":"The whole house would shake when the lorry went past, and the plates on the shelf would roll towards the edge. My mother would pull the window shut and fan herself with a piece of card. The news that summer was enough to excite anyone, and the town seemed about to change. I would rock on the veranda and drink cold tea in the heat. It was hard to sleep. Once I saw my father shiver in July, which frightened me more than the news did. He said it was only the fever. He was never quite the same after it.","zh":"卡车开过的时候，整栋房子都晃，架上的盘子在往边沿滚。母亲会把窗关上，拿一张硬纸片扇风。那年夏天的消息，谁听了都激动，整个镇子像是要变。我就坐在廊下摇着，热天里喝凉茶。很难睡得着。有一回我看见父亲七月里发抖，这比那些消息还让我害怕。他说只是发烧。那以后他就不太一样了。"},"shape":{"tw":[["build",0],["chip",3],["body",2],["structure",6],["figure",3],["cup",3],["cause",2],["fit",6],["form",0]],"en":"The cup had a chip on one side, and that alone changed the shape of the whole thing. My father would hold it up and study the form of it, the curve of the handle, the way it fitted his hand. He said the structure of a good cup is a small piece of engineering. His own body was failing by then, and he had lost the figure he once had. He would build shelves in the shed to keep his hands busy. Nobody could tell him the cause of the chip. He liked the cup more for it. I keep it on my desk now.","zh":"那只杯子的边上崩了一小块，就这一块把整只杯子的样子都改了。父亲会把它举起来，看它的形，看柄的弯，看它握在手里的样子。他说一只好杯子的构造，就是一件小小的工程。那时他自己的身体在垮，原来的身架也没了。他在棚子里做架子，好让手闲不下来。谁也说不出那块崩口是怎么来的。因为这个，他反而更喜欢这只杯子。它现在放在我的桌上。"},"share":{"tw":[["deal",0],["cut",3],["use",2],["profit",6],["portion",0],["end",3],["attempt",2],["stock",6],["parcel",0]],"en":"The deal over the shop was that each of the three would take a share of the profit, and each would have a portion of the stock. My father's cut was the smallest, and at the end of the first year it came to nothing. He made one attempt to change it and was refused. He would parcel out the work himself and use his own van to move the goods. He never said a bitter word about it in front of the others. I only learned how bad it was years later, from a letter he never sent. I still have that letter.","zh":"关于那家铺子的约定是：三个人各分一份利润，各拿一部分存货。父亲那一份最小，第一年到头什么也没落下。他试过一次要改，被回绝了。他自己把活计分派下去，用自己的车拉货。在别人面前他从没说过一句怨话。过了好些年我才知道那有多糟，是从一封他从没寄出的信里看到的。那封信我还留着。"},"ship":{"tw":[["send",0],["forward",3],["board",2],["vessel",6],["transport",0],["tender",3],["move",2],["boat",6],["embark",0]],"en":"The ship was a small vessel that had been used to transport coal, and by that year it could hardly move. Men would send their boxes down to the harbour and then wait to board. A tender took them out in two trips, and the crossing itself lasted nine hours. Nobody embarked without a paper bag in hand. My mother would stand at the rail and look forward, past the bows, at nothing in particular. She said a boat is only a boat until the land goes away. Half the village came down to see it off. It never came back up the coast.","zh":"那条船是条运过煤的小船，到那年几乎开不动了。男人们把箱子送到港口，然后等着上船。一艘接驳船分两趟把人送上去，横渡本身要走九个钟头。谁上船手里都拎着个纸袋。母亲会站在栏杆边朝前看，越过船头，什么也不特别看。她说，船就是船，直到陆地消失。半村人都下来送它。它再没有沿着海岸回来过。"},"shoot":{"tw":[["charge",0],["break",3],["fire",2],["sneak",6],["film",0],["chip",3],["grow",2],["catch",6],["hit",2]],"en":"My uncle used to shoot with an old camera, not a gun, and he would sneak up on birds in the garden to get them close. He had to charge the battery for a day before each trip, and if the film was not loaded the whole morning was lost. He would catch a bird in the middle of a jump, wings up, and then grow quiet for an hour. Once a chip of stone hit the lens and he had to stop. He said a photograph is a small fire you keep alive. Nobody could break the habit. He did it until he was eighty-two.","zh":"我叔拍照，用的是台老相机，不是枪，他会悄悄靠近园子里的鸟，凑得很近。每次出门前电池都要充一天，胶卷要是没装好，一早上就白费了。他能拍到鸟腾空的一瞬，翅膀张着，然后他会安静一个钟头。有一次一块碎石打到镜头上，他只好停下。他说，一张照片就是一小簇你得看着不让它灭的火。这习惯谁也改不了。他一直拍到八十二岁。"},"shop":{"tw":[["store",0],["market",3],["course",2],["warehouse",6],["rat",0],["antique",3],["inform",2],["factory",6],["frequent",0]],"en":"The shop was a store of old things, and half of what was in it came from a warehouse on the other side of the market. My mother was such a frequent visitor that the owner would inform her of every new arrival. Over the years she took a course in antique glass, and she could tell a copy from the real thing across the room. There was a rat in the back that nobody could catch. In front of the door stood a table of small chairs made in a factory somewhere. I have the one she bought. It is the only thing of hers I kept.","zh":"那家铺子是个卖旧东西的店，里面一半的东西来自市场另一头的一个仓库。母亲去得太勤了，店主每有新货就跟她说。这些年她上过一门古董玻璃的课，隔着屋子就能看出哪件是仿的。后头有只老鼠，谁也抓不着。门前摆着一张桌子，上面是某个厂子做的小椅子。她买的那把在我这儿。她的东西我只留了这一件。"},"sleep":{"tw":[["rest",2],["bundle",3],["accommodate",2],["wake",1],["pain",6],["nap",3],["hibernate",3],["awake",6],["slumber",0]],"en":"My grandfather could sleep anywhere, at any hour, and he would take a nap sitting up. The house had to accommodate nine people, so he would roll himself in a bundle of coats and lie down in the corner. He would never wake before six, even when the pain in his back was bad. In winter he slept like something that hibernates, and we would not disturb him for any reason. My grandmother used to say that sleep was his rest and his medicine both. I do not think he was ever fully awake before noon. His slumber was the deepest I have ever known.","zh":"我爷爷在哪儿都能睡，什么钟点都能睡，还能坐着打盹。那屋子得住九个人，他就把自己裹进一摞外套里，往墙角一躺。他总是六点前不醒，哪怕背疼得厉害。冬天他睡得像个冬眠的东西，我们有什么事都不去吵他。奶奶常说，睡觉对他既是休息也是药。我看他中午以前就没完全醒过。他那种沉睡，是我见过最深的。"},"slip":{"tw":[["mistake",2],["lead",3],["forget",2],["bounce",6],["steal",0],["stay",3],["move",2],["knock",6],["trip",0]],"en":"I made one slip on the wet step, and the whole tray went over. It was a small mistake, but it led to three days of cleaning. I did not want to forget how it felt, so I wrote the date on the wall of the yard. A ball would bounce against that wall all afternoon. Somebody had tried to steal the milk twice that month, and my mother would not stay quiet about it. She would move the box inside every night and knock the ice off the step. After my trip on the ice, she bought a mat. I still watch that step.","zh":"我在湿台阶上滑了一跤，整盘东西都翻了。这错不大，可害我收拾了三天。我不想忘了那种滋味，就把日子写在院墙上。整个下午都有球往那面墙上弹。那个月有人两次想偷牛奶，母亲不肯把这事忍着不说。她每天夜里把箱子搬进屋，再把台阶上的冰敲掉。我在冰上绊那一回之后，她买了块垫子。那个台阶我现在还会多看一眼。"},"smell":{"tw":[["feel",0],["nose",3],["suggest",2],["smoke",6],["look",0],["scent",3],["atmosphere",2],["stench",6],["sense",0]],"en":"When I opened the kitchen door, the smell of smoke met me at once. My nose knew something was wrong before my eyes did, and the whole room had a heavy atmosphere. I could feel the heat from the old stove. A thin line of smoke rose from a pan, and the stench grew worse every second. I looked under the pan and found a black mark. That would suggest the wires had burned. I lost all sense of time and just stood there. Some sweet scent from yesterday's bread still hung in the air, which made the moment even stranger.","zh":"我推开厨房门，一股烟味马上扑过来。眼睛还没看见，鼻子就已经知道出了事，整间屋子都弥漫着一股沉闷的气息。我能感觉到那台旧炉子的热气。一缕烟从锅里升起来，臭味一秒比一秒重。我往锅底下看，发现一块黑色的印子。那说明电线已经烧了。我一时没了时间感，只是呆站着。昨天剩下的面包的甜香还飘在空气里，让这一刻更古怪。"},"smoke":{"tw":[["pot",0],["cigarette",3],["pitch",2],["dust",6],["weed",0],["inhale",3],["consume",2],["smell",6],["fume",0]],"en":"My uncle spent the morning burning dry weed in the back yard. Thick smoke rose from the pile and hung above the fence. He said the fumes would keep the insects away. I helped him carry the old pot and watched the dust settle on everything. He lit a cigarette and stood there, watching the fire eat the wood. The smoke was black as pitch. I had to hold my breath, because every time I tried to inhale, my throat hurt. The smell stayed on my coat for days, and the fire seemed to consume the whole pile before noon.","zh":"我叔一上午都在后院烧干草。浓烟从草堆上升起来，挂在篱笆上方。他说这些烟能把虫子赶走。我帮他搬来那只旧锅，看着灰尘落在所有东西上。他点了根烟站着，看火一点点吃掉木头。烟黑得像沥青。我只好屏住呼吸，因为每次想吸气，喉咙就疼。那股味儿在我外套上留了好几天，火到中午前像是把整堆都吞掉了。"},"sort":{"tw":[["class",0],["count",3],["choose",2],["mind",6],["form",0],["like",3],["category",2],["sense",6],["screen",0]],"en":"On Saturday my sister helped sort books at the charity shop. The manager asked her to count every box first and then choose a place for each one. In her mind, the books fell into two groups: those people would like, and those nobody would touch. She had to form a clear plan. Each class of book went to its own shelf, and every category had a small sign. She used an old screen to check the covers for damage. It made good sense to keep the children's books low, where small hands could reach them. By five, the whole shop looked new.","zh":"周六我妹妹去慈善商店帮忙整理书。店长让她先把每个箱子数一遍，再给每本书挑个位置。在她心里，书分成两类：人们会喜欢的，和谁都不碰的。她得理出一个清楚的计划。每一类书各上自己的架，每个类别都配个小牌子。她用一块旧筛板检查封面有没有破损。把童书放低、让小手够得着，这很合理。到五点，整家店看着像新的。"},"spot":{"tw":[["bit",0],["end",3],["change",2],["bottom",6],["position",0],["high",3],["dirty",2],["straight",6],["post",0]],"en":"We walked until we found a quiet spot at the end of the lake, just past a wooden post. From that high position we could see the whole valley. My boots were dirty from the long path, and there was a small bit of mud on my coat. I put the map straight on the ground and sat down. The place had not changed much since our last visit. At the bottom of the hill, the water was almost still. It was a good spot for lunch. Then a cold wind came, and we knew it was time to move on.","zh":"我们一直走到湖的尽头，才找到一处安静的落脚点，就在一根木桩过去一点。站上那个高处，整个山谷都看得见。走了这么长的路，我的靴子脏了，外套上也有一小点泥。我把地图直接摊在地上，坐了下来。这地方跟上次来比没什么变化。山脚下，水面几乎不动。在这儿吃午饭挺好。后来起了冷风，我们就知道该走了。"},"spring":{"tw":[["form",0],["burst",3],["grow",2],["summer",6],["jump",2],["hop",3],["move",2],["winter",6],["bounce",3]],"en":"In spring the garden began to grow again, and my little sister could not sit still. She would jump on the old sofa, whose springs had lost their form years ago, and every hop sent her a little higher. I told her to bounce gently, but she would not move. All summer she practised, and by winter she could land on her feet. One cold morning the old spring burst through the cloth and cut the seat. She cried for a minute, then said it was only cloth, and asked when we could buy a new one before next spring.","zh":"春天一到，园子又开始生长，我妹妹坐不住。她在那张旧沙发上蹦，沙发的弹簧早没了形，每跳一下都把她弹得高一点。我叫她轻点弹，她就是不肯挪窝。整个夏天她都在练，到冬天已经能稳稳落地。一个冷早上，那根旧弹簧顶破布面，把坐垫划开了。她哭了一分钟，然后说不过是块布罢了，还问我们能不能在明年春天前买个新的。"},"square":{"tw":[["straight",0],["plaza",3],["position",2],["round",1],["around",6],["feather",0],["settle",2],["gate",6],["solid",0]],"en":"The old plaza had a small square of grass in the middle, and a low gate at each corner. I stood in one position and looked straight across it. A white feather drifted through the air, went round once, and then began to settle on the ground. Around the square, people walked slowly in the evening light. The stone under my feet felt solid and cold. Nothing moved except the feather. I thought of all the feet that had crossed this ground before mine. I waited a long time, and at last it came to rest at the edge of the grass.","zh":"那座老广场中央有一小块方形草地，四个角各有一道矮门。我站在一个位置上，笔直地望过去。一根白羽毛在空中飘着，转了一圈，慢慢落向地面。广场四周，人们在暮色里慢慢走着。脚下的石头又硬又凉。除了那根羽毛，什么也没动。我想起在我之前有多少双脚踩过这片地。我等了很久，它最后停在草地边上。"},"stay":{"tw":[["check",2],["stand",3],["act",2],["change",1],["leave",6],["continue",0],["meet",2],["wait",6],["rest",0]],"en":"I had to check in at the small hotel and then decide whether to stay the night. The woman behind the desk did not act surprised when I asked for a quiet room. I said I would wait, and had to stand by the window while she looked for a key. Outside, the rain had started, and that made the choice easier. Then she said the price would not change, so I could stay as long as I liked. I had planned to meet a friend, but I was too tired. I decided to leave it till morning and continue my journey after a good rest.","zh":"我得先在小旅馆办入住，再决定要不要住一晚。我说想要个安静的房间，柜台后的女人一点不显得意外。我说我等，就站在窗边，看她找钥匙。外面下起了雨，这让选择容易了些。她说价钱不会变，我想住多久都行。我本来打算见个朋友，可实在累了。我决定推到早上，好好歇一晚再继续赶路。"},"steal":{"tw":[["buy",0],["hook",3],["move",2],["grab",6],["slip",0],["pocket",3],["gain",2],["retrieve",6],["bargain",0]],"en":"At the market my cousin tried to steal a small silver hook from a table. He did not want to buy it; he only wanted the gain. I watched his hand move toward it and grab the edge of the cloth. A coin began to slip from his pocket and fell on the ground. The old woman turned and saw him. He tried to retrieve it, but she had already picked it up. We had to bargain hard before she let us leave. In the end we paid for it, and I told him never to try that again.","zh":"在集市上，我表弟想从一张桌子上偷一个小银钩。他不是想买，只想占那个便宜。我看着他的手朝它伸过去，抓住布边。一枚硬币开始从他口袋里滑出来，掉在地上。老妇人转过身看见了他。他想把它捡回去，可她已经先拿在手里了。我们费了好大劲讨价还价，她才放我们走。最后我们付了钱，我告诉他以后再也别干这种事。"},"step":{"tw":[["measure",0],["cut",3],["mark",2],["push",6],["tone",0],["trip",3],["move",2],["change",6],["abuse",0]],"en":"The carpenter took one step back and looked at the board again. The old shop was quiet except for the saw. He had to measure it twice before he could cut it clean. With a pencil he made a small mark near the end. His tone was quiet, but he did not like to be pushed. If anyone rushed him, he would stop and say there was no need for abuse. A single wrong move could ruin the whole piece. Nothing would change his way of working. As he lifted the wood, he nearly tripped over a box on the floor.","zh":"木匠往后退了一步，又看了看那块木板。这间旧作坊里除了锯子声，静得很。他量了两遍才下刀，切得利落。他用铅笔在末端画了个小记号。他语气很轻，但不喜欢被人催。谁要是催他，他就停下来说用不着那样数落人。一个动作做错，整块料就毁了。没什么能改他的做法。他抬木头时，差点被地上的箱子绊倒。"},"stick":{"tw":[["beat",0],["club",3],["force",2],["loose",6],["stay",0],["bow",3],["leg",2],["right",6],["bind",3]],"en":"In the garden my grandfather used a straight stick to hold up a young tree. He would bind it with a soft rope, but not too tight, and leave the knot loose. When the wind was strong, the tree had to stay upright, so he pushed the stick deep into the soil. He had to use some force, because the ground was hard. His dog lay at his right leg and watched. If the dog came too close, he would gently beat the grass with a small club. Then he would bow his head and check the rope once more.","zh":"在园子里，我爷爷用一根直木棍撑住一棵小树。他用软绳把它绑起来，但不绑太紧，结留得松松的。风大的时候树得立住，所以他把木棍深深插进土里。他得使点劲，因为地很硬。他的狗趴在他右腿边看着。狗要是靠太近，他就用小木棒轻轻打一下草。然后他低下头，又检查了一遍绳子。"},"still":{"tw":[["however",0],["compose",3],["change",2],["though",6],["quiet",5],["gag",3],["comfort",2],["once",6],["calm",5]],"en":"The house was still at last, and the night air felt calm and cool. My mother sat by the lamp to compose a long letter. She said the quiet was a comfort after such a busy week. However, she did not stay calm for long. Once the phone rang, she had to stop. Though she tried to keep her tone even, I could hear that something had changed. She made a small gag about her own memory, and we both laughed. I felt the day fall away from me. Then she went back to her page, and the room grew still again.","zh":"屋里终于静下来了，夜里的空气又凉又平和。我妈坐在灯边写一封长信。她说忙了一周，这份安静是种安慰。可她没能安静多久。电话一响，她就得停下。虽然她努力把语气放平，我还是听出有什么变了。她拿自己的记性开了个小玩笑，我们俩都笑了。我觉得这一天的疲惫都落了下去。然后她又回到那页纸上，屋里重新静了下来。"},"stone":{"tw":[["rock",0],["crystal",3],["kill",2],["wood",6],["pit",0],["gravel",3],["material",2],["brick",6],["gem",0]],"en":"My father was digging a pit in the yard when his spade hit a large stone. He set the rock aside and looked at it. The soil around it was dry and hard. It was heavy and grey, the same material as the wall behind him. He had built that wall himself, brick by brick, and mixed the gravel with his own hands. Under the stone he found a small crystal that shone like a gem. He said it was not worth much, but it would not kill anyone to keep it. Beside it lay a piece of old wood, black with age.","zh":"我爸在院子里挖坑，铁锹碰到一块大石头。他把那块石头挪到一边看。周围的土又干又硬。它又重又灰，和他身后那堵墙是同一种料。那墙是他自己一块砖一块砖砌的，沙砾也是他亲手和的。石头下面，他发现一小块水晶，亮得像宝石。他说这不值多少钱，可留着也不碍事。旁边还躺着一块旧木头，黑得发陈。"},"strike":{"tw":[["discover",0],["beat",3],["blow",2],["halt",6],["fall",0],["bottom",3],["find",2],["break",6],["hit",0]],"en":"A heavy storm was about to strike the small town, and the workers had to halt their work at the old factory. They had already planned a strike for better pay, and now the weather made things worse. The first blow of wind came at noon. It was strong enough to beat against the windows and break a branch off the tree. I ran to find my father at the bottom of the yard. A stone fell and hit the roof. My mother called us in, but nobody moved. That night we would discover that the whole wall had begun to crack.","zh":"一场大雨要打向小镇，老工厂的工人只好停下手里的活。他们本来就打算罢工要求加钱，现在天气又添了乱。正午刮来第一阵风，猛烈得拍打窗户，还吹断了一根树枝。我跑去院子最里头找我爸。一块石头掉下来砸在屋顶上。我妈喊我们进屋，可谁也没动。那天晚上我们才发现，整堵墙已经开始裂了。"},"stuff":{"tw":[["block",0],["paper",3],["fill",2],["fun",6],["material",0],["waste",3],["push",2],["maybe",6],["shove",0]],"en":"The garage was full of stuff nobody had used for years. My brother and I had to block the door and sort it into piles. There were boxes of old paper, and a great deal of waste we could not keep. The whole job was not much fun. We would push one heavy box, then shove another out to the road. Maybe, I said, we should just leave it all. By noon the space was clear, and we used the last box to fill the gap under the shelf. My mother said the whole material would go to the recycling van.","zh":"车库里堆满了多少年没人用的东西。我和弟弟只好把门堵上，一点点分成堆。有几箱旧纸张，还有一大堆留不得的废品。这活儿一点不好玩。我们推走一个沉箱子，又把另一个搡到路边。我说，也许干脆全扔了算了。到中午，地方空出来了，我们用最后一个箱子填上架子下面的空当。我妈说这些材料都要给回收车拉走。"},"subject":{"tw":[["field",0],["major",3],["term",2],["context",6],["issue",0],["question",3],["affect",2],["instance",6],["matter",0]],"en":"In my first term at college I had to choose a main subject. My teacher said the choice would affect the rest of my life, which I thought was too much to say. I liked history best, because it is a field where every small issue has a context. She asked me a simple question: what do I want to do with it? For instance, I could study law, or teach. She told me there was no need to hurry. It did not matter how long I took. In the end I picked history as my major, and I have never been sorry.","zh":"上大学的第一个学期，我得选一门主修科目。老师说这个选择会影响我一辈子，我觉得这话说得太满了。我最喜欢历史，因为在这个领域里，每个小问题都有自己的来龙去脉。她问了我一个简单的问题：我打算拿它做什么？比如，我可以学法律，也可以去教书。她说不用着急。最后我选了历史作主修，从没后悔过。"},"suit":{"tw":[["cause",0],["agree",3],["meet",2],["complaint",6],["fit",0],["trump",3],["match",2],["white",6],["accommodate",0]],"en":"At the club we would meet every Friday to play cards in the back room. My uncle always wore the same old suit, grey and worn, and a white shirt that no longer fit him well. He would never agree to change it. He liked to hold his cards close and wait for a good match. When he finally played a trump, the whole table went quiet. His only complaint was that the room could not accommodate so many players. Nobody could cause him to hurry. He said a good suit of cards, like a good suit of clothes, needs patience.","zh":"在俱乐部，我们每周五都在里屋碰头打牌。我叔总穿着同一套旧西装，灰扑扑的，还有件早就不合身的白衬衫。他从不答应换。他喜欢把牌捏得紧紧的，等一手好牌。等他一甩出王牌，整张桌子都安静了。他唯一的抱怨是这屋子坐不下这么多人。谁也催不动他。他说一副好牌跟一套好衣服一样，都得有耐心。"},"support":{"tw":[["back",3],["accept",3],["act",2],["aim",6],["bear",0],["carry",3],["agree",2],["maintain",6],["hold",0]],"en":"The old bridge could no longer hold the weight of the trucks, and the town had to act fast. My father worked there for a month, helping to build new support under each end. His aim was simple: to make it safe again. He would carry heavy beams and bear the cold wind without a word. At home, my mother had to maintain the house alone, and my back began to ache from the work. In the end we all had to accept that we could not agree on everything. People came from far away to see it. The new bridge opened in spring.","zh":"那座老桥再也撑不住卡车的重量，镇上必须赶快动手。我爸在那儿干了一个月，帮着在两头重建支撑。他的目的很简单：让它重新变结实。他扛起重梁，顶着冷风一句怨言也没有。在家里，我妈得一个人撑着这个家，我的背也开始因为干活而酸痛。最后我们都得接受，不可能事事都意见一致。人们从老远赶来看新桥。新桥在春天通了。"},"table":{"tw":[["board",0],["call",3],["arrange",2],["sit",6],["defer",0],["hold",3],["delay",2],["open",6],["postpone",0]],"en":"The board was going to meet at the long table on Monday, but the manager had to postpone it. He said he would call each member and arrange a new time. I had to sit in the empty room while he made his calls. The delay was not his fault; the figures were not ready. He decided to defer the whole thing until the numbers were checked. I wrote a short note on the table and left it there. On Tuesday he called again to say the meeting would hold on Friday, and the room would open at nine.","zh":"董事会本来周一要在那张长桌边开会，可经理不得不推迟。他说会挨个打电话通知大家，另约时间。他打电话的时候，我只能坐在空屋里等。这次拖延不怪他，数字还没弄好。他决定等数字核对完再谈整件事。我在桌上写了张短条留在那儿。周二他又打来电话，说会议改在周五开，房间九点开门。"},"talk":{"tw":[["mouth",0],["continue",3],["address",2],["why",6],["sing",3],["shout",3],["conversation",2],["call",6],["speak",0]],"en":"The old teacher gave a talk about the river to a room of students. She did not shout, and she never had to call for quiet. When she opened her mouth, everyone listened. She would speak slowly and then continue, as if she had all night. Her address was simple and warm, and it held our attention to the end. I did not want that hour to end, and I took notes all the way through. Afterwards a girl asked why the water had changed colour. That short conversation stayed with me for years. Sometimes, walking home, I still hear her speak, and I could sing her words like a song.","zh":"那位老教师在一屋子学生面前做了一场关于这条河的演讲。她不喊，也从不用叫大家安静。她一开口，所有人都听着。她慢慢讲，接着往下说，好像有一整夜的时间。她的话朴素又温和，一直把我们吸引到最后。我舍不得那一小时结束，从头到尾都在记笔记。散场后一个女孩问，为什么河水变了颜色。那段短短的交谈我记了好多年。有时回家的路上，我还能听见她说话，真想把她的话像歌一样唱出来。"},"taste":{"tw":[["try",0],["finish",3],["experience",2],["mix",6],["sample",0],["sweet",3],["know",2],["blend",6],["smack",0]],"en":"My aunt let me try her soup before dinner. I had to sample it twice, because the first taste was too sweet. She wanted to know if the blend was right, so she mixed in a little salt and let me taste again. It was not the taste I expected, and for a moment I did not know what to say. I had never had that experience before. She said cooking was like this: you have to finish slowly and trust your own mouth. When the soup was right, she would smack her lips and smile. The whole kitchen smelled of herbs.","zh":"晚饭前，我姑姑让我尝尝她的汤。我得尝两遍，因为第一口的味道太甜了。她想知道混得对不对，就加了一点点盐，又让我尝。这味道和我预想的不一样，有那么一会儿我不知道该说什么。这种体验我以前从没有过。她说做菜就是这样：得慢慢收尾，还要信自己的嘴。汤对味了，她就咂咂嘴笑一下。整间厨房都是香草味。"},"tear":{"tw":[["charge",0],["shred",3],["cry",2],["riot",6],["pull",0],["cleave",3],["drop",2],["disperse",6],["rent",3]],"en":"The news said there had been a riot in the town square, and the police had to charge into the crowd. People began to disperse along the side streets, and some ran past our gate. My mother sat by the window and started to cry. She held an old letter and began to pull at it, as if she wanted to shred it or cleave it in two. A single tear made a drop on the paper. Then she tore it clean, and the rent showed a name she had tried to forget. I did not ask her about the name. The crowd was gone by dark.","zh":"新闻说镇广场上出了乱子，警察不得不冲进人群。人们沿着小巷四散开，有人从我们家门口跑过。我妈坐在窗边，哭了起来。她拿着一封旧信，开始拉扯，像是要把它撕碎，或者干脆掰成两半。一滴眼泪落在纸上。然后她把它撕开，那道口子里露出一个她想忘掉的名字。我没问她那是谁。天黑前，人群散了。"},"test":{"tw":[["run",0],["control",3],["check",2],["final",6],["try",0],["float",3],["attempt",2],["match",6],["exam",0]],"en":"On the day of the final exam, my hands would not stay still. I had made one last attempt to check my notes the night before. The teacher said we could not run out of time if we worked steadily. Halfway through, I lost control of my pen and dropped it. I had to try again from the top of the page. Later, at the pond, we put my small boat in the water to see if it would float. It did not sink, and it did not match the design in my book, but it was a good test.","zh":"期末考试那天，我的手一直静不下来。前一晚我还做了最后一次尝试，把笔记对了一遍。老师说只要稳稳地做，时间就不会不够。做到一半，我握不住笔，把它掉在了地上。我只好从这页的最上面重新来。后来在池塘边，我们把我的小船放进水里，看它能不能浮起来。它没沉，虽然和我书上画的样子不太一样，但这算是一次不错的试验。"},"think":{"tw":[["consider",0],["feel",3],["change",2],["why",6],["guess",0],["hold",3],["concentrate",2],["sure",6],["imagine",2]],"en":"I sat on the step and tried to think about the offer. I had to consider what I would lose if I left my old job. My mother said I should hold on a little longer and not change too fast. I could not guess what the manager really wanted. When I tried to concentrate, my mind went blank. I began to imagine a small flat in another town, with a window I could open. The evening light made everything look far away. I was not sure about anything. I asked myself why I felt so afraid of a simple choice.","zh":"我坐在台阶上，想好好琢磨那份工作机会。我得想清楚，辞掉旧工作会失去什么。我妈说再撑一撑，别换得太急。我猜不透经理到底要什么。想集中精神的时候，脑子却一片空白。我开始想象另一座城里的一间小公寓，有一扇能推开的窗户。暮色让一切都显得很远。我什么都不确定。我问自己，为什么一个简单的选择会让我这么怕。"},"throw":{"tw":[["drop",0],["ground",3],["express",2],["grab",6],["hold",0],["pass",3],["move",2],["ball",6],["cast",0]],"en":"In the yard the boys would throw a worn ball to each other until the light went. My little brother could not hold it long; he would drop it, then grab it again from the ground. He wanted to express how fast he could move, so he ran around us in a circle. When I tried to pass the ball to him, he missed. It was only a game, so we both laughed. On his next try he would cast it so high that we had to run after it. Our father said a good throw comes from the whole body, not just the arm.","zh":"院子里，男孩们会把一个旧球互相扔来扔去，直到天光暗下来。我弟弟抱不了多久，球会掉下去，他再从地上捡起来。他想让人看看自己跑得多快，就绕着我们跑了一圈。我想把球传给他，他接丢了。这本来就是个玩，我们俩都笑了。下一回他把球扔得老高，我们只好追着跑。我爸说，好的一投靠的是整个身子，不只是手臂。"},"tire":{"tw":[["wear",0],["retire",3],["consume",2],["refresh",1],["brake",6],["exhaust",3],["devolve",2],["wheel",6],["weary",0]],"en":"On the long drive home, one front tire began to wear thin, and the car started to pull to the side. My father had to brake slowly and stop by the road. He was too weary to change the wheel himself, and the heat would exhaust him further. He said the journey had begun to consume his strength. His plan was to retire early that year, and now he wished he had. We found a small garage where the work devolved to a young mechanic, who put on a spare. A short rest seemed to refresh my father, and by dusk we were moving again.","zh":"开车回家的长途上，一只前胎越来越薄，车开始往一边偏。我爸只好慢慢刹车，停在路边。他太累了，自己换不动轮子，天热又让他更乏。他说这趟路开始耗他的力气。他本来就打算那年早点退休，这时真希望自己已经退了。我们找到一家小修理铺，活儿落到一个年轻师傅手里，他装上了备胎。歇了这一小会儿，我爸像是缓过来了，天擦黑时我们又上路了。"},"track":{"tw":[["course",0],["drive",3],["bar",2],["speed",6],["cover",0],["round",3],["line",2],["tour",6],["cross",0]],"en":"The old track beside the river had been laid for a small train, but now people used it for a race. My uncle would drive us there and wait by the wooden bar at the gate. The riders had to cover three rounds before the finish, and their speed was hard to believe. Each one kept to his own line. A guide gave us a short tour of the sheds before the start. The dust they raised hung over the path. We watched them cross the far end of the course, then come back toward us in a wide curve.","zh":"河边那条旧轨道原本是给一列小火车铺的，如今人们拿它来赛跑。我叔会开车带我们去，在门口的横木边等着。骑手们要跑完三圈才算完，他们的速度快得让人不敢信。每个人都守着自己那条线。开赛前，一个向导带我们简短地看了看那些棚子。他们扬起的尘土飘在小路上。我们看着他们冲过赛道那头，又划着一道大弯朝我们回来。"},"train":{"tw":[["check",0],["charge",3],["control",2],["taxi",6],["educate",2],["hold",3],["position",2],["traffic",6],["prepare",0]],"en":"We had to check the time before we left for the station, because the train would not wait. My mother called a taxi, and we sat in heavy traffic all the way across town. She could not control her worry. At the gate a woman in a uniform began to charge each passenger for the bags. We had to hold our tickets in our hands and prepare for the rush. The train stood in its usual position on the far platform. We reached the platform just in time. I used the long ride to educate myself about the city from the window.","zh":"出发前我们得先核对时间，因为火车不会等人。我妈叫了辆出租车，我们从城这头到那头一路堵着。她管不住自己的担心。检票口有个穿制服的女人开始按行李向每位乘客收费。我们只好把票攥在手里，为那阵拥挤做准备。火车就停在远处站台上它一贯的位置。我们及时赶到了站台。我一路上都在透过车窗让自己多了解这座城市。"},"treat":{"tw":[["address",0],["feed",3],["affect",2],["patient",6],["cover",0],["nurse",3],["provide",2],["pain",6],["deal",0]],"en":"The nurse had to treat an old patient whose pain had grown worse all week. She would feed him slowly and then cover him with a thin blanket. His illness had begun to affect his mood, and he did not like to deal with strangers. She knew his address by heart, though she had never been to his house. The hospital could not provide a private room, so he stayed in the ward. She told him she would treat him like her own father. One small kindness was enough for the day. He said she was the only one who had time for him.","zh":"那位护士要照料一位老病人，他疼了整整一周，越来越重。她会慢慢喂他吃饭，再给他盖上一床薄毯。病痛开始影响他的情绪，他也不喜欢跟生人打交道。她牢牢记着他的住址，虽然从没去过他家。医院腾不出单人病房，他就住在普通病房里。她对他说，会像照顾自己的父亲一样照料他。这一天，一点点善意就够了。他说，只有她还肯为他花时间。"},"trip":{"tw":[["slip",0],["run",3],["catch",2],["visit",6],["travel",3],["flight",3],["experience",2],["journey",6],["trigger",0]],"en":"Last summer we took a long trip to the coast. The flight was short, but the journey from the airport took hours. My sister had to run to catch the last bus and nearly made me slip on the wet steps. We planned to visit an old town the next morning. That was the experience I remember best: narrow streets, low doors, and a warm wind from the sea. Nothing seemed able to trigger a bad mood that week. Even when it began to rain, we only travelled more slowly and laughed about it. We did not want to go home.","zh":"去年夏天我们去了趟海边，路途很长。飞机很快就到，可从机场进城却花了几个小时。我妹妹得跑去赶末班车，还差点让我在湿台阶上滑一跤。我们打算第二天早上逛一座老城。那是我记得最清楚的一段：窄窄的街、矮矮的门，还有从海上吹来的暖风。那一周好像没什么能让人扫兴。就算下起雨来，我们也只是走慢一点，还笑个不停。我们都不想回家。"},"turn":{"tw":[["act",0],["better",3],["change",2],["hard",6],["bit",0],["bottom",3],["move",2],["enough",6],["grow",0]],"en":"The road made a sharp turn at the bottom of the hill, and we had to slow down. My father took each bend slowly, because the surface was hard and worn. A bit of rain had made it worse. Nothing could stop the car from sliding a little. He said the car would act strangely if we went too fast, and we did not have enough time to change a wheel. So he let me move over and take a turn at the wheel on the straight part. I grew more careful that day. We were both better drivers by the time we reached home.","zh":"山路在山脚下拐了个急弯，我们只好减速。每个弯我爸都开得很慢，因为路面又硬又旧。一点雨让它更糟。没什么能挡住车子稍微打滑。他说开太快车就会不听使唤，而我们又没时间换轮胎。于是他让我挪过去，在直路上由我开一段。那天我变得谨慎多了。到家的时候，我们俩都开得比以前好了。"},"view":{"tw":[["catch",0],["expect",3],["look",2],["beyond",6],["consider",3],["guess",3],["think",2],["clear",6],["position",0]],"en":"We climbed the hill to catch the view before it got dark. From that position the whole valley lay below us, clear to the far edge. You could look beyond the woods and guess where the river turned. I had not expected so much green. I began to consider how many people must have stood here before. My brother said he could not think of a better place. A cool wind came up, and the air felt thin and fresh. We stayed until the light went, and even then we did not want to leave. It was the kind of evening you remember for years.","zh":"我们爬上山，赶在天黑前看那片风景。站在那个位置，整个山谷都在脚下，一直到天边都清清楚楚。你可以望过树林，猜猜河在哪儿拐弯。我没料到会有这么多绿色。我开始想，从前有多少人站过这里。我弟弟说他想不出比这更好的地方。起了凉风，空气又薄又清。我们待到天光散尽，那时也不想走。这样的傍晚，能让人记上好多年。"},"visit":{"tw":[["call",3],["order",3],["meet",2],["trip",6],["see",3],["frequent",3],["stay",2],["attend",6],["chat",0]],"en":"On Sunday we paid a short visit to our neighbour. My mother made the call first to see if she was well enough for guests. We had to order some cakes on the way and pick them up at the shop. It was a small trip, but we liked to go. Our neighbour would meet us at the door and chat about her garden for an hour. She was a frequent host and never let us stay quiet. We would attend to whatever she asked and see to the tea. I always left feeling lighter than when I came.","zh":"星期天我们去看望了邻居，短坐一会儿。我妈先打了个电话，看她身体好点没有，能不能待客。路上我们还得订几块蛋糕，再到店里取。这一趟不远，但我们乐意去。邻居会在门口迎我们，然后聊上她园子里的花花草草，一聊就是一个钟头。她常常请客，从不让我们冷场。她让做什么我们就帮着做什么，再张罗茶水。每次走的时候，我都比来时轻松。"},"wash":{"tw":[["race",0],["pan",3],["clean",2],["brush",6],["lap",0],["soak",3],["cover",2],["drain",6],["laundry",0]],"en":"After dinner I had to wash the dishes while my sister dealt with the laundry. The pan had burned a little, so I had to soak it first. Then I took a brush to the hard marks and worked until the metal was clean. Water ran over the edge and began to cover the floor near the drain. The cat came to lap the water from the floor. My little brother ran a race around the table and splashed my legs. He thought it was funny. I let him have his fun, then went back to the sink and finished the rest.","zh":"晚饭后我得洗碗，我妹妹去弄要洗的衣服。锅底糊了一点，我先把它泡上。然后我拿刷子对着那些硬印子刷，直到锅底干净。水从边上漫出来，开始淹到下水道附近的地板。猫过来舔地上的水。我弟弟绕着桌子跑了一圈，把我的腿溅湿了。他觉得好玩。我让他闹了一阵，又回到水池边把剩下的洗完。"},"watch":{"tw":[["catch",0],["test",3],["shift",2],["why",6],["check",2],["wake",3],["surveillance",2],["look",6],["follow",0]],"en":"My uncle worked the night watch at a warehouse, and his shift began at ten. Every hour he had to check the doors and look at the small screen by the gate. The cameras gave him a kind of surveillance he did not enjoy. The alarm system gave a short test every evening. Once he had to follow a man along the fence and catch him at the corner. That night he could not wake me, but he told me the story the next day. I asked him why he stayed. He said a quiet job was a good job, and he would keep the watch as long as he could.","zh":"我叔在一间仓库上夜班，十点交接。每个钟头他都要查门，看一眼门口那台小屏幕。那些摄像头让他有种被盯着看的感觉，他并不喜欢。警报系统每晚都会做一次短测试。有一回，他得沿着围栏跟住一个人，在拐角处把他抓住。那天晚上他没能叫醒我，第二天才把这事讲给我听。我问他为什么还干这个。他说清静的活儿就是好活儿，能守多久他就守多久。"},"wear":{"tw":[["bear",0],["black",3],["act",2],["jacket",6],["break",0],["blue",3],["dress",2],["attire",6],["tire",0]],"en":"On a cold morning I could not decide what to wear. My old jacket had begun to break at the shoulder, and the blue dress I liked was much too thin. I did not want to act as if it did not matter. My mother said the black coat would bear the wind better, and that was the right attire for the day. She helped me into the jacket and checked the collar. I did not want to tire her with so many questions. In the end I wore the warm one and left. Outside it was still dark, and the frost lay on the gate.","zh":"一个冷早上，我拿不定主意穿什么。我那件旧外套肩膀开始开线，我喜欢的那条蓝裙子又太薄。我不想装得好像这无所谓。我妈说黑大衣更挡风，那天穿这个正合适。她帮我套上外套，看了看领子。我本不想拿一堆问题烦她，可她很耐心。最后我穿了那件暖和的出了门。外面天还黑着，门口的草上结着霜。"},"wet":{"tw":[["tight",0],["water",3],["change",2],["dry",1],["rain",6],["stiff",0],["sprinkle",3],["cool",6],["moisture",0]],"en":"The rain came in the afternoon and left the yard wet for hours. My shoes were tight and heavy with water, so I had to change them at the door. I hung my coat by the fire to dry, but the cloth stayed stiff and cold. A light sprinkle fell again just before evening. The cool air brought a little moisture into the room, and the windows felt damp. I stayed inside and listened to it on the roof. My mother said the weather would not last, and she was right. By morning the stones were dry again.","zh":"下午下起了雨，把院子打湿了好几个钟头。我的鞋又紧又重，全是水，进门就得换掉。我把外套挂在火边想烘干，布却一直又硬又凉。傍晚前，又飘了一阵小雨。凉气把一点湿意带进屋里，窗子摸上去潮潮的。我待在屋里，听着屋顶上的雨声。我妈说这天气长不了，她说对了。到早上，石头又干了。"},"wheel":{"tw":[["roll",0],["bowl",3],["force",2],["rear",6],["cycle",0],["ordinary",3],["machine",2],["brake",6],["rack",0]],"en":"The rear wheel of my bicycle began to rub against the brake, so I took the whole thing to the shop. An ordinary machine like mine still needs care, the man said. He put the frame in a rack and let the wheel roll on its own. I had to use some force to turn it, which showed where it was bent. He worked like a small cycle of small steps: lift, turn, and check. At last it spun freely. The shop smelled of oil and dust. He would not take money, so I left him a bowl of fruit from our garden.","zh":"我自行车后轮开始蹭刹车，我就整车推去了店里。那人说，像我这种普通机器也得照顾。他把车架架在架子上，让轮子自己转。我得使点劲才转得动，这一转就知道哪儿弯了。他干活像个小小的循环，一步一步来：抬起来、转一转、再查一查。最后轮子转得很顺。店里满是机油和灰尘的味道。他不肯收钱，我就把院子里摘的一碗水果留给了他。"},"whole":{"tw":[["altogether",0],["complex",3],["object",2],["half",1],["rest",6],["solid",0],["compound",3],["unit",3]],"en":"The old farm was a whole world of its own, made of several buildings joined into one compound. A solid stone wall ran all the way around it. My father treated the farm as a single unit, and he knew every part of it. Half of the roof needed work, and the rest would last a few more years. In spring the water came up from below. He said fixing it altogether was a complex job, not something one man could do in a week. The main object of his plan was simple: keep the yard dry. He would not rest until it was done.","zh":"那座旧农场自成一个小世界，几栋房子连成一片院子。一道结实的石墙绕了一圈。我爸把它当成一个整体，每一处他都熟。屋顶有一半要修，剩下的还能再撑几年。春天水会从底下冒上来。他说要整修下来是件复杂的事，不是一个人一周能干完的。他计划的主要目标很简单：让院子保持干燥。活儿不完，他就不肯歇。"},"win":{"tw":[["advance",0],["carry",3],["victory",2],["lose",1],["clinch",6],["gain",0],["hit",3],["chance",6],["acquire",0]],"en":"Our small team did not expect to win against the older players. We had to advance slowly and wait for a chance to hit the ball past them. In the second half my brother began to carry the whole side. One good shot helped us clinch the game at the last minute. The victory was small but real. Even the manager, who hated to lose, smiled at the end. We did not gain much money from it, but we did acquire something better: the belief that we could do it again. We shook hands with the other side and walked home in the dark.","zh":"我们这支小队伍没指望能赢那些年纪更大的对手。我们只能慢慢推进，等机会把球打到他们身后。下半场我弟弟开始一个人扛起全队。最后关头一个好球帮我们把比赛拿下。这场胜利不大，却是真的。连那个最输不起的教练，最后也笑了。我们没挣到多少钱，却得到了更好的东西：相信自己还能再来一次。我们跟对手握了手，摸黑走回家。"},"wish":{"tw":[["care",0],["hope",3],["express",2],["ask",6],["like",0],["please",3],["order",2],["tell",6],["want",0]],"en":"At the end of the meal my sister made a wish and blew out the candles. She would not tell us what it was, though we all asked. My mother said she hoped it would come true. To please her, I had ordered a small cake in the morning, the kind she likes best. Nobody wanted to leave the table. I tried to express how much that quiet evening meant to me, but the words did not come. So I only said I cared about her, and that was enough. The room felt warm even after the candles were out.","zh":"饭快吃完时，我妹妹许了个愿，吹灭了蜡烛。她不肯告诉我们许的什么愿，尽管我们都问了。我妈说但愿能成真。为了让她高兴，我早上订了个小蛋糕，是她最喜欢的那种。谁都不想离桌。我想说这个安静的晚上对我有多重要，可话到嘴边说不出来。于是我只好说我惦记她，这就够了。即便蜡烛灭了，屋里还是暖的。"},"work":{"tw":[["act",0],["answer",3],["fix",2],["idle",1],["well",6],["bring",0],["break",3],["own",6],["form",0]],"en":"For my first week at work I did not have much to do. The owner of the shop told me to act as if I had been there for years. My job was to fix small things: a broken lamp, a door that would not close, a table that stood badly. If I was idle too long, he would call me over and give me a new form to fill in. He would not answer questions during busy hours. The shop was small and warm. By Friday he said I had done well, and that he might bring me on full time.","zh":"上班的第一周，我没多少事做。店老板让我装得像是已经在这儿干了很多年。我的活儿是修些小东西：一盏坏灯、一扇关不严的门、一张放不平的桌子。我要是闲太久，他就把我叫过去，给我一张新表格填。忙的时候他是不回答问题的。店里又小又暖。到了周五，他说我干得不错，还说也许让我转正。"},"worry":{"tw":[["care",0],["fear",3],["mind",2],["say",6],["concern",0],["burden",3],["rub",2],["blame",6],["interest",0]],"en":"My mother began to worry when my brother did not come home by dark. She tried to hide her fear, but she kept looking at the door. In her mind she was already out in the street, searching for him. Her only concern was that something had gone wrong. I told her I would care for him, whatever had happened, and not to take the whole burden on herself. She would rub her hands together and say nothing. At last the phone rang, and we learned he had only missed the last bus. My father began to blame himself for letting him go alone. That night she had no interest in her dinner.","zh":"天黑了弟弟还没回家，我妈开始担心。她想藏住怕，可眼睛老往门口瞟。在她心里，人已经跑到街上找他去了。她只担心是不是出了什么事。我跟她说，不管发生了什么，我会照顾他，别把这份担子都压在自己身上。她只是搓着手，一句话不说。最后电话响了，我们才知道他只是错过了末班车。我爸开始怪自己不该让他一个人去。那之后她对晚饭一点兴趣都没有。"},"write":{"tw":[["save",0],["arrange",3],["record",2],["read",6],["pen",0],["cross",3],["trace",2],["book",6],["spell",0]],"en":"Every Sunday my grandmother would write a long letter to her sister. She kept a special pen for it and always used the same blue paper. I would read the words over her shoulder and watch her cross out a line, then write it again. She liked to arrange her thoughts first, so she would trace the shape of each word in the air before it went down. Each letter held a small record of the week. She told me to save every letter I ever received. Now I have a whole book of hers, and I still cannot spell some of the names she wrote.","zh":"每个星期天，我奶奶都会给她妹妹写一封长信。她为写信留着一支专门的笔，纸也总用同一种蓝的。我会从她肩后读那些字，看她划掉一行，再重写。她喜欢先理清想法，所以落笔前会在空气里描一描每个字的形状。每一封信都像一小份关于那一周的记录。她叫我把我收到的每一封信都留着。如今我有她整整一本书的信，可有些她写过的名字，我还是拼不出来。"},"church":{"tw":[["ecclesiastic",4],["cathedral",3],["body",2],["catholic",6],["basilica",3],["service",2],["chapel",6]],"en":"The old church stood at the top of the hill, and beyond it you could see the towers of the cathedral. On Sunday the whole village came up for the service. An ecclesiastic in a plain robe read the names of the dead from a book. Beside him a small chapel held candles for those who could not come. People of every kind, catholic or not, stood together in the cold. Even the basilica further down the road could not hold a crowd like this. The body of the building was cold, but the singing was warm. Nobody spoke above a whisper.","zh":"那座老教堂立在山冈顶上，越过它就能看见大教堂的塔楼。礼拜天，全村的人都上来做礼拜。一位穿素袍的教士照着书念亡者的名字。他旁边一间小礼拜堂里点着蜡烛，给来不了的人留着。无论是不是天主教徒，各种各样的人都在冷风里站在一起。就连路那头的大教堂也装不下这样一群人。这栋建筑的主体是冷的，歌声却是暖的。没有人大声说话。"},"engine":{"tw":[["engineer",4],["locomotive",0],["generator",3],["motor",2],["diesel",6],["catapult",3],["prototype",6]],"en":"In the shed by the station, an old engineer was working on the engine of a small locomotive. He had built the first prototype himself, years ago, and it still ran on diesel. A generator stood in the corner, humming beside the tools. The floor was dark with oil, and it smelled of hot metal. He had once tried to fit an electric motor into it, but the machine was too heavy. Above the door hung a strange catapult he had made as a boy. Outside, a train went by and shook the wall. He said the secret of any engine was patience, not power.","zh":"车站旁的棚屋里，一位老工程师正在修一台小机车的发动机。第一台样机是他多年前亲手造的，至今还烧柴油。角落里立着一台发电机，在工具旁边嗡嗡响。地板上油黑一片，满是热金属的味道。他曾试着给它装一个电动机，可这机器太重了。门上方挂着一个他小时候做的古怪投石机。外面有列火车经过，把墙都震动了。他说任何发动机的秘诀都是耐心，不是力气。"},"govern":{"tw":[["governance",4],["rule",0],["reign",3],["control",2],["mandate",6],["regulate",0],["unify",6]],"en":"For many years one old mayor governed our small island. His reign was long and quiet, and people trusted him. He knew every family by name, and every field. He believed good governance meant few new rules, and he would not regulate every little thing. He had a clear mandate from the voters, and he used it well. His aim was to unify the two villages, not to control them. He listened more than he spoke, and the water stayed clean. When he finally retired, the council had to govern without him. It took them a year to agree on anything.","zh":"很多年里，一位老镇长管理着我们这个小岛。他的任期又长又平静，人们信得过他。他叫得出每一户人家、每一块田的名字。他相信好的治理就是少立新规矩，不愿事事都去管。选民给了他清清楚楚的授权，他也用得妥当。他的目标是让两个村子合到一起，而不是去控制它们。他更多是听，不是讲，水质也一直干净。等他终于退下来，议事会就得在没有他的情况下治理这地方了。他们花了一年才在一件事上谈拢。"},"high":{"tw":[["highness",4],["overdrive",3],["degree",2],["low",1],["lower",6],["gear",2],["school",6]],"en":"We drove up into the hills, and the road climbed to a very high point before it turned. My uncle shifted into a lower gear and told me not to go into overdrive on the bends. The engine worked at a high degree of heat that day. Down in the valley we could see a low cloud over the school. From up here, everything looked small. He said that even his highness the mayor would have to slow down on a road like this. We laughed, and the car rolled on. The air was thin and cold. I wished the drive would never end.","zh":"我们开车往山里走，路一直爬到很高的地方才拐弯。我叔换了低挡，叫我在弯道上别用超速挡。那天发动机热得厉害。谷底那边，我们能看见一小片低云压在学校的上方。从这高处看下去，什么都变小了。他说，就连他那位市长大人，碰上这样的路也得慢下来。我们都笑了，车继续往前滚。空气又薄又冷。我真希望这趟车永远不要停。"},"idea":{"tw":[["ideal",4],["mind",0],["plan",3],["opinion",2],["theme",0],["impression",3],["purpose",2]],"en":"The whole idea came to me while I was walking home. In my mind I could already see the small shop, clean and warm. I asked my friend what she thought, and her opinion was the same as mine. The plan was simple: sell bread in the morning and close by noon. The theme of the place would be old and quiet, like a kitchen from long ago. I wanted to give people the impression that they had come home. That was the real purpose of it all. It was not an ideal plan, but it was ours.","zh":"这个主意是我走回家时想出来的。在我心里，那家小店已经清清楚楚：干净、暖和。我问朋友怎么想，她的看法和我一样。计划很简单：早上卖面包，中午就关门。这家店的调子要老派、安静，像很久以前的厨房。我想让人有种回到家似的感觉。这就是它真正的意义。这计划算不上多理想，可它是我们自己的。"},"inform":{"tw":[["informative",4],["report",3],["change",2],["advise",6],["tell",3],["communicate",2],["consult",6]],"en":"The manager called me in to inform me about a change in the schedule. He wanted me to consult the team before anything was decided. His report was short and clear, and he asked me to tell the others that morning. I had to communicate the news in a way that would not worry them. The talk was more informative than I had expected. He even asked me to advise him on the best day for the meeting. I wrote it down twice so I would not forget a single name. It felt good to be trusted with it. By noon everyone knew.","zh":"经理把我叫进去，通知我日程有变动。他希望在做决定之前，我先跟团队商量一下。他的报告简短清楚，让我当天上午就告诉大家。我得把这个消息传达出去，还不能让大伙儿担心。这次谈话比我预想的更有内容。他甚至让我就哪天开会最合适给他出主意。我写了两遍，生怕漏掉一个名字。被托付这件事，感觉挺好。到中午，所有人都知道了。"},"long":{"tw":[["longing",4],["yearn",0],["ache",3],["desire",2],["short",1],["once",6],["over",6]],"en":"She had been away for a long time, and a quiet longing had settled in her chest. She would yearn for the sound of rain on her old roof. There was an ache in her that no letter could ease. Her only desire was to go back, if only for a short visit. Once she had promised herself she would never return. Now, as the year moved over into spring, she began to think again. The road home was long, but she knew every turn. It was not far in miles, only in years. She left her bag by the door, ready.","zh":"她离家很久了，胸口慢慢积起一丝安静的思念。她会想念老屋顶上雨点的声音。她心里有块地方隐隐作痛，是信件治不好的。她唯一的愿望就是回去一趟，哪怕只住短短几天。她曾对自己发誓再也不回去了。如今，当一年跨进春天，她又开始动摇了。回家的路很长，可每一个拐弯她都认得。那不算多远，远的是那些年月。她把包放在门边，随时准备走。"},"money":{"tw":[["monetary",4],["fund",3],["currency",2],["pay",6],["sterling",3],["wealth",2],["tax",6]],"en":"My parents saved money for years before they could buy the shop. They kept a small fund in a box, in notes of every currency they had ever earned. My mother said the monetary side was always the hardest part. She would pay the tax on time and count what was left. She did not care about wealth; she only wanted enough. Once she was paid in sterling by a traveller, and she kept that note for luck. Every month they put a little aside, even in hard weeks. The box was old and the clasp was loose. It is still in the box today.","zh":"我爸妈攒了很多年的钱，才买下那家店。他们在一个盒子里存着一小笔钱，是他们挣过的各种货币的纸币。我妈说，钱这一头的事从来最难。她按时交税，再数数还剩多少。她不在乎什么财富，只想要够用。有一回，一个过路人用英镑付了她钱，她就把那张钞票留着图个吉利。每个月就算再紧，他们也要存一点。盒子很旧，扣子也松了。到今天它还在那个盒子里。"},"student":{"tw":[["study",4],["pupil",0],["theologian",3],["intellectual",2],["graduate",6],["scholar",3],["school",6]],"en":"As a student I was never the best in the school, but I liked to study. One of my teachers was a quiet scholar who had once wanted to be a theologian. She treated every pupil the same and never raised her voice. She was an intellectual in the truest sense: she read for hours and asked good questions. When my brother had to graduate, she came to the small party at our house. Years later she told me that teaching was the only work she had ever wanted. She had a way of making a hard idea feel simple. I still think of her.","zh":"做学生的时候，我从来不是学校里最好的，但我喜欢念书。我有一位老师，是个安静的学者，年轻时还想当神学家。她对每个学生都一样，从不提高嗓门。她是个真正的知识分子：一读就是几个钟头，问题也问得好。我弟弟毕业时，她来参加了我们家那个小聚会。多年以后她告诉我，教书是她唯一想干的事。她有种本事，能把难懂的道理讲得简单。我到今天还会想起她。"},"tooth":{"tw":[["dental",4],["canine",3],["bone",2],["scar",6],["fang",3],["structure",2],["claw",6]],"en":"The dentist looked at my back tooth and said it would need a small filling. She showed me the structure of a jaw on a poster behind her head. She said the bone under the gum was still strong. A dog has a long canine and sharp fangs, she said, while a person has flat teeth for grinding. I had a small scar on my chin from a fall as a child, and she asked about it. I told her the story of the dog whose claw had caught me, and she laughed. Then she began the dental work, and I closed my eyes.","zh":"牙医看了看我后面的牙，说得补一小块。她指着身后墙上的图，给我讲牙床的结构。她说，牙龈底下的骨头还结实。她说，狗有长长的犬齿和尖尖的獠牙，而人的牙是平的，用来磨东西。我下巴上有道小疤，是小时候摔的，她问起这事。我给她讲了那条狗用爪子勾住我的经过，她笑了。然后她开始做牙，我闭上了眼睛。"},"voice":{"tw":[["vocal",4],["sound",2],["bass",3],["express",2],["tone",6],["pronounce",2],["touch",6]],"en":"In the school choir my sister had the strongest voice. She could hold a low note in a deep bass tone that made the whole room quiet. The teacher said she should train her vocal cords, but never force them. She learned to pronounce the old words clearly, and to express each line with feeling. Sometimes she would touch my arm and sing a note for me alone. The sound of it stayed in my head all day. She never sang for praise, only for the joy of it. I could not sing at all, but I loved to listen. It was enough for me.","zh":"在学校合唱队里，我妹妹的嗓音最亮。她能用一个低沉的男低音拖住一个音符，让整间屋子都静下来。老师说她的声带要练，但不能硬撑。她学会了把那些老词咬清楚，还学会每一句都唱出感情。有时她会碰碰我的胳膊，单独为我唱一个音。那声音在我脑子里响一整天。她唱歌不是为了夸奖，只是为了那份高兴。我一点也不会唱，可我特别爱听。对我来说，这就够了。"},"war":{"tw":[["warrior",4],["warfare",0],["campaign",2],["peace",1],["military",6],["conflict",2],["army",6]],"en":"In history class we studied a long war and the men who fought in it. The teacher said every warrior on both sides believed he was right. The campaign had lasted years, and the whole army had marched through snow. We read about the new kinds of warfare that appeared in that time. The museum held a military uniform with a hole in the chest. Afterwards I walked home slowly and thought about peace. It was only a lesson, but it stayed with me. That night I could not sleep, because the old conflict felt close to me, as if it had happened yesterday.","zh":"历史课上，我们学了一场漫长的战争和在战争中打仗的人。老师说，两边每个战士都相信自己是正义的。这场战役打了好些年，整支军队踏过雪地行军。我们读到那时出现的各种新式战法。博物馆里陈列着一件军装，胸口有个洞。下课后我慢慢走回家，想着和平。这不过是一堂课，却留在了我心里。那晚我睡不着，因为那段旧日冲突离我很近，仿佛是昨天才发生的。"},"accept":{"tw":[["admit",0],["agree",3],["refuse",1],["seek",6],["bear",0],["believe",3],["negotiate",6],["assume",0]],"en":"When the manager offered me the job, I did not accept it at once. I asked for a day to think, because I could not bear to decide too fast. He did not refuse me; he only said he would wait. I had to negotiate a small point about the hours, and he agreed in the end. He told me to seek advice from anyone I trusted. I began to assume I would take it, though I did not admit this even to myself. It was a quiet office, and the pay was fair. I still do not believe I made a mistake.","zh":"经理把这份工作给我时，我没有马上答应。我请他给我一天想想，因为我实在不敢决定得太快。他没有拒绝，只说会等。工时上有一小点我得谈，最后他同意了。他让我去找信得过的人商量。我开始设想自己会接下它，虽然连对自己也没承认。那是一间安静的办公室，待遇也公道。到现在我仍不觉得这是个错。"},"age":{"tw":[["mature",0],["reign",3],["change",2],["rejuvenate",1],["life",6],["antiquity",3],["develop",2],["same",6]],"en":"At his age my grandfather had seen the whole town change. His life had begun in a time of antiquity, he liked to say, and he had watched the young grow up and leave. A king had once had his reign in those years, though that was before I was born. My grandfather was slow to mature, my mother joked, and never the same for two days. He had also watched the town develop new roads and new houses. To rejuvenate himself he would walk to the river every morning and sit in the sun. He said a long age teaches you patience.","zh":"在我爷爷这把年纪，他眼看着整个镇子变了样。他总爱说，他的一生开始得很早很早，那时还是古旧的年月，他看着年轻人长大、离开。那些年里曾有位国王在位，不过那是我出生前的事了。我妈打趣说，他这个人成熟得慢，两天一个样。他也看着镇子修起新路、盖起新房子。为了让自己恢复点精神，他每天早上都走到河边，坐在太阳底下。他说活得久，能教会你耐心。"},"amount":{"tw":[["total",0],["figure",3],["magnitude",2],["excess",6],["measure",0],["advance",3],["value",6],["quantity",0]],"en":"The total on the bill was larger than I had expected. I had to measure each item again and write down the figure, because the amount of paper alone surprised me. The quantity of ink we had used was small, but the value of the work was high. There was an excess of charges I did not understand. The shop asked for an advance before they would begin. I read it twice and still could not believe it. Only then did I see the magnitude of the job I had taken on. In the end I paid and said nothing.","zh":"账单上的总数比我预想的多。我只好把每样东西又量了一遍，把数目写下来，因为光是纸张的量就让我吃了一惊。我们用的墨并不多，可这活儿的价值不低。里面有些收费我根本看不懂，多出来一大截。店家要求先付一笔预付款才肯开工。我读了两遍，还是不敢相信。到这时我才看清自己接下的是多大一件事。最后我付了钱，什么也没说。"},"back":{"tw":[["cover",0],["tail",3],["bet",2],["ahead",1],["game",0],["champion",3],["lie",2],["second",0]],"en":"At the race I put a small bet on a horse I had never seen. The champion from last year was ahead of the others from the start, but my horse stayed near the back of the pack. Its tail was the last thing I could see as they came round. For a second I thought I had lost my money. Then the leader began to tire, and mine moved up. I lay my ticket on the bench and waited. The race was a long game, and the cover of the stands kept off the rain.","zh":"赛场上，我在一匹从没见过的马上下了一小注。去年的冠军一开跑就冲在前面，我那匹马却一直待在队伍后头。等它们转过弯来，我只能看见它的尾巴。有那么一秒，我以为钱没了。接着领先的马开始没劲，我的那匹往上赶。我把票放在长凳上等着。这是一场漫长的较量，看台的顶棚挡住了雨。"},"bad":{"tw":[["big",0],["worse",3],["quality",2],["good",1],["little",6],["tough",0],["evil",3],["bit",6]],"en":"The storm that week was bad, and the roof began to leak in the big room. My father said the quality of the old tiles was poor, and the rain would only make things worse. There was a little water in a dish on the floor. He had a tough job ahead, up on the roof in the wind. He did not believe in evil luck, only in good work. He took off his coat, climbed up, and fixed a bit of the edge before dark. By morning the leak had stopped, but the wall was stained. We would have to paint it in spring.","zh":"那一周的暴风雨来得很凶，大房间的屋顶开始漏。我爸说这些旧瓦质量差，雨一下只会更糟。地板上一个盘子里接了一小点水。他眼前是桩难办的活儿，得顶着风爬到屋顶上去。他不信什么厄运，只信好好干活。他脱了外套爬上去，天黑前把边上一小块修好了。到早上漏水是停了，可墙上留了痕。等春天还得重新刷一遍。"},"bag":{"tw":[["base",0],["pouch",3],["pack",2],["plastic",6],["dish",0],["steal",2],["bottle",6],["pocket",0]],"en":"My mother packed a bag for the picnic and put it on the base of the cart. Inside were a plastic dish, a bottle of water, and a small pouch of salt. She told me to pack the fruit on top so it would not get crushed. On the way a boy tried to steal the bag from the cart, but he only reached the pocket and ran off. My father laughed and said nothing had been taken. We spread a cloth and sat down on the grass. We ate by the river and were home before dark. It was a good day after all.","zh":"我妈为野餐装了一个袋子，放在推车的最下面。里面有一个塑料盘、一瓶水，还有一小袋盐。她让我把水果放在最上面，免得压坏。路上有个男孩想从车上偷走袋子，可他只够到口袋就跑了。我爸笑了，说什么也没丢。我们摊开布，坐在草地上。我们在河边吃了饭，天黑前就到家了。那一天到头来还挺好。"},"bird":{"tw":[["skirt",0],["parrot",3],["cry",2],["shark",6],["hiss",0],["observe",2],["whale",6],["shuttle",0]],"en":"In the garden a bright bird sat on the fence and would not move. It looked like a small parrot, and when my sister came near, it gave a sharp cry and a low hiss. I stood still and began to observe it. Its long tail feathers hung down over the wood like a skirt. That morning the news had shown a whale and a shark in the same bay, and now this little thing seemed just as strange. Then a shuttle bus passed, and the bird flew off. I have never seen one like it since.","zh":"园子里有只颜色鲜亮的鸟停在篱笆上，不肯动。它看着像只小鹦鹉，我妹妹一靠近，它就尖声一叫，还低低地嘶了一声。我站住不动，开始仔细看它。它长长的尾羽像条裙子，垂在木头上。那天早上的新闻里，同一片海湾出现了鲸和鲨鱼，如今这小东西看着也一样稀奇。一辆班车开过，鸟就飞走了。从那以后我再没见过那样的鸟。"},"birth":{"tw":[["bear",0],["drop",3],["produce",2],["death",1],["child",6],["nativity",0],["twin",3],["maternal",6]],"en":"On the farm we waited all night for the birth of the first lamb. The old ewe had to bear it alone, and we could only watch from the door. Just before dawn she began to produce a second one: twins. My aunt, whose maternal care never failed, wrapped them both in cloth to keep them warm. My youngest cousin, still a child, held one in her arms. A single drop of blood on the straw told us all was well. That night there had been no thought of death, only of new life. I still remember the small nativity in the barn.","zh":"在农场上，我们为第一只羊羔的出生守了一整夜。老母羊只能自己生，我们只能站在门边看。天快亮时，她又生出一只：一对双胞胎。我姑姑那份母性的照料从不含糊，用布把两只都裹起来保暖。我最小的表妹还是个孩子，把一只抱在怀里。草上的一滴血告诉我们一切顺利。那一晚没人想到死，只想到新生命。我至今还记得谷仓里那一幕小小的降生。"},"bit":{"tw":[["act",0],["chew",3],["taste",2],["pretty",6],["chip",0],["scale",3],["little",6],["minute",0]],"en":"I broke off a bit of chocolate and let it melt on my tongue. It had a pretty sweet taste, and I began to chew the little pieces slowly. My sister said it was a common act of greed, and she was right. I measured a chip of it on the kitchen scale, just to see, and the number was tiny. It took only a minute to eat the lot. It was a small pleasure on a slow afternoon. I did not tell anyone about it. Then I had to wash the dish and start again with what was left.","zh":"我掰下一小块巧克力，让它在舌头上化开。味道甜得很讨喜，我开始慢慢嚼那些小碎块。我妹妹说这是典型的贪嘴，她说得没错。我还拿厨房的秤称了一小片，就想看看，数字小得可怜。吃光它只用了一分钟。这是慢悠悠的下午里一点小小的享受。这事我谁也没告诉。然后我只好洗碗，再拿剩下的重来一遍。"},"blood":{"tw":[["line",0],["family",3],["genealogy",2],["heart",6],["rip",0],["side",3],["stomach",6],["stock",0]],"en":"The doctor took a little blood from my arm to check my heart. He said my family had a long line of strong people on my mother's side. My grandfather had once drawn up a whole genealogy of our stock, tracing every branch back for years. I had a small rip in my coat, and I held my stomach while I waited, more nervous than I wanted to admit. An old woman in the next chair told me not to worry. When the result came, the doctor only smiled. She said we are all the same inside. There was nothing wrong with me.","zh":"医生从我胳膊上取了一点血，检查我的心脏。他说我母亲这一支，家里世世代代都是硬朗的人。我爷爷曾把我们家这一脉的家谱整理得清清楚楚，往上追了好多年，每一支都不落。我外套上有个小口子，等着的时候我捂着肚子，比嘴上承认的要紧张。旁边椅子上的老太太叫我别担心。结果出来时，医生只是笑笑。她说，人里头其实都一样。我什么毛病都没有。"},"body":{"tw":[["trunk",0],["church",3],["system",2],["blood",6],["personify",0],["public",3],["message",2],["hand",6]],"en":"The old statue in front of the church showed a whole body carved from one piece of stone. Its trunk was plain, and one hand was missing. Someone had tried to personify the town itself in that figure, as if the place could stand and look at us. Inside, the museum had a small system of rooms, each with its own message. There was a picture of a heart and the blood inside it. A guide said it had belonged to the public for two hundred years. People walked past it without a second look. It had stood there for a long time.","zh":"教堂前的旧雕像是一整个人体，由一整块石头刻成。它的躯干平平的，一只手缺了。有人想把这座小镇本身拟人化在那个人像里，好像这地方能站起来看着我们。里面，博物馆是一小套房间连成的，每间都有自己的话要说。有一张图画的是一颗心，还有里面流动的血。向导说，它两百年来一直属于公众。人们从它旁边走过，连头都不回。它在那儿站了很久很久。"},"business":{"tw":[["job",0],["position",3],["commerce",2],["industry",6],["line",0],["career",3],["corporate",6],["occupation",0]],"en":"My aunt ran a small business in the market, and she had done so all her working life. Her job began before light, when she would open the shutters and arrange the goods. In her line of trade, commerce was simple: buy cheap, sell fair, and know your customers. She had never wanted a corporate position or a big career. She said a good occupation was one you did not dread in the morning. The local industry grew around shops like hers. She knew every face that came through the door. And she never once thought of leaving it.","zh":"我姑姑在市场里经营一家小店，一辈子的营生都在那儿。天不亮她就开工，拉起卷帘门，摆好货。在她这一行里，买卖的道理很简单：进得便宜，卖得公道，认得熟客。她从没想过进什么大公司，也没想过飞黄腾达。她说，好职业就是早上不会让你害怕去上的那种。当地的产业就是围着这样的小店发展起来的。从门口进来的每张脸她都认得。她也从没想过要离开。"},"buy":{"tw":[["steal",0],["subscribe",3],["pay",2],["sell",1],["offer",6],["purchase",0],["cash",6],["bargain",0]],"en":"At the market my father wanted to buy a new coat, but first he had to sell the old one. The seller would not offer a good price, so they began to bargain. In the end he agreed to pay in cash. It was his first purchase of the year, and it made him happy. He told me never to steal, but to save and buy things honestly. I asked him if we could subscribe to a magazine as well, and he said maybe next month. The coat was warm and dark and fitted him well. I still have it today.","zh":"在集市上，我爸想买一件新外套，可先得把旧的卖掉。卖家不肯出好价，两人就开始讲价。最后他同意付现金。这是他今年头一笔购置，他很高兴。他告诉我千万别偷东西，要攒钱，光明正大地买。我问他能不能顺便订一本杂志，他说下个月再说。那件外套又暖又深色，穿在他身上正合适。到今天我还留着它。"},"camp":{"tw":[["pack",0],["loop",3],["change",2],["where",6],["tent",0],["pitch",2],["fire",6],["encamp",0]],"en":"We left home early to camp by the lake. Where the road ended, we had to pack everything into our bags and walk the last mile. We chose a flat place and began to pitch the tent. A loop of rope held the front open. Then my father started a small fire to cook on. We could not change the weather, but the night was still and warm. A family had encamped near us, and their voices carried over the water until late. I slept badly, but I did not mind. In the morning the lake was as flat as glass.","zh":"我们一早出门，去湖边露营。路到头的地方，我们只好把东西都装进包里，走完最后一段。我们挑了一块平地，开始支帐篷。一根绳圈把前面撑开。然后我爸生了小火做饭。天气我们改不了，好在这一夜又静又暖。有一家人也在我们旁边扎了营，他们的说话声越过水面，一直到很晚。我睡得不好，可我不在乎。早上湖面平得像玻璃。"},"centre":{"tw":[["eye",0],["listen",3],["move",2],["main",6],["heart",0],["seat",3],["international",6],["middle",0]],"en":"We met in the centre of town, by the main square, and walked to the concert hall together. My seat was near the middle of the row, close to the stage. I could not take my eye off the singer, who stood right at the heart of the light. Her voice seemed to move through the whole room and hold every listener still. There was an international group in the front row who had come a long way to hear her. All I could do was listen. When it ended, nobody moved for a moment. Then everyone stood up and clapped.","zh":"我们在市中心那家大广场碰面，一起走到音乐厅。我的座位在那一排的中间，离舞台很近。我的眼睛离不开那位歌手，她就站在光的最里头。她的声音好像穿过整个大厅，把每个听的人都定住了。前排有一群从很远地方赶来的外国听众。我能做的只有听。一曲终了，好一会儿没人动。然后所有人都站起来鼓掌。"},"club":{"tw":[["order",0],["hunt",3],["hit",2],["league",6],["lodge",0],["wood",3],["meet",2],["team",6]],"en":"Our club met every Thursday in a small lodge at the edge of the wood. There was a league in the county, and our team was not the best, but we played hard. The coach would order us to run until the light went, and then we would hunt for the ball in the long grass. I could hit it further than anyone, but my hands were always cold. Afterwards we would sit by the fire and talk about the next match. The wood gave us sticks for the winter fire. It was the best part of my week.","zh":"我们俱乐部每周四在林边一间小屋里碰头。县里有个联赛，我们队不是最强的，但踢得很拼。教练会命令我们跑到天黑，然后我们就在深草里找球。我踢得比谁都远，可手总是凉的。结束后我们会坐在火边，聊下一场比赛。林子给我们捡来冬天烧火的柴。那是我一周里最好的时光。"},"coat":{"tw":[["cake",0],["egg",3],["cover",2],["scarf",6],["surface",0],["fur",3],["dress",2],["yellow",6]],"en":"On a cold morning my mother put on her heavy coat and a wool scarf. She was going to make a cake for the village fair. The surface of the table was covered with flour. She broke an egg into the bowl and began to mix. A yellow dress hung on the back of the door, waiting for the fair. Beside it lay a fur hat she never wore. The kitchen smelled of sugar and warm milk. She told me to cover the cake and keep it warm, and not to touch it until the evening. It was the best cake she ever made.","zh":"一个冷早上，我妈穿上厚外套，围上羊毛围巾。她要做个蛋糕，送去村里的集市。桌面上一层薄薄的粉。她往碗里磕了个鸡蛋，开始搅。门背后挂着一条黄裙子，等着集市那天穿。旁边放着一顶毛皮帽子，她从来不戴。厨房里满是糖和温牛奶的味道。她叫我把蛋糕盖好保温，不到晚上别去碰。那是她做过最好吃的蛋糕。"},"collect":{"tw":[["gather",0],["catch",3],["store",2],["obtain",6],["compile",0],["farm",3],["check",6],["cod",0]],"en":"Every autumn we would collect apples from the old trees on the farm. My grandfather would gather them into baskets and store the best ones in the shed. It was hard to obtain good fruit in a wet year, he said, and you had to check each one. He had tried to compile a list of the trees, with their names and ages. Once he caught a boy taking apples without asking, but he only laughed and gave him a bag. Later, at the market, he sold dried cod beside the fruit.","zh":"每年秋天，我们都会到农场上那几棵老树去收苹果。我爷爷把苹果收进筐里，把最好的存在棚屋中。他说，雨水多的年份很难得到好果子，每一个都得查过。他曾想给这些树编一份名单，写上名字和年龄。有一回他撞见一个男孩不问自取地摘苹果，可他只是笑笑，还给了他一个袋子。后来在市场，他在水果旁边卖起了干鳕鱼。"},"cool":{"tw":[["chill",0],["ice",3],["change",2],["heat",1],["hot",6],["poise",0],["quench",3],["bit",6]],"en":"After a long walk in the heat, I wanted something cool to drink. I put a little ice in a glass and watched it change into water. The first sip seemed to quench a thirst I had carried all day. A small wind moved through the garden. My father kept his poise even in the hottest weather; he would not rush and would not complain. He said the summer chill of the evening was the best part of the day. I drank the last bit and lay back in the shade. I closed my eyes and let it pass over me.","zh":"在热天里走了很久，我只想喝点凉的。我在杯子里放了几块冰，看着它化成水。第一口好像把我一整天的渴都浇下去了。一阵小风穿过园子。再热的天，我爸也沉得住气，不慌也不抱怨。他说傍晚那点凉意是一天里最好的时候。我喝掉最后一点，靠回阴凉里。我闭上眼，任它拂过我身上。"},"cost":{"tw":[["price",3],["charge",3],["value",2],["pay",6],["toll",0],["expense",3],["necessitate",2],["increase",6]],"en":"The repair came at a higher cost than we had planned. The mechanic gave me the price on paper, and I had to pay it before I could take the car. There was an extra charge for the parts, and the toll on the road home would add a little more. My father said the real value of the work was not in the money. Still, the expense would increase our troubles that month, and would necessitate some small cuts at home. In the end the car ran as well as new. That was worth more than the sum we paid.","zh":"这次修车的花费比我们计划的高。修理工把价钱写在纸上给我，我得先付钱才能把车开走。零件还另外收了费，回家路上的过路费又要多添一点。我爸说，这活儿真正的价值不在钱上。可这笔开销还是会让我们那个月更紧张，家里也得省下一些。最后车开起来跟新的一样。这比我们付的那笔钱值多了。"},"couple":{"tw":[["pair",2],["ride",3],["family",2],["husband",6],["match",0],["serve",3],["join",2],["mate",0]],"en":"My sister and her husband were a quiet couple who ran a small guesthouse by the sea. Every guest got the same welcome: a warm meal served at a long table, where strangers would join them and talk like old mates. In summer the two of them would ride an old bike down to the market, a pair of baskets on the back. People said they were a perfect match. Their whole family came once a year, and on those nights she would serve soup until the pot was empty. Nothing there was ever hurried, and few guests wanted to leave.","zh":"我姐姐和她丈夫是一对安静的人，在海边开了家小客栈。每位客人受到的招待都一样：长桌上热腾腾的饭，陌生人坐下来跟他们一起吃，聊得像老相识。夏天两人会骑一辆旧自行车去集市，后座挂着两只篮子。人人都说他们是天生的一对。每年全家来一次，那些晚上她会一直盛汤，直到锅底见空。那屋里什么都不着急，走的时候也少有人舍得。"},"double":{"tw":[["image",0],["hit",2],["single",1],["triple",6],["repeat",0],["raise",2],["straight",6],["dual",0]],"en":"A man in the print shop had to make a double copy of every photograph, because the image on the first sheet often came out grey. He would raise the whole plate and press it down straight, then repeat the move until the lines were clean. A single mistake could ruin a run of a hundred. When a job was late he would hit the old machine with his hand, and it would start again. Some machines were dual, with two rolls; the best ones could print a triple set at once. He never threw away a bad sheet.","zh":"印刷铺里的一个人得把每张照片都印成双份，因为第一张纸上的影像常常发灰。他会把整块印版抬起来，笔直地按下去，再重复这个动作，直到线条干净。出一次错就能毁掉一百张。活儿赶得紧时他会用手拍一下旧机器，它就又转起来了。有些机器是双滚筒的，最好的一台一次能印三份。他从不扔掉一张印坏的纸。"},"down":{"tw":[["blue",0],["submarine",3],["better",2],["back",6],["kill",0],["doctor",2],["close",6],["land",0]],"en":"From the top of the cliff the path went straight down to a small beach, and the water there was a deep blue. My uncle had been a doctor on a submarine before he came back to live with us. He said you learn to close your eyes and sleep when the boat goes down, because the land is far and the sea is not gentle. Twice he had to help kill a fire in the engine room. He told the story better each year. The worst night, he said, was when they had to bring a sick man back up and land him before morning.","zh":"从崖顶有条小路直通下面一片小沙滩，那儿的海水是深蓝色的。我叔在回到我们身边之前，曾在一艘潜艇上当过医生。他说船一下潜，你就得学会闭眼睡觉，因为陆地在很远的地方，海又不温柔。有两次他得帮忙扑灭机舱里的火。这故事他一年比一年讲得好。他说最难的那一夜，是他们把一个病人送上水面，赶在天亮前送上了岸。"},"employ":{"tw":[["use",0],["fill",3],["state",2],["involve",6],["apply",0],["play",3],["enable",6],["engage",0]],"en":"The old mill used to employ forty people, and now it takes only twelve. When the manager wants to fill a place, he asks people to apply at the gate, and he reads every form himself. The work does not involve much skill; you learn it in a week. A good worker will engage with the machine the way a player engages with a game. New tools enable one man to do what three once did. The state pays part of the wage in winter. I worked there one summer, and I used to watch the older men, who knew every sound the mill could make.","zh":"那家旧厂从前雇四十个人，如今只留十二个。经理想补一个缺，就让人们到大门口来应聘，每张表他都亲自看。这活儿不需要多少技术，一个星期就学会了。好工人跟机器打交道，就像玩家跟游戏打交道。新工具让一个人能干过去三个人的活。冬天国家替厂里付一部分工资。我在那儿干过一个夏天，常看那些老师傅，机器的每一声响他们都听得出来。"},"excite":{"tw":[["charge",0],["work",3],["disturb",2],["mystify",6],["shake",0],["disgust",3],["disappoint",6],["stir",0]],"en":"The new play did not excite the small audience the way the director had hoped. The first act seemed to mystify them, and the second began to disgust a few who had come for a comedy. Not even a sudden charge of drums could shake or disturb the calm in the room. One loud note did stir a boy in the front row, but most people only shifted in their seats. The director feared the ending would disappoint everyone. Yet when the lights went up, a few stood and clapped for the young woman who had done all the work. That alone was enough to excite him again.","zh":"这出新戏没能让小小的观众席兴奋起来，导演本指望它能。第一幕似乎把大家弄糊涂了，第二幕开始让几个想看喜剧的人觉得恶心。连一阵骤然响起的鼓点也没能搅动、惊扰屋里的那份安静。只有一声响让前排一个男孩动了动，其余人只是挪了挪身子。导演担心结局会让所有人失望。可灯亮起来时，还是有几个人站起来，为那个干了全部活儿的年轻女人鼓掌。单是这一点，就足够让他再兴奋一年。"},"eye":{"tw":[["centre",0],["seat",3],["hole",2],["ear",6],["heart",0],["look",2],["nose",6],["middle",0]],"en":"My grandfather had a seat in the centre of the old hall, and from there he could keep one eye on everything. He would look at the stage, then at the people around him, and say he could read a whole story from a face. A small hole in the ceiling let in a thin line of light, right over the middle of the room. He had a good ear for music and a warm heart for anyone who sang badly. Once, when a young woman tripped, he only touched his nose and smiled. Age had taken much from him, but not his eye.","zh":"我爷爷在旧礼堂正中有一个座位，从那儿他能用一只眼睛盯住所有动静。他会看看台上，再看看周围的人，说他能从一个脸上读出一整个故事。天花板上有个小洞，透下一道细细的光，正好落在屋子中央。他耳朵好，对唱得再糟的人也有一颗热心。有一次一个年轻女人绊了一下，他只是摸了摸鼻子，笑了笑。年纪带走了他很多东西，但没带走他这双眼睛。"},"fat":{"tw":[["fertile",0],["belly",3],["change",2],["thin",1],["milk",6],["plump",0],["lipid",2],["diet",6]],"en":"On my uncle's farm the land was fertile and the cows gave good milk, so nothing stayed thin for long. The oldest cow was plump, with a heavy belly, and the vet said her diet had too much fat in it. My uncle would change the feed each season and watch the animals grow. He liked a good layer of fat on a pig; it kept the meat soft. In the cold months the extra lipid under the skin kept them warm. He said a farm teaches you that fat is not always a fault.","zh":"我叔的农场土地肥沃，奶牛产的奶也好，所以什么都瘦不下来。最老的那头牛胖乎乎的，肚子很沉，兽医说它的饲料里脂肪太多。我叔每季换一次料，看着牲畜长起来。他喜欢猪身上有一层好膘，肉才软嫩。天冷的时候，皮底下那层多余的脂质能给它们保暖。他说农活会教你，肥不一定是毛病。"},"figure":{"tw":[["build",0],["allow",3],["body",2],["ground",1],["same",6],["enter",0],["imagine",2],["form",0]],"en":"The potter would build a small figure from a single lump of clay, first the body, then the arms, then the face. She could imagine the whole form before she touched it. The ground near her bench was always dusty, and she would allow no one to enter her workroom. Each piece took the same care, whether it was a bird or a queen. She said the number on the price card did not figure much in her mind; the shape did. She made nothing that was ever quite finished.","zh":"陶工会用一团泥捏出一个小人，先做身子，再做胳膊，再做脸。还没动手，她心里就已经有了整个形状。她工作台边的地上总是蒙着灰，她不许任何人进她的工作室。每一件都同样用心，不管是只鸟还是位女王。她说价签上的数字在她心里不算什么，形状才算。她做的东西从没有真正完工的。"},"finger":{"tw":[["feel",0],["index",3],["touch",2],["nose",6],["thumb",3],["indicate",2],["hand",6],["digit",2]],"en":"The old clockmaker would feel each little wheel with one finger before he set it in place. He never used his thumb for fine work; the index finger was the one he trusted. When a part was too small to see, he would bring his nose almost to the bench and let his touch tell him the truth. He could indicate a fault without a word, just by tapping the dial. Once he cut one hand and could not work for a week, and he said the smallest finger knew things the eye could not. To him every digit was a tool.","zh":"老钟表匠在装每一只小轮子之前，都要先用一根手指摸一摸。细活儿他从不用拇指，信得过的是那根食指。碰上小到看不清的零件，他会把鼻子凑到工作台前，靠手感辨出真相。他不用说话，敲敲表盘就能指出毛病。有一次他割破了一只手，一个星期干不了活，他说最小的那根手指知道眼睛不知道的事。对他来说每根指头都是工具。"},"flat":{"tw":[["straight",0],["box",2],["sharp",1],["above",6],["plane",0],["plain",2],["lower",6],["mat",0]],"en":"The workbench in the shed was flat and old, and my father kept it that way with a plane he had owned for years. He would lay a mat under each piece so it would not slip, and then draw a straight line along the edge. Above the bench hung a box of tools, and the lower shelf held the heavy ones. A sharp blade was the whole secret, he said. The plain wood would take a finish only if the surface was true. I learned to check with my palm, not my eye.","zh":"棚子里那张工作台又平又旧，我爸用一把用了多年的刨子把它一直保持这样。他会在每块木料下垫一张垫子，免得滑，再沿着边画一条直线。台子上方挂着一箱工具，下面那层架子放重的。他说秘诀全在一把快刃上。只有台面真正平整，素木才吃得住漆。我学会了用手掌去摸，而不是用眼睛看。"},"forget":{"tw":[["leave",0],["slip",3],["lose",2],["mind",1],["maybe",6],["block",0],["neglect",2],["imagine",6]],"en":"My grandfather began to forget small things first: where he had left his keys, the name of a street, the day of the week. He would lose his way in a town he had lived in all his life. Sometimes a word would slip away in the middle of a sentence, and he would laugh, though his mind was not laughing. The doctors said a small block in the brain could do this. He would neglect to eat, and we would have to remind him. Maybe, he said, it is better to imagine the past than to hold it.","zh":"爷爷是先从小事上开始忘的：钥匙搁哪儿了、一条街的名字、今天是星期几。他会在一座住了一辈子的镇上迷路。有时话说到一半，一个词就溜走了，他会笑，可他的脑子并没在笑。医生说脑里有一小块堵塞就能这样。他会忘了吃饭，我们得提醒他。他说，也许想象过去比抓住过去更好。"},"forward":{"tw":[["ahead",0],["position",2],["reverse",1],["goal",6],["forth",0],["transport",2],["right",6],["fore",0]],"en":"The boat moved forward with every pull, and the cox would call the time from the back. Our position in the race was third, then second, and we could see the leaders just ahead. The wind held us back, so the coach told us to lean forth and not to reverse our rhythm. On the right bank an old transport barge sat low in the water, and someone waved. Our only goal was the bridge. I could not feel my arms, but I kept pulling. Fore and aft the oars rose and fell together.","zh":"船随着每一次划桨向前走，舵手在后头喊节奏。我们在比赛里先是第三，然后第二，能看见前面的领头船就在不远处。风顶着我们，教练叫我们身体前倾、别乱了节奏。右岸停着一条笨重的运输驳船，有人在招手。我们唯一的目标就是那座桥。胳膊早就没了知觉，我还是一直划。船头船尾，桨一起升起，一起落下。"},"friend":{"tw":[["champion",0],["companion",3],["advocate",2],["foe",1],["father",6],["ally",0],["confederate",3],["wife",6]],"en":"My father was a quiet man, but in a fight he was a true friend. When a neighbour was accused of stealing, he stood up as her champion and spoke for her like an advocate in a court. Her only companion in that room was him. The rest had turned into a foe overnight. He called in an old ally from the next village, a man some people thought a confederate of thieves, and together they found the missing receipt. My mother, his wife, said nothing until they came home. Then she smiled and put the kettle on.","zh":"我爸是个安静的人，可真到较劲的时候，他是个够格的朋友。有个邻居被指偷东西，他站出来替她当靠山，像法庭上的辩护人一样为她说话。那屋里，她唯一的同伴就是他。其余的人一夜之间都成了对头。他请来邻村一个老盟友，有人说那人是贼的同伙，两人一起找出了那张丢失的收据。我妈，也就是他妻子，一直到他们回家都没作声。然后她笑了，把水壶放上炉子。"},"full":{"tw":[["good",0],["beat",2],["empty",1],["same",6],["total",0],["change",2],["own",6],["wide",0]],"en":"The hall was full an hour before the film began, and the queue outside was wide and noisy. A good film, the manager said, always beat a bad one on the first night, and this one was both. The room had been empty all week, and now every seat was taken. The same thing happened every winter, and each time he would change the posters by the door. He would say the total had doubled over the year. His own small office was behind the screen. When the lights went down, nobody spoke.","zh":"电影开场前一小时，放映厅就坐满了，外头排的队又宽又吵。经理说，头一晚好片子总能压过烂片子，而这一部两者都占。整整一周厅里都空着，现在每个位子都有人。每年冬天都是这样，每回他都会换掉门口的海报。他会说这一年的总数翻了一倍。他自己的小办公室就在银幕后面。灯一暗，谁都不说话了。"},"further":{"tw":[["advance",0],["carry",3],["support",2],["result",6],["encourage",0],["feed",3],["due",6],["boost",0]],"en":"The teacher said we needed further tests before we could trust the result. She would encourage us to advance one step at a time, and to carry our notes to every lesson. The school gave small support for materials, nothing more. We had to feed the plants by hand each morning and write down every change. A boost of light made one row grow faster, but that was due to the weather, not to our plan. When the first numbers came in better than we hoped, we could not stop talking about it.","zh":"老师说，在相信这个结果之前，我们还需要做进一步的试验。她会鼓励我们一步一步推进，把笔记带到每一节课上。学校给的材料费很少，就这么点支持。我们得每天早上亲手给植物喂水，记下每一点变化。多一点光照让一排长得更快，可那是天气的缘故，不是我们的方案。当第一批数据比我们希望的还好时，我们聊得停不下来。"},"glass":{"tw":[["ice",0],["goblet",3],["change",2],["plastic",6],["chalk",0],["mirror",2],["metal",6],["glaze",0]],"en":"The glassblower would take a long metal pipe and draw a ball of hot glass from the fire. He would change the shape for every customer, and the fire decided how far he could go. A goblet was the hardest thing to make, because the rim had to be thin and even. It was nothing like a plastic cup, he said; glass has a memory. He would draw a chalk line on the bench to mark each size. A pale blue glaze, like ice on a window, was his favourite finish, and when it was done it would shine like a mirror.","zh":"吹玻璃的人会拿一根长长的金属管，从火里带出一团滚烫的玻璃。他会为一个客人换一个形状，火决定他能走多远。高脚杯是最难做的，因为杯口又薄又匀。他说这跟塑料杯完全是两回事，玻璃是有记性的。他会用粉笔在案子上画线，标出每个尺寸。一层淡蓝的釉，像窗上的冰，是他最喜欢的收尾，做成之后会亮得像面镜子。"},"guess":{"tw":[["imagine",0],["tell",3],["calculate",2],["maybe",6],["judge",0],["estimate",2],["else",6],["suppose",0]],"en":"At the village fair there was a contest to guess the weight of a huge pumpkin. You could not calculate it exactly, so everyone had to estimate, and most people were far out. A farmer would judge each answer with a serious face and then tell them how close they were. Somebody asked if there was anything else to win, and the answer was no. I suppose the whole thing was silly, but it was fun. Maybe the winner simply had luck. I could imagine a hundred pumpkins of that size in one field, and not one of them easy. My own guess was four kilos wrong.","zh":"村子的集市上有个比谁猜得准的节目，猜一个大南瓜有多重。你没法精确算出来，只能估，多数人都差得离谱。一个农夫会一本正经地评判每个答案，然后告诉他们猜得有多近。有人问还有别的什么可赢吗，回答是没有。我想这事挺傻，可也真有意思。也许赢的人就是运气好。我能想象一整片地里长着一百个这么大的南瓜，而且一个都不好估。我自己的答案差了四公斤。"},"guy":{"tw":[["cat",0],["tease",3],["man",2],["pretty",6],["rib",0],["mock",2],["good",6],["roast",0]],"en":"The guy who lived next door was a good cook, and every summer he would roast a whole fish on the fire in his garden. His cat would sit on the wall and watch, one eye on the plate. He liked to tease his friends and would mock them gently, but he never meant harm. A rib or two about my old car was the price of dinner. He was a small, pretty quiet man until you knew him. One evening he told us how his father had taught him to cook. No one laughed then, and it turned into a very fine night.","zh":"隔壁那家伙是个好厨子，每年夏天都会在花园的火上烤一整条鱼。他的猫蹲在墙上看着，一只眼睛盯着盘子。他爱逗朋友，会轻轻地挖苦几句，可绝没有恶意。拿我那辆旧车开一两个玩笑，就是这顿饭的价钱。他不熟的时候是个安静的小个子，熟了才知道他多有意思。有天晚上他讲起他父亲是怎么教他做饭的。那会儿没人笑，一夜就这么过得很舒心。"},"have":{"tw":[["accept",3],["bring",3],["change",2],["lack",1],["already",6],["bear",3],["carry",3],["cause",0]],"en":"My aunt did not have much, but she would never accept help from anyone. Every week she would bring bread to the old woman upstairs and carry her shopping up the stairs. She said a lack of money was no cause for shame, and she could bear any amount of it. Things changed slowly in that building. She was already old herself, and her back hurt, but she kept going. She would sit with the woman and have tea, and neither of them said much. That small kindness was the only thing she could give, and she gave it.","zh":"我姑妈没什么钱，可她从不接受任何人的帮助。每个星期她都会给楼上的老太太送面包，帮她把买的东西搬上楼。她说缺钱不丢人，多少她都受得住。那栋楼里的事变得很慢。她自己年纪也大了，背又疼，可她还是照做。她会坐下来跟老太太喝杯茶，两个人都不怎么说话。那份小小的善意是她唯一能给的东西，她就这么给了。"},"history":{"tw":[["story",0],["annals",3],["past",2],["life",6],["account",0],["record",2],["literature",6],["chronicle",0]],"en":"My grandfather spent his last years writing the history of our family. He kept every account in a thick book, and he would read the old annals of the town to fill the gaps. The past, he said, is not one story but a hundred. He had lived a long life in one valley and could record the name of every field. He told us about a chronicle his own father had kept, and about the literature of the village fair. When he finished, he gave the book to me.","zh":"爷爷最后那几年一直在写我们家的历史。他把每一笔都用一本厚本子记下来，还会翻镇上的旧年鉴补上空白。他说过去不是一段故事，而是一百段。他在一个山谷里活了一辈子，能报出每一块地的名字。他跟我们讲过他父亲留下的一部编年记，还有村里集市上的那些文字。写完以后，他把本子交给了我。"},"horse":{"tw":[["buck",0],["hack",3],["provide",2],["dog",6],["knight",0],["pony",3],["cat",6],["cavalry",0]],"en":"At the riding school there was an old horse who would buck whenever a beginner took the reins. My sister, who was small, was given a pony instead, and she loved it. The school would provide a hat and a stick for every child. A dog and a cat lived in the yard and followed the riders about. On the wall hung a picture of a knight on horseback, and beside it a photo of the cavalry from a war long ago. I would hack out along the lane on Sundays, happy and slow.","zh":"马术学校里有一匹老马，哪个新手一拉缰绳它就尥蹶子。我妹妹个子小，被分到一匹小马驹，她喜欢得不得了。学校会给每个孩子发一顶帽子和一根鞭子。院子里还养着一条狗一只猫，跟着骑手转。墙上挂着一幅画，画的是骑在马上的骑士，旁边是一张很久以前那场战争里骑兵的照片。星期天我会骑着马慢慢溜达到小路那头，又自在又悠闲。"},"house":{"tw":[["family",2],["chamber",3],["play",2],["senate",6],["home",3],["lodge",3],["room",6],["sign",0]],"en":"The old house at the end of the lane had once been a public building. Long ago a small senate or council had met in its largest chamber, and men would stand and play at politics for hours. Later it became a family home, and each room held children. My grandfather lived there last, alone. He kept the old sign above the door, a wooden board with the town name on it. In winter the lodge at the back was the warmest place. When he died we sold the house, and I have not been inside since.","zh":"巷子尽头那座老屋以前是公家的地方。很久以前，一个小型元老会或议事会曾在它最大的厅里开过会，男人们一站就是几个钟头，拿政治当游戏。后来它成了一户人家的宅子，每个房间都住着孩子。最后是我爷爷一个人住在那儿。他把那块写着镇名的木牌留在了门楣上。冬天，屋后的门房是最暖和的地方。他去世后我们把房子卖了，我再没进去过。"},"hurt":{"tw":[["pain",0],["burn",3],["upset",2],["worse",6],["damage",2],["catch",3],["trouble",6],["harm",0]],"en":"My brother had a bad hurt after he fell from the ladder onto the stone floor. The pain was worst in his back, and the doctor said the damage could be worse than it looked. He had also caught a burn on his arm from the lamp. For a week he could not move without trouble, and the least noise would upset him. My mother said there was no harm in asking for help, but he would not. He sat by the window and watched the field. It took a whole spring before he could lift a box again, and he was never quite the same.","zh":"我哥从梯子上摔到石板地上，伤得不轻。最疼的是背，医生说损伤可能比看上去更重。他胳膊上还被灯燎出一块烫伤。有一个星期，他一动就麻烦，最轻的响动都会让他心烦。我妈说开口求人不丢人，可他就是不肯。他坐在窗边望着地里。整整一个春天过去，他才能再抬起一只箱子，而他也再没完全恢复成原来的样子。"},"joke":{"tw":[["laugh",0],["pun",3],["act",2],["stuff",6],["trick",0],["communicate",2],["fun",6],["gag",3]],"en":"My uncle could never tell a joke straight. He would act out every part, put on a voice, and add a terrible pun at the end. Half the fun was watching him try. The best gag he knew was about a man who lost his hat, and he told it every year. We would laugh until our sides hurt, though we had heard it all before. He said all that stuff about timing was mostly luck. His real trick was to keep people waiting for the last word. He could communicate more in one silly minute than most people manage in an hour.","zh":"我叔讲笑话从来讲不直。他会把每个角色都演一遍，换着嗓子，末了再塞一个糟糕的双关。一半的乐趣就在于看他怎么讲。他最拿手的一个段子讲的是一个人把帽子丢了，他每年都讲。我们笑得肚子疼，尽管早就听过。他说那些关于火候的话多半是碰运气。他真正的诀窍是让人等着最后一句。他一分钟傻话能传达的东西，比大多数人一个钟头还多。"},"kind":{"tw":[["form",0],["like",3],["category",2],["mind",6],["variety",0],["brand",3],["little",6],["genial",0]],"en":"The little shop on the corner sold every kind of tea you could name. The owner, a genial old man, would open a box and let you smell each one before you chose. There was a wide variety in a single shelf, and each brand had its own form and colour. He would ask what you had in mind and then point to a category you had never tried. I like the smoky ones best. He never rushed a customer, and he never sold the same leaf twice. I went there for years, and I still miss it.","zh":"街角那家小店卖你想得出的每一种茶。老板是个和气的老头，会打开盒子让你先闻一闻再挑。一层架子上就有很多花样，每个牌子都有自己的形状和颜色。他会问你想找什么，然后指给你一个你从没试过的品类。我最喜欢那些带烟熏味的。他从不催客人，也从不把同一批叶子卖两次。我在那儿买了好些年，到现在还惦记着。"},"lady":{"tw":[["madam",0],["duchess",3],["woman",2],["lord",1],["queen",6],["dame",0],["countess",3],["daughter",6]],"en":"In the great hall there hung a portrait of a lady in a dark dress, and the guide said she had been a duchess before she married. Beside her stood her lord, stiff and proud. Her daughter, a countess, was painted in the next room, and a queen looked down from the wall above the stairs. The old dame who kept the house would call every visitor madam, even the children. She was a small woman with a loud, kind voice. She said the family had lost its money long ago, and now only the house was left. I bought a postcard and walked home slowly.","zh":"大厅里挂着一幅画像，画中那位女士穿着深色长裙，导游说她出嫁前是一位公爵夫人。她身旁站着她丈夫，也就是那位老爷，身子挺拔，一脸傲气。隔壁房间画着她女儿，一位伯爵夫人；楼梯上方的墙上还有一位王后俯视着来客。看守这座宅子的老太太管每位游客都叫夫人，连孩子也不例外。她是个嗓门响亮、心地和善的小个子女人。她说这家人的钱早就败光了，如今只剩这座房子。我买了张明信片，慢慢走回了家。"},"laugh":{"tw":[["joke",0],["roar",3],["cry",1],["loud",6],["laughter",0],["chuckle",3],["fun",6],["gag",0]],"en":"The comedian opened with a joke so old that the whole room began to roar before he finished it. A loud man at the back gave a great cry of delight, and even the quiet ones had a chuckle. His best gag was about a broken boat, and it never failed. For an hour there was nothing but laughter in the small hall. I had not had so much fun in months. When he left the stage, his face was wet and his voice was gone. We walked home under the street lights, still laughing at the last line.","zh":"那位喜剧演员一上来讲了个老掉牙的笑话，还没讲完满屋子就哄然大笑。后排一个嗓门很大的男人痛快地喊了一嗓子，连安静的人也都轻声笑了。他最拿手的一个段子讲的是一条破船，从没失手过。整整一个钟头，小礼堂里除了笑声什么都没有。我好几个月没这么开心过。他下台的时候，满脸是汗，嗓子也哑了。我们走在路灯下往家走，还在为最后一句笑个不停。"},"lip":{"tw":[["mouth",0],["collar",3],["edge",2],["tongue",6],["rim",0],["margin",2],["ear",6],["brim",0]],"en":"The cold wind made her lip dry before we had gone a hundred steps. She pulled her collar up to her mouth and said nothing. Snow lay along the edge of the road, and the brim of her old hat was white with it. I could not feel my ears. At home she poured tea to the very rim of the cup, and a thin margin of the table stayed dry. She burned her tongue on the first sip and laughed. We sat by the window and watched the snow fill the garden, warm at last. It seemed the whole street had gone quiet.","zh":"还没走出一百步，冷风就把她的嘴唇吹干了。她把衣领拉到嘴边，一言不发。路边积着雪，她那顶旧帽子的帽檐上也白了一层。我的耳朵早没了知觉。回到家，她把茶倒到杯口那么满，桌面上只留一条窄窄的干边。第一口她就烫到了舌头，笑了一声。我们坐在窗边，看雪一点点把园子填满，身上终于暖了。整条街好像都静了下来。"},"lose":{"tw":[["miss",0],["drop",3],["regress",2],["find",1],["chance",6],["suffer",2],["forget",3],["enough",6]],"en":"When the new road opened, the small shop began to lose its customers. The owner would drop his prices again and again, but nothing helped. He did not want to regress to selling only bread, yet he had to. There was one last chance: a market day in spring. He could not forget the first year, when people had come from miles away, and he knew he would miss the bell over the door most of all. There was not enough money to pay the rent. He began to suffer in silence, and would not speak of it to anyone. In the end his son found him a job in the city, and the shop closed.","zh":"新路一通车，那家小店就开始流失客人。老板一遍遍地降价，可什么用都没有。他不想倒退到只卖面包的地步，可也只能这样。最后还有一个机会：春天的一场集市。他忘不了头一年，那时人们从几里外赶来；他也知道，他最想念的是门上那声铃响。钱不够付房租。他开始一个人默默受着，对谁都不提。最后他儿子替他在城里找了份活，店也关了。"},"low":{"tw":[["blue",0],["gear",2],["high",1],["less",6],["first",0],["utter",2],["rate",6],["small",0]],"en":"The old truck could not climb the hill in high gear, so the driver would shift down low and let it crawl. The rate of fuel in the tank was falling fast, and he had less than he needed. His first worry was the steep bend ahead. The motor gave a low, blue cloud of smoke, and he would utter a short word under his breath. A small car waited behind him, patient and slow. At the top he stopped and let the engine rest. The whole valley lay below, and the sky was clear.","zh":"那辆旧卡车挂高档爬不上坡，司机只好换到低档，让它慢慢往上蹭。油箱里的油掉得很快，他手里的比需要的还少。他头一个担心的就是前面那道陡弯。发动机吐出一团低低的、发蓝的烟，他压着嗓子嘟囔了一句。后面一辆小车耐心地跟着，开得很慢。到了坡顶他停下，让发动机歇一歇。整个山谷铺在脚下，天也晴了。"},"machine":{"tw":[["car",0],["wheel",3],["shape",2],["automatic",6],["automobile",0],["lever",3],["produce",2],["equipment",6]],"en":"The new machine in the factory could do the work of six men. It would pull a long strip of steel through two wheels and shape it into a door. A worker would push a lever, and the rest was automatic. The whole plant had once made cars, and an old automobile stood in the yard as a sign of that time. Now the equipment produced parts for other factories. My father said the machine never got tired and never asked for more pay. He liked it and feared it at the same time. In winter the hall was cold, but the machine stayed warm.","zh":"厂里这台新机器能顶六个人的活。它把一条长长的钢带从两个轮子中间拉过去，压成门的形状。工人推一下手柄，剩下的全是自动的。这家厂从前造过汽车，院子里摆着一辆旧汽车，算是那个年头的标记。如今这些设备给别的厂子生产零件。我爸说，机器从不累，也从不多要工钱。他一边喜欢它，一边又怕它。冬天厂房里很冷，可机器是热的。"},"mean":{"tw":[["base",0],["drive",3],["associate",2],["reason",6],["think",0],["mention",3],["change",6],["tight",0]],"en":"The old man who owned our building was mean in a quiet way. He would drive to the shop to save a coin, and he never once mentioned the broken step. His base was the money he kept under the floor, not any real plan. He could not think of a reason to spend, and no one could change his mind. He would associate with nobody, and he kept the door of his office tight shut. We thought him cruel at the time. Later I learned he had lost everything once, and never trusted the world again.","zh":"我们这栋楼的房东是个不动声色的吝啬人。为了省一枚硬币他会开车去商店，门口那级破台阶却一次都没提过。他的底子就是藏在地板下的那些钱，谈不上什么打算。他找不出花钱的理由，谁也改不了他的主意。他跟谁都不来往，办公室的门总是关得严严的。当时我们觉得他狠心。后来我才知道，他从前一无所有过，从此再不信这世道。"},"mess":{"tw":[["deal",0],["flood",3],["meal",2],["bad",6],["fix",0],["disorder",2],["stuff",6],["hole",0]],"en":"After the flood, the kitchen was a total mess. Water had come through a hole in the roof and turned the floor into a shallow lake. Boxes of stuff floated against the wall, and the disorder was hard to believe. We had to skip one meal that day. My father said there was a deal to be done with the insurance, and he would fix the roof himself. The smell was bad for a week. We worked in silence, carrying wet things out to the yard. My mother kept saying it could have been much worse. We had to throw away a whole shelf of food.","zh":"洪水过后，厨房一片狼藉。水从屋顶的窟窿里漏下来，把地板变成了浅浅的湖。一箱箱杂物漂到墙边，乱得叫人不敢信。那天我们少了一顿饭。我爸说保险那边有笔账可以谈，屋顶他自己修。那股味儿熏了一个星期。我们一声不响地干活，把湿东西一趟趟搬到院子里。我妈一直说，这已经算好的了。我们只好扔掉整整一架子吃的。"},"middle":{"tw":[["centre",0],["deep",3],["early",1],["east",6],["eye",0],["seat",3],["long",6],["heart",0]],"en":"I had a seat in the middle of the carriage, with a long view down the aisle. The train left early, before the sun was up, and headed east along the river. The water was deep and dark. I could keep one eye on the fields and one on my book. In the centre of the carriage a family ate breakfast from a paper bag. My heart was not in the journey; I was going to say goodbye to someone. Somewhere in the middle of the afternoon the light changed, and I closed the book and slept.","zh":"我的座位在车厢正中，一眼能望到过道那头。火车一大早就开了，天还没亮，顺着河往东走。河水又深又暗。我可以一只眼看田野，一只眼看书。车厢中央有一家人就着纸袋吃早饭。我的心不在旅途上，我是去跟一个人告别的。到了下午某个时候，光线变了，我合上书睡着了。"},"minute":{"tw":[["bit",0],["climax",3],["note",2],["kick",6],["hour",0],["pinpoint",3],["header",6],["moment",0]],"en":"The last minute of the match was the climax of the whole season. Our best player took a corner, and a tall boy met it with his head, a clean header into the goal. For a moment nobody moved. Then the whole stand gave a kick of sound, and even the coach wrote a note on his card. He had spent an hour pinpointing where the other team was weak. Every bit of it mattered now. The game had been dull until that one second. I do not remember the final score, only the way the ball hit the net.","zh":"比赛最后一分钟是整个赛季的高潮。我们最好的球员开出一个角球，一个高个子男孩用头顶上去，干净利落地把球顶进了球门。有那么一瞬，谁都没动。接着整片看台轰地炸开了，连教练都在小本上记了一笔。他花了一个钟头找出对方的软肋。此刻每一点都算数了。在那秒之前，这场比赛一直很闷。终场比分我记不清了，只记得球撞进网的那一刻。"},"oil":{"tw":[["crude",0],["grease",3],["cover",2],["gas",6],["petroleum",3],["bless",2],["supply",6],["anoint",0]],"en":"My father worked in a garage, where the smell of oil never left his hands. He would use thick grease on the wheels and check the supply of petroleum in the back room. Crude oil came in by lorry once a month, and he would cover the drums with a sheet. He also drove the gas truck when the other man was sick. On Sundays he served at the old church, where the priest would bless the water and anoint the sick with oil. He said the same oil had two lives, one for machines and one for people.","zh":"我爸在一家修车铺干活，那儿的油味从来没离开过他的双手。他会给轮子上厚厚的黄油，再查一遍里屋的石油存量。原油每个月用卡车运来一次，他会拿块布把油桶盖上。别人生病时，他还开那辆运送燃气的车。星期天他在老教堂帮忙，神父用油给病人祝福、涂抹。他说同一种油有两种性命，一种给机器，一种给人。"},"paper":{"tw":[["report",0],["tabloid",3],["cover",2],["print",6],["newspaper",3],["gazette",3],["press",2],["sheet",6]],"en":"The local paper came out once a week, and the whole office was three rooms and two old machines. The editor would print the news on a single wide sheet, and the press made a great noise as it worked. He wrote every report himself, from the school fair to the price of bread. He hated the big tabloid papers and would not cover a story the way they did. The old gazette had been in the family for fifty years. When people stopped buying the newspaper, he kept going for another year, then closed the door quietly.","zh":"这份本地报纸一周出一期，整个编辑部就是三个房间和两台旧机器。编辑把新闻印在一张整幅的大纸上，印刷机一开动就轰轰响。每一篇报道他都自己写，从学校的集市到面包的价钱。他讨厌那些大报小报，绝不按他们的路数去报道一件事。这份老报在他们家已经五十年了。等到人们不再买报纸，他又撑了一年，然后悄悄关上了门。"},"part":{"tw":[["break",3],["base",3],["change",2],["entire",6],["office",0],["bit",3],["concern",2],["piece",0]],"en":"The bicycle had one broken part, a small piece near the base of the frame, and it was the only thing wrong with it. I had to take the entire wheel off to reach it. In the office down the street they sold a new bit for three pounds, and I carried it home in my pocket. The change was easy, once I understood it. My only concern was the brake. I took a short break and then began. When I was finished, the old bike ran better than it had in years.","zh":"那辆自行车坏了一个零件，是车架底座附近的一小块，除此之外没别的毛病。为了够到它，我得把整个轮子卸下来。街那头的事务所里，一个新的小配件卖三镑，我揣在兜里带回了家。弄明白以后，换起来不难。我唯一不放心的是刹车。我歇了一小会儿就动手了。修完以后，这辆旧车跑得比好几年里任何时候都好。"},"pay":{"tw":[["bear",0],["charge",3],["settle",2],["cash",6],["salary",0],["foot",3],["money",6],["wage",0]],"en":"My first wage was small, but I was glad to have it. My father said I should settle every bill at once and never bear a debt. Once a month I would take my salary in cash and put half of it away. The shop on the corner would charge more than the market, so I walked further to save. Money was tight in those years, and we all knew it. When my sister needed new shoes, I paid for them without a word. It was not much, but it was mine, and I learned to keep one foot on the ground.","zh":"我拿的第一笔工钱不多，可我很高兴有它。我爸说，每笔账都要当下结清，永远别背着债。每个月我会把工资领成现金，一半存起来。街角那家店比集市上要价高，我就多走几步路去省。那些年钱紧，我们心里都清楚。妹妹需要新鞋的时候，我一声不吭就把钱付了。钱不多，可那是我自己的；我也学会了脚下踩稳。"},"perfect":{"tw":[["complete",5],["polish",3],["better",2],["good",6],["pure",0],["tense",2],["easy",6],["gross",0]],"en":"She wanted every note to be perfect, and she would practise until the room went dark. The piece was not complete yet; two bars still came out wrong, and she would polish them a hundred times. Her teacher said a good player must be easy with the bow, never tense. The tune was pure and simple, and that made it harder, not better. She would listen to the whole thing again, gross faults and small ones alike. On the night she played well, and nobody in the room moved. She was not perfect, but she was close.","zh":"她要求每一个音都完美，一直练到屋里全黑。这支曲子还没练成，有两小节总是出错，她会把那两小节磨上一百遍。老师说，好乐手拉弓要松，绝不能发紧。这调子又纯又简单，反倒更难，不见得好。她会把整首再听一遍，大毛病小毛病都不放过。演出那晚她拉得很好，满屋没有一个人动。她不算完美，可也差不远了。"},"photograph":{"tw":[["picture",0],["stereo",3],["record",2],["copy",6],["shoot",0],["photocopy",3],["nude",6],["snap",0]],"en":"In the old studio the photographer would shoot portraits all day, and on the wall hung a photograph of a stone statue, a nude figure in grey light. He kept a record of every job in a thick book and would make a copy for each customer. A picture of a wedding could take an hour; a single snap was quick. He had a photocopy of an old review beside the door. A stereo played quietly in the back room. He said the camera could not lie, but a person could. I went there once to have my portrait taken, and I still keep it.","zh":"在那间老影棚里，摄影师整天拍人像；墙上挂着一张照片，拍的是一尊石像，灰光里一个赤裸的身影。他把每一项活都记在一本厚册子里，再给每位客人留一份拷贝。一张婚礼照要拍一个钟头，随手一按的快照却很快。门边放着一份旧评论的复印件。里屋轻轻放着一台音响。他说相机不会撒谎，人却会。我去那儿拍过一次肖像，到现在还留着。"},"place":{"tw":[["home",0],["address",3],["move",2],["next",6],["lay",3],["end",3],["rest",6],["office",0]],"en":"This was the place where my grandmother died, in a small bed by the window. Her home had been there for sixty years, and she would not move, even at the end. I know the address by heart. In the next room stood her old desk, and on it she would lay her letters in a neat pile. The office where she once worked was far away now. When we sold the place, I took the desk and a photograph. Sometimes I put my hand on it and rest for a moment.","zh":"这就是我奶奶去世的地方，窗边的一张小床。她的家在那一住就是六十年，到最后一刻也不肯搬。那个地址我背得出来。隔壁房间放着她那张旧书桌，她总把信整整齐齐地摊在上面。她从前上班的办公室如今远得很。房子卖掉时，我要了那张桌子，还有一张照片。有时我会把手放上去，歇一会儿。"},"play":{"tw":[["act",2],["beat",3],["change",2],["game",6],["bet",2],["catch",3],["best",6],["bring",0]],"en":"Every Sunday the men would play a game of cricket on the field behind the pub. My uncle would act as captain, though he was the worst player there. He would bet a pound on his own team and then lose it. We would catch the ball badly and run in the wrong direction. The best player was a quiet young man who never said a word. When the light began to change, they would bring out the old scorebook. The team they could never beat was the one from the next village.","zh":"每个星期天，男人们都会在酒馆后面的场地上打一场板球。我叔会当队长，尽管他是打得最差的。他会往自己队上押一镑，然后输掉。我们接球接不好，跑也跑错方向。打得最好的是个安静的年轻人，一句话也不说。天色变了，他们就把旧记分本拿出来。有个村子来的队他们怎么也赢不了。"},"point":{"tw":[["charge",0],["address",3],["control",2],["close",6],["degree",0],["corner",3],["clear",6],["head",0]],"en":"At the meeting the young man made one clear point, and everyone stopped talking. The road bent at a blind corner, and a child had nearly been hurt there. He had the address of a man in charge of the whole district, and he would not let the matter close. The council said they could not control the traffic, but he asked for one small degree of action: a sign. He stood with his head down, reading his notes. Nobody could argue with him. Before the year was out, the sign was there, and the corner was safe.","zh":"会上，那个年轻人说清了一点，大家都停下了话头。那条路在一个看不清的拐角处拐弯，有个孩子差点在那儿出事。他拿到了全区分管人的地址，绝不肯让这件事就这么了结。镇上说交通管不了，可他只求小小一步：一块标志牌。他低着头站在那里念自己的稿子。谁也说不过他。不到年底，牌立起来了，那个拐角也安全了。"},"prepare":{"tw":[["cook",0],["dress",3],["change",2],["try",6],["fix",3],["lay",3],["bring",6],["ready",0]],"en":"My mother would prepare the whole meal herself and would let nobody help. She would cook for two days, dress the table with her best cloth, and lay a small flower by every plate. If something went wrong, she would change the plan without a word. She would try each dish before the guests came, and fix anything that was not right. We were told to be ready by seven. My father would bring out the good wine and open it early. Then the doorbell would ring, and she would smile as if nothing had cost her any effort.","zh":"我妈会一个人准备整桌饭，谁帮忙都不要。她要忙上两天，铺上最好的桌布，在每只盘子边摆一小朵花。要是出了岔子，她会一声不响地改主意。客人来之前，每道菜她都要先尝一口，不对的地方就调整。我们七点前必须准备好。我爸会把好酒拿出来，早早开了。接着门铃一响，她就像什么都没费过力气似的笑起来。"},"price":{"tw":[["cost",2],["rig",3],["worth",2],["market",6],["damage",0],["value",2],["drop",6],["toll",0]],"en":"In the market the price of fish would drop in the afternoon, when the ice began to melt. A good seller would never rig the scales, my father said, because a lie costs more than it earns. He knew the real worth of every box, and he knew the market better than anyone. The toll on the road had gone up, and that damage showed in what we paid. He would argue over a small cost for ten minutes. But when a poor woman came, he would give her the fish for half its value.","zh":"集市上，鱼的价钱到了下午就会跌，那会儿冰开始化了。我爸说，好卖家从不做手脚动秤，因为一句假话赔进去的比挣来的还多。他清楚每一箱鱼真正值多少，也比谁都懂行情。路上的过路费涨了，这笔损耗就落在我们付的钱里。为了一点点成本他能争上十分钟。可要是来了个穷妇人，他会按半价把鱼给她。"},"promise":{"tw":[["call",0],["bet",3],["guess",2],["pledge",6],["hope",0],["read",3],["bring",6],["anticipate",0]],"en":"He had made a promise to his daughter, and he meant to keep it. Every night he would call her from the road and read her a page of a book. He could not guess how long the work would last, but he would not break his word. He had made a pledge to her, and to himself. I bet he never missed a single night. He would bring her a small thing every time he came home, and it gave them both something to hope for. He learned to anticipate what she would like, and she was never disappointed.","zh":"他对女儿许下过一个诺言，也真心想守住它。每天晚上他都会在路上给她打电话，念一页书给她听。他猜不出这活儿还要干多久，但他不会食言。他对她，也对自己，立下了誓。我敢说他一个晚上都没落下过。每次回家他都会给她带点小东西，这也让两人都有了盼头。他慢慢学会了猜她喜欢什么，她从来没失望过。"},"put":{"tw":[["arrange",2],["load",3],["change",2],["back",6],["lay",3],["plant",3],["move",2],["order",0]],"en":"In spring my mother would put new plants along the wall and arrange the pots by height. She would load the wheelbarrow with soil and move it to the far end of the garden. Then she would lay each small plant in its hole and press the earth down. In the back of the house she grew herbs in an old box. She liked to change the order of the beds every year. She would stand at the gate and look at it, tired and pleased. By June the whole garden was full, and the neighbours stopped to look.","zh":"春天，我妈会沿墙种下新苗，再按高矮把花盆摆开。她装上满满一车土，推到园子最里头。然后她把每株小苗放进坑里，把土按实。屋后她用一只旧箱子种香草。她喜欢每年把几块花圃的顺序换一换。她会站在门口看着园子，又累又满足。到六月，整个园子都满了，邻居也会停下来看。"},"ready":{"tw":[["cook",0],["dress",3],["change",2],["want",6],["fix",3],["mount",3],["leave",6],["prepare",0]],"en":"On the morning of the journey nobody was ready. My father would cook eggs while my mother would dress the children and try to fix a broken zip. We had to change our plans at the last minute, because the car would not start. My brother did not want to leave his dog behind. He would mount the steps to the house and look back twice. We had spent a week preparing for the trip, and now we were late. In the end we left with the sun already high. It was the best holiday we ever had.","zh":"出门那天早上，谁也没准备好。我爸煎鸡蛋，我妈给孩子们穿衣服，还想修好一条坏拉链。最后一刻我们不得不改主意，因为车发动不起来。弟弟不愿把狗留下。他会走上屋前的台阶，回头看两回。这趟出行我们准备了一个星期，这会儿却要迟了。最后我们出发时，太阳已经老高了。那是我们过得最好的一次假期。"},"reply":{"tw":[["answer",3],["field",3],["state",2],["letter",6],["respond",0],["counter",3],["message",6],["response",0]],"en":"I sent a letter to the office and waited for a reply. A week passed, then two. I would check the counter by the door each morning for a message, but there was nothing. I did not know how to respond if the answer was no. In the end I wrote again, and set out the state of my case in plain words. Then a short response came, and it was yes. I read it standing in the field behind the house, with the wind in my face. I have kept that letter ever since.","zh":"我给那家事务所寄了一封信，等着回音。一个星期过去，又过了两个。每天早上我都会到门口的柜台看看有没有留言，可什么都没有。要是答复是不，我不知该怎么回应。最后我又写了一封，用最直白的话说明我的情况。回信很短，答案是同意。我站在屋后的田野里读它，风吹在脸上。那封信我一直留着。"},"rough":{"tw":[["approximate",0],["prepare",2],["smooth",1],["stretch",6],["fierce",0],["site",2],["pretty",6],["harsh",0]],"en":"They had to prepare the site before any work could begin, and the ground was rough. The plan was only approximate, so every day brought a change. A fierce wind came off the hill and made the men harsh with each other. They would stretch a long string across the field to mark the line, then smooth the earth with heavy machines. The site was pretty in the early light, though nobody said so. Halfway through the summer the work stopped for lack of money. Nobody came to finish it.","zh":"动工之前他们得先把场地准备好，而地面很粗糙。图样只是个大致的安排，所以天天都有变动。山那边刮来一阵猛风，吹得人人说话都硬邦邦的。他们会在地里拉一根长长的绳子标出线，再用重型机器把土碾平。清晨的光里，这片工地其实挺好看，只是没人说。到了夏天过半，工程因缺钱停了下来。再没人回来把它做完。"},"save":{"tw":[["write",0],["record",3],["spend",2],["help",6],["spare",0],["conserve",3],["chance",6],["preserve",0]],"en":"My uncle would write down every penny he spent, and he kept the record in a small black book. He did it not to save money but to remember. He would conserve the old house as it was, and never spend a pound on himself. A spare room was always ready for a visitor. When a young man came to help, he asked for nothing in return. He said the only chance we have is to preserve what is good. He was a careful man to the end. He would never throw anything away.","zh":"我叔会把花掉的每一分钱都记下来，账记在一本小黑册子里。他这么做不是为了省钱，是为了记住。他会把老屋原样保存下来，自己却不肯多花一镑。总有一间空房给来客预备着。有个年轻人来帮忙，他一分钱也不要。他说，我们唯一的机会就是把好东西保住。他一辈子都是个仔细的人。他什么也不肯扔。"},"say":{"tw":[["order",0],["add",3],["express",2],["why",6],["read",2],["answer",3],["want",6],["state",0]],"en":"The teacher would say the same thing every morning: read the question twice before you answer. She did not want a clever reply; she wanted the truth. She would order us to write one page, then add a second. When a boy could not express himself, she would sit beside him and wait. I used to ask her why the old books mattered, and she would state her reason without a single extra word. She was the best teacher I ever had. I have not forgotten that year. She taught me to be careful with words.","zh":"老师每天早上都说同样一句话：答题之前把题目读两遍。她要的不是机灵的回答，是实话。她会命令我们写一页，然后再加上一页。哪个男孩表达不出来，她就坐到他旁边等着。我常问她那些旧书为什么重要，她会把理由说得一字不多。她是我遇到过最好的老师。那一年我一直没忘。她教会我说话要小心。"},"see":{"tw":[["catch",3],["card",3],["bet",2],["why",6],["check",3],["care",2],["how",6],["consider",3]],"en":"From my seat by the window I could see the whole street. An old man sat at a table outside the cafe and played cards with two friends. I could not see how he won so often. He would check his hand, then bet a small coin and smile. I began to see why the others never left early. They did not care about the money; they cared about the game. I used to consider him the calmest man in the town. It was a small thing, but I would catch his eye and he would nod, and I came back to that window many times.","zh":"从窗边的座位上，我能看见整条街。一位老人坐在咖啡馆外的桌旁，跟两个朋友打牌。我看不出他怎么总赢。他会看看手里的牌，押上一枚小硬币，然后一笑。我渐渐看明白了，那两个人为什么从不早走。他们不在乎钱，在乎的是这局牌。我常常觉得他是全镇最沉得住气的人。这本来是件小事，可我好多次又回到那扇窗边。"},"short":{"tw":[["dead",0],["position",2],["long",1],["same",6],["light",0],["contact",2],["well",6],["little",0]],"en":"The visit was short, because the road was long and the light was already failing. We sat by the bed in the same position we had held for hours. My aunt was very ill, and the doctor said there was little hope. She could not speak well, but she held my hand. It was the last real contact we had. A dead calm lay over the house that afternoon. I have not forgotten that short hour. Nothing was ever said about it afterwards. It was the last time I saw her.","zh":"那次探望很短，因为路远，天光也快没了。我们坐在床边，保持着同一姿势好几个钟头。姑妈病得很重，医生说希望不大。她说不太出话，却一直攥着我的手。那是我们最后一次真正的接触。那天下午，屋里静得死沉。那短短的一个钟头，我一直没忘。后来谁也没再提过这件事。那是我最后一次见她。"},"single":{"tw":[["ace",0],["hit",2],["double",1],["individual",0],["digit",2],["same",6],["exclusive",0]],"en":"He served an ace on the first point, and the crowd stood up. It was not a single good shot but a whole run of them. He would hit the ball so hard that his opponent could only watch. The score went up to double figures before the first set was over. Every individual in the stand was on his feet. He was the exclusive owner of that court for one afternoon. At the end he raised one digit to the sky, the same gesture his father had used. I have never seen a player so calm.","zh":"第一个球他就发了个直接得分，看台上的人全站了起来。那不是一个好球，而是一连串好球。他抽得那么狠，对手只能干看着。第一盘还没打完，比分就上了两位数。看台上每一个人都站了起来。那天下午，这片球场好像只属于他一个人。结束时他朝天竖起一根手指，跟他父亲当年一模一样。我从没见过这么沉着的球员。"},"spend":{"tw":[["drop",0],["blow",3],["pay",2],["raise",6],["pass",0],["save",3],["alone",6],["expend",0]],"en":"He would spend his whole wage in three days and then live on bread for the rest of the month. He liked to pay for his friends and would never let them drop a coin in the pot. A single blow of bad luck could leave him with nothing. He would raise a glass and pass it round the table, laughing. He could not save, and he did not want to. Alone at the end of the night, he would count what was left and expend the last of it on a room.","zh":"他三天就能把一个月的工钱花光，剩下的日子啃面包。他喜欢替朋友付账，从不让他们往钱罐里丢一个子儿。一次倒霉就能让他两手空空。他会举起杯子，笑着在桌上传一圈。他攒不下钱，也不想攒。夜深人散，他一个人数数还剩多少，把最后一点花在一间房上。"},"stage":{"tw":[["leg",0],["plane",3],["state",2],["tour",6],["present",0],["wing",3],["travel",2],["first",6]],"en":"The band would travel from town to town, and every stage was different. On the first night the singer's leg was still bad, so he sat on a chair. A plane flew low over the hall and shook the lights. The tour had begun in a poor state, and nobody was sure it would last. A young woman stood in the wing and watched, waiting to be called. They would present the same songs every night, and still people came. By the last show they had played to a full house in every town.","zh":"这支乐队一个镇一个镇地跑，每一处台子都不一样。头一晚主唱的腿还没好利索，只好坐在椅子上唱。一架飞机低低掠过礼堂上方，震得灯都在晃。巡演一开始就不太顺，谁也不敢说撑不撑得住。一个年轻女人站在侧幕后面看着，等着被叫上场。他们每晚都唱同样的歌，来的人还是不少。到最后一场，他们每到一个镇都是满座。"},"station":{"tw":[["post",0],["locate",3],["move",2],["radio",6],["send",0],["fort",3],["position",2],["bus",6]],"en":"The small station stood on the cliff, where a fort had once been. A radio sent the weather news to the boats below every morning. It was hard to locate from the sea, and the men would move along the path with a lamp. My father had a post there for six years. He would send his report and then watch the bus come up the hill. From his position at the window he could see the whole bay. I still walk up that path sometimes. It was a fine place to work.","zh":"那座小站建在崖上，从前那儿有座炮台。每天早晨，一台无线电把天气消息发给下面的渔船。从海上很难找到它，人们得提着灯沿小路走。我爸在那儿守了六年。他会发完报告，再看着公交车爬上山坡。从窗边他的位置上，能望见整个海湾。有时我还会走上那条小路。那是个干活的好地方。"},"store":{"tw":[["shop",0],["bottle",3],["hardware",2],["warehouse",6],["fund",0],["issue",3],["retail",6],["memory",0]],"en":"The old store sold everything from a bottle of oil to a bag of nails, and people came from the next town for it. Half the shop was a warehouse of boxes, and the other half was pure hardware, crowded on the walls. The owner would issue a bill by hand and put the money in a tin for the fund. In those days retail was a slow and personal trade. He knew every customer by name. Now the store lives only in my memory. When he died, his son tried to keep the place open.","zh":"这家老店什么都卖，从一瓶油到一袋钉子，人们从邻镇赶来。铺子一半是堆箱子的仓库，另一半全是五金，挂满了墙。老板会手写一张单据，把钱放进铁盒里当公积金。那时候做零售是件慢悠悠、讲人情的事。他叫得出每位客人的名字。如今这家店只活在我的记忆里了。他去世后，他儿子还想把店撑下去。"},"story":{"tw":[["history",0],["legend",3],["record",2],["novel",6],["report",0],["myth",3],["picture",6],["tale",0]],"en":"My grandmother would tell us a story every night, and the same tale would change each time. She knew the history of the whole village and had a legend for every stone. There was one about a hidden box that everyone said was a myth, though she swore it was true. She would read a novel in the afternoon and turn it into a picture for us at night. I began to write her stories down. The record I kept is the only report of those evenings. I still open that book when I want her voice in the room.","zh":"奶奶每天晚上都给我们讲一个故事，同一个故事每回讲得都不一样。她知道整个村子的来历，每块石头都有一段传说。有一个讲的是个藏起来的箱子，人人都说那是瞎编的，她却一口咬定是真的。她下午读小说，晚上就把它讲成我们眼前的一幅画。我开始把她的故事记下来。我留下的那份记录，是那些夜晚唯一的记载。想她的时候，我就翻开那本书。"},"sweet":{"tw":[["fresh",0],["candy",3],["course",2],["dry",1],["honey",6],["confection",0],["taste",2],["ginger",6]],"en":"The cake was too sweet for me, but my brother ate two pieces. My mother would use honey instead of sugar, and a little ginger to give it a taste. She would serve it as the last course of the meal. The shop down the road sold a small candy for a penny, and we would buy one each. Her sweets were never dry and always fresh. A neighbour once said she could turn any fruit into a confection. I learned to bake from her, and I still use her recipe.","zh":"这蛋糕对我来说太甜了，可我弟弟吃了两块。我妈会用蜂蜜代替糖，再放一点姜提味。她会把它留作饭后最后一道。街那头的铺子一分钱卖一颗小糖，我们一人买一颗。她做的甜点从不发干，总是新鲜的。有个邻居说过，她能把任何果子做成糖点。我跟着她学会了烘焙，她的方子我到现在还在用。"},"tax":{"tw":[["assess",0],["tariff",3],["charge",2],["pension",6],["task",0],["excise",3],["strain",2],["pay",6]],"en":"Each spring the man from the office would come to assess the shop, and my father would spend a week getting the papers ready. There was a tax on everything: a tariff on the imported tea, an excise on the drink, a small charge on each sale. The work was a heavy strain on him, and it was never a task he enjoyed. Half his pension, he said, went back to the state in one form or another. Yet he would pay it without a word. He said a country costs money, like everything else.","zh":"每年春天，事务所的人都会来给店铺估税，我爸要花一个星期把材料备齐。什么都要交税：进口茶叶有关税，酒有消费税，每一笔买卖还有一笔小费。这活儿压得他很累，也从来不是他乐意干的事。他说，他那份养老金有一半以各种名目又交了回去。可他还是一声不响地交了。他说，国家也是要花钱的，跟别的都一样。"},"teach":{"tw":[["instruct",0],["ground",3],["inform",2],["educate",6],["thatch",0],["coach",3],["pirate",2],["understand",6]],"en":"The old thatcher would teach his trade to anyone who would listen, and he had one young man to instruct that year. He would ground him in the basics first: how to cut the straw, how to lay it, how to tie it down. He wanted the boy to understand the reason behind each move, not just to copy it. He would inform the customer of every step. He was not there to educate anyone, he said, only to fix the house. A coach of the village team once asked him why the roof was so thick, and he said it was to keep out the rain. Some people thought him a pirate with his prices, but he was honest to the last pound.","zh":"那位老茅匠愿意把手艺教给任何肯听的人，那年他带了一个年轻人。他先让他打基础：怎么割草，怎么铺，怎么捆紧。他要这孩子弄懂每个动作背后的道理，而不只是照做。村里球队的教练有一次问他屋顶为什么那么厚，他说是为了挡雨。每一步他都会跟主家讲清楚。他说他不是来教书的，只是来修房子。有人觉得他要价像海盗，可他老实到最后一镑。"},"total":{"tw":[["add",0],["average",3],["count",2],["million",6],["full",0],["whole",5],["least",6],["entire",0]],"en":"At the end of the fair the whole village would count the money for the church roof. They would add up every box and write the total on a board by the door. The least they had ever raised was twenty pounds, and this year it was a hundred. A million would not have surprised them. The average gift was small, but the hall was full both nights, and the entire town seemed to help. My mother said it was the whole village that paid for that roof. We were all proud of that little board.","zh":"集市结束时，全村人会一起清点为修教堂屋顶募来的钱。他们把每只箱子里的钱加在一起，把总数写在门口的板子上。他们最少的一次募到二十镑，今年是一百。就算是一百万他们也不会吃惊。捐款平均下来不多，可两个晚上礼堂都坐满了，好像全城的人都来帮忙了。我妈说，掏钱修那屋顶的是整个村子。那块小木牌，我们都为它骄傲。"},"travel":{"tw":[["move",0],["fall",3],["motion",2],["service",6],["trip",0],["fly",3],["access",6],["journey",0]],"en":"The only service to the village was a bus that left at dawn. The journey took six hours, and the road would fall and rise along the valley. We would move slowly, with the motion of the old engine rocking us to sleep. A bird would fly beside the window for a mile or more. For many people the bus was their only access to a hospital or a market. My grandmother made that trip four times a year. She would travel with a small bag and a paper of food, and never once complain.","zh":"通往村子的唯一一趟车，是天不亮就出发的公交。这趟行程要六个钟头，路顺着山谷一起一落。车走得很慢，旧发动机的晃动把我们摇睡。有只鸟会跟着车窗飞上一里多地。对很多人来说，这趟车是他们去医院或集市的唯一门路。我奶奶一年要坐四回。她总带着一个小包和一包干粮上路，从不抱怨一句。"},"trouble":{"tw":[["bother",0],["hell",3],["hurt",2],["without",6],["pain",0],["matter",3],["affect",2],["problem",0]],"en":"We had trouble with the car in the middle of nowhere, and it was a problem we could not solve. There was no light and no water, and the cold began to affect us all. The pain in my father's back was getting worse. He said it was no matter and told us not to bother him. It hurt him to bend, but he would not say a word. To go on without help was the only way. It was a small hell of an hour before a lorry stopped.","zh":"车在前不着村后不着店的地方出了毛病，这是我们解决不了的问题。没有灯，也没有水，寒气开始侵到每个人身上。我爸背上的疼越来越厉害。他说没什么要紧，叫我们别烦他。他一弯腰就疼，却一个字也不说。没有外援，只能硬往前走。熬了像地狱般的一个钟头，才有一辆卡车停下来。"},"walk":{"tw":[["pass",0],["foot",3],["play",2],["ride",1],["sit",6],["step",3],["travel",2],["room",6]],"en":"Every evening my grandfather would take a slow walk to the end of the lane and back. He would pass the old school, where he used to play as a boy, and stop to watch the children. His foot dragged a little now, and he would step carefully over the roots. He would not ride; the walk was the point. If I came with him, we would sit on a low wall and watch the light go. There was room for both of us and our thoughts. He would travel only with his stick and a quiet word.","zh":"每天傍晚，爷爷都会慢慢走到巷子尽头再走回来。他会路过那座旧学校，小时候他就在那儿玩耍，如今会停下来看看孩子们。他的一只脚现在有点拖，遇到树根会小心地迈过去。他不骑车，走路才是正经事。要是我陪他，我们就在一道矮墙上坐下，看天光一点点褪去。那地方容得下我们俩，也容得下我们的心事。他上路只带一根拐杖和一句轻话。"},"want":{"tw":[["need",2],["cry",3],["miss",2],["sure",6],["wish",3],["hope",3],["demand",2],["desire",0]],"en":"She did not want much: a room of her own, and someone to talk to. She would cry at night, when she thought nobody could hear. She would miss the house where she had lived for fifty years. She was sure her family would come, though they never did. She had a wish to see the sea once more, and a deep desire to die at home. She would demand nothing, and that was the hardest part. I used to sit with her and hope for the same things she did. She only needed to be heard.","zh":"她要的不多：一间自己的屋子，一个能说话的人。夜里她以为没人听见，就会哭。她会想念那座住了五十年的房子。她确信家里人一定会来，可他们从没来过。她有个心愿，想再看一次海；还有个很深的愿望，想死在家里。她什么也不强求，而这一点最难。我那时常坐在她身边，跟她盼着同样的事。她要的，只是有人听她说。"},"warm":{"tw":[["quick",0],["chafe",3],["change",2],["cool",1],["cold",6],["strong",0],["dry",6],["tender",0]],"en":"The night was cold, and my grandfather would build a fire to keep the room warm. He had a quick way with the wood and never used too much. He would chafe his hands over the flames and then hold them to his face. The change in the room was slow but sure. A strong wind came down the chimney, and the fire would fall and rise again. He would dry his coat by the hearth and then sit down. His voice was tender when he talked about my grandmother. It was the cool of the evening, he said, that he loved most.","zh":"那天晚上很冷，爷爷会生起火来，让屋里暖和。他劈柴有一套，从不烧多。他会在火苗上搓搓手，再把手贴到脸上。屋里的变化很慢，却实实在在。一股强风从烟囱灌下来，火一低又窜起来。他会把外套在炉边烘干，然后坐下。他讲起我奶奶的时候，声音很柔。他说，黄昏那点凉意，是他最喜欢的。"},"weather":{"tw":[["brave",0],["wave",3],["sail",2],["rain",6],["endure",0],["wind",3],["lean",2],["cold",6]],"en":"Bad weather had kept the boats in the harbour for a week, and the sea was still rough. The wind would lean the old trees almost to the ground. Rain came in across the bay in long grey lines. My grandfather was brave in a quiet way; he had learned to endure the long nights at sea. He would sail out when others stayed home. A great wave once took the nets and nearly took him. He came back cold and silent, and never spoke of it. The village remembered that night for many winters.","zh":"连着一个星期，坏天气把船都困在港里，海面还是很凶。风把老树吹得几乎贴到地面。雨从海湾那边成片成片地斜过来，灰蒙蒙的。爷爷有一种不声张的胆气；他早学会了挨过海上漫长的夜。别人留在家里，他偏要出海。有一次一个巨浪卷走了渔网，差点也把他卷走。他回来时又冷又沉默，一字不提。那一夜，村里人记了好多个冬天。"},"white":{"tw":[["clean",0],["bone",3],["man",2],["black",1],["green",6],["blank",0],["chalk",3],["brown",6]],"en":"In the art room the teacher gave every student a sheet of clean white paper. She would draw with chalk, a black line here, a green and a brown shape there. My page stayed blank for a long time. Beside me an old man was making a picture of a bone, and it was very good. He said a white space could say as much as a dark one. The room smelled of chalk and old wood. When the bell rang, I had only drawn a few lines, but I kept the sheet.","zh":"美术教室里，老师给每个学生发了一张干净的白纸。她会用粉笔画，这儿一道黑线，那儿一个绿的和一个棕色的形状。我的纸空白了好半天。旁边一位老人正画一根骨头，画得非常好。他说，一片白就跟一片黑一样能说话。屋里飘着粉笔和旧木头的味道。下课铃响时，我只画了几笔，可那张纸我留了下来。"},"woman":{"tw":[["char",0],["wife",3],["class",2],["man",1],["girl",6],["broad",3],["adult",2],["mother",6]],"en":"The woman who kept the vegetable stall had once been a char, cleaning offices at night. She was the wife of a sailor, and her mother had run the same stall before her. A class of girls from the school came by every Tuesday, and she would give them each an apple. The man at the next stall said she had broad hands and a soft heart. She treated every adult the same, rich or poor. I bought from her for years. When she died, the market was never quite the same place.","zh":"守着那个菜摊的女人，从前是个打扫办公室的杂役，夜里做清洁。她是一个水手的妻子，她的母亲从前也摆这个摊。每个星期二，有一班女学生会路过，她会给她们一人一个苹果。隔壁摊的男人说她手掌宽厚，心也软。她待每个成年人都一个样，不管穷富。我跟她买了好些年。她去世以后，那个集市就再也不是原来的样子了。"},"advertise":{"tw":[["push",0],["bill",3],["announce",2],["merchandise",6],["plug",3],["praise",2],["sell",6]],"en":"To advertise the new shop, my cousin would push flyers through every door in the street. He would announce a free gift for the first customer and praise his own goods in a loud voice. The bill for the printing was more than he had planned. He would plug the shop on the local radio, badly, and people loved it. A pile of merchandise sat in the window for a week. In the end it worked, and he sold more in one month than in the year before. He was proud of himself for a long time.","zh":"为了给新店做宣传，我表哥把传单塞进街上每一户的门缝。他会宣布第一位客人有赠品，再扯着嗓子夸自家的货。印刷的账单比他想的多。他在本地电台给店里做广告，说得磕磕巴巴，大家反倒爱听。一堆货物在橱窗里摆了一个星期。到头来还真管用，他一个月的销量比前一年一整年还多。他为此得意了好久。"},"animal":{"tw":[["creature",0],["giant",3],["organism",2],["insect",6],["beast",0],["larva",3],["fauna",0]],"en":"At the pond my father would show me every small creature he could find. Under a stone there was often a larva, and once we saw a giant insect with shining wings. He said every organism in that water had its own work to do. He would name the fauna of the valley like old friends, from the smallest beetle to the beast that left tracks in the mud. Once a fox came to the edge and drank, a wild animal in the open. I learned to sit still and watch.","zh":"在池塘边，我爸会把他能找到的每一种小生物指给我看。石头底下常常有条幼虫，有一次我们还看见一只长着亮翅膀的大虫子。他说那片水里的每个生命都有自己的事要做。他会像念老朋友的名字一样数出山谷里的各种动物，从最小的甲虫到在泥里留下脚印的野兽。有一次一只狐狸走到水边喝水，一只野生的动物就那么坦然地露着面。我学会了坐着不动地看。"},"area":{"tw":[["country",0],["corner",3],["environment",2],["field",0],["front",3],["extent",2],["region",2]],"en":"After the storm, the whole area looked different. In one front corner of the field, the wind had torn down a line of young trees, and the damage reached across the region. My father stood at the edge and tried to judge the extent of it. He said the country had not seen such weather in years, and that the environment would take a long time to recover. We walked the wet ground slowly, side by side. Even the far side of the valley, past the low stone wall, was quiet and broken.","zh":"风暴过后，整个地区都变了样。田里靠前的一角，风把一排小树刮倒了，破坏一直延伸到整个区域。我父亲站在边上，想估量一下范围有多大。他说这地方多年没见过这种天气，环境要很久才能恢复。我们并排慢慢走过那片湿地。就连山谷那一头、矮石墙那边，也安静而残破。"},"begin":{"tw":[["start",3],["act",2],["end",1],["resume",6],["commence",0],["talk",2],["next",6]],"en":"At nine the meeting would begin, and nobody was ready. The manager took a breath, said we would commence with the short report, and then he began to talk about the numbers. He stopped in the middle, waited, and told us the work would start again next week. There was an act at the fair that evening, and he wanted to end the day there. When the break was over, he asked us to resume. I wrote everything down and stayed until the room was empty. On the way out, a woman asked me what had been decided. I said I did not know, and that was the truth.","zh":"会议九点开始，可谁都没准备好。经理吸了口气，说我们先从那份简短报告讲起，然后他就开始谈那些数字。他中途停下，等了一会儿，告诉我们工作下周重新开始。那天晚上集市上有个节目，他想在那里结束一天。休息结束后，他让大家接着来。我把一切都记下来，一直待到屋里空了。出去时有个女人问我决定了什么。我说我不知道，而这是实话。"},"best":{"tw":[["better",0],["beat",2],["good",6],["scoop",0],["attempt",2],["play",6],["trump",0]],"en":"We played cards on Sunday, and my sister had the best hand of the night. She had a good eye for the game and would not beat about the bush. Every attempt to trump her failed, one after another. The better player always wins, she said, and she took the whole scoop of coins. It was only a small play, but she loved it. I made one last attempt, lost again, and laughed with the rest. She kept her coins in a little tin box and counted them twice before she left. My father watched from the door and said nothing.","zh":"星期天我们打牌，我妹妹摸到了那晚最好的一手牌。她打牌眼很毒，从不绕弯子。每一次想盖过她的尝试都失败了，一个接一个。她说，好手总是赢，然后把那一堆硬币全揽过去。不过是小打小闹，可她就爱这个。我又试了最后一次，还是输，跟着大家笑起来。她把硬币收在一只小铁盒里，走之前数了两遍。我父亲站在门口看着，什么也没说。"},"black":{"tw":[["dark",5],["man",2],["white",1],["blue",6],["dim",0],["red",6]],"en":"The old man wore a black coat all winter, even when the sun was out. In the dim light of the hall his back looked almost blue, and only the white of his collar showed. He had a red scarf that he never took off, and he kept it folded under his arm like something precious. When the room grew dark, he would sit by the window and watch the street. I once asked him why. He said black hides the years better than any other colour. He was the quietest man on our street.","zh":"那位老人整个冬天都穿一件黑外套，哪怕出太阳也穿。走廊里光线昏暗，他的背看上去几乎发蓝，只有白领子露出来。他有一条红围巾，从不摘下，总像宝贝似的叠好夹在腋下。屋里暗下来时，他就坐在窗边看街。我问过一次为什么。他说黑色比别的颜色更藏得住年岁。他是我们街上最安静的人。"},"blue":{"tw":[["dark",0],["sky",2],["red",6],["low",0],["dye",2],["black",6],["naughty",0]],"en":"We dyed cloth in the yard all afternoon. My aunt wanted a deep blue for the curtains, so she mixed the dye with water and waited. The sky above us was a pale blue at first, then grew dark before we were done. My little cousin was naughty and dipped his hands in the pot, and they came out red. He held them up like a prize. We laughed, but my aunt made him wash them with the black soap until the colour was low and faint. By evening the line of cloth dried in the wind, and the whole yard smelled of wet dye.","zh":"我们在院子里染了一下午的布。我姑妈想要一块深蓝色的窗帘，于是把染料和上水，等着。头顶的天起初是淡蓝的，没等我们忙完就暗了下来。我小表弟很顽皮，把手伸进染缸，拿出来是红的。他举着两手像得了奖。我们笑，可姑妈让他用黑肥皂洗，一直洗到颜色淡下去。到傍晚，绳上的布在风里晾干，满院子都是湿染料的气味。"},"bone":{"tw":[["drum",0],["study",2],["tooth",6],["pearl",0],["white",2],["skull",6],["ivory",0]],"en":"In the study at the back of the museum, my teacher showed us a single bone. It was white as a pearl and smooth as ivory, and she said it had once been part of a skull. We had to write down its shape and size. Someone had tied a small drum beside it, and the skin was tight. I thought of my own tooth and how a fall could break something like this. Nobody spoke. The room smelled of old wood and dust. I asked what it had been, and she said a young man, long ago.","zh":"博物馆后面的研究室里，老师给我们看了一根骨头。它白得像珍珠，光得像象牙，她说这曾经是头骨的一部分。我们得记下它的形状和大小。旁边有人系了面小鼓，鼓面绷得很紧。我想起自己的牙，还有一次摔倒会不会把这样的东西摔断。谁都没说话。屋里是旧木头和灰尘的气味。我问它原来属于谁，她说是一个年轻人，很久以前。"},"box":{"tw":[["corner",0],["flat",3],["blow",2],["piece",6],["chest",3],["hit",2],["spot",6]],"en":"The box sat in the corner of the attic, flat and grey with dust. My brother gave it a blow with his hand, and a piece of the lid came off at once. Inside was an old chest of letters tied with string. He did not hit it again, afraid of what else might break. On the lid was a small spot where someone had spilled ink years ago. We carried it down to the kitchen and opened it slowly. The first letter was from my grandmother, written before I was born.","zh":"那口箱子放在阁楼的角落里，扁扁的，蒙着一层灰。我哥用手一拍，一块箱盖立刻掉了下来。里面是一只旧木匣，装着用绳子捆好的信。他没敢再拍，怕还有别的会碎。箱盖上有个小斑点，是多年前有人溅上的墨。我们把它搬到厨房，慢慢打开。第一封信是我奶奶写的，写在我出生之前。"},"bread":{"tw":[["scratch",0],["cracker",3],["cover",2],["toast",6],["sugar",0],["butter",6],["loot",0]],"en":"From scratch, my grandmother made bread every Friday. She would cover the dough with a cloth and let it rise by the stove. At breakfast we had toast with butter and a little sugar, and my father would eat a cracker while he read. The house smelled warm all morning. She said the loaf was better than any loot, because you could not steal the smell of it. We ate it while it was still hot. In winter she would bake two and give one to the neighbours. Nobody ever asked her why she did it; they only said thank you at the door.","zh":"每个星期五，我奶奶都从头做起烤面包。她用布把面团盖上，放在炉子边发起来。早饭我们吃抹黄油、撒一点糖的吐司，我父亲一边看报一边啃块脆饼。整个上午屋里都是暖香。她说这面包比任何抢来的东西都好，因为那股香味你偷不走。我们趁热吃。冬天她会烤两个，送一个给邻居。没人问过她为什么这么做，只在门口道声谢。"},"card":{"tw":[["bill",2],["paper",2],["check",6],["board",0],["record",2],["file",6],["notice",0]],"en":"At the front desk a young clerk pulled a card from the file and read it twice. On the board behind her hung a notice about new prices. She checked the bill, wrote the number on a sheet of paper, and put the card back. The record showed that the account had been open for years. I waited while she looked for one more file. Then she looked up and told me everything was in order. I paid in cash and asked her to keep the receipt. She smiled and said the office would send the rest by post.","zh":"前台一位年轻职员从档案里抽出一张卡片，读了两遍。她身后的板子上挂着一张新价目告示。她核了账单，把数字写在一张纸上，又把卡片放回去。记录显示这个账户开了好多年。我等着她再找一份档案。然后她抬起头，说一切都没问题。我付了现金，请她留好收据。她笑笑，说剩下的办公室会寄给我。"},"chair":{"tw":[["lead",0],["head",2],["floor",6],["president",0],["position",2],["board",6],["chairman",0]],"en":"The chairman of the board took his chair at the head of the table and asked us to sit. He had held the position for ten years and was said to lead without raising his voice. The president of the club sat beside him, hands flat on the floor of the old stage. Nobody moved. A young man with a folder stood at the back. When the chairman spoke, the whole room turned toward him. For an hour we argued about the budget, and then he closed the meeting with a single sentence.","zh":"董事会主席在长桌首端拉开椅子，请我们坐下。他这个位子坐了十年，据说从不大声就带得住人。俱乐部的会长坐在他旁边，双手平摊在旧台子的地面上。没人动。一个拿着文件夹的年轻人站在后面。主席一开口，满屋子的人都转向他。我们为预算争了一个钟头，然后他用一句话结束了会议。"},"child":{"tw":[["baby",3],["peanut",3],["offspring",2],["parent",1],["pregnant",6],["fry",0],["mother",6]],"en":"When my mother was pregnant with her second child, my father fried bread and eggs for us every morning. My baby sister slept in a small basket by the window, and I was told to be quiet. My parent would carry her on one arm while he did the rest. Someone gave us a bag of peanuts and we shared it. He said the offspring of a quiet house grow up calm. I did not understand it then, but I do now. We had very little, but nobody in that room felt poor.","zh":"我妈怀着第二个孩子的时候，我爸每天早上给我们煎面包和鸡蛋。我小妹睡在窗边的小篮子里，大人叫我别出声。我爹一只胳膊抱着她，另一只手把别的活干了。有人送了我们一袋花生，我们分着吃。他说安静人家养出的孩子性子也静。我那时不懂，现在懂了。我们没什么东西，可那间屋里谁都不觉得自己穷。"},"choice":{"tw":[["pick",0],["decision",3],["choose",6],["option",0],["pleasure",3],["neither",6],["prime",0]],"en":"I had a choice between two jobs in the same town. Neither option was perfect, and it was a hard decision. The first had better pay but long hours; the second was quiet and close to home. To pick between them was not easy. My father said the prime thing was not the money. You must choose for yourself, he told me. In the end I took the smaller office, and it was a pleasure to walk there each morning. Ten years later I still pass the other building and wonder, without regret.","zh":"同一个镇上有两份工作摆在我面前，我二选一。两个都不完美，这决定很难下。头一份钱多，可工时很长；第二份清静，离家也近。要在两者间挑一个并不容易。我父亲说，最要紧的不是钱。你得自己选，他对我说。最后我去了那间小办公室，每天走去上班都是件乐事。十年后我路过另一栋楼，还会想一想，但不后悔。"},"choose":{"tw":[["prefer",0],["field",3],["choice",6],["select",0],["elect",3],["want",6],["opt",0]],"en":"Every spring the village would choose a new leader for the field committee. People could select anyone they wanted, or they could opt to leave the paper blank. My uncle said he would prefer the older woman, though the choice was close. I wanted to elect someone young for a change. On the day of the vote, the whole square was quiet. He told me to choose carefully and not to follow the crowd. I marked my paper in the little booth and folded it twice. Walking home, I felt older than I was.","zh":"每年春天村里都要为农田委员会选一个新负责人。大家想选谁都行，也可以选择让那张纸空着。我叔说他更中意那位年长的女人，虽然两人票数很近。我倒想换换，选个年轻人上来。投票那天，整个广场很静。他叫我仔细选，别跟着人群走。我在小隔间里在纸上画了记号，折了两回。走回家时，我觉得自己比实际年龄老了些。"},"cold":{"tw":[["stale",0],["cool",5],["hot",1],["warm",6],["frigid",0],["chill",3],["dry",6]],"en":"The morning was cold and the air in the kitchen was dry. The bread from yesterday had gone stale, so my mother warmed it over the stove. She said a hot drink would help, but the water in the pot was only cool. I pulled my coat tight against the chill and stood by the window. Outside the wind was frigid and the ground was white. We did not talk much. She put a warm cup in my hands and told me to drink. That was the winter I learned that cold can be a kind of quiet.","zh":"那天早上很冷，厨房里的空气也干。昨天的面包已经不新鲜了，我妈在炉子上把它热了热。她说喝点热的好，可壶里的水只是温的。我紧了紧外套挡住那股寒气，站在窗边。外面风冷得刺骨，地上白茫茫的。我们没怎么说话。她把一只热杯子塞进我手里，让我喝。就是那个冬天，我知道了冷也可以是一种安静。"},"come":{"tw":[["arrive",2],["address",3],["change",2],["want",6],["fall",3],["land",3],["follow",0]],"en":"The letter did not come on Monday. It would arrive, my father said, but the post was slow after the storm. He had written the wrong address, and the change cost us a week. I wanted to follow it, so I walked to the office myself. Snow began to fall as I waited, and by the time I reached the door it had begun to land on my shoulders. The clerk found it at last, under a pile of papers. I read it standing up, and then I sat down on the step.","zh":"那封信星期一没来。我父亲说会到的，可风暴过后邮路慢。他把地址写错了，这一改耽误了我们一个星期。我想跟一跟，就自己走到了邮局。等的时候下起雪来，走到门口时，雪花已经落在我的肩上。职员终于找到了，压在一堆纸底下。我站着把信读完，然后在台阶上坐了下来。"},"dark":{"tw":[["black",5],["condition",2],["light",1],["bright",6],["blue",0],["pale",6],["night",3]],"en":"It was already dark when the light went out. The whole street turned black in a second, and only the pale moon showed. My sister's face looked blue in the cold. We sat on the floor and waited for the condition to improve, but the night was long. Then a small bright flame appeared in the window next door, and someone laughed. We laughed too. It was the first time in years that the street had been so quiet. Then the flame went to the next window, and the next, and the street came slowly back to life.","zh":"灯灭的时候天已经黑了。整条街一下子变成一片黑，只有淡淡的月亮亮着。我妹妹的脸在冷里显得发蓝。我们坐在地上，等情形好转，可那一夜很长。后来隔壁窗口亮起一小簇明亮的火苗，有人笑了一声。我们也笑了。那是多年来这条街头一回这么静。接着火苗移到下一个窗口，又一个窗口，街上慢慢又活了过来。"},"deep":{"tw":[["late",0],["middle",2],["shallow",1],["long",6],["thick",0],["apart",6],["bass",0]],"en":"The river was deep in the middle and shallow near the bank, so we had to walk apart to cast. It was late, and a thick fog hung over the water. My father said the bass would not bite in such cold. We stood a long way from the road and listened. Far off a drum sounded from the village. He told me to keep my line low and wait. It was the longest evening I remember. The fish never came. At dawn we folded the line and walked home, and he said nothing the whole way.","zh":"河中间很深，靠岸的地方浅，所以我们得分开站才能下钩。天已经晚了，水面上挂着厚雾。我父亲说这么冷鲈鱼不会咬钩。我们站在离大路很远的地方听动静。远处村里传来鼓声。他叫我压低钓线等着。那是我记得的最漫长的一个傍晚。鱼始终没来。天亮时我们收了线走回家，他一路上什么都没说。"},"doubt":{"tw":[["question",0],["misgiving",3],["distrust",2],["reason",6],["suspense",3],["disbelieve",2],["prove",6]],"en":"There was some doubt about who had taken the money. The clerk could not prove anything, and the manager began to distrust everyone in the room. I had a small misgiving of my own. The question was simple: who had the key that night? Nobody could answer, and the suspense was hard to bear. I did not disbelieve my friend, but I could not find a reason to defend him either. In the end the money was found in a coat, and nobody ever said sorry. I learned that doubt can sit in a room longer than any proof.","zh":"钱是谁拿的，这事有些说不清。职员什么都证明不了，经理开始不信任屋里的每一个人。我自己心里也有点不踏实。问题很简单：那晚钥匙在谁手里？谁都说不上来，那种悬着的滋味很难熬。我不是不信我朋友，可我也找不出什么理由替他说话。最后钱在一件外套里找到了，却没人道过歉。我明白了，疑心能在一间屋里待得比任何证据都久。"},"dry":{"tw":[["wry",0],["air",3],["change",2],["sweet",1],["water",6],["scorch",3],["cold",6]],"en":"The summer was dry and the air smelled of dust. Our small garden had begun to scorch in the sun, so we carried water from the well twice a day. My mother made a wry face when she saw the leaves. The change came at last with a cold wind from the hills. That evening the sky turned grey, and a sweet smell of rain filled the yard. We stood outside and let it fall on us. Nobody spoke for a long time. The garden did not recover that year, but the rain made us glad for a week.","zh":"那年夏天很干，空气里一股尘土味。我们的小园子开始被太阳烤焦，于是我们一天两趟从井里挑水。我妈看见叶子时撇了撇嘴。变化终于随一阵从山里来的冷风到了。傍晚天变灰，院子里满是雨要来的那种甜味。我们站在外面，任它淋在身上。很久谁都没说话。园子那年没能缓过来，可那场雨让我们高兴了一个星期。"},"egg":{"tw":[["ball",0],["spawn",3],["coat",2],["butter",6],["roe",3],["pelt",2],["milk",6]],"en":"Every spring the fish swim up the river to spawn, and their roe lies in the shallow water like small orange balls. My uncle would catch a few, clean them, and cook them with butter and milk. The skin he left on made a thin coat that kept them soft. The wind was cold and would pelt the window with rain. We ate the eggs with bread and said nothing. Later the river would be full of fish again. On the way home my uncle told me how the young ones would come back, years later, to the same water.","zh":"每年春天鱼都游上河来产卵，鱼卵像一颗颗小橙球躺在浅水里。我叔会捞上几条，收拾干净，用黄油和牛奶煎。他留着的那层皮形成薄薄一层衣，让鱼肉保持嫩。风很冷，夹着雨点打在窗上。我们就着面包吃鱼卵，谁也没说话。以后河里又会满是鱼。回家的路上，叔叔告诉我，那些小鱼多年后还会回到同一片水里。"},"exact":{"tw":[["claim",2],["call",3],["proof",6],["demand",0],["command",3],["specific",6],["accurate",0]],"en":"The manager wanted an exact number before he would sign anything. He did not accept my claim without proof, and he would not take a rough guess. His demand was specific: give me the accurate figure by noon. Then he picked up the phone to call the office and gave a short command to the clerk. I went back to my desk and counted everything twice. When I returned, he read the page slowly and nodded. I had never worked so carefully in my life. That evening I checked the same list three more times before I left.","zh":"经理在签字之前要一个精确的数字。没有证据，他就不接受我的说法，也不肯听个大概的估计。他的要求很明确：中午前把准确的数目给我。然后他拿起电话打给办公室，简短地吩咐了那位职员一句。我回到座位上，把每样东西数了两遍。回来时，他慢慢看完那页纸，点了点头。我这辈子从没这么仔细地做过事。那天晚上，我走之前又把同一张单子核了三遍。"},"fair":{"tw":[["clean",5],["join",2],["foul",1],["opportunity",6],["average",0],["appeal",6],["carnival",0]],"en":"The fair came to the field behind the school, and the whole town seemed to join in. There was a small carnival with lights, and an average crowd for a warm evening. My sister said the prices were not fair. We bought a clean white hat and watched the games. One player made a foul, and the crowd shouted. It was a good opportunity for the children, and the appeal of the music kept us there until dark. We walked home slowly, and she held my arm all the way.","zh":"集市来到学校后面的空地上，全镇的人好像都来凑热闹了。有个亮着灯的小游乐园，就一个暖和的傍晚来说，人算一般。我妹妹说价钱不公平。我们买了一顶干净的白帽子，看人玩那些游戏。有个玩家犯了规，人群就喊起来。对孩子们来说这是个好机会，音乐好听，把我们留到天黑。我们慢慢走回家，她一路挽着我的胳膊。"},"fast":{"tw":[["quick",5],["diet",3],["slow",1],["pace",6],["tight",0],["better",6],["firm",0]],"en":"My cousin could run fast, but he was on a diet that left him weak. He kept a slow pace at first, then a quick one, his shoes tight on the track. He said it was better to finish firm than to start strong. I watched him from the gate with a bottle of water. When he passed me, his face was calm and set. He did not stop until the light went down behind the hill. Later I asked him why he trained so hard, and he only smiled. He said a slow start had almost kept him from the race.","zh":"我表哥能跑得很快，却因在节食而没力气。他起初慢慢跑，随后加快，鞋子紧紧贴着跑道。他说，稳稳跑完比一开始冲得猛要好。我提着水瓶在门口看他。他经过我身边时，脸平静而绷着。他一直跑到山那头的光暗下去才停。后来我问他为什么练得这么狠，他只是笑。他说，起步太慢差点让他连比赛都赶不上。"},"fine":{"tw":[["ok",0],["book",2],["coarse",1],["well",6],["ticket",0],["penalty",2],["good",6]],"en":"The library sent me a fine for a book I had kept too long. The ticket said the penalty would grow each week. I told the woman at the desk that it was not ok, that I had been ill. She was good about it and said I could pay half. The paper of the old book felt coarse under my thumb. I said I was well enough now, and I wrote my name on the form. She smiled and wished me a fine weekend. I paid and left, and on the steps I promised never to keep a book so long again.","zh":"图书馆因为我超期留了一本书，给我寄来一张罚款单。单子上说罚金每周都会涨。我跟柜台的女士说这不行，我生病了。她很好说话，说我可以只付一半。那本旧书的纸摸上去粗粗的。我说我现在身体好了，在表格上写下名字。她笑笑，祝我周末愉快。我交了钱就走，在台阶上暗暗发誓再也不把书留这么久了。"},"fish":{"tw":[["angle",3],["rail",3],["catch",2],["meat",6],["salmon",3],["search",2],["shrimp",6]],"en":"We would fish from the old rail on the pier, my father and I, and search the water for any sign of movement. He taught me to angle the line so the bait would sink slowly. That day we did not catch a salmon, only a few shrimp and one small fish. He said the meat of the salmon was worth the wait. We stayed until the light failed, with our backs to the cold wind. On the walk home he talked about his own father, and the boats they had used before I was born.","zh":"我和父亲常在码头的旧栏杆边钓鱼，盯着水面找任何动静。他教我把钓线斜着放，好让饵慢慢下沉。那天我们没钓到鲑鱼，只有几只虾和一条小鱼。他说鲑鱼的肉值得等。我们一直待到天光暗下去，背对着冷风。回家的路上，他讲起他自己的父亲，还有我出生前他们用过的那些船。"},"forest":{"tw":[["wood",0],["jungle",3],["land",2],["pine",6],["timber",0],["plant",2],["swamp",6]],"en":"Behind the house the forest began and ran for miles. The wood was old, mostly pine and dark timber, and in the wet months part of it turned into swamp. My father would plant small trees along the edge each spring, and he knew every path on the land. Once we walked to the far side, where the trees grew so close they made a kind of jungle. He said a forest like this could not be bought with money, only kept. That was the last summer we walked it together.","zh":"房子后面就是森林，一直绵延好几英里。林木很老了，多半是松树和深色的成材木，到了潮湿的月份，有一部分会变成沼泽。每年春天我父亲都沿着边栽些小树，地里的每条路他都认得。有一回我们走到最远的那头，树挨得那么密，简直成了一片丛林。他说这样的森林花钱买不来，只能守着。那是我和他最后一次一起走过它。"},"general":{"tw":[["cosmopolitan",0],["head",2],["local",1],["chief",6],["ecumenical",0],["command",2],["secretary",6]],"en":"At the head of the table sat a retired general with a cosmopolitan manner. He had once held command of a large camp and had a local chief beside him. His secretary took notes in a small book. He spoke of the world with an ecumenical spirit, as if every town were his own. I was young and said little. When he shook my hand, he asked where I came from and listened to the answer as if it mattered. Years later I read his name in an old report, and I remembered that quiet evening.","zh":"长桌首端坐着一位退役将军，举止带着见过世面的气度。他曾经统辖一座大营，身边坐着当地的头人。他的秘书拿着小本子记东西。他谈起世界时怀着一视同仁的心，仿佛哪座城镇都是他的。我那时年轻，话不多。他握我的手时，问我是哪里人，听得很认真，仿佛这很重要。多年后我在一份旧报告里看到他的名字，又想起那个安静的傍晚。"},"girl":{"tw":[["daughter",0],["maid",3],["woman",2],["boy",1],["kid",6],["lass",3],["female",2]],"en":"Next door lived a girl of about ten, the daughter of the woman who kept the shop. She helped like a maid, carrying boxes and sweeping the step, and every boy and kid on the street liked her. Her mother called her a lass and told her to be careful. She was the only female in a house of four brothers and did not seem to mind. I watched her one afternoon, laughing at the gate. She grew up, left the town, and I never saw her again. But I still remember the way she carried those boxes without ever asking for help.","zh":"隔壁住着个十来岁的女孩，是开小店那女人的女儿。她像个帮工似的干活，搬箱子、扫台阶，街上每个男孩和小孩都喜欢她。她妈叫她丫头，叮嘱她小心点。家里四个兄弟，就她一个女孩，她好像也不在意。有天下午我在门口看着她笑。她长大了，离开了镇子，我再没见过她。可我至今记得她搬那些箱子的样子，从不开口求人。"},"glance":{"tw":[["glimpse",0],["hit",2],["preview",6],["glint",0],["look",2],["stumble",6],["peek",0]],"en":"I caught a glance of the letter as she turned, only a glimpse before she closed the drawer. There was a glint of gold at the edge of the paper. I tried not to peek, but I took one more look. Later I stumbled on the same box in the hall, and it hit my foot. She never said a word about it. Years afterward she showed me a preview of the old pages and smiled. It was a letter from my father, written the year before he died. I read it twice and put it back where I had found it.","zh":"她转身时，我瞥见了那封信，只一眼，抽屉就关上了。纸边有一点金光一闪。我本想不去偷看，可还是多看了一眼。后来我在过道里被同一只箱子绊了一下，撞到了脚。她从没提过这事。多年以后，她让我先看了那些旧信的一小部分，微微笑着。那是我父亲写的信，写在他去世前一年。我读了两遍，又放回原处。"},"god":{"tw":[["idol",0],["superior",2],["divine",6],["divinity",0],["effigy",2],["heaven",6],["deity",0]],"en":"In the old church the people prayed to a god they called the divine one. On the wall hung a small idol, an effigy of some ancient deity, and the light made it look almost alive. My grandmother said she did not need a statue to reach heaven. She spoke of divinity as something you could feel in your hands. Her superior in the order agreed with her. I sat at the back and listened. She was the only person in that room who never seemed afraid. When the candles went out, she took my hand and led me into the cold street without a word.","zh":"在那座老教堂里，人们向一位他们称为圣者的神祈祷。墙上挂着一尊小神像，是某位古神的塑像，灯光下看上去几乎活了。我奶奶说她不需要雕像也能上天堂。她说神性是一种你用手就能感觉到的东西。她在教会里的上司也同意她。我坐在后排听着。满屋子人里，只有她从不显得害怕。蜡烛灭时，她牵着我的手，一句话不说就带我走进寒冷的街上。"},"group":{"tw":[["radical",0],["race",3],["meet",2],["member",6],["team",3],["unit",2],["joint",6]],"en":"A small group of us would meet every Thursday in the back room. Each member belonged to a different club and had a different idea of the race ahead. One man held more radical views than the rest. We worked as one team, and in time we became a single unit. The joint project was small but ours. I still keep the list of names from those years. We lost touch after the work ended, but once a year one of them writes to me. He always asks about the others, and I never know what to say.","zh":"我们一小群人每个星期四在后屋碰头。每个人属于不同的俱乐部，对前面的那场角逐各有各的看法。有个人的想法比别人激进得多。我们像一个队那样干活，慢慢地成了一个整体。共同的项目不大，却是我们自己的。那些年的名单我还留着。活干完后大家便断了来往，可每年总有一个人给我写信，每次都问起其余的人，而我总不知该怎么答。"},"hate":{"tw":[["hatred",0],["abhor",3],["dislike",2],["love",1],["shame",6],["detest",0],["fear",6]],"en":"I did not hate the man who took my place; I only disliked him at first. My mother said hatred eats the one who holds it, and that fear does more harm than anger. I learned to abhor cruelty, and in time to detest any kind of lie. But I could not love him either, and that was my shame. We shook hands years later, in the street, and said nothing of the past. He was old by then, and thinner than I remembered. I walked home slowly and felt lighter than I had in years.","zh":"我并不恨那个顶了我位子的人，起初只是不喜欢他。我妈说，恨会啃噬怀着恨的人，而恐惧比愤怒伤害更大。我学会了憎恶残忍，后来也厌恶任何谎言。可我也没法喜欢他，这就是我的羞愧之处。多年后我们在街上握了手，谁都没提过去。那时他老了，比我记忆中瘦。我慢慢走回家，觉得多年没这么轻松过。"},"heavy":{"tw":[["big",5],["character",2],["light",1],["ground",6],["great",0],["fire",6],["hard",0]],"en":"The box was heavy, too big for me to carry alone. It held a great many books, and the ground was soft from the rain. My uncle had a hard, quiet character and would not complain. He took one end and I took the other, and we set it by the fire. The work was light compared with the farm, he said. We sat down and drank tea in the warmth. When I left that evening, he walked me to the gate and told me to come back with better shoes.","zh":"那口箱子很沉，大得我一个人搬不动。里面装了很多书，地上被雨泡软了。我叔性子又硬又静，从不抱怨。他抬一头，我抬一头，把箱子放到火边。他说，跟农场里的活比，这算轻的。我们坐下，在暖意里喝茶。那天傍晚我走时，他送我到门口，叫我下次来换双好鞋。"},"hell":{"tw":[["pit",0],["trouble",2],["heaven",1],["crazy",6],["sin",0],["cry",6],["blaze",0]],"en":"The summer was so hot it felt like hell. The old factory was a pit of dust, and the blaze of the furnaces never went out. The men said the heat would drive them crazy. My father called the long shifts a kind of trouble he could not leave. Someone began to cry near the gate. He told me that heaven and sin were far away compared with a day like this, and told me to go home. I walked the long road back and counted the windows that still had light. There were not many.","zh":"那年夏天热得像地狱。老厂是个满是灰尘的坑，炉火的烈焰从不熄灭。工人们说这热会把人逼疯。我父亲把这些长班叫做一种他离不开的苦。门口有人哭起来。他对我说，比起这样的一个白天，天堂和罪都远得很，然后叫我回家。我沿着长路往回走，数那些还亮着灯的窗户。没几扇。"},"ice":{"tw":[["glass",0],["cool",2],["hot",6],["frost",3],["cover",2],["dust",6],["chalk",0]],"en":"The pond had a cover of ice, thin as glass. In the frost the reeds looked white as chalk, and a little dust of snow lay on the bank. I put my hand on the cold surface; it was cool at first, then so cold it burned like hot iron. My sister drew lines with a stick. We heard the ice crack once, far out, and stepped back together. She asked if we could walk across it, and I said no. We went home the long way, along the road.","zh":"池塘上覆着一层冰，薄得像玻璃。霜里芦苇白得像粉笔，岸上落着一点雪末。我把手按在冰冷的表面上，起初是凉的，接着冷得像烧红的铁。我妹妹用一根棍子在上面画线。远处冰响了一声，我们一齐往后退。她问能不能从冰上走过去，我说不行。我们绕远路，沿着大道回了家。"},"imagine":{"tw":[["guess",0],["dream",3],["else",6],["suppose",0],["suspect",3],["maybe",6],["think",3]],"en":"I like to imagine a quiet town where nothing ever goes wrong. I suppose everyone has a dream like that. Maybe you think it is foolish. I guess I do, too. But when I suspect that something bad is coming, I go back to that picture and let it hold me. There is nothing else I can do about it. So I close my eyes and try to think of the light on the water. It is a small habit, but it has carried me through some hard mornings. My sister says I should live in the real world, and she is probably right.","zh":"我喜欢想象一座安静的镇子，那里从不出差错。我想每个人都有这样的梦吧。也许你觉得这很傻。我猜我也有点傻。可每当我猜到坏事要来时，我就回到那幅画面里，让它托着我。除此之外我也做不了什么。于是我闭上眼，努力去想水面上的光。这不过是个小习惯，却陪我熬过了一些难熬的清晨。我妹妹说我该活在现实里，她说的大概没错。"},"inside":{"tw":[["within",0],["belly",3],["surface",2],["empty",6],["interior",5],["midst",3],["hand",6]],"en":"Inside the old house everything was quiet. The interior was empty except for one chair, and the surface of the floor was grey with dust. A small bird had got within the walls and could not find its way out. I held it in the palm of my hand and felt its belly move. In the midst of that silence it seemed very loud. I carried it to the door and let it go. It sat on the step for a moment, as if deciding, and then flew straight up into the grey light.","zh":"老屋里面一片寂静。屋子里空荡荡的，只有一把椅子，地板表面蒙着灰色的尘。一只小鸟钻进了墙里，找不到出路。我把它捧在手心，感到它的肚子在动。在那片寂静当中，这动静显得很响。我把它拿到门口放走。它在台阶上停了一会儿，像在拿主意，然后直直飞进灰白的天光里。"},"key":{"tw":[["discover",0],["list",2],["major",6],["paint",0],["space",2],["step",6],["identify",0]],"en":"The key to the old shed was hidden under a stone. On the wall inside hung a list of names, and someone had used paint to mark a major date. I wanted to discover who had lived there, so I began to identify the families one by one. There was very little space on the page, and I had to write small. Step by step the whole story came together. I still have that list in a drawer, and sometimes I read the names aloud. Nobody in the family can remember them now.","zh":"旧棚子的钥匙藏在石头下面。里面墙上挂着一份名单，有人用油漆标出了一个重要的日子。我想弄清谁曾住在这里，便一个一个去辨认那些人家。纸上的空白很小，我只能写得很小。一步一步地，整个故事就拼了起来。那张单子还在我抽屉里，有时我会把名字念出声来。如今家里已没人记得他们了。"},"large":{"tw":[["big",0],["size",2],["small",1],["well",6],["great",5],["vast",6],["heavy",0]],"en":"A large table took up most of the room, far too big for the small kitchen. We measured its size twice, but it would not fit. My aunt said a great house needed great things, and this one was vast and heavy. It was well made, she added, and could not be cut down. In the end we left it where it stood and ate around it. For years it was the centre of that house. Every meal, every argument, every quiet evening happened at that table. When the house was sold, the new family kept it too, and I was glad.","zh":"一张大桌子占了屋里大半地方，对这间小厨房来说大得离谱。我们量了两遍尺寸，还是放不下。我姑妈说大房子就该配大东西，这张又大又沉。她还说做工很好，不能锯短。最后我们由它立在那儿，围着它吃饭。好多年里，它都是那所房子的中心。每一顿饭、每一次争吵、每一个安静的傍晚，都在这张桌边发生。房子卖掉后，新人家也把它留了下来，我很高兴。"},"luck":{"tw":[["chance",0],["misfortune",3],["condition",2],["good",6],["lot",0],["happy",6],["fortune",0]],"en":"Some people talk about luck as if it were a thing you could hold. My father said it was mostly chance and a good condition of mind. He had known his share of misfortune, and a lot of hard years, yet he stayed happy. He called it his fortune to have work and a warm room. I did not always believe him. But when things went well, I did not argue. He died in a bad winter, and I remember thinking that he had been right about most things. Not about luck, perhaps, but about the rest.","zh":"有些人谈运气，好像它是件能攥在手里的东西。我父亲说，那多半是机遇，加上一副好心态。他历过自己的那份不顺，也有过许多艰难的年份，可他一直高高兴兴。他把有活干、有间暖屋子叫做自己的福气。我并不总信他。可事情顺的时候，我也不争辩。他在一个寒冬里走了，我记得自己当时想，大多数事上他都是对的。也许不是运气，但是其余的一切。"},"mark":{"tw":[["check",0],["line",3],["add",2],["cross",0],["spot",3],["book",2],["note",0]],"en":"The teacher asked us to check our work and mark every mistake. She drew a line under the wrong word, then a small cross beside it. I had to add a note at the top of the page and write my name in the book. There was one spot of ink on the corner. I read the whole page again before I handed it in. That night I dreamed of red lines crossing the paper, one after another. In the morning I understood what she had been trying to show me.","zh":"老师让我们检查自己的作业，把每个错都标出来。她在错字下面画了一道线，又在旁边画了个小叉。我得在纸头上加一句批注，再把名字写在簿子上。角上有一个墨点。交上去之前，我把整页又读了一遍。那天夜里，我梦见红色的线一道道划过纸面。第二天早上，我明白了她想让我看到的东西。"},"market":{"tw":[["mart",0],["offer",3],["change",2],["stock",6],["bazaar",3],["class",2],["retail",6]],"en":"Every Saturday my mother went to the market and came back with a full bag. She liked the small mart better than the big shops, and she knew every stall in the bazaar. She would offer a low price, then wait for the change in the seller's face. The stock was different each week, and once she found a coat fit for a wedding. It was cheaper than retail, she said, and better made. She belonged to a class of shoppers who never paid the first price. I went with her once, and I could not keep up. She moved through the crowd like water through a gate.","zh":"每个星期六，我妈都去市场，回来时拎着满满一袋。比起大商店，她更喜欢那家小集市，市场里每个摊位她都认得。她先压个低价，再等卖主脸上的变化。货每周都不一样，有一次她找到一件适合婚礼穿的外套。她说比零售便宜，做工还更好。她属于那种从不照头价付钱的主顾。我跟她去过一回，根本跟不上。她在人堆里穿行，像水从闸门里流过去。"},"marry":{"tw":[["tie",0],["unite",2],["daughter",6],["wed",0],["officiate",2],["mother",6],["espouse",0]],"en":"My cousin decided to marry in the spring. An old friend would officiate, and the two families would unite for a single day. His mother cried when she heard, and his daughter carried the rings. The tie between the two houses went back many years. They chose to wed in a small hall, and to espouse their promises quietly, without a crowd. I was asked to hold the door. The hall was cold that morning, and someone had forgotten to bring flowers. It did not matter; nobody looked at the walls.","zh":"我表哥决定春天结婚。一位老朋友来主持，两家人会在这一天合成一家。他母亲听说后哭了，他女儿捧的戒指。两家的渊源能追溯好多年。他们决定在一间小礼堂里成婚，不声不响地互许承诺，不要人群。让我去把门。那天早上礼堂很冷，有人忘了带花。没关系，没人去看那几面墙。"},"near":{"tw":[["close",5],["push",3],["far",1],["outskirts",6],["dear",0],["where",6],["good",0]],"en":"The station was near enough to walk, on the outskirts of the town. My mother said it was close, but on a hot day it did not feel so. I would push the pram up the long hill, past the houses where the gardens were full of roses. She was dear to everyone on that road. Far behind us the factory smoke rose. That was the year I learned how good a short walk could be. Now the town has grown, and the station is no longer at the edge. But the hill is still there.","zh":"车站近得可以走过去，就在镇子边上。我妈说很近，可大热天里一点也不觉得近。我推着婴儿车上那道长坡，路过那些花园里开满玫瑰的人家。那条路上人人都喜欢她。远远的，在我们身后，工厂的烟升起来。就是那一年，我知道了短短一段路也能让人舒服。如今镇子大了，车站也不在边上了。可那道坡还在。"},"pair":{"tw":[["couple",3],["ride",3],["join",2],["behind",6],["match",0],["serve",3],["mate",0]],"en":"A pair of old shoes stood behind the door, a couple of sizes too small for me. I would ride my bike to the shop to have them mended, then join the queue and wait. The man behind the counter had a mate who did the work. He said the two shoes did not match, but that a good pair could still serve for years. I paid and left. They lasted two winters and one hard spring. When I finally threw them out, I stood by the bin for a while.","zh":"门后放着一双旧鞋，比我的脚小了两号。我骑车去店里修，然后排进队里等。柜台后面那个人有个搭档专门做这活。他说这两只鞋不是一对，可好鞋还能穿好多年。我付了钱就走。它们又撑过两个冬天和一个难熬的春天。最后我把它们扔掉时，在垃圾桶边站了一会儿。"},"park":{"tw":[["green",0],["lot",2],["hill",6],["common",0],["gear",2],["road",6],["commons",0]],"en":"On Sundays we walked through the park at the top of the hill. The green was full of children, and the road beyond it led down to the common. My father would leave the car in the lot and carry the gear himself. He said the commons belonged to everyone, and nobody should fence it in. We sat on the grass until the light went. Those afternoons are the clearest thing I have kept from my childhood. Nothing happened in them, and that was the point. My sister would run down the hill and back, and I would count the times she did it.","zh":"星期天我们穿过山顶上的公园。草地上满是孩子，旁边那条路通向下边的公地。我父亲把车停在停车场，自己扛着东西。他说公地是大家的，谁都不该把它圈起来。我们坐在草地上，直到天光暗下去。那些下午是我从童年里留下来的最清晰的画面。什么也没发生，而这正是它的意思。我妹妹会跑下山坡再跑回来，我就数她跑了几趟。"},"particular":{"tw":[["special",0],["highlight",3],["proposition",2],["general",1],["instance",6],["detail",0],["item",0]],"en":"There was one particular thing about that house I could not forget. For instance, the way the light fell on the stairs in the late afternoon. Every detail of it is still clear to me, though in general the rest has gone. My aunt would highlight a single item on her list each week and make it a small celebration. It was not a special day, only an ordinary one, but the proposition pleased her. I have tried to live that way myself, and it is harder than it sounds. You need patience, and a good memory for small things.","zh":"那所房子里有一件特别的事，我怎么也忘不掉。比如说，傍晚光落在楼梯上的样子。它的每个细节在我心里都还清楚，尽管大体上其余的都已模糊。我姑妈每星期会在单子上挑出一样，把它过成一个小小的节庆。那不是特别的日子，只是平常的一天，可这个主意让她高兴。我也试着那样过日子，做起来比听起来难。你得有耐心，还得记性好，记得住小事。"},"plus":{"tw":[["positive",5],["advantage",3],["quality",2],["minus",1],["extra",6],["resource",3],["regular",6]],"en":"The price plus the bag fee came to more than I had. On the plus side, the quality was high, and there was an extra discount for regular buyers. The seller said the coat needed little resource to make and would not wear quickly. That was a real advantage, my mother said. She counted the minus points too: no return, no change. Still, the good parts were positive enough. We took it home and it lasted for years. I wore it through two winters and one long illness. It never once let the wind through.","zh":"价钱加上袋子费，比我带的钱还多。往好里说，质量很高，常客还有额外的折扣。卖主说这外套做起来不费什么料，也不容易穿坏。我妈说，这是实打实的好处。她也没忘了算坏的方面：不能退，不能换。不过好处还是够多的。我们把它带回家，穿了好些年。我穿着它过了两个冬天和一场漫长的病。它一次也没让风透进来。"},"pop":{"tw":[["kill",0],["appear",2],["hop",6],["start",0],["drink",2],["music",6],["popular",0]],"en":"The little cafe played pop music all afternoon, and it was popular with the students. Now and then a man would appear at the door with a guitar, hop onto a stool, and start to play. Nobody tried to kill the noise; they only ordered another drink. I sat near the window with my notes. When the music stopped, the room seemed empty. I stayed until closing, longer than I meant to. The owner turned off the lights one by one and told me to come back soon. I did, for a while, every Thursday, always at the same table.","zh":"那家小咖啡馆一下午都放着流行音乐，学生们都爱来。时不时有个男人拎着吉他出现在门口，跳上一张凳子，弹起来。没人想把这声音压下去，只是又点一杯喝的。我拿着本子坐在窗边。音乐一停，屋里显得空落落的。我一直待到打烊，比打算的久。店主一盏盏关灯，叫我快些再来。有一阵子我真来了，每星期四，总坐同一张桌子。"},"problem":{"tw":[["job",0],["matter",3],["question",2],["change",6],["trouble",0],["puzzle",3],["possible",6]],"en":"The problem with the old pump was simple, but nobody had the time to fix it. It was my job to find out what was wrong. I asked one question after another and wrote the answers down. The change of parts was possible, though not cheap. The whole matter was a puzzle I could not solve alone. In the end we had no more trouble, and two men had it running by evening. They charged very little and refused the tea my mother offered. She said they were the last of a kind.","zh":"那台旧水泵的毛病并不复杂，可没人有空修。弄清哪里出问题是我的活。我一个接一个地问，把答案记下来。换零件是可行的，只是不便宜。整件事是个我一个人解不开的谜。最后我们再没出岔子，傍晚时两个男人把它弄转了。他们收钱很少，还推辞了我妈端来的茶。她说他们是最后一类这样的人了。"},"quarter":{"tw":[["draw",0],["kill",2],["drop",6],["tail",0],["divide",2],["net",6],["stern",0]],"en":"A quarter of the crew stood at the stern of the boat and watched the net come in. My uncle would draw it slowly, hand over hand, and divide the catch into small piles. A single bad fish could kill the mood on deck. He cut one into quarters and threw the tail to the gulls. A drop of water fell from his chin. The sea was flat and grey all around us. Nobody spoke for a long time. Then he laughed and said the fish had won again. We turned the boat toward the harbour, and the sun went down behind the hills.","zh":"四分之一的船员站在船尾，看着渔网收上来。我叔慢慢往上拉，一手接一手，把捕到的鱼分成好几小堆。一条坏鱼就能把甲板上的兴致全毁了。他把一条切成四块，把尾巴扔给海鸥。一滴水从他下巴落下来。四周的海又平又灰。好一会儿没人说话。后来他笑了，说鱼又赢了。我们把船转向港口，太阳落到山后面去了。"},"real":{"tw":[["actual",5],["coin",2],["nominal",1],["good",6],["really",0],["better",6],["material",0]],"en":"The coin in my hand was real, not a copy. Its actual value was small, only nominal, but it was old and made of good material. I really wanted to keep it, though my brother said a better one could be found in any shop. He did not understand why I held on to it. It was the only thing left from that house. For years it sat in a tin on the shelf, and I never spent it. Some things are worth less than they cost to lose. When I finally gave it away, the shop was closing and the man behind the counter was kind.","zh":"我手里那枚硬币是真的，不是仿的。它实际的面值很小，只是名义上的，可它很旧，用料也好。我真的很想留着，尽管我哥说随便哪家店都能找到更好的。他不懂我为什么攥着不放。那是那所房子里唯一留下的东西。它在那只铁盒里搁了好些年，我一次也没花掉。有些东西的价值，还比不上失去它的代价。最后我把它送出去时，那家店正要关门，柜台后的人很和气。"},"realise":{"tw":[["clear",0],["perceive",3],["know",2],["accomplish",6],["see",0],["fulfil",6],["understand",0]],"en":"Only later did I realise what he had meant. It was clear to me then that he had tried to fulfil a promise made long ago, and that he would not rest until it was done. I could see it in the way he worked. I did not fully understand it at the time, and I did not perceive how tired he was. Now I know. He had accomplished more than he ever said. I wish I had told him so. There is a lot I would say now, if the chance came back.","zh":"直到后来，我才明白他那句话的意思。那时我看清了，他是想兑现很久以前许下的一个诺言，事没办完他就不肯歇。我从他干活的样子里看得出来。当时我并没有完全懂，也没察觉他已经那么累。现在我知道了。他做成的比他嘴上说的多得多。我真希望当时告诉过他。如果机会能回来，我现在有许多话要说。"},"reason":{"tw":[["cause",0],["find",3],["present",2],["ground",0],["why",3],["think",2],["argue",0]],"en":"There was no reason for the delay, or none that anyone would present. I tried to find the cause myself, standing on the wet ground by the gate. My father thought it was the rain. My aunt would argue that it was the new manager. Nobody could say why the train had stopped, only that it had. I stopped asking questions and waited. In the end it came, an hour late, full of tired faces. I found a seat by the window and slept until my stop. Nobody ever explained it, and after a while nobody cared.","zh":"这趟误点没什么理由，或者说没人肯说出个理由。我自己站在门口湿漉漉的地上，想找出原因。我父亲觉得是下雨。我姑妈偏说是新来的经理。谁都说不清火车为什么停，只知道它停了。我不再问了，就等着。它终于来了，晚了一个钟头，挤满疲倦的脸。我在窗边找了个座位，一直睡到我的站。没人解释过，过一阵子也没人在意了。"},"sex":{"tw":[["gender",0],["tempt",3],["class",2],["abuse",6],["arouse",0],["distinguish",2],["homosexual",6]],"en":"At the clinic the clerk handed me a form with a line for sex. He said the word had been changed to gender on the newer forms. I was tempted to leave it blank, but he asked me to distinguish it from the line for age. A young man of another class sat beside me, and he said he was homosexual and did not mind the old wording. The question, he added, had begun to arouse a quiet debate. Nobody wanted any abuse of private details. I wrote my answer and handed the form back. It was the only honest thing on the page.","zh":"在诊所里，职员递给我一张表格，上面有一栏问性别。他说新表格里这个词已经改成了性别一项的另一种说法。我本想空着不填，可他请我把它和年龄那一栏区分开。旁边坐着一位来自另一个阶层的年轻人，他说自己是同性恋，并不介意旧的措辞。他还说，这个问题近来悄悄引起了一场讨论。谁都不愿意自己的私人信息被滥用。我写下答案，把表交了回去。那是那一页上唯一诚实的东西。"},"shut":{"tw":[["close",0],["draw",3],["open",1],["stop",6],["closed",0],["seal",3],["run",6]],"en":"The shop was shut, and a small sign said closed for the day. I tried to open the door, then gave up. The wind had begun to draw the clouds across the sky. I ran to the next street to find another one, but the shutters were down there too. I wanted to close my eyes, to stop and think, but the rain pushed me on. A man was sealing a box by the wall. I asked him when the shops would open again. He did not know either, and he said the whole town closed early in such weather. I walked home with wet shoes and no bread.","zh":"店已经关了，一块小牌子写着今天歇业。我试着推门，后来作罢。风开始把云往天上拉。我跑到下一条街想找另一家，可那里的卷帘门也拉下了。我想停下来想想，雨却推着我往前走。有个人正在墙边封一只箱子。我问他店什么时候再开。他也不知道，只说这种天气里全镇都早早关门。我湿着鞋回了家，什么也没买到。"},"slight":{"tw":[["little",0],["snub",3],["dismiss",2],["sharp",6],["thin",5],["sudden",6],["fragile",0]],"en":"She gave me a slight as she passed, a small snub I did not expect. It was a little thing, and yet it stung. Her face was thin and sharp in the cold light. I wanted to dismiss it, the way one dismisses a sudden noise, but I could not. There was something fragile under her calm. I stood there and said nothing. Later I learned that she had been ill for weeks and had not told anyone. The slight had cost her more than it cost me. I never mentioned it, and neither did she.","zh":"她走过时对我冷淡了一下，那是我没料到的一次小小怠慢。本是件小事，却扎人。冷光里她的脸又瘦又利。我想把它置之不理，就像不去理会一声突响，可我做不到。她的平静底下有什么脆弱的东西。我站在原处，什么也没说。后来我才知道，她病了好几个星期，谁也没告诉。那点冷淡，她付出的代价比我还大。我从没提过，她也没有。"},"small":{"tw":[["little",5],["size",2],["big",1],["well",6],["low",0],["main",6],["minor",0]],"en":"A small boat took us across the river. Its size surprised me; it looked too little for three people. My father said a big boat was not always safer. The main thing was to keep it low in the water and row well. There was one minor leak near the front, which he fixed with a cloth. We reached the other bank before noon. On the far side a dog was waiting, as if it had known we were coming. It followed us all the way to the village. I was twelve that summer, and I still think of that river as mine.","zh":"一条小船把我们载过河。它的尺寸让我吃惊，看着太小，装不下三个人。我父亲说大船不一定就更安全。要紧的是让它压得低低的，把桨划好。船头有个小漏洞，他用一块布补上了。中午前我们就到了对岸。那边有条狗在等着，好像早知道我们要来。它一路跟到村里。那年夏天我十二岁，到现在我还觉得那条河是我的。"},"smile":{"tw":[["grin",3],["beam",3],["express",2],["laugh",6],["sneer",3],["grimace",2],["touch",6]],"en":"She gave me a small smile at the door. It was not a grin and not a laugh, only the quiet way she had of showing that she was glad. Her face would beam for a moment, then go still. She never used a sneer, and I never saw her grimace. To express warmth, she would touch your arm and say nothing. I miss that more than anything. She is gone now, and the house is quiet in a different way. I still open the door slowly, as if she might be standing there.","zh":"在门口她对我微微一笑。那不是咧嘴的笑，也不是大笑，只是她那种安静地表示高兴的方式。她的脸会亮一下，随即又静下来。她从不用冷笑，我也没见过她皱脸。她要表示亲切时，就碰一下你的胳膊，什么也不说。我最想念的就是这个。她如今不在了，屋子里静得不一样。我开门时还是会慢一点，好像她可能就站在那儿。"},"snow":{"tw":[["blow",0],["flurry",3],["layer",2],["rain",6],["coke",0],["precipitate",2],["fog",6]],"en":"Snow began to fall in the afternoon, at first a light flurry, then a steady rain of white. The wind would blow it against the windows and pile a thick layer on the step. Fog covered the yard before dark. My uncle went out to bring in the coke, and his boots left deep marks in the snow. The cold seemed to precipitate a silence over the whole street. Nobody came to the door that evening. Even the dogs were quiet, and the only sound was the soft weight of the snow itself.","zh":"下午开始下雪，先是一阵轻飘的雪絮，随后成了绵密的白雨。风把它吹到窗上，在台阶上积起厚厚一层。天黑前雾罩住了院子。我叔出去把焦炭搬进来，靴子在雪里留下深深的印子。寒气仿佛让整条街一下子沉入寂静。那天傍晚没人来敲门。连狗都静了，唯一的声响就是雪本身落下的那点分量。"},"sport":{"tw":[["fun",0],["freak",3],["athlete",2],["club",6],["play",2],["pun",3],["feature",0]],"en":"Sport was the one thing he loved. He was no athlete, only a quiet boy who liked to play in the field behind the school. Every club wanted him because he made the games fun. Once he made a pun about the ball, and the whole team laughed. The others called him a freak for joking so much, but never unkindly. The main feature of those afternoons was his laugh. I did not play well, and it never mattered to him. He would wait at the gate until I was ready to walk home.","zh":"运动是他唯一喜欢的事。他算不上运动员，只是个爱在学校后面空地上玩的安静男孩。每个俱乐部都想要他，因为有他在，比赛就有趣。有一次他拿球开了个玩笑，全队都笑了。别人笑他太爱说笑，管他叫怪人，可从没有恶意。那些下午最大的特色就是他的笑声。我玩得不好，他一点也不在意。他会在门口一直等到我准备回家。"},"straight":{"tw":[["flat",0],["stretch",3],["section",2],["round",6],["neat",0],["consecutive",6],["square",0]],"en":"The road ran straight across the flat land for a long stretch. In one section there were neat rows of trees on both sides, all the same height. The fields were square, and the sky above them was round and wide. We drove without stopping for three consecutive hours. It was the straightest road I have ever known. My mother slept in the back, and my father kept his eyes on the white line. I watched the fields and said nothing for hours. When we finally turned off, the whole world seemed to bend.","zh":"那条路笔直地穿过平地，延伸了好长一段。其中有一段，两边是整整齐齐的树，高矮全都一样。田是方方正正的，田上的天又圆又阔。我们一连开了三个钟头没停。那是我见过的最直的一条路。我妈在后座睡着，我爸盯着那条白线。我看了好几个钟头的田野，一句话没说。等我们终于拐下大路，整个世界仿佛都弯了。"},"suggest":{"tw":[["advise",0],["advance",3],["express",2],["indicate",0],["recommend",3],["inform",2],["propose",0]],"en":"My manager would suggest a change and then wait for us to think about it. She liked to advise rather than order, and she would recommend a plan only after we had spoken. Once she asked me to express my own view first. The figures seemed to indicate a slow advance in sales. She would inform the director and propose a small test. I learned a lot from the way she worked. Years later, in another office, I found myself doing the same thing. I would ask a question and then say nothing at all.","zh":"我上司会提一个改动，然后等我们自己去想。她喜欢提建议而不是下命令，只有在我们都发过言之后，她才会推荐一个方案。有一回她让我先说说自己的想法。那些数字似乎显示销量在缓慢上升。她会通知主管，再提个小试验。我从她做事的方式里学了不少。多年后，在另一间办公室，我发现自己也这么做了。我会先问一个问题，然后就什么也不说。"},"surprise":{"tw":[["storm",0],["catch",3],["act",2],["despite",6],["amaze",3],["change",2],["doubt",6]],"en":"The storm came as a surprise to everyone in the village. Despite the warning on the radio, nobody had expected it so early. The change in the sky would amaze even the oldest farmer. I had no doubt that we would lose the roof. My father made a quick act of tying the door and catching the loose shutters. By morning the wind was gone and the street was quiet. We walked outside and found a tree across the road. Nobody was hurt, and that was the only thing that mattered.","zh":"那场风暴让村里每个人都吃了一惊。尽管收音机里报了警，谁也没料到它来得这么早。天上的变化连最老的农夫看了都要吃惊。我毫不怀疑我们会丢掉屋顶。我父亲赶紧动手，把门拴好，抓住松了的窗板。到早上，风停了，街上安静下来。我们走到外面，发现一棵树横在路上。没人受伤，这才是唯一要紧的事。"},"swim":{"tw":[["float",0],["school",3],["travel",2],["surf",6],["drown",0],["crawl",3],["skate",6]],"en":"In summer I would swim in the lake every morning. A school of small fish would float near the shore, and I could see them from above. My brother liked to travel to the coast to surf, but I never learned. He said I swam like a slow crawl and would drown in real waves. In winter we would skate on the same water, hard as glass. Those were the years when the lake was still clean enough to drink. Now there is a fence around it, and a sign with rules.","zh":"夏天我每天早上都到湖里游泳。一群小鱼会浮在岸边，我从上面就能看见。我哥喜欢跑到海边去冲浪，我却一直没学会。他说我游得像慢吞吞的自由泳，到了真正的大浪里非淹死不可。冬天我们就在同一片水上滑冰，硬得像玻璃。那些年湖水还干净得能喝。如今湖周围围了栏，还立了块写满规矩的牌子。"},"tape":{"tw":[["record",2],["cut",3],["attach",2],["video",6],["write",3],["strip",2],["cassette",6]],"en":"I found an old tape in a drawer, a cassette from years ago. On the label was my mother's writing, small and careful. I had to cut a strip of it where it was torn, then attach the ends again. It held a record of a family dinner, and someone had made a short video of the same evening. I played it once and sat still in the dark. I could hear my father laughing at something nobody remembered. I have not played it since, and I never will. Some things are better kept than used.","zh":"我在抽屉里找到一盘旧磁带，是好多年前的那种盒式带。标签是我妈的字。有一处撕了，我得剪下一小条，再把两头接上。里面录着一顿家宴，那个晚上还有人拍了一小段视频。我放了一遍，就一动不动地坐在黑里。我听见我父亲在为什么事笑，而那事谁也不记得了。从那以后我再没放过，也永远不会放了。有些东西留着比用掉更好。"},"thick":{"tw":[["deep",5],["inside",2],["thin",1],["brush",6],["dense",0],["beneath",6],["compact",0]],"en":"The fog was thick over the valley, deep and dense in the low places. Beneath it the fields were hidden, and only the tops of the trees showed. I walked with a thin stick, tapping the path ahead. The brush on both sides grew close and compact, and once I lost the way. Inside the fog everything sounded near. A dog barked somewhere to my left, and then again, closer. I stopped and waited until I could tell which way it came from. The sound led me back to the road, and I never forgot it.","zh":"山谷上罩着浓雾，低处又深又密。雾底下田野都看不见了，只有树梢露出来。我拿着一根细棍，敲着前面的路走。两边的灌木长得又近又密，有一回我迷了路。雾里面，什么声音听着都很近。我左边什么地方有条狗叫了一声，接着又叫，更近了。我停下来，等到能分辨出声音是从哪个方向来的。那声音把我引回了路上，我一直没忘。"},"understand":{"tw":[["read",3],["catch",3],["how",6],["realise",0],["follow",3],["know",6],["see",0]],"en":"I could not understand the letter at first. I read it twice, then a third time, trying to catch the meaning behind the words. I did not know how to answer it. My sister read it too, and she began to realise what had happened. I could follow the facts, but not the feeling. Only later, in the quiet of the evening, did I see what he had tried to say. By then it was too late to write back. I keep the letter in a book, and sometimes I take it out.","zh":"起初我看不懂那封信。我读了两遍，又读第三遍，想抓住字面背后的意思。我不知道该怎么回。我姐也读了，她开始明白发生了什么事。我能跟得上那些事实，却跟不上那份心情。直到后来，在傍晚的安静里，我才看清他想说的是什么。那时再回信已经太晚了。我把信夹在一本书里，有时会拿出来看看。"},"way":{"tw":[["room",0],["fit",3],["choice",2],["direction",0],["form",3],["course",2],["fashion",0]],"en":"There was only one way to fit everything into the small room, and I found it at last. I had no choice but to move the desk and turn it the other way. The direction of the light helped. In this form the space looked twice as big. My mother said it was the fashion now to keep things plain. I took the course she suggested and left the walls bare. For a week the room felt like someone else's. Then one morning it felt like mine, and I stopped moving the furniture.","zh":"要把所有东西塞进这间小屋，只有一种办法，我终于找到了。我别无选择，只能挪开桌子，把它转到另一个方向。光的方向帮了忙。这样一摆，空间看着大了一倍。我妈说如今时兴把东西收拾得素净。我照她提的路子做了，让墙空着。有一个星期，这屋子像别人家的。后来有天早上，它像我的了，我就不再挪家具了。"},"web":{"tw":[["net",0],["tent",3],["object",2],["internet",6],["network",0],["trap",2],["video",6]],"en":"A spider had built a web between the fence and the old tent in the garden. The net was fine as thread, and a small object, a dead fly, hung in the middle. I watched a video about spiders on the internet that evening, and I learned how they make the network strong. It is a kind of trap that never needs repair. In the morning the web was gone. I looked for it again the next day, and the day after that. Nothing stayed in that garden for long.","zh":"一只蜘蛛在篱笆和园里那顶旧帐篷之间结了张网。网丝细得像线，中间挂着个小东西，一只死苍蝇。那天晚上我在网上看了一段讲蜘蛛的视频，知道了它们怎么把这张网织得结实。那是一种从不需要修补的陷阱。到了早上，网不见了。第二天我又去找，第三天也去找。那园子里什么都留不长久。"},"wrong":{"tw":[["damage",0],["treat",2],["right",1],["why",6],["else",6],["amiss",0],["awry",0]],"en":"Something was wrong with the old machine, and I could not say why. Every part looked right, yet the whole thing had gone awry. I checked the damage twice. There was nothing else I could do that night. My father said not to treat it as a great problem, that a small thing was amiss somewhere. In the morning he found it and laughed. A wire had come loose, and it had taken him a single minute. He said most wrong things are smaller than they look. I have remembered that ever since, more than once.","zh":"那台旧机器出了毛病，我说不清是为什么。每个零件看着都对，可整体却失了常。我把损坏的地方查了两遍。那晚我再也做不了别的。我父亲说别把它当成什么大问题，不过是哪儿有点小毛病。第二天早上他找到了，笑起来。原来是一根线松了，他只花了一分钟。他说，大多数出错的事都比看上去要小。这句话我后来记了很久，不止一回想起。"},"zero":{"tw":[["nought",0],["adjust",2],["mean",6],["zip",0],["digit",2],["maximum",6],["null",0]],"en":"The temperature fell to zero before morning, and the little gauge showed a single digit. I had to adjust the setting to its maximum, but it did nothing. The reading stayed at nought. My father said the number did not mean anything at all; it was null, a zip. We put on two coats and went out anyway. The path was hard and bright, and our breath made small clouds. I could not feel my fingers, but I did not want to go back inside. That was the coldest night I can remember, and the house never warmed up the next day.","zh":"天亮前气温降到了零度，小仪表上只显示一个数字。我只好把设定调到最大，可它毫无反应。读数一直停在零。我父亲说这个数根本说明不了什么，是空的，等于没有。我们套上两件外套照样出了门。小路又硬又亮，我们的呼吸结成一小团一小团的白气。我手指都冻麻了，却不想回屋去。那是我记得的最冷的一夜，第二天屋里也一直没暖和起来。"}}});
